{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "67771d47e52f6a51",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "To protect against such attacks, servers MUST ensure that replay of tokens is prevented or limited.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6a5b1fa270b71e0d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD provide mitigations for this attack by limiting the usage and lifetime of address validation tokens; see Section 8.1.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc970aea011be634",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "Thus, a token SHOULD have an expiration time, which could be either an explicit expiration time or an issued timestamp that can be used to dynamically calculate the expiration time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "We use a duplicate filter to prevent tokens from being used more than once.",
      "id": "b03c0a1813eff965",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 123,
      "quote": "Servers are encouraged to allow tokens to be used only once, if possible; tokens MAY include additional information about clients to further narrow applicability or reuse.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0f69ad4340d389f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD ensure that tokens sent in Retry packets are only accepted for a short time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ac3a44fbc250d35",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "Tokens sent in Retry packets SHOULD include information that allows the server to verify that the source IP address and port in client packets remain constant.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6a8999883bf39233",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 239,
      "quote": "A server MAY provide clients with an address validation token during one connection that can be used on a subsequent connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "tracking_issue": "418",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "77d0b55e5b688c02",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 245,
      "quote": "Tokens sent in NEW_TOKEN frames MUST include information that allows the server to verify that the client IP address has not changed from when the token was issued.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "tracking_issue": "346",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ade60299d731d06",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 252,
      "quote": "A token issued with NEW_TOKEN MUST NOT include information that would allow values to be linked by an observer to the connection on which it was issued.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "tracking_issue": "345",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "3e37a73b0f9e3b35",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 259,
      "quote": "A server MUST ensure that every NEW_TOKEN frame it sends is unique across all clients, with the exception of those sent to repair losses of previously sent NEW_TOKEN frames.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "tracking_issue": "387",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "0725264c3c86457f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 266,
      "quote": "A server MAY provide clients with an address validation token during one connection that can be used on a subsequent connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "tracking_issue": "394",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "668eb355034f445b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 275,
      "quote": "Requiring the server to provide a different connection ID, along with the original_destination_connection_id transport parameter defined in Section 18.2, forces the server to demonstrate that it, or an entity it cooperates with, received the original Initial packet from the client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "78fa7c6674f4b528",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 319,
      "quote": "When a server receives an Initial packet with an address validation token, it MUST attempt to validate the token, unless it has already completed address validation.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f5e7c5f7f3cc3f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 344,
      "quote": "Tokens that are provided in NEW_TOKEN frames (Section 19.7) need to be valid for longer but SHOULD NOT be accepted multiple times.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "tracking_issue": "347",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "4af236aead5fa324",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 351,
      "quote": "Clients that want to break continuity of identity with a server can discard tokens provided using the NEW_TOKEN frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "tracking_issue": "388",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "c58aba4ba811afc7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 378,
      "quote": "Information that allows the server to distinguish between tokens from Retry and NEW_TOKEN MAY be accessible to entities other than the server.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d6868339d4d2733",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 402,
      "quote": "A token sent in a NEW_TOKEN frame or a Retry packet MUST be constructed in a way that allows the server to identify how it was provided to a client.  These tokens are carried in the same field but require different handling from servers.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "21f9acd69f6e33e8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 416,
      "quote": "There is no need for a single well-defined format for the token because the server that generates the token also consumes it.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6438ba3c543a24d4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 427,
      "quote": "An address validation token MUST be difficult to guess.  Including a random value with at least 128 bits of entropy in the token would be sufficient, but this depends on the server remembering the value it sends to clients.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "952ec3378fbf9b84",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 434,
      "quote": "A token-based scheme allows the server to offload any state associated with validation to the client.  For this design to work, the token MUST be covered by integrity protection against modification or falsification by clients.  Without integrity protection, malicious clients could generate or guess values for tokens that would be accepted by the server.  Only the server requires access to the integrity protection key for tokens.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8cf3402472674bd5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 497,
      "quote": "A token sent in a NEW_TOKEN frames or a Retry packet MUST be constructed in a way that allows the server to identify how it was provided to a client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f887ec4c745e4491",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 552,
      "quote": "Tokens sent in Retry packets SHOULD include information that allows the server to verify that the source IP address and port in client packets remain constant.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ff498c10212efd75",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 592,
      "quote": "Thus, a token SHOULD have an expiration time, which could be either an explicit expiration time or an issued timestamp that can be used to dynamically calculate the expiration time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7847856d43d7c69",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 624,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD ensure that tokens sent in Retry packets are only accepted for a short time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e276faca6a6d3b89",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 642,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD provide mitigations for this attack by limiting the usage and lifetime of address validation tokens; see Section 8.1.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e34c11c4bb6a4c7c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 676,
      "quote": "To protect against such attacks, servers MUST ensure that replay of tokens is prevented or limited.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d0cdf58b7a4121f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 699,
      "quote": "For this design to work, the token MUST be covered by integrity protection against modification or falsification by clients.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb7425a2d3e8b7b8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 746,
      "quote": "For this design to work, the token MUST be covered by integrity protection against modification or falsification by clients.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/address_token/default.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "13daecf3a6a0d583",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 183,
      "quote": "An endpoint that uses this design MUST either use the same connection ID length for all connections or encode the length of the connection ID such that it can be recovered without state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic/src/provider/connection_id.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f5438ba07719483",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "A receiver that sends only non-ack-eliciting packets, such as ACK frames, might not receive an acknowledgement for a long period of time.  This could cause the receiver to maintain state for a large number of ACK frames for a long period of time, and ACK frames it sends could be unnecessarily large.  In such a case, a receiver could send a PING or other small ack-eliciting frame occasionally, such as once per round trip, to elicit an ACK from the peer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/ack/settings.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fff00c95b97ec45b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "ACK Delay:  A variable-length integer encoding the acknowledgement delay in microseconds; see Section 13.2.5.  It is decoded by multiplying the value in the field by 2 to the power of the ack_delay_exponent transport parameter sent by the sender of the ACK frame; see Section 18.2.  Compared to simply expressing the delay as an integer, this encoding allows for a larger range of values within the same number of bytes, at the cost of lower resolution.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/ack/settings.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5aefea42a68e0c7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST acknowledge all ack-eliciting Initial and Handshake packets immediately",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/ack/settings.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c246c5b85549720c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "When a packet containing an ACK frame is acknowledged, the receiver can stop acknowledging packets less than or equal to the Largest Acknowledged field in the sent ACK frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/ack/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dea29a996a348895",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "The management of application error codes is left to application protocols.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/application/error.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-20.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "db1eebc55e3db945",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST be able to deliver stream data to an application as an ordered byte-stream.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/buffer/reassembler.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2bf3276319a34934",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 230,
      "quote": "Once a final size for a stream is known, it cannot change.  If a RESET_STREAM or STREAM frame is received indicating a change in the final size for the stream, an endpoint SHOULD respond with an error of type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/buffer/reassembler.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1d46b552cdd1fae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "QUIC permits the use of a generic code in place of a specific error code; see Section 11 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  For TLS alerts, this includes replacing any alert with a generic alert, such as handshake_failure (0x0128 in QUIC).  Endpoints MAY use a generic error code to avoid possibly exposing confidential information.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/connection/close.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "67598e99d4e57e99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "Sending a CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1d in an Initial or Handshake packet could expose application state or be used to alter application state.  A CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1d MUST be replaced by a CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1c when sending the frame in Initial or Handshake packets.  Otherwise, information about the application state might be revealed.  Endpoints MUST clear the value of the Reason Phrase field and SHOULD use the APPLICATION_ERROR code when converting to a CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1c.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/connection/close.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3f3d33fb19323674",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Each connection possesses a set of connection identifiers, or connection IDs, each of which can identify the connection. Connection IDs are independently selected by endpoints; each endpoint selects the connection IDs that its peer uses.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/connection/id.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "477ae01528322282",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 221,
      "quote": "When an Initial packet is sent by a client that has not previously received an Initial or Retry packet from the server, the client populates the Destination Connection ID field with an unpredictable value.  This Destination Connection ID MUST be at least 8 bytes in length.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/connection/id.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ef1bb4f3e6d2a63",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 350,
      "quote": "An endpoint that uses this design MUST either use the same connection ID length for all connections or encode the length of the connection ID such that it can be recovered without state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/connection/id.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2160169107b21492",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "A connection will time out if no packets are sent or received for a period longer than the time negotiated using the max_idle_timeout transport parameter; see Section 10.  However, state in middleboxes might time out earlier than that.  Though REQ-5 in [RFC4787] recommends a 2-minute timeout interval, experience shows that sending packets every 30 seconds is necessary to prevent the majority of middleboxes from losing state for UDP flows [GATEWAY].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/connection/limits.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "07b9ab0a21dc0219",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Prior to validating the client address, servers MUST NOT send more than three times as many bytes as the number of bytes they have received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/connection/limits.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "69abfb9a7acc8085",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "In addition to counting packets sent, endpoints MUST count the number of received packets that fail authentication during the lifetime of a connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "11565c5939538494",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "The Key Phase bit is initially set to 0 for the first set of 1-RTT packets and toggled to signal each subsequent key update.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "61f8c6d2d80f06e9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Endpoints responding to an apparent key update MUST NOT generate a timing side-channel signal that might indicate that the Key Phase bit was invalid (see Section 9.4).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb8b47056d5f406b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "The same header protection key is used for the duration of the connection, with the value not changing after a key update (see Section 6).  This allows header protection to be used to protect the key phase.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cfe89f1cf06d5998",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "Once generated, the next set of packet protection keys SHOULD be retained, even if the packet that was received was subsequently discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c639b2b4243e0235",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "After this period, old read keys and their corresponding secrets SHOULD be discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a783bb45523980ec",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "These updated keys MAY replace the previous keys at that time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "180212e5e4ea11c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY allow a period of approximately the Probe Timeout (PTO; see [QUIC-RECOVERY]) after promoting the next set of receive keys to be current before it creates the subsequent set of packet protection keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d92a841171a38b9d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 131,
      "quote": "Packets with higher packet numbers MUST be protected with either the same or newer packet protection keys than packets with lower packet numbers.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e7b0117d103dba20",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "Sending keys MUST be updated before sending an acknowledgement for the packet that was received with updated keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "35061e3f43ac31dc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 156,
      "quote": "The endpoint MUST update its send keys to the corresponding key phase in response, as described in Section 6.1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dab49bc0c242cb09",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 162,
      "quote": "Endpoints responding to an apparent key update MUST NOT generate a timing side-channel signal that might indicate that the Key Phase bit was invalid (see Section 9.4).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "17b275836631ee34",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old read keys for no more than three times the PTO after having received a packet protected using the new keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1a61ba7172b3b019",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 171,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old keys for some time after unprotecting a packet sent using the new keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "104ac1883b69337d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 184,
      "quote": "In addition to counting packets sent, endpoints MUST count the number of received packets that fail authentication during the lifetime of a connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1f8aec9477a0fe3e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 190,
      "quote": "If a key update is not possible or integrity limits are reached, the endpoint MUST stop using the connection and only send stateless resets in response to receiving packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "268ce322d030fff0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 196,
      "quote": "If the total number of received packets that fail authentication within the connection, across all keys, exceeds the integrity limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST immediately close the connection with a connection error of type AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED and not process any more packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f6b4e9a97e80a96",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 213,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST initiate a key update before sending more protected packets than the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD permits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d1de4e8ad616782",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 239,
      "quote": "If the total number of encrypted packets with the same key exceeds the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST stop using those keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "df6c62d1909d8ffa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 244,
      "quote": "If a key update is not possible or integrity limits are reached, the endpoint MUST stop using the connection and only send stateless resets in response to receiving packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c206d2dbf74e1435",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 254,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST count the number of encrypted packets for each set of keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "eac71bb105a71e24",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 268,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old read keys for no more than three times the PTO after having received a packet protected using the new keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bfb306e93fa0087f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 353,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old keys for some time after unprotecting a packet sent using the new keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d1b764154a18cb9a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 363,
      "quote": "After this period, old read keys and their corresponding secrets SHOULD be discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ce287691eae7b134",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 372,
      "quote": "For this reason, endpoints MUST be able to retain two sets of packet protection keys for receiving packets: the current and the next.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0abcf1c3ee65970e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 402,
      "quote": "In addition to counting packets sent, endpoints MUST count the number of received packets that fail authentication during the lifetime of a connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "357022de47101199",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 441,
      "quote": "If the total number of received packets that fail authentication within the connection, across all keys, exceeds the integrity limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST immediately close the connection with a connection error of type AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED and not process any more packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d518f88ec61ea83b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 487,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST count the number of encrypted packets for each set of keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "51b3517774ca81f4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 534,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST initiate a key update before sending more protected packets than the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD permits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d032f4772ecda74",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 545,
      "quote": "If the total number of encrypted packets with the same key exceeds the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST stop using those keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/keyset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "11be776677e6a56b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 6,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST count the number of encrypted packets for each set of keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/application/limited.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2f46bde2122e74f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "The output of this algorithm is a 5 byte mask that is applied to the protected header fields using exclusive OR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/header_crypto.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7693a35e027d1e45",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "Figure 6 shows a sample algorithm for applying header protection. Removing header protection only differs in the order in which the packet number length (pn_length) is determined (here \"^\" is used to represent exclusive OR). mask = header_protection(hp_key, sample) pn_length = (packet[0] & 0x03) + 1 if (packet[0] & 0x80) == 0x80: # Long header: 4 bits masked packet[0] ^= mask[0] & 0x0f else: # Short header: 5 bits masked packet[0] ^= mask[0] & 0x1f # pn_offset is the start of the Packet Number field. packet[pn_offset:pn_offset+pn_length] ^= mask[1:1+pn_length]",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/header_crypto.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e6f2f2f479d173a4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "initial_salt = 0x38762cf7f55934b34d179ae6a4c80cadccbb7f0a",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6d9c8ffd09608d9c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "client_initial_secret = HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret, \"client in\", \"\", Hash.length)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1fbb882851383f95",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "server_initial_secret = HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret, \"server in\", \"\", Hash.length)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dfc72f68488f0259",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "These packets use an 8-byte client-chosen Destination Connection ID of 0x8394c8f03e515708.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "appendix-A",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2d9e44e4a1135986",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "client_initial_secret = HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret, \"client in\", \"\", 32) = c00cf151ca5be075ed0ebfb5c80323c4 2d6b7db67881289af4008f1f6c357aea",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa11ffc4777901b2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "server_initial_secret = HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret, \"server in\", \"\", 32) = 3c199828fd139efd216c155ad844cc81 fb82fa8d7446fa7d78be803acdda951b",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1009a3ade3d74c5e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "The client sends an Initial packet.  The unprotected payload of this packet contains the following CRYPTO frame, plus enough PADDING frames to make an 1162-byte payload: 060040f1010000ed0303ebf8fa56f129 39b9584a3896472ec40bb863cfd3e868 04fe3a47f06a2b69484c000004130113 02010000c000000010000e00000b6578 616d706c652e636f6dff01000100000a 00080006001d00170018001000070005 04616c706e0005000501000000000033 00260024001d00209370b2c9caa47fba baf4559fedba753de171fa71f50f1ce1 5d43e994ec74d748002b000302030400 0d0010000e0403050306030203080408 050806002d00020101001c0002400100 3900320408ffffffffffffffff050480 00ffff07048000ffff08011001048000 75300901100f088394c8f03e51570806 048000ffff",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a08fc6dd1452ae3e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "The unprotected header indicates a length of 1182 bytes: the 4-byte packet number, 1162 bytes of frames, and the 16-byte authentication tag.  The header includes the connection ID and a packet number of 2: c300000001088394c8f03e5157080000449e00000002",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0edf808a1032e31d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "Protecting the payload produces output that is sampled for header protection.  Because the header uses a 4-byte packet number encoding, the first 16 bytes of the protected payload is sampled and then applied to the header as follows: sample = d1b1c98dd7689fb8ec11d242b123dc9b mask = AES-ECB(hp, sample)[0..4] = 437b9aec36 header[0] ^= mask[0] & 0x0f = c0 header[18..21] ^= mask[1..4] = 7b9aec34 header = c000000001088394c8f03e5157080000449e7b9aec34",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "83c9da7019784665",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "The resulting protected packet is: c000000001088394c8f03e5157080000 449e7b9aec34d1b1c98dd7689fb8ec11 d242b123dc9bd8bab936b47d92ec356c 0bab7df5976d27cd449f63300099f399 1c260ec4c60d17b31f8429157bb35a12 82a643a8d2262cad67500cadb8e7378c 8eb7539ec4d4905fed1bee1fc8aafba1 7c750e2c7ace01e6005f80fcb7df6212 30c83711b39343fa028cea7f7fb5ff89 eac2308249a02252155e2347b63d58c5 457afd84d05dfffdb20392844ae81215 4682e9cf012f9021a6f0be17ddd0c208 4dce25ff9b06cde535d0f920a2db1bf3 62c23e596d11a4f5a6cf3948838a3aec 4e15daf8500a6ef69ec4e3feb6b1d98e 610ac8b7ec3faf6ad760b7bad1db4ba3 485e8a94dc250ae3fdb41ed15fb6a8e5 eba0fc3dd60bc8e30c5c4287e53805db 059ae0648db2f64264ed5e39be2e20d8 2df566da8dd5998ccabdae053060ae6c 7b4378e846d29f37ed7b4ea9ec5d82e7 961b7f25a9323851f681d582363aa5f8 9937f5a67258bf63ad6f1a0b1d96dbd4 faddfcefc5266ba6611722395c906556 be52afe3f565636ad1b17d508b73d874 3eeb524be22b3dcbc2c7468d54119c74 68449a13d8e3b95811a198f3491de3e7 fe942b330407abf82a4ed7c1b311663a c69890f4157015853d91e923037c227a 33cdd5ec281ca3f79c44546b9d90ca00 f064c99e3dd97911d39fe9c5d0b23a22 9a234cb36186c4819e8b9c5927726632 291d6a418211cc2962e20fe47feb3edf 330f2c603a9d48c0fcb5699dbfe58964 25c5bac4aee82e57a85aaf4e2513e4f0 5796b07ba2ee47d80506f8d2c25e50fd 14de71e6c418559302f939b0e1abd576 f279c4b2e0feb85c1f28ff18f58891ff ef132eef2fa09346aee33c28eb130ff2 8f5b766953334113211996d20011a198 e3fc433f9f2541010ae17c1bf202580f 6047472fb36857fe843b19f5984009dd c324044e847a4f4a0ab34f719595de37 252d6235365e9b84392b061085349d73 203a4a13e96f5432ec0fd4a1ee65accd d5e3904df54c1da510b0ff20dcc0c77f cb2c0e0eb605cb0504db87632cf3d8b4 dae6e705769d1de354270123cb11450e fc60ac47683d7b8d0f811365565fd98c 4c8eb936bcab8d069fc33bd801b03ade a2e1fbc5aa463d08ca19896d2bf59a07 1b851e6c239052172f296bfb5e724047 90a2181014f3b94a4e97d117b4381303 68cc39dbb2d198065ae3986547926cd2 162f40a29f0c3c8745c0f50fba3852e5 66d44575c29d39a03f0cda721984b6f4 40591f355e12d439ff150aab7613499d bd49adabc8676eef023b15b65bfc5ca0 6948109f23f350db82123535eb8a7433 bdabcb909271a6ecbcb58b936a88cd4e 8f2e6ff5800175f113253d8fa9ca8885 c2f552e657dc603f252e1a8e308f76f0 be79e2fb8f5d5fbbe2e30ecadd220723 c8c0aea8078cdfcb3868263ff8f09400 54da48781893a7e49ad5aff4af300cd8 04a6b6279ab3ff3afb64491c85194aab 760d58a606654f9f4400e8b38591356f bf6425aca26dc85244259ff2b19c41b9 f96f3ca9ec1dde434da7d2d392b905dd f3d1f9af93d1af5950bd493f5aa731b4 056df31bd267b6b90a079831aaf579be 0a39013137aac6d404f518cfd4684064 7e78bfe706ca4cf5e9c5453e9f7cfd2b 8b4c8d169a44e55c88d4a9a7f9474241 e221af44860018ab0856972e194cd934",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/crypto/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
