    },
    {
      "id": "7613b08a76bbd64c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 183,
      "quote": "The IANA has allocated 2001:0200::/48 for IPv6 benchmarking, which is a 48-bit prefix from the RFC 4773 pool.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/inet/ipv6.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5180",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "44e1ee6ca2f83329",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "IANA is to record the allocation of the IPv6 global unicast address prefix  2001:DB8::/32 as a documentation-only prefix  in the IPv6 address registry.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/inet/ipv6.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3849",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "02260ddebe3e5b35",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 194,
      "quote": "The IANA has assigned the FC00::/7 prefix to \"Unique Local Unicast\".",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/inet/ipv6.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4193",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d717763b6ab3480a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 197,
      "quote": "They are not expected to be routable on the global Internet.  They are routable inside of a more limited area such as a site.  They may also be routed between a limited set of sites.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/inet/ipv6.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4193",
      "target_section": "section-1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "314b8b4b19f70c1f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 205,
      "quote": "Link-Local addresses have the following format: |   10     | |  bits    |         54 bits         |          64 bits           | +----------+-------------------------+----------------------------+ |1111111010|           0             |       interface ID         | +----------+-------------------------+----------------------------+",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/inet/ipv6.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4291",
      "target_section": "section-2.5.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbac9a7b27f6e51d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 214,
      "quote": "binary 11111111 at the start of the address identifies the address as being a multicast address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/inet/ipv6.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4291",
      "target_section": "section-2.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aeb5c0d0d4ca4f44",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 389,
      "quote": "+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+ |Version| Traffic Class |           Flow Label                  | +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+ |         Payload Length        |  Next Header  |   Hop Limit   | +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+ |                                                               | +                                                               + |                                                               | +                         Source Address                        + |                                                               | +                                                               + |                                                               | +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+ |                                                               | +                                                               + |                                                               | +                      Destination Address                      + |                                                               | +                                                               + |                                                               | +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/inet/ipv6.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8200",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5926c780076bcdf1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 161,
      "quote": "To achieve that end, the endpoint SHOULD ensure that all packets it sends are at least 22 bytes longer than the minimum connection ID length that it requests the peer to include in its packets, adding PADDING frames as necessary.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/encoding.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "514e4f6ef5fcbc34",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 178,
      "quote": "in sampling packet ciphertext for header protection, the Packet Number field is assumed to be 4 bytes long",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/encoding.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.4.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "57d1f9a4bb18a972",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "Handshake Packet { Header Form (1) = 1, Fixed Bit (1) = 1, Long Packet Type (2) = 2, Reserved Bits (2), Packet Number Length (2), Version (32), Destination Connection ID Length (8), Destination Connection ID (0..160), Source Connection ID Length (8), Source Connection ID (0..160), Length (i), Packet Number (8..32), Packet Payload (..), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "466b1c93918a1d9b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "A Handshake packet uses long headers with a type value of 0x2",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9a836fc548e1b87c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "50e0153302d7b9d6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "The value included prior to protection MUST be set to 0.  An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a packet that has a non-zero value for these bits after removing both packet and header protection as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d40c7d7aa70edc19",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Initial Packet { Header Form (1) = 1, Fixed Bit (1) = 1, Long Packet Type (2) = 0, Reserved Bits (2), Packet Number Length (2), Version (32), Destination Connection ID Length (8), Destination Connection ID (0..160), Source Connection ID Length (8), Source Connection ID (0..160), Token Length (i), Token (..), Length (i), Packet Number (8..32), Packet Payload (..), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a24804225b0b8cda",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "An Initial packet uses long headers with a type value of 0x0.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "423e6c0bbdbc0b2f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Token Length:  A variable-length integer specifying the length of the Token field, in bytes.  This value is 0 if no token is present.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fe9122445e9e69f3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Token:  The value of the token that was previously provided in a Retry packet or NEW_TOKEN frame; see Section 8.1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2b8a77dcac3dbfc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "In order to properly form a Version Negotiation packet, servers SHOULD be able to read longer connection IDs from other QUIC versions.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2ceda4602f8c6ba1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 6,
      "quote": "Key Phase:  The next bit (0x04) of byte 0 indicates the key phase, which allows a recipient of a packet to identify the packet protection keys that are used to protect the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/key_phase.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d50d3997f620be7d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Long Header Packet { Header Form (1) = 1, Fixed Bit (1) = 1, Long Packet Type (2), Type-Specific Bits (4), Version (32), Destination Connection ID Length (8), Destination Connection ID (0..160), Source Connection ID Length (8), Source Connection ID (0..160), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4bf6e2f9fb43bfb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Header Form:  The most significant bit (0x80) of byte 0 (the first byte) is set to 1 for long headers.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d4084818ce02b1df",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "Fixed Bit:  The next bit (0x40) of byte 0 is set to 1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba3480caf1708b63",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Long Packet Type:  The next two bits (those with a mask of 0x30) of byte 0 contain a packet type.  Packet types are listed in Table 5.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "92f7b92b5efdfdac",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "Type-Specific Bits:  The semantics of the lower four bits (those with a mask of 0x0f) of byte 0 are determined by the packet type.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "03765b0b07cacc70",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Version: The QUIC Version is a 32-bit field that follows the first byte.  This field indicates the version of QUIC that is in use and determines how the rest of the protocol fields are interpreted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e3b6e6795ee671ba",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Destination Connection ID Length:  The byte following the version contains the length in bytes of the Destination Connection ID field that follows it.  This length is encoded as an 8-bit unsigned integer.  In QUIC version 1, this value MUST NOT exceed 20.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7c89a05acc3afd6b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "Destination Connection ID:  The Destination Connection ID field follows the Destination Connection ID Length field, which indicates the length of this field.  Section 7.2 describes the use of this field in more detail.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8136b9581c6007cd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "556d45bf71d7ec8c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Source Connection ID Length:  The byte following the Destination Connection ID contains the length in bytes of the Source Connection ID field that follows it.  This length is encoded as a 8-bit unsigned integer.  In QUIC version 1, this value MUST NOT exceed 20 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a1dac283102149f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "Source Connection ID:  The Source Connection ID field follows the Source Connection ID Length field, which indicates the length of this field.  Section 7.2 describes the use of this field in more detail.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c785418efd77a9be",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf473f570e00a03d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "In this version of QUIC, the following packet types with the long header are defined: +======+===========+================+ | Type | Name      | Section        | +======+===========+================+ | 0x00 | Initial   | Section 17.2.2 | +------+-----------+----------------+ | 0x01 | 0-RTT     | Section 17.2.3 | +------+-----------+----------------+ | 0x02 | Handshake | Section 17.2.4 | +------+-----------+----------------+ | 0x03 | Retry     | Section 17.2.5 | +------+-----------+----------------+ Table 5: Long Header Packet Types",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e7946fa448e653da",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "Reserved Bits:  Two bits (those with a mask of 0x0c) of byte 0 are reserved across multiple packet types.  These bits are protected using header protection; see Section 5.4 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b27bba68ccb8b854",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 178,
      "quote": "Packet Number Length:  In packet types that contain a Packet Number field, the least significant two bits (those with a mask of 0x03) of byte 0 contain the length of the Packet Number field, encoded as an unsigned two-bit integer that is one less than the length of the Packet Number field in bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9c3734fe571acba4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "Length:  This is the length of the remainder of the packet (that is, the Packet Number and Payload fields) in bytes, encoded as a variable-length integer (Section 16).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "50f4b4044ca1a2da",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 190,
      "quote": "Packet Number:  This field is 1 to 4 bytes long.  The packet number is protected using header protection; see Section 5.4 of [QUIC-TLS].  The length of the Packet Number field is encoded in the Packet Number Length bits of byte 0; see above.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/long.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2f5a513618525e3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "The packet number is an integer in the range 0 to 2^62-1.  This number is used in determining the cryptographic nonce for packet protection.  Each endpoint maintains a separate packet number for sending and receiving.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8cd0b29dedbdf4ef",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Packet numbers are limited to this range because they need to be representable in whole in the Largest Acknowledged field of an ACK frame (Section 19.3).  When present in a long or short header however, packet numbers are reduced and encoded in 1 to 4 bytes; see Section 17.1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "56e65a30bc3c6b38",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "Initial space:  All Initial packets (Section 17.2.2) are in this space. Handshake space:  All Handshake packets (Section 17.2.4) are in this space. Application data space:  All 0-RTT (Section 17.2.3) and 1-RTT (Section 17.3.1) packets are in this space.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3dfa9db26e0eb6c8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Packet numbers are integers in the range 0 to 2^62-1 (Section 12.3). When present in long or short packet headers, they are encoded in 1 to 4 bytes.  The number of bits required to represent the packet number is reduced by including only the least significant bits of the packet number.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "18ead20c6a92bd81",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "the sender MUST use a packet number size able to represent more than twice as large a range as the difference between the largest acknowledged packet number and the packet number being sent.  A peer receiving the packet will then correctly decode the packet number, unless the packet is delayed in transit such that it arrives after many higher-numbered packets have been received.  An endpoint SHOULD use a large enough packet number encoding to allow the packet number to be recovered even if the packet arrives after packets that are sent afterwards.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3cf1cc83fdceb22",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "As a result, the size of the packet number encoding is at least one bit more than the base-2 logarithm of the number of contiguous unacknowledged packet numbers, including the new packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "763bf9c745dc66ed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "For example, if an endpoint has received an acknowledgment for packet 0xabe8b3 and is sending a packet with a number of 0xac5c02, there are 29,519 (0x734f) outstanding packet numbers.  In order to represent at least twice this range (59,038 packets, or 0xe69e), 16 bits are required. In the same state, sending a packet with a number of 0xace8fe uses the 24-bit encoding, because at least 18 bits are required to represent twice the range (131,222 packets, or 0x020096).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "708d2fe00c64a0a1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "At a receiver, protection of the packet number is removed prior to recovering the full packet number.  The full packet number is then reconstructed based on the number of significant bits present, the value of those bits, and the largest packet number received in a successfully authenticated packet.  Recovering the full packet number is necessary to successfully complete the removal of packet protection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 164,
      "quote": "DecodePacketNumber(largest_pn, truncated_pn, pn_nbits): expected_pn  = largest_pn + 1 pn_win       = 1 << pn_nbits pn_hwin      = pn_win / 2 pn_mask      = pn_win - 1 // The incoming packet number should be greater than // expected_pn - pn_hwin and less than or equal to // expected_pn + pn_hwin // // This means we cannot just strip the trailing bits from // expected_pn and add the truncated_pn because that might // yield a value outside the window. // // The following code calculates a candidate value and // makes sure it's within the packet number window. // Note the extra checks to prevent overflow and underflow. candidate_pn = (expected_pn & ~pn_mask) | truncated_pn if candidate_pn <= expected_pn - pn_hwin and candidate_pn < (1 << 62) - pn_win: return candidate_pn + pn_win if candidate_pn > expected_pn + pn_hwin and candidate_pn >= pn_win: return candidate_pn - pn_win return candidate_pn",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf9c44e14d0494ec",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "Duplicates are rejected through the use of a sliding receive window. How the window is implemented is a local matter, but the following text describes the functionality that the implementation must exhibit. The \"right\" edge of the window represents the highest, validated Sequence Number value received on this SA.  Packets that contain sequence numbers lower than the \"left\" edge of the window are rejected.  Packets falling within the window are checked against a list of received packets within the window.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/sliding_window.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4303",
      "target_section": "section-3.4.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0d9f6a1122406686",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "DecodePacketNumber(largest_pn, truncated_pn, pn_nbits): expected_pn  = largest_pn + 1 pn_win       = 1 << pn_nbits pn_hwin      = pn_win / 2 pn_mask      = pn_win - 1 // The incoming packet number should be greater than // expected_pn - pn_hwin and less than or equal to // expected_pn + pn_hwin // // This means we cannot just strip the trailing bits from // expected_pn and add the truncated_pn because that might // yield a value outside the window. // // The following code calculates a candidate value and // makes sure it's within the packet number window. // Note the extra checks to prevent overflow and underflow. candidate_pn = (expected_pn & ~pn_mask) | truncated_pn if candidate_pn <= expected_pn - pn_hwin and candidate_pn < (1 << 62) - pn_win: return candidate_pn + pn_win if candidate_pn > expected_pn + pn_hwin and candidate_pn >= pn_win: return candidate_pn - pn_win return candidate_pn",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/number/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "5646229325539c72",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Retry Packet { Header Form (1) = 1, Fixed Bit (1) = 1, Long Packet Type (2) = 3, Unused (4), Version (32), Destination Connection ID Length (8), Destination Connection ID (0..160), Source Connection ID Length (8), Source Connection ID (0..160), Retry Token (..), Retry Integrity Tag (128), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb86159aa3bec88b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "a Retry packet uses a long packet header with a type value of 0x03.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e3057da4ab28873",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Retry Token:  An opaque token that the server can use to validate the client's address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "98a1fc67771b6592",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "Retry Integrity Tag:  Defined in Section 5.8 (\"Retry Packet Integrity\") of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "56277a119d4727a0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "Retry Pseudo-Packet { ODCID Length (8), Original Destination Connection ID (0..160), Header Form (1) = 1, Fixed Bit (1) = 1, Long Packet Type (2) = 3, Unused (4), Version (32), DCID Len (8), Destination Connection ID (0..160), SCID Len (8), Source Connection ID (0..160), Retry Token (..), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5fdf8ba0180d97d7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 126,
      "quote": "This value MUST NOT be equal to the Destination Connection ID field of the packet sent by the client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f1daba603d71d486",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 186,
      "quote": "Retry packets (see Section 17.2.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) carry a Retry Integrity Tag that provides two properties: it allows the discarding of packets that have accidentally been corrupted by the network, and only an entity that observes an Initial packet can send a valid Retry packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "04eeee7e4ba36949",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 205,
      "quote": "The value in the Unused field is set to an arbitrary value by the server; a client MUST ignore these bits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ce76977a92045f60",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 231,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4268a64547941fe4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 248,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard a Retry packet with a zero-length Retry Token field.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7c5d97226cb38562",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 369,
      "quote": "For this design to work, the token MUST be covered by integrity protection against modification or falsification by clients.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7544f314f0c43c76",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 383,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard a Retry packet with a zero-length Retry Token field.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/retry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "fc9bb5b7a00331f1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "1-RTT Packet { Header Form (1) = 0, Fixed Bit (1) = 1, Spin Bit (1), Reserved Bits (2), Key Phase (1), Packet Number Length (2), Destination Connection ID (0..160), Packet Number (8..32), Packet Payload (..), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8179d998e7e8f473",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "Header Form:  The most significant bit (0x80) of byte 0 is set to 0 for the short header. Fixed Bit:  The next bit (0x40) of byte 0 is set to 1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5de50922ab92e0a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "Spin Bit:  The third most significant bit (0x20) of byte 0 is the latency spin bit, set as described in Section 17.4.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d13cceab21101a1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Reserved Bits:  The next two bits (those with a mask of 0x18) of byte 0 are reserved.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a855355c9f7dd96b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Reserved Bits:  The next two bits (those with a mask of 0x18) of byte 0 are reserved.  These bits are protected using header protection; see Section 5.4 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e73206911079475",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "Packet Number Length:  The least significant two bits (those with a mask of 0x03) of byte 0 contain the length of the Packet Number field, encoded as an unsigned two-bit integer that is one less than the length of the Packet Number field in bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbaca64b7694416f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "Destination Connection ID:  The Destination Connection ID is a connection ID that is chosen by the intended recipient of the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9cb186cbbc912d1e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "Packet Number:  The Packet Number field is 1 to 4 bytes long.  The packet number is protected using header protection; see Section 5.4 of [QUIC-TLS].  The length of the Packet Number field is encoded in Packet Number Length field.  See Section 17.1 for details.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "25e7635c143e951a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 112,
      "quote": "Packet Payload:  1-RTT packets always include a 1-RTT protected payload.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b1d5caa43e12a7d4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 213,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a packet that has a non-zero value for these bits, after removing both packet and header protection, as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/short.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b695dfd4e13d6b7f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "Stateless Reset { Fixed Bits (2) = 1, Unpredictable Bits (38..), Stateless Reset Token (128), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/stateless_reset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "020699b6572a8140",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST send Stateless Resets formatted as a packet with a short header.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/stateless_reset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2822cb1811c01b89",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "These values assume that the stateless reset token is the same length as the minimum expansion of the packet protection AEAD.  Additional unpredictable bytes are necessary if the endpoint could have negotiated a packet protection scheme with a larger minimum expansion.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/stateless_reset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3abfc6f42c37b99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a Stateless Reset that is three times or more larger than the packet it receives to avoid being used for amplification.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/stateless_reset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5001b9bc0e78bf57",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST ensure that every Stateless Reset that it sends is smaller than the packet that triggered it, unless it maintains state sufficient to prevent looping.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/stateless_reset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a40a4dddf9ae16fc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "The remainder of the first byte and an arbitrary number of bytes following it are set to values that SHOULD be indistinguishable from random.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/stateless_reset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "463c53d4ba6293f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "The remainder of the first byte and an arbitrary number of bytes following it are set to values that SHOULD be indistinguishable from random.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/stateless_reset.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d5dba80d93061fed",
      "level": "Auto",
