    {
      "id": "4123fc4d3937faa5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "Version Negotiation Packet { Header Form (1) = 1, Unused (7), Version (32) = 0, Destination Connection ID Length (8), Destination Connection ID (0..2040), Source Connection ID Length (8), Source Connection ID (0..2040), Supported Version (32) ..., }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/version_negotiation.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7059964fc2481b3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "The value in the Unused field is set to an arbitrary value by the server.  Clients MUST ignore the value of this field.  Where QUIC might be multiplexed with other protocols (see [RFC7983]), servers SHOULD set the most significant bit of this field (0x40) to 1 so that Version Negotiation packets appear to have the Fixed Bit field.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/version_negotiation.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5f88a1f9963c436f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "The Version field of a Version Negotiation packet MUST be set to 0x00000000.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/version_negotiation.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "efa3b0e579fd0276",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "The server MUST include the value from the Source Connection ID field of the packet it receives in the Destination Connection ID field.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/version_negotiation.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "09e7649550eb558a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "The value for Source Connection ID MUST be copied from the Destination Connection ID of the received packet, which is initially randomly selected by a client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/version_negotiation.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7233a5d9a5e1c62",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "0-RTT Packet { Header Form (1) = 1, Fixed Bit (1) = 1, Long Packet Type (2) = 1, Reserved Bits (2), Packet Number Length (2), Version (32), Destination Connection ID Length (8), Destination Connection ID (0..160), Source Connection ID Length (8), Source Connection ID (0..160), Length (i), Packet Number (8..32), Packet Payload (..), }",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/zero_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7e89e7e61c1cd9b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "A 0-RTT packet uses long headers with a type value of 0x1,",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/zero_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "03c6fa72b69596c4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/packet/zero_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b02d790926e04412",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 166,
      "quote": "Upon successful validation, an endpoint MAY continue to set an ECT codepoint in subsequent packets it sends, with the expectation that the path is ECN-capable.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7dfa7290b21a623",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 181,
      "quote": "If validation fails, then the endpoint MUST disable ECN. It stops setting the ECT codepoint in IP packets that it sends, assuming that either the network path or the peer does not support ECN.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2b90c7715202709a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 290,
      "quote": "If an ACK frame newly acknowledges a packet that the endpoint sent with either the ECT(0) or ECT(1) codepoint set, ECN validation fails if the corresponding ECN counts are not present in the ACK frame. This check detects a network element that zeroes the ECN field or a peer that does not report ECN markings.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e0e1f7ba810ad173",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 318,
      "quote": "ECN validation also fails if the sum of the increase in ECT(0) and ECN-CE counts is less than the number of newly acknowledged packets that were originally sent with an ECT(0) marking.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d2ce353c8770d425",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 345,
      "quote": "ECN validation can fail if the received total count for either ECT(0) or ECT(1) exceeds the total number of packets sent with each corresponding ECT codepoint.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "be319e04503806ab",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 440,
      "quote": "From the \"unknown\" state, successful validation of the ECN counts in an ACK frame (see Section 13.4.2.1) causes the ECN state for the path to become \"capable\", unless no marked packet has been acknowledged.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "52f26b49d2d26567",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 468,
      "quote": "A sender can detect suppression of reports by marking occasional packets that it sends with an ECN-CE marking. If a packet sent with an ECN-CE marking is not reported as having been CE marked when the packet is acknowledged, then the sender can disable ECN for that path by not setting ECN-Capable Transport (ECT) codepoints in subsequent packets sent on that path [RFC3168].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1362daf7dad3713c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 500,
      "quote": "A sender can detect suppression of reports by marking occasional packets that it sends with an ECN-CE marking. If a packet sent with an ECN-CE marking is not reported as having been CE marked when the packet is acknowledged, then the sender can disable ECN for that path by not setting ECN-Capable Transport (ECT) codepoints in subsequent packets sent on that path [RFC3168].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d64c386236e0be48",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "If an endpoint has cause to expect that IP packets with an ECT codepoint might be dropped by a faulty network element, the endpoint could set an ECT codepoint for only the first ten outgoing packets on a path, or for a period of three PTOs",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "90f11eb804d90e07",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 143,
      "quote": "On paths with a \"testing\" or \"capable\" state, the endpoint sends packets with an ECT marking -- ECT(0) by default; otherwise, the endpoint sends unmarked packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6c58d93916763bd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "A sender can detect suppression of reports by marking occasional packets that it sends with an ECN-CE marking.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9112eb89c518e406",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "Upon successful validation, an endpoint MAY continue to set an ECT codepoint in subsequent packets it sends, with the expectation that the path is ECN-capable.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b9a82b81e8920fa0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 162,
      "quote": "If validation fails, then the endpoint MUST disable ECN. It stops setting the ECT codepoint in IP packets that it sends, assuming that either the network path or the peer does not support ECN.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ce615564d638536d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 202,
      "quote": "Network routing and path elements can change mid-connection; an endpoint MUST disable ECN if validation later fails.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cde3d132192b4a99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 233,
      "quote": "If an ACK frame newly acknowledges a packet that the endpoint sent with either the ECT(0) or ECT(1) codepoint set, ECN validation fails if the corresponding ECN counts are not present in the ACK frame. This check detects a network element that zeroes the ECN field or a peer that does not report ECN markings.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e611df783e7c466",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 270,
      "quote": "From the \"unknown\" state, successful validation of the ECN counts in an ACK frame (see Section 13.4.2.1) causes the ECN state for the path to become \"capable\", unless no marked packet has been acknowledged.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b15a20949f9a402e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 292,
      "quote": "ECN validation also fails if the sum of the increase in ECT(0) and ECN-CE counts is less than the number of newly acknowledged packets that were originally sent with an ECT(0) marking.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9790033947b287fa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 304,
      "quote": "ECN validation can fail if the received total count for either ECT(0) or ECT(1) exceeds the total number of packets sent with each corresponding ECT codepoint.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8b14d0fd63537279",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 316,
      "quote": "A receiver can misreport ECN markings to alter the congestion response of a sender.  Suppressing reports of ECN-CE markings could cause a sender to increase their send rate.  This increase could result in congestion and loss.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "34169af20e1b1b9c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 322,
      "quote": "A sender can detect suppression of reports by marking occasional packets that it sends with an ECN-CE marking.  If a packet sent with an ECN-CE marking is not reported as having been CE marked when the packet is acknowledged, then the sender can disable ECN for that path by not setting ECN-Capable Transport (ECT) codepoints in subsequent packets sent on that path [RFC3168].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d53ca4cad5e97d8e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 418,
      "quote": "Even if validation fails, an endpoint MAY revalidate ECN for the same path at any later time in the connection. An endpoint could continue to periodically attempt validation.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/ecn.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f62464c6ff930e0c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "it might be possible over time to identify specific UDP ports that are common targets of attacks or particular patterns in datagrams that are used for attacks.  Endpoints MAY choose to avoid sending datagrams to these ports or not send datagrams that match these patterns prior to validating the destination address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/migration.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "894598ea0371342a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY prevent connection attempts or migration to a loopback address.  Endpoints SHOULD NOT allow connections or migration to a loopback address if the same service was previously available at a different interface or if the address was provided by a service at a non-loopback address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/migration.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a509bbccfcf3a6c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "Similarly, endpoints could regard a change in address to a link-local address [RFC4291] or an address in a private-use range [RFC1918] from a global, unique-local [RFC4193], or non-private address as a potential attempt at request forgery.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/migration.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "df05618bf7fcca14",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "o  the System Ports, also known as the Well Known Ports, from 0-1023 (assigned by IANA) o  the User Ports, also known as the Registered Ports, from 1024- 49151 (assigned by IANA) o  the Dynamic Ports, also known as the Private or Ephemeral Ports, from 49152-65535 (never assigned)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/migration.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6335",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b79809e84036e1cf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 254,
      "quote": "Some UDP protocols are vulnerable to reflection attacks, where an attacker is able to direct traffic to a third party as a denial of service.  For example, these source ports are associated with applications known to be vulnerable to reflection attacks, often due to server misconfiguration: *  port 53 - DNS [RFC1034] *  port 123 - NTP [RFC5905] *  port 1900 - SSDP [SSDP] *  port 5353 - mDNS [RFC6762] *  port 11211 - memcache",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9308",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c09c1319638b58f0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 169,
      "quote": "When using IPv4, there is no currently equivalent size specified, and a default BASE_PLPMTU of 1200 bytes is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c0e618918fc2865a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 274,
      "quote": "Datagrams containing Initial packets MAY exceed 1200 bytes if the sender believes that the network path and peer both support the size that it chooses.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e3fb00e009cbe461",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 380,
      "quote": "When supported, this mechanism MAY also be used by DPLPMTUD to acknowledge reception of a probe packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "de3cf5a6d654d9d5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 458,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD select the set of probe packet sizes to maximize the gain in PLPMTU from each search step.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "972df49d985a00e3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 463,
      "quote": "To avoid excessive load, the interval between individual probe packets MUST be at least one RTT, and the interval between rounds of probing is determined by the PMTU_RAISE_TIMER.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2f9db7aeea98f611",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 595,
      "quote": "The PL is REQUIRED to be robust in the case where probe packets are lost due to other reasons (including link transmission error, congestion).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "63b7d00ad640bfe8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 895,
      "quote": "When used with an acknowledged PL (e.g., SCTP), DPLPMTUD SHOULD NOT continue to generate PLPMTU probes in this state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "6266fe0da1b6d52b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 969,
      "quote": "Endpoints could limit the content of PMTU probes to PING and PADDING frames, since packets that are larger than the current maximum datagram size are more likely to be dropped by the network.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "3a00b634250da583",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 975,
      "quote": "Probe loss recovery: It is RECOMMENDED to use probe packets that do not carry any user data that would require retransmission if lost.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7e3f354409fe885a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 981,
      "quote": "DPLPMTUD MAY choose to use only one of these methods to simplify the implementation.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ddf462e946b9bde0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "The DISABLED state is the initial state before probing has started.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c00792167fac8991",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "The SEARCHING state is the main probing state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c56266b137a7bbd4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "The SEARCH_COMPLETE state indicates that a search has completed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f414125fcbef8b5d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "The MAX_PROBES is the maximum value of the PROBE_COUNT counter (see Section 5.1.3).  MAX_PROBES represents the limit for the number of consecutive probe attempts of any size.  Search algorithms benefit from a MAX_PROBES value greater than 1 because this can provide robustness to isolated packet loss.  The default value of MAX_PROBES is 3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ca0efaef8029a01d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "The PMTU_RAISE_TIMER is configured to the period a sender will continue to use the current PLPMTU, after which it reenters the Search Phase.  This timer has a period of 600 seconds, as recommended by PLPMTUD [RFC4821].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cd9eb7a0d8f8fe09",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "QUIC MUST NOT be used if the network path cannot support a maximum datagram size of at least 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2d4c6a14fcca33f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "When using IPv4, there is no currently equivalent size specified, and a default BASE_PLPMTU of 1200 bytes is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "75b34f9cee4462f8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 484,
      "quote": "The BASE_PLPMTU is a configured size expected to work for most paths. The size is equal to or larger than the MIN_PLPMTU and smaller than the MAX_PLPMTU.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "415ed5608d9e18cd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 489,
      "quote": "The Packetization Layer PMTU is an estimate of the largest size of PL datagram that can be sent by a path, controlled by PLPMTUD",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "799e915fba3de00a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 495,
      "quote": "The PROBED_SIZE is the size of the current probe packet as determined at the PL.  This is a tentative value for the PLPMTU, which is awaiting confirmation by an acknowledgment.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "933af5753d2b7de6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 503,
      "quote": "The PROBE_COUNT is a count of the number of successive unsuccessful probe packets that have been sent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "270fc9a9023535e1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 513,
      "quote": "The PMTU_RAISE_TIMER is configured to the period a sender will continue to use the current PLPMTU, after which it reenters the Search Phase.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ce50f6317934b136",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 531,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD set the initial value of BASE_PLPMTU (Section 5.1 of [DPLPMTUD]) to be consistent with QUIC's smallest allowed maximum datagram size.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c13ca7a2b757ad3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 538,
      "quote": "Datagrams containing Initial packets MAY exceed 1200 bytes if the sender believes that the network path and peer both support the size that it chooses.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "909ecbf21c06c682",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 604,
      "quote": "When supported, this mechanism MAY also be used by DPLPMTUD to acknowledge reception of a probe packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3bd131648cf9f18",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 668,
      "quote": "To avoid excessive load, the interval between individual probe packets MUST be at least one RTT, and the interval between rounds of probing is determined by the PMTU_RAISE_TIMER.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fa30609a3e91f348",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 691,
      "quote": "The PL is REQUIRED to be robust in the case where probe packets are lost due to other reasons (including link transmission error, congestion).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2ed3bb8640230ef4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 817,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD select the set of probe packet sizes to maximize the gain in PLPMTU from each search step.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1e2c6ed60a524727",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 920,
      "quote": "When used with an acknowledged PL (e.g., SCTP), DPLPMTUD SHOULD NOT continue to generate PLPMTU probes in this state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "be3ebb92de643d8a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 940,
      "quote": "Endpoints could limit the content of PMTU probes to PING and PADDING frames, since packets that are larger than the current maximum datagram size are more likely to be dropped by the network.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4e36bf7a2c109350",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 945,
      "quote": "Probe loss recovery: It is RECOMMENDED to use probe packets that do not carry any user data that would require retransmission if lost.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "db5d9b6abc2e478a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 950,
      "quote": "DPLPMTUD MAY choose to use only one of these methods to simplify the implementation.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/path/mtu.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f6a23f8a5953a876",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 355,
      "quote": "UpdateRateSample() is invoked multiple times when a stretched ACK acknowledges multiple data packets. In this case we use the information from the most recently sent packet, i.e., the packet with the highest \"P.delivered\" value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "3.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb43683f510e284e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 386,
      "quote": "Since it is physically impossible to have data delivered faster than it is sent in a sustained fashion, when the estimator notices that the ack_rate for a flight is faster than the send rate for the flight, it filters out the implausible ack_rate by capping the delivery rate sample to be no higher than the send rate.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "2.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa5866d1dd5dc438",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 236,
      "quote": "The amount of data delivered MAY be tracked in units of either octets or packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2082c6ba3f3d74d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 288,
      "quote": "If there are no packets in flight yet, then we can start the delivery rate interval at the current time, since we know that any ACKs after now indicate that the network was able to deliver those packets completely in the sampling interval between now and the next ACK.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a7cdaf142d65ec4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 294,
      "quote": "Upon each packet transmission, the sender executes the following steps: SendPacket(Packet P): if (SND.NXT == SND.UNA)  /* no packets in flight yet? */ C.first_sent_time  = C.delivered_time = Now() P.first_sent_time = C.first_sent_time P.delivered_time  = C.delivered_time P.delivered       = C.delivered P.is_app_limited  = (C.app_limited != 0)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "be492b4d2cbe8d2d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 330,
      "quote": "For each packet that was newly SACKed or ACKed, UpdateRateSample() updates the rate sample based on a snapshot of connection delivery information from the time at which the packet was last transmitted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6cc87d7a07deae7d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 356,
      "quote": "UpdateRateSample() is invoked multiple times when a stretched ACK acknowledges multiple data packets. In this case we use the information from the most recently sent packet, i.e., the packet with the highest \"P.delivered\" value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3ab02984fd28ba1a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 380,
      "quote": "Since it is physically impossible to have data delivered faster than it is sent in a sustained fashion, when the estimator notices that the ack_rate for a flight is faster than the send rate for the flight, it filters out the implausible ack_rate by capping the delivery rate sample to be no higher than the send rate.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation-02",
      "target_section": "2.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2118a25c08e1a85a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 430,
      "quote": "MarkConnectionAppLimited(): C.app_limited = (C.delivered + packets_in_flight) ? : 1",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bandwidth/estimator.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3b8b55bcf1ace7d0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "a 1-round-trip max of delivered bandwidth (rs.delivery_rate)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c9c4c36b9097a50f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "a 1-round-trip max of delivered volume of data (rs.delivered)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e2549c73de9d5a46",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateLatestDeliverySignals(): BBR.loss_round_start = 0 BBR.bw_latest       = max(BBR.bw_latest,       rs.delivery_rate) BBR.inflight_latest = max(BBR.inflight_latest, rs.delivered) if (rs.prior_delivered >= BBR.loss_round_delivered) BBR.loss_round_delivered = C.delivered BBR.loss_round_start = 1",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b848fa02123fd014",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateCongestionSignals(): BBRUpdateMaxBw() if (rs.losses > 0) BBR.loss_in_round = 1 if (!BBR.loss_round_start) return  /* wait until end of round trip */ BBRAdaptLowerBoundsFromCongestion() BBR.loss_in_round = 0",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4548b164dc74ed27",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "When not explicitly accelerating to probe for bandwidth (Drain, ProbeRTT, ProbeBW_DOWN, ProbeBW_CRUISE), BBR responds to loss by slowing down to some extent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "069e7f2df8eccfe3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "BBRAdaptLowerBoundsFromCongestion(): if (BBRIsProbingBW()) return if (BBR.loss_in_round()) BBRInitLowerBounds() BBRLossLowerBounds()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c960d068907f7465",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "BBRAdvanceLatestDeliverySignals(): if (BBR.loss_round_start) BBR.bw_latest       = rs.delivery_rate BBR.inflight_latest = rs.delivered",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d4eaa14a06b6d5fe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "BBRResetCongestionSignals(): BBR.loss_in_round = 0 BBR.bw_latest = 0 BBR.inflight_latest = 0",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/congestion.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d685ac88581071a8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "The data rate model parameters together estimate both the sending rate required to reach the full bandwidth available to the flow (BBR.max_bw), and the maximum pacing rate control parameter that is consistent with the queue pressure objective (BBR.bw).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "de60bc1312e93606",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "The windowed maximum recent bandwidth sample - obtained using the BBR delivery rate sampling algorithm [draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation] - measured during the current or previous bandwidth probing cycle (or during Startup, if the flow is still in that state).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a356cd25f9016c90",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "The long-term maximum sending bandwidth that the algorithm estimates will produce acceptable queue pressure, based on signals in the current or previous bandwidth probing cycle, as measured by loss.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7e85e560495e8b57",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "The short-term maximum sending bandwidth that the algorithm estimates is safe for matching the current network path delivery rate, based on any loss signals in the current bandwidth probing cycle. This is generally lower than max_bw or bw_hi (thus the name).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5b1f6d2835e3a967",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "The maximum sending bandwidth that the algorithm estimates is appropriate for matching the current network path delivery rate, given all available signals in the model, at any time scale. It is the min() of max_bw, bw_hi, and bw_lo.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e8406c81909cace0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "The virtual time used by the BBR.max_bw filter window.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "52faa1fa0bfe45a3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "The filter window length for BBR.MaxBwFilter = 2 (representing up to 2 ProbeBW cycles, the current cycle and the previous full cycle)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2be49dccf1219390",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "BBRAdvanceMaxBwFilter(): BBR.cycle_count++",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "202377d1d4ae62d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateMaxBw() BBRUpdateRound() if (rs.delivery_rate >= BBR.max_bw || !rs.is_app_limited) BBR.max_bw = update_windowed_max_filter( filter=BBR.MaxBwFilter, value=rs.delivery_rate, time=BBR.cycle_count, window_length=MaxBwFilterLen)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1e93a4dcd9e38041",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "By default, the estimator discards application-limited samples, since by definition they reflect application limits.  However, the estimator does use application-limited samples if the measured delivery rate happens to be larger than the current BBR.max_bw estimate, since this indicates the current BBR.Max_bw estimate is too low.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f6e1f21a52127ec6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "BBRInitLowerBounds(): if (BBR.bw_lo == Infinity) BBR.bw_lo = BBR.max_bw",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "57c48a5c2ca26f0e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "BBRLossLowerBounds(): BBR.bw_lo       = max(BBR.bw_latest, BBRBeta * BBR.bw_lo)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "39b6ff1f4fce3776",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 137,
      "quote": "BBRResetLowerBounds(): BBR.bw_lo       = Infinity",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "55196c62f17f87f9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 145,
      "quote": "BBRBoundBWForModel(): BBR.bw = min(BBR.max_bw, BBR.bw_lo, BBR.bw_hi)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_rate.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "11fee86ab1eb45cf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "The data volume model parameters together estimate both the volume of in-flight data required to reach the full bandwidth available to the flow (BBR.max_inflight), and the maximum volume of data that is consistent with the queue pressure objective (cwnd).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "145cf41f5e32b935",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "The windowed minimum round-trip time sample measured over the last MinRTTFilterLen = 10 seconds.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "be409852d4adbb2e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "A volume of data that is the estimate of the recent degree of aggregation in the network path.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ed0021015f826f3e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "the start of the time interval for estimating the excess amount of data acknowledged due to aggregation effects.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.12",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2d5fab85ec506385",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "the volume of data marked as delivered since BBR.extra_acked_interval_start.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.12",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6057f9b2ecab59b0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Analogous to BBR.bw_hi, the long-term maximum volume of in-flight data that the algorithm estimates will produce acceptable queue pressure, based on signals in the current or previous bandwidth probing cycle, as measured by loss.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b1470954db9282be",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Analogous to BBR.bw_lo, the short-term maximum volume of in-flight data that the algorithm estimates is safe for matching the current network path delivery process, based on any loss signals in the current bandwidth probing cycle.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "74587199d171af15",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "The window length of the BBR.ExtraACKedFilter max filter window: 10 (in units of packet-timed round trips).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.12",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "71dc3c6ed7d6bf5e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateACKAggregation(): /* Find excess ACKed beyond expected amount over this interval */ interval = (Now() - BBR.extra_acked_interval_start) expected_delivered = BBR.bw * interval /* Reset interval if ACK rate is below expected rate: */ if (BBR.extra_acked_delivered <= expected_delivered) BBR.extra_acked_delivered = 0 BBR.extra_acked_interval_start = Now() expected_delivered = 0 BBR.extra_acked_delivered += rs.newly_acked extra = BBR.extra_acked_delivered - expected_delivered extra = min(extra, cwnd) BBR.extra_acked = update_windowed_max_filter( filter=BBR.ExtraACKedFilter, value=extra, time=BBR.round_count, window_length=BBRExtraAckedFilterLen)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "79efb7a71763a730",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 175,
      "quote": "if (BBR.inflight_lo == Infinity) BBR.inflight_lo = cwnd",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c4e3b25d1ad617c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 191,
      "quote": "BBR.inflight_lo = max(BBR.inflight_latest, BBRBeta * BBR.infligh_lo)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c7e59388bde1247f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 204,
      "quote": "BBR.inflight_lo = Infinity",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/data_volume.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "352f1bfe3abf00e6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "In Drain, BBR aims to quickly drain any queue created in Startup by switching to a pacing_gain well below 1.0, until any estimated queue has been drained. It uses a pacing_gain that is the inverse of the value used during Startup, chosen to try to drain the queue in one round",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/drain.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0cb715f27eca1cc1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "BBR.pacing_gain = 1/BBRStartupCwndGain  /* pace slowly */",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/drain.rs",
