    },
    {
      "id": "42fc8bc460897a31",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "BBRCheckDrain(): if (BBR.state == Drain and packets_in_flight <= BBRInflight(1.0)) BBREnterProbeBW()  /* BBR estimates the queue was drained */",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/drain.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "804952dff80f14ab",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "BBRCheckDrain(): if (BBR.state == Drain and packets_in_flight <= BBRInflight(1.0)) BBREnterProbeBW()  /* BBR estimates the queue was drained */",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/drain.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d10fc2a4709cc988",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "BBRInitFullPipe(): BBR.filled_pipe = false BBR.full_bw = 0 BBR.full_bw_count = 0",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7684d67ed9f3f49",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "A boolean that records whether BBR estimates that it has ever fully utilized its available bandwidth (\"filled the pipe\").",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.13",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c160f67e8e2668d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "A recent baseline BBR.max_bw to estimate if BBR has \"filled the pipe\" in Startup.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.13",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a19b2d1242630a5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "The number of non-app-limited round trips without large increases in BBR.full_bw.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.13",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7069816164d474b1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "BBRCheckStartupFullBandwidth(): if BBR.filled_pipe or !BBR.round_start or rs.is_app_limited return  /* no need to check for a full pipe now */ if (BBR.max_bw >= BBR.full_bw * 1.25)  /* still growing? */ BBR.full_bw = BBR.max_bw    /* record new baseline level */ BBR.full_bw_count = 0 return BBR.full_bw_count++ /* another round w/o much growth */ if (BBR.full_bw_count >= 3) BBR.filled_pipe = true",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8e459a1bf8b33f8d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "Once per round trip, upon an ACK that acknowledges new data, and when the delivery rate sample is not application-limited (see [draft- cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation]), BBR runs the \"full pipe\" estimator",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3efc62f2b36eada0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "A second method BBR uses for estimating the bottleneck is full is by looking at sustained packet losses Specifically for a case where the following criteria are all met: *  The connection has been in fast recovery for at least one full round trip. *  The loss rate over the time scale of a single full round trip exceeds BBRLossThresh (2%).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Chromium and Linux TCP BBRv2 both use 8 lost bursts in a round trip",
      "id": "8ef86505045d8f08",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 156,
      "quote": "*  There are at least BBRStartupFullLossCnt=3 discontiguous sequence ranges lost in that round trip.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The BBRv2 RFC reference to \"fast recovery\" here is more applicable to TCP.",
      "id": "6a588cc0fec43f7e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "*  The connection has been in fast recovery for at least one full round trip.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/full_pipe.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8f7429d1c878607",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "BBRInitPacingRate(): nominal_bandwidth = InitialCwnd / (SRTT ? SRTT : 1ms) BBR.pacing_rate =  BBRStartupPacingGain * nominal_bandwidth",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8ec8e6015e61c7a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "if (BBR.pacing_rate < 1.2 Mbps) floor = 1 * SMSS else floor = 2 * SMSS BBR.send_quantum = min(BBR.pacing_rate * 1ms, 64KBytes) BBR.send_quantum = max(BBR.send_quantum, floor)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC recommends limiting bursts to the initial congestion window",
      "id": "6d3dbd4921ba3a0f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "BBR.send_quantum = min(BBR.pacing_rate * 1ms, 64KBytes)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6291ebf847e270b8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 156,
      "quote": "BBR.next_departure_time = max(Now(), BBR.next_departure_time) packet.departure_time = BBR.next_departure_time pacing_delay = packet.size / BBR.pacing_rate",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "52cabf878af3e934",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "The static discount factor of 1% used to scale BBR.bw to produce BBR.pacing_rate.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5b0be76a4d50d6a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "BBRSetPacingRateWithGain(pacing_gain): rate = pacing_gain * bw * (100 - BBRPacingMarginPercent) / 100 if (BBR.filled_pipe || rate > BBR.pacing_rate) BBR.pacing_rate = rate",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d67d1a2656b643e8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 206,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "057c16c44e1c9bf4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 224,
      "quote": "BBR.send_quantum = min(BBR.pacing_rate * 1ms, 64KBytes)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "263948336f459c64",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 237,
      "quote": "BBRSetPacingRateWithGain(pacing_gain): rate = pacing_gain * bw * (100 - BBRPacingMarginPercent) / 100 if (BBR.filled_pipe || rate > BBR.pacing_rate) BBR.pacing_rate = rate",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "92cf81dfb1cec91e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 279,
      "quote": "if (BBR.pacing_rate < 1.2 Mbps) floor = 1 * SMSS else floor = 2 * SMSS BBR.send_quantum = min(BBR.pacing_rate * 1ms, 64KBytes) BBR.send_quantum = max(BBR.send_quantum, floor)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/pacing.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c111d6ca67f5e4f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "After ProbeBW_REFILL refills the pipe, ProbeBW_UP probes for possible increases in available bandwidth by using a BBR.pacing_gain of 1.25, sending faster than the current estimated available bandwidth.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "40f1253c5b449269",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "a BBR flow in ProbeBW mode cycles through the four Probe bw states - DOWN, CRUISE, REFILL, and UP",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ebe144bdd3642e89",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "In the ProbeBW_DOWN phase of the cycle, a BBR flow pursues the deceleration tactic, to try to send slower than the network is delivering data, to reduce the amount of data in flight, with all of the standard motivations for the deceleration tactic (discussed in \"State Machine Tactics\", above). It does this by switching to a BBR.pacing_gain of 0.9, sending at 90% of BBR.bw.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ede918166fd51ee5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "During ProbeBW_REFILL BBR uses a BBR.pacing_gain of 1.0, to send at a rate that matches the current estimated available bandwidth",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc8be4166ae1fa81",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "In the ProbeBW_CRUISE phase of the cycle, a BBR flow pursues the \"cruising\" tactic (discussed in \"State Machine Tactics\", above), attempting to send at the same rate the network is delivering data. It tries to match the sending rate to the flow's current available bandwidth, to try to achieve high utilization of the available bandwidth without increasing queue pressure. It does this by switching to a pacing_gain of 1.0, sending at 100% of BBR.bw.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f6fa4bc3277600a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 217,
      "quote": "BBRCheckTimeToProbeBW() if (BBRHasElapsedInPhase(BBR.bw_probe_wait) || BBRIsRenoCoexistenceProbeTime()) BBRStartProbeBW_REFILL() return true return false",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6742ca709e70048",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 246,
      "quote": "BBRProbeInflightHiUpward() if (!is_cwnd_limited or cwnd < BBR.inflight_hi) return  /* not fully using inflight_hi, so don't grow it */ BBR.bw_probe_up_acks += rs.newly_acked if (BBR.bw_probe_up_acks >= BBR.probe_up_cnt) delta = BBR.bw_probe_up_acks / BBR.probe_up_cnt BBR.bw_probe_up_acks -= delta * BBR.bw_probe_up_cnt BBR.inflight_hi += delta if (BBR.round_start) BBRRaiseInflightHiSlope()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3f9d4bbcb1fa7405",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "BBRRaiseInflightHiSlope(): growth_this_round = 1MSS << BBR.bw_probe_up_rounds BBR.bw_probe_up_rounds = min(BBR.bw_probe_up_rounds + 1, 30) BBR.probe_up_cnt = max(cwnd / growth_this_round, 1)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae4eb196364556b0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 282,
      "quote": "BBR takes an approach where the additive increase to BBR.inflight_hi exponentially doubles each round trip",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e22d44538dd6ecc8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 295,
      "quote": "BBRHasElapsedInPhase(interval) return Now() > BBR.cycle_stamp + interval",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "35dac15be609d870",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 310,
      "quote": "BBRIsRenoCoexistenceProbeTime() reno_rounds = BBRTargetInflight() rounds = min(reno_rounds, 63) return BBR.rounds_since_bw_probe >= rounds",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0857f7af82040f0f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 326,
      "quote": "BBRStartProbeBW_CRUISE() BBR.state = ProbeBW_CRUISE",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "86f8dedb6a5f2cbb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 344,
      "quote": "BBRStartProbeBW_UP() BBR.ack_phase = ACKS_PROBE_STARTING BBRStartRound() BBR.cycle_stamp = Now() /* start wall clock */ BBR.state = ProbeBW_UP BBRRaiseInflightHiSlope()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "09151652023f8b2d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 368,
      "quote": "BBRStartProbeBW_REFILL() BBRResetLowerBounds() BBR.bw_probe_up_rounds = 0 BBR.bw_probe_up_acks = 0 BBR.ack_phase = ACKS_REFILLING BBRStartRound() BBR.state = ProbeBW_REFILL",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "44110f5c05f3fb8f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 397,
      "quote": "BBRStartProbeBW_DOWN() BBRResetCongestionSignals() BBR.probe_up_cnt = Infinity /* not growing inflight_hi */ BBRPickProbeWait() BBR.cycle_stamp = Now()  /* start wall clock */ BBR.ack_phase  = ACKS_PROBE_STOPPING BBRStartRound() BBR.state = ProbeBW_DOWN",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1de04125c062a74b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 421,
      "quote": "BBRPickProbeWait() /* Decide random round-trip bound for wait: */ BBR.rounds_since_bw_probe = random_int_between(0, 1); /* 0 or 1 */ /* Decide the random wall clock bound for wait: */ BBR.bw_probe_wait = 2sec + random_float_between(0.0, 1.0) /* 0..1 sec */",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3960918dbf936ec",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 462,
      "quote": "BBREnterProbeBW(): BBRStartProbeBW_DOWN()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0193b7dc503e513",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 494,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateProbeBWCyclePhase(): if (!BBR.filled_pipe) return  /* only handling steady-state behavior here */ BBRAdaptUpperBounds() if (!IsInAProbeBWState()) return /* only handling ProbeBW states here: */ switch (state) ProbeBW_DOWN: if (BBRCheckTimeToProbeBW()) return /* already decided state transition */ if (BBRCheckTimeToCruise()) BBRStartProbeBW_CRUISE() ProbeBW_CRUISE: if (BBRCheckTimeToProbeBW()) return /* already decided state transition */ ProbeBW_REFILL: /* After one round of REFILL, start UP */ if (BBR.round_start) BBR.bw_probe_samples = 1 BBRStartProbeBW_UP() ProbeBW_UP: if (BBRHasElapsedInPhase(BBR.min_rtt) and inflight > BBRInflight(BBR.max_bw, 1.25)) BBRStartProbeBW_DOWN()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "18e2e102ab1bd4c1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 618,
      "quote": "BBRAdaptUpperBounds() if (BBR.ack_phase == ACKS_PROBE_STARTING and BBR.round_start) /* starting to get bw probing samples */ BBR.ack_phase = ACKS_PROBE_FEEDBACK if (BBR.ack_phase == ACKS_PROBE_STOPPING and BBR.round_start) /* end of samples from bw probing phase */ if (IsInAProbeBWState() and !rs.is_app_limited) BBRAdvanceMaxBwFilter() if (!CheckInflightTooHigh()) /* Loss rate is safe. Adjust upper bounds upward. */ if (BBR.inflight_hi == Infinity or BBR.bw_hi == Infinity) return /* no upper bounds to raise */ if (rs.tx_in_flight > BBR.inflight_hi) BBR.inflight_hi = rs.tx_in_flight",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "73b421d1defe88e3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 704,
      "quote": "if (BBR.ack_phase == ACKS_PROBE_STARTING and BBR.round_start) /* starting to get bw probing samples */ BBR.ack_phase = ACKS_PROBE_FEEDBACK if (BBR.ack_phase == ACKS_PROBE_STOPPING and BBR.round_start) /* end of samples from bw probing phase */ if (IsInAProbeBWState() and !rs.is_app_limited) BBRAdvanceMaxBwFilter()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cfc7dce06b9df2f3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 748,
      "quote": "BBRHandleInflightTooHigh() BBR.bw_probe_samples = 0;  /* only react once per bw probe */ if (!rs.is_app_limited) BBR.inflight_hi = max(rs.tx_in_flight, BBRTargetInflight() * BBRBeta)) If (BBR.state == ProbeBW_UP) BBRStartProbeBW_DOWN()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b8134ec57c4541df",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 793,
      "quote": "BBRCheckTimeToCruise()) if (inflight > BBRInflightWithHeadroom()) return false /* not enough headroom */ if (inflight <= BBRInflight(BBR.max_bw, 1.0)) return true  /* inflight <= estimated BDP */",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "81eb190312c2afb2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 824,
      "quote": "In the ProbeBW_DOWN phase of the cycle, a BBR flow pursues the deceleration tactic, to try to send slower than the network is delivering data, to reduce the amount of data in flight, with all of the standard motivations for the deceleration tactic (discussed in \"State Machine Tactics\", above). It does this by switching to a BBR.pacing_gain of 0.9, sending at 90% of BBR.bw.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "73c7b1d3b2b2ec8f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 836,
      "quote": "After ProbeBW_REFILL refills the pipe, ProbeBW_UP probes for possible increases in available bandwidth by using a BBR.pacing_gain of 1.25, sending faster than the current estimated available bandwidth.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a91a686ede794b42",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 846,
      "quote": "During ProbeBW_REFILL BBR uses a BBR.pacing_gain of 1.0, to send at a rate that matches the current estimated available bandwidth",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "463201568ed2c332",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 855,
      "quote": "In the ProbeBW_CRUISE phase of the cycle, a BBR flow pursues the \"cruising\" tactic (discussed in \"State Machine Tactics\", above), attempting to send at the same rate the network is delivering data. It tries to match the sending rate to the flow's current available bandwidth, to try to achieve high utilization of the available bandwidth without increasing queue pressure. It does this by switching to a pacing_gain of 1.0, sending at 100% of BBR.bw.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_bw.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0ae826e6c88df6e6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the minimum duration for which ProbeRTT state holds inflight to BBRMinPipeCwnd or fewer packets: 200 ms.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.14.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cfb15ebc9ac82570",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "BBREnterProbeRTT(): BBR.state = ProbeRTT BBR.pacing_gain = 1",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "07e746b180573afe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the gain value for calculating the cwnd during ProbeRTT: 0.5",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.14.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "97f999f861fc0240",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "BBRHandleProbeRTT() /* Ignore low rate samples during ProbeRTT: */ MarkConnectionAppLimited() if (BBR.probe_rtt_done_stamp == 0 and packets_in_flight <= BBRProbeRTTCwnd()) /* Wait for at least ProbeRTTDuration to elapse: */ BBR.probe_rtt_done_stamp = Now() + ProbeRTTDuration /* Wait for at least one round to elapse: */ BBR.probe_rtt_round_done = false BBRStartRound() else if (BBR.probe_rtt_done_stamp != 0) if (BBR.round_start) BBR.probe_rtt_round_done = true if (BBR.probe_rtt_round_done) BBRCheckProbeRTTDone()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f04d9631bdcacd55",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "BBRCheckProbeRTT() if (BBR.state != ProbeRTT and BBR.probe_rtt_expired and not BBR.idle_restart) BBREnterProbeRTT() BBRSaveCwnd() BBR.probe_rtt_done_stamp = 0 BBR.ack_phase = ACKS_PROBE_STOPPING BBRStartRound() if (BBR.state == ProbeRTT) BBRHandleProbeRTT() if (rs.delivered > 0) BBR.idle_restart = false",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7e6e5167c460aba2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "BBRCheckProbeRTTDone(): if (BBR.probe_rtt_done_stamp != 0 and Now() > BBR.probe_rtt_done_stamp) /* schedule next ProbeRTT: */ BBR.probe_rtt_min_stamp = Now() BBRRestoreCwnd() BBRExitProbeRTT()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5e080c0cc4084a2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 182,
      "quote": "BBRExitProbeRTT() BBRResetLowerBounds() if (BBR.filled_pipe) BBRStartProbeBW_DOWN() BBRStartProbeBW_CRUISE() else BBREnterStartup()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "95a99e9ca171dd46",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 195,
      "quote": "as an optimization, since the connection is exiting ProbeRTT, we know that infligh is already below the estimated BDP, so the connection can proceed immediately to ProbeBW_CRUISE",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "65e7dc5236a3430a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 209,
      "quote": "BBRProbeRTTCwnd(): probe_rtt_cwnd = BBRBDPMultiple(BBR.bw, BBRProbeRTTCwndGain) probe_rtt_cwnd = max(probe_rtt_cwnd, BBRMinPipeCwnd) return probe_rtt_cwnd",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa8f81d5737a7d25",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 332,
      "quote": "BBRProbeRTTCwnd(): probe_rtt_cwnd = BBRBDPMultiple(BBR.bw, BBRProbeRTTCwndGain) probe_rtt_cwnd = max(probe_rtt_cwnd, BBRMinPipeCwnd) return probe_rtt_cwnd",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/probe_rtt.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "81a8932f8597fe53",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 6,
      "quote": "If the congestion window is reduced immediately, a single packet can be sent prior to reduction.  This speeds up loss recovery if the data in the lost packet is retransmitted and is similar to TCP as described in Section 5 of [RFC6675].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/recovery.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa93a650d62f3089",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "A recovery period ends and the sender enters congestion avoidance when a packet sent during the recovery period is acknowledged.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/recovery.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e63921a24d08c063",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "If the congestion window is reduced immediately, a single packet can be sent prior to reduction.  This speeds up loss recovery if the data in the lost packet is retransmitted and is similar to TCP as described in Section 5 of [RFC6675].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/recovery.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a7e5ee75cfc782c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 6,
      "quote": "Several aspects of the BBR algorithm depend on counting the progress of \"packet-timed\" round trips, which start at the transmission of some segment, and then end at the acknowledgement of that segment. BBR.round_count is a count of the number of these \"packet-timed\" round trips elapsed so far.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/round.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "19c870da5f666a42",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "BBRInitRoundCounting(): BBR.next_round_delivered = 0 BBR.round_start = false BBR.round_count = 0",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/round.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "957f03639e024ab9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateRound(): if (packet.delivered >= BBR.next_round_delivered) BBRStartRound() BBR.round_count++ BBR.rounds_since_probe++ BBR.round_start = true else BBR.round_start = false",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/round.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "05f101b720b4c773",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "BBRStartRound(): BBR.next_round_delivered = C.delivered",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/round.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "629f8f49796e7605",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the minimum gain value for calculating the pacing rate that will allow the sending rate to double each round (4*ln(2) ~= 2.77)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/startup.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5372c09911672676",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the minimum gain value for calculating the cwnd that will allow the sending rate to double each round (2.0)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/startup.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a51208f5091111c3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "BBREnterStartup(): BBR.state = Startup BBR.pacing_gain = BBRStartupPacingGain BBR.cwnd_gain = BBRStartupCwndGain",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/startup.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9ae3997e72b9d889",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "BBRCheckStartupDone(): BBRCheckStartupFullBandwidth() BBRCheckStartupHighLoss() if (BBR.state == Startup and BBR.filled_pipe) BBREnterDrain()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/startup.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d52933653d482761",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "BBRCheckStartupDone(): BBRCheckStartupFullBandwidth() BBRCheckStartupHighLoss() if (BBR.state == Startup and BBR.filled_pipe) BBREnterDrain()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/startup.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ea89728a3aa01b1c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "When not explicitly accelerating to probe for bandwidth (Drain, ProbeRTT, ProbeBW_DOWN, ProbeBW_CRUISE), BBR responds to loss by slowing down to some extent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0284d6c8aeccd081",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "BBRInflightHiFromLostPacket(rs, packet): size = packet.size /* What was in flight before this packet? */ inflight_prev = rs.tx_in_flight - size /* What was lost before this packet? */ lost_prev = rs.lost - size lost_prefix = (BBRLossThresh * inflight_prev - lost_prev) / (1 - BBRLossThresh) /* At what inflight value did losses cross BBRLossThresh? */ inflight = inflight_prev + lost_prefix return inflight",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "079c4aa37024c8a2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the minimum gain value for calculating the pacing rate that will allow the sending rate to double each round (4*ln(2) ~= 2.77)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "153d58aef167eb8f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 192,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the minimum gain value for calculating the cwnd that will allow the sending rate to double each round (2.0)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "6750e86fad6c53e4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 205,
      "quote": "In Drain, BBR aims to quickly drain any queue created in Startup by switching to a pacing_gain well below 1.0, until any estimated queue has been drained. It uses a pacing_gain that is the inverse of the value used during Startup, chosen to try to drain the queue in one round",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4693b7008c435374",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 212,
      "quote": "BBREnterDrain(): BBR.state = Drain BBR.pacing_gain = 1/BBRStartupCwndGain  /* pace slowly */ BBR.cwnd_gain = BBRStartupCwndGain      /* maintain cwnd */",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "dbdba2b610ed0ee8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 245,
      "quote": "In the ProbeBW_DOWN phase of the cycle, a BBR flow pursues the deceleration tactic, to try to send slower than the network is delivering data, to reduce the amount of data in flight, with all of the standard motivations for the deceleration tactic (discussed in \"State Machine Tactics\", above). It does this by switching to a BBR.pacing_gain of 0.9, sending at 90% of BBR.bw.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e294029e7d2fa462",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 258,
      "quote": "BBREnterProbeRTT(): BBR.state = ProbeRTT BBR.pacing_gain = 1",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf4e693d206021be",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 272,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the gain value for calculating the cwnd during ProbeRTT: 0.5",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.14.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a0228b098cfd2268",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 296,
      "quote": "BBROnInit(): init_windowed_max_filter(filter=BBR.MaxBwFilter, value=0, time=0) BBR.min_rtt = SRTT ? SRTT : Inf BBR.min_rtt_stamp = Now() BBR.probe_rtt_done_stamp = 0 BBR.probe_rtt_round_done = false BBR.prior_cwnd = 0 BBR.idle_restart = false BBR.extra_acked_interval_start = Now() BBR.extra_acked_delivered = 0 BBRResetCongestionSignals() BBRResetLowerBounds() BBRInitRoundCounting() BBRInitFullPipe() BBRInitPacingRate() BBREnterStartup()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c12b24979290354e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 342,
      "quote": "BBRBDPMultiple(gain): if (BBR.min_rtt == Inf) return InitialCwnd /* no valid RTT samples yet */ BBR.bdp = BBR.bw * BBR.min_rtt return gain * BBR.bdp",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "67f0748802193bb8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 375,
      "quote": "BBRTargetInflight() return min(BBR.bdp, cwnd)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3cb4fbb8b865df80",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 407,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateMaxInflight() BBRUpdateAggregationBudget() inflight = BBRBDPMultiple(BBR.cwnd_gain) inflight += BBR.extra_acked BBR.max_inflight = BBRQuantizationBudget(inflight)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "10b87ad063d3f648",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 425,
      "quote": "BBRInflight(gain) inflight = BBRBDPMultiple(gain) return BBRQuantizationBudget(inflight)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b756362799c482f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 452,
      "quote": "BBRInflightWithHeadroom() if (BBR.inflight_hi == Infinity) return Infinity headroom = max(1, BBRHeadroom * BBR.inflight_hi) return max(BBR.inflight_hi - headroom, BBRMinPipeCwnd)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "db4af7f0163c26af",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 480,
      "quote": "BBRQuantizationBudget(inflight) BBRUpdateOffloadBudget() inflight = max(inflight, BBR.offload_budget) inflight = max(inflight, BBRMinPipeCwnd) if (BBR.state == ProbeBW && BBR.cycle_idx == ProbeBW_UP) inflight += 2 return inflight",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ffa881f1017d52c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 591,
      "quote": "BBRBoundCwndForModel(): cap = Infinity if (IsInAProbeBWState() and BBR.state != ProbeBW_CRUISE) cap = BBR.inflight_hi else if (BBR.state == ProbeRTT or BBR.state == ProbeBW_CRUISE) cap = BBRInflightWithHeadroom() /* apply inflight_lo (possibly infinite): */ cap = min(cap, BBR.inflight_lo) cap = max(cap, BBRMinPipeCwnd) cwnd = min(cwnd, cap)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.7",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa8abd2d40f48a2d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 644,
      "quote": "if (BBR.filled_pipe) cwnd = min(cwnd + rs.newly_acked, BBR.max_inflight)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "87373019573e8924",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 667,
      "quote": "else if (cwnd < BBR.max_inflight || C.delivered < InitialCwnd) cwnd = cwnd + rs.newly_acked",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d0331080b8d51868",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 722,
      "quote": "BBRBoundCwndForProbeRTT(): if (BBR.state == ProbeRTT) cwnd = min(cwnd, BBRProbeRTTCwnd())",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7895a524797458ee",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 768,
      "quote": "BBRSaveCwnd() if (!InLossRecovery() and BBR.state != ProbeRTT) return cwnd else return max(BBR.prior_cwnd, cwnd)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2b180660d028043e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 791,
      "quote": "BBRRestoreCwnd() cwnd = max(cwnd, BBR.prior_cwnd)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a0b64d5e061b766d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 815,
      "quote": "Upon entering Fast Recovery, set cwnd to the number of packets still in flight (allowing at least one for a fast retransmit): BBROnEnterFastRecovery(): BBR.prior_cwnd = BBRSaveCwnd() cwnd = packets_in_flight + max(rs.newly_acked, 1) BBR.packet_conservation = true",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.6.4.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "3e305cb80eca0ee4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 825,
      "quote": "if (!BBR.bw_probe_samples) return /* not a packet sent while probing bandwidth */ rs.tx_in_flight = packet.tx_in_flight /* inflight at transmit */ rs.lost = C.lost - packet.lost /* data lost since transmit */ rs.is_app_limited = packet.is_app_limited; if (IsInflightTooHigh(rs)) rs.tx_in_flight = BBRInflightHiFromLostPacket(rs, packet) BBRHandleInflightTooHigh(rs)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d1eebb4ec069936a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 935,
      "quote": "BBRHandleRestartFromIdle(): if (packets_in_flight == 0 and C.app_limited) BBR.idle_restart = true BBR.extra_acked_interval_start = Now() if (IsInAProbeBWState()) BBRSetPacingRateWithGain(1)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.4.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8d815ca5ab4ec233",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "A BBR implementation MAY use a generic windowed min filter to track BBR.min_rtt. However, a significant savings in space and improvement in freshness can be achieved by integrating the BBR.min_rtt estimation into the ProbeRTT state machine",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/windowed_filter.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.5.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fee7bc33d5da5b2e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "A boolean recording whether the BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay has expired and is due for a refresh with an application idle period or a transition into ProbeRTT state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/windowed_filter.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.14.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "85fc26e3e97b4121",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 111,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the minimum time interval between ProbeRTT states: 5 secs.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/windowed_filter.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.14.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e06cf66ed7d0385",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "A constant specifying the length of the BBR.min_rtt min filter window, MinRTTFilterLen is 10 secs.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/windowed_filter.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "176fbe66d5d43e4c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "BBRUpdateMinRTT() BBR.probe_rtt_expired = Now() > BBR.probe_rtt_min_stamp + ProbeRTTInterval if (rs.rtt >= 0 and (rs.rtt < BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay or BBR.probe_rtt_expired)) BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay = rs.rtt BBR.probe_rtt_min_stamp = Now() min_rtt_expired = Now() > BBR.min_rtt_stamp + MinRTTFilterLen if (BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay < BBR.min_rtt or min_rtt_expired) BBR.min_rtt       = BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay BBR.min_rtt_stamp = BBR.probe_rtt_min_stamp",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr/windowed_filter.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e70cd9961b5ae2a4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "The maximum tolerated per-round-trip packet loss rate when probing for bandwidth (the default is 2%).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "24438378d21af590",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "The default multiplicative decrease to make upon each round trip during which the connection detects packet loss (the value is 0.7)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "faeb47cc5b0505ee",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "The multiplicative factor to apply to BBR.inflight_hi when attempting to leave free headroom in the path (e.g. free space in the bottleneck buffer or free time slots in the bottleneck link) that can be used by cross traffic (the value is 0.85).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5b7d0ae0a2edf3cc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "The minimal cwnd value BBR targets, to allow pipelining with TCP endpoints that follow an \"ACK every other packet\" delayed-ACK policy: 4 * SMSS.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b068a126ff2ab86",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "The following state transition diagram summarizes the flow of control and the relationship between the different states: | V +---> Startup  ------------+ |        |                 | |        V                 | |     Drain  --------------+ |        |                 | |        V                 | +---> ProbeBW_DOWN  -------+ | ^      |                 | | |      V                 | | |   ProbeBW_CRUISE ------+ | |      |                 | | |      V                 | | |   ProbeBW_REFILL  -----+ | |      |                 | | |      V                 | | |   ProbeBW_UP  ---------+ | |      |                 | | +------+                 | |                          | +---- ProbeRTT <-----------+",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3663dd3340fa434c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "IsInAProbeBWState() state = BBR.state return (state == ProbeBW_DOWN or state == ProbeBW_CRUISE or state == ProbeBW_REFILL or state == ProbeBW_UP)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.3.3.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4e8400ed9ebab503",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 255,
      "quote": "The sum of the size in bytes of all sent packets that contain at least one ack-eliciting or PADDING frame and have not been acknowledged or declared lost.  The size does not include IP or UDP overhead, but does include the QUIC header and Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data (AEAD) overhead. Packets only containing ACK frames do not count toward bytes_in_flight to ensure congestion control does not impede congestion feedback.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-B.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "13d9c383c286e33a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 281,
      "quote": "True if the connection has fully utilized its cwnd at any point in the last packet-timed round trip.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "51f3b6e50fa31d1d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 329,
      "quote": "BBROnTransmit(): BBRHandleRestartFromIdle()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4303c24bbcc1f53c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 401,
      "quote": "On every ACK, the BBR algorithm executes the following BBRUpdateOnACK() steps in order to update its network path model, update its state machine, and adjust its control parameters to adapt to the updated model: BBRUpdateOnACK(): BBRUpdateModelAndState() BBRUpdateControlParameters()",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-core/src/recovery/bbr.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-cardwell-iccrg-bbr-congestion-control-02",
      "target_section": "4.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
