    },
    {
      "id": "5a0e76be86882f59",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 661,
      "quote": "it is recommended to use QUIC's Original Destination Connection ID (ODCID, the CID chosen by the client when first contacting the server)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-events/events/common.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-marx-qlog-event-definitions-quic-h3-02",
      "target_section": "4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "67a35d35539f8ba3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 774,
      "quote": "If the sender wants to elicit a faster acknowledgement on PTO, it can skip a packet number to eliminate the acknowledgment delay.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-events/events/common.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8e2799c27d515cec",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 780,
      "quote": "An endpoint that acknowledges packets it has not received might cause a congestion controller to permit sending at rates beyond what the network supports.  An endpoint MAY skip packet numbers when sending packets to detect this behavior.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-events/events/common.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6de05dff051e7c70",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 5,
      "quote": "QUIC implementations each have their own list of application level protocols and versions thereof they support.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-events/events/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-marx-qlog-event-definitions-quic-h3-02",
