    },
    {
      "id": "142aeada4e84f635",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "Senders SHOULD limit bursts to the initial congestion window",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-platform/src/features/gso.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e66559a1e66ce72",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "o  the Dynamic Ports, also known as the Private or Ephemeral Ports, from 49152-65535 (never assigned)",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-platform/src/io/testing/network.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6335",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "978af1763dffa1cb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "UDP datagrams MUST NOT be fragmented at the IP layer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-platform/src/syscall.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "88ba38930e5af764",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "In IPv4 [IPv4], the Don't Fragment (DF) bit MUST be set if possible, to prevent fragmentation on the path.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-platform/src/syscall.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "76d5c7e820219813",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "In IPv4, a probe packet MUST be sent with the Don't Fragment (DF) bit set in the IP header and without network layer endpoint fragmentation.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-platform/src/syscall.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a06a5133b43ac6e1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "A PL implementing this specification MUST suspend network layer processing of outgoing packets that enforces a PMTU [RFC1191][RFC8201] for each flow utilizing DPLPMTUD and instead use DPLPMTUD to control the size of packets that are sent by a flow.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-platform/src/syscall.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0186e463aa390a24",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "The ALPN used by the QUIC performance protocol is \"perf\".",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/client/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f6a34172bc8bba5d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Since the goal here is to measure the efficiency of the QUIC implementation and not any application protocol, the performance application layer should be as light-weight as possible.  To this end, the client and server application layer may use a single preallocated and initialized buffer that it queues to send when any payload needs to be sent out.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cd511059c1f80e7b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "Every stream opened by the client uses the first 8 bytes of the stream data to encode a 64-bit unsigned integer in network byte order to indicate the length of data the client wishes the server to respond with.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d08bf7a85b5aa811",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "The ALPN used by the QUIC performance protocol is \"perf\".",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/server/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b3ce3d94b818baa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "On the server side, any stream that is closed before all 8 bytes are received should just be ignored, and gracefully closed on its end (if applicable).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/server/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3c6952d921c8b85",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 119,
      "quote": "On the server side, any stream that is closed before all 8 bytes are received should just be ignored, and gracefully closed on its end (if applicable).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/server/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "2.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8c76ae7e97c30f9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 137,
      "quote": "When a client uses a bidirectional stream to request a response payload from the server, the server sends the requested data on the same stream.  If no data is requested by the client, the server merely closes its side of the stream.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/server/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "2.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b52dc32c1c2d21f6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 154,
      "quote": "When a client uses a unidirectional stream to request a response payload from the server, the server opens a new unidirectional stream to send the requested data.  If no data is requested by the client, the server need take no action.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-qns/src/server/perf.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-banks-quic-performance-00",
      "target_section": "2.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9dff6c3b4472db05",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 337,
      "quote": "A cipher suite MUST NOT be negotiated unless a header protection scheme is defined for the cipher suite.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/cipher_suite.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "06544aa7cd3aaff4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension;",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/client.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "06dac9ba9b4467d3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "A client MUST authenticate the identity of the server.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/client.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ff3892d7e82b2059",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT offer TLS versions older than 1.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/lib.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d83c14f909a39375",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension;",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/server.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d89c1cc13c79a503",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "QUIC is only able to convey an alert level of \"fatal\".  In TLS 1.3, the only existing uses for the \"warning\" level are to signal connection close; see Section 6.1 of [TLS13].  As QUIC provides alternative mechanisms for connection termination and the TLS connection is only closed if an error is encountered, a QUIC endpoint MUST treat any alert from TLS as if it were at the \"fatal\" level.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/session.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d8d9e05a2d7409e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "endpoints that receive ClientHello or EncryptedExtensions messages without the quic_transport_parameters extension MUST close the connection with an error of type 0x16d (equivalent to a fatal TLS missing_extension alert, see Section 4.8).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/session.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ede3619837a05d30",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 145,
      "quote": "Unless another mechanism is used for agreeing on an application protocol, endpoints MUST use ALPN for this purpose.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/session.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f09f268d9de19b31",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "Client                                              Server ClientHello                     -------->       ServerHello (ALPN extension &                               (ALPN extension & list of protocols)                              selected protocol) [ChangeCipherSpec] <--------       Finished [ChangeCipherSpec] Finished                        --------> Application Data                <------->       Application Data",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-rustls/src/session.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7301",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9a4d16c55d08d589",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 446,
      "quote": "This specification defines the following cipher suites for use with TLS 1.3. +------------------------------+-------------+ | Description                  | Value       | +------------------------------+-------------+ | TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256       | {0x13,0x01} | |                              |             | | TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384       | {0x13,0x02} | |                              |             | | TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 | {0x13,0x03} | |                              |             | | TLS_AES_128_CCM_SHA256       | {0x13,0x04} | |                              |             | | TLS_AES_128_CCM_8_SHA256     | {0x13,0x05} | +------------------------------+-------------+",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-tls/src/callback.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446",
      "target_section": "appendix-B.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "66f34cb3bdfb337e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 470,
      "quote": "QUIC can use any of the cipher suites defined in [TLS13] with the exception of TLS_AES_128_CCM_8_SHA256.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-tls/src/callback.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc5f238987ffede7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 497,
      "quote": "When using ALPN, endpoints MUST immediately close a connection (see Section 10.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) with a no_application_protocol TLS alert (QUIC error code 0x178; see Section 4.8) if an application protocol is not negotiated.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-tls/src/callback.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "de8f01db8dd83199",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 503,
      "quote": "While [ALPN] only specifies that servers use this alert, QUIC clients MUST use error 0x178 to terminate a connection when ALPN negotiation fails.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-tls/src/callback.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "689657dfdaab4240",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 515,
      "quote": "Unless another mechanism is used for agreeing on an application protocol, endpoints MUST use ALPN for this purpose.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-tls/src/callback.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "108893e03ab71cdf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 520,
      "quote": "Client                                              Server ClientHello                     -------->       ServerHello (ALPN extension &                               (ALPN extension & list of protocols)                              selected protocol) [ChangeCipherSpec] <--------       Finished [ChangeCipherSpec] Finished                        --------> Application Data                <------->       Application Data",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-tls/src/callback.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7301",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "292abe3e1573764c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "Endpoints acknowledge all packets they receive and process.  However, only ack-eliciting packets cause an ACK frame to be sent within the maximum ack delay.  Packets that are not ack-eliciting are only acknowledged when an ACK frame is sent for other reasons. When sending a packet for any reason, an endpoint SHOULD attempt to include an ACK frame if one has not been sent recently.  Doing so helps with timely loss detection at the peer. In general, frequent feedback from a receiver improves loss and congestion response, but this has to be balanced against excessive load generated by a receiver that sends an ACK frame in response to every ack-eliciting packet.  The guidance offered below seeks to strike this balance.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3aeed290a77e7906",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "Even if an endpoint does not set an ECT field on packets it sends, the endpoint MUST provide feedback about ECN markings it receives, if these are accessible.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "79b82353ddd2ce11",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 157,
      "quote": "When a packet containing an ACK frame is sent, the Largest Acknowledged field in that frame can be saved.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "905a86089439137c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 264,
      "quote": "ECN counts are only incremented when QUIC packets from the received IP packet are processed.  As such, duplicate QUIC packets are not processed and do not increase ECN counts; see Section 21.10 for relevant security concerns.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c174f441a7b15fca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 275,
      "quote": "An endpoint measures the delays intentionally introduced between the time the packet with the largest packet number is received and the time an acknowledgment is sent.  The endpoint encodes this acknowledgement delay in the ACK Delay field of an ACK frame; see Section 19.3.  This allows the receiver of the ACK frame to adjust for any intentional delays, which is important for getting a better estimate of the path RTT when acknowledgments are delayed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0cfe39d56ea66c19",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 290,
      "quote": "In order to assist loss detection at the sender, an endpoint SHOULD generate and send an ACK frame without delay when it receives an ack- eliciting packet either: *  when the received packet has a packet number less than another ack-eliciting packet that has been received, or",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c521257aa9f28feb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 300,
      "quote": "*  when the packet has a packet number larger than the highest- numbered ack-eliciting packet that has been received and there are missing packets between that packet and this packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f28a2184b0005084",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 307,
      "quote": "Similarly, packets marked with the ECN Congestion Experienced (CE) codepoint in the IP header SHOULD be acknowledged immediately, to reduce the peer's response time to congestion events.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5bce7445158068e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 323,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a PATH_CHALLENGE on an active path SHOULD send a non-probing packet in response.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0ff2403b0a37f417",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 331,
      "quote": "Endpoints acknowledge all packets they receive and process.  However, only ack-eliciting packets cause an ACK frame to be sent within the maximum ack delay.  Packets that are not ack-eliciting are only acknowledged when an ACK frame is sent for other reasons.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f45295eda009dda3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "packets containing only ACK frames do not count towards bytes in flight and are not congestion controlled.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_transmission_state.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ffad9e080e9fe78f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "In general, frequent feedback from a receiver improves loss and congestion response, but this has to be balanced against excessive load generated by a receiver that sends an ACK frame in response to every ack-eliciting packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_transmission_state.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d0509a65ca091f54",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "packets containing only ACK frames do not count towards bytes in flight and are not congestion controlled",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/ack/ack_transmission_state.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "273599fb1c7f15ff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 111,
      "quote": "Packets containing frames besides ACK or CONNECTION_CLOSE frames count toward congestion control limits and are considered to be in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/close_sender.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7458271382f6070e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 170,
      "quote": "|  Note: Allowing retransmission of a closing packet is an |  exception to the requirement that a new packet number be used |  for each packet; see Section 12.3.  Sending new packet numbers |  is primarily of advantage to loss recovery and congestion |  control, which are not expected to be relevant for a closed |  connection.  Retransmitting the final packet requires less |  state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/close_sender.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f22d3df4dfb4ba24",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 266,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD limit the rate at which it generates packets in the closing state.  For instance, an endpoint could wait for a progressively increasing number of received packets or amount of time before responding to received packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/close_sender.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6b7dbb0ee15c9cf5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 308,
      "quote": "When comparing a datagram to stateless reset token values, endpoints MUST perform the comparison without leaking information about the value of the token.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_id_mapper.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4b12df9c8c8d5679",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "When an endpoint has no validated path on which to send packets, it MAY discard connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4b4d041b75cf599d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "If an endpoint has no state about the last validated peer address, it MUST close the connection silently by discarding all connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fa9dfa755bf910d5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "An endpoint enters the closing state after initiating an immediate close.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7cc95d7fbacd8b4c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "The draining state is entered once an endpoint receives a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame, which indicates that its peer is closing or draining.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "66c61b9778dcd6c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "If the last 16 bytes of the datagram are identical in value to a stateless reset token, the endpoint MUST enter the draining period and not send any further packets on this connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae010132439b3541",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 293,
      "quote": "Client                                                  Server Initial[0]: CRYPTO[CH] -> Initial[0]: CRYPTO[SH] ACK[0] Handshake[0]: CRYPTO[EE, CERT, CV, FIN] <- 1-RTT[0]: STREAM[1, \"...\"] Initial[1]: ACK[0] Handshake[0]: CRYPTO[FIN], ACK[0] 1-RTT[0]: STREAM[0, \"...\"], ACK[0] -> Handshake[1]: ACK[0] <- 1-RTT[1]: HANDSHAKE_DONE, STREAM[3, \"...\"], ACK[0] Figure 5: Example 1-RTT Handshake",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "45cff286392d2c1a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 342,
      "quote": "Each endpoint advertises a max_idle_timeout, but the effective value at an endpoint is computed as the minimum of the two advertised values (or the sole advertised value, if only one endpoint advertises a non-zero value).  By announcing a max_idle_timeout, an endpoint commits to initiating an immediate close (Section 10.2) if it abandons the connection prior to the effective value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1c5f77141a354881",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 352,
      "quote": "To avoid excessively small idle timeout periods, endpoints MUST increase the idle timeout period to be at least three times the current Probe Timeout (PTO).  This allows for multiple PTOs to expire, and therefore multiple probes to be sent and lost, prior to idle timeout.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b175741fff8156ae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 368,
      "quote": "An endpoint restarts its idle timer when a packet from its peer is received and processed successfully.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1d4159722090e13a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 389,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST discard its handshake keys when the TLS handshake is confirmed (Section 4.1.2).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b6ab865044c4e43e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 405,
      "quote": "An endpoint also restarts its idle timer when sending an ack-eliciting packet if no other ack- eliciting packets have been sent since last receiving and processing a packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "133c69789d5e024d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 495,
      "quote": "QUIC deployments SHOULD provide mitigations for the Slowloris attacks, such as increasing the maximum number of clients the server will allow, limiting the number of connections a single IP address is allowed to make, imposing restrictions on the minimum transfer speed a connection is allowed to have, and restricting the length of time an endpoint is allowed to stay connected.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "98a152466fb0d029",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 503,
      "quote": "While there are legitimate uses for all messages, implementations SHOULD track cost of processing relative to progress and treat excessive quantities of any non-productive packets as indicative of an attack.  Endpoints MAY respond to this condition with a connection error or by dropping packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ef5f9daef4d6b1e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 742,
      "quote": "An endpoint that wishes to communicate a fatal connection error MUST use a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame if it is able.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab18445d48072ccd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 770,
      "quote": "The closing and draining connection states exist to ensure that connections close cleanly and that delayed or reordered packets are properly discarded.  These states SHOULD persist for at least three times the current PTO interval as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f36d0a65425d3783",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 808,
      "quote": "In the closing state, an endpoint retains only enough information to generate a packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame and to identify packets as belonging to the connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba49ac8316d5624b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 813,
      "quote": "An endpoint's selected connection ID and the QUIC version are sufficient information to identify packets for a closing connection; the endpoint MAY discard all other connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "029561a2dc3b35de",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 937,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD pace sending of all in-flight packets based on input from the congestion controller.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "437052ec1f753df5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 941,
      "quote": "Senders MUST either use pacing or limit such bursts.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ceb5129153a31b80",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1028,
      "quote": "Once its closing or draining state ends, an endpoint SHOULD discard all connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "256f432ab1186dc4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1154,
      "quote": "The design of QUIC relies on endpoints retaining a stable address for the duration of the handshake.  An endpoint MUST NOT initiate connection migration before the handshake is confirmed, as defined in section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b965402bc973f6c5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1160,
      "quote": "An endpoint in the closing state MUST either discard packets received from an unvalidated address or limit the cumulative size of packets it sends to an unvalidated address to three times the size of packets it receives from that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fb8120f24f67204a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1183,
      "quote": "When a server is blocked by anti-amplification limits, receiving a datagram unblocks it, even if none of the packets in the datagram are successfully processed.  In such a case, the PTO timer will need to be re-armed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "29633441c13579d7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1193,
      "quote": "An endpoint in the closing state sends a packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in response to any incoming packet that it attributes to the connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7343ef20b4906640",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1222,
      "quote": "Once a client has received a valid Initial packet from the server, it MUST discard any subsequent packet it receives on that connection with a different Source Connection ID.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "916cc21b06edcf1b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1229,
      "quote": "Any further changes to the Destination Connection ID are only permitted if the values are taken from NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames; if subsequent Initial packets include a different Source Connection ID, they MUST be discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "de8867cef7b26f4f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1283,
      "quote": "A server MUST discard an Initial packet that is carried in a UDP datagram with a payload that is smaller than the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client may coalesce packets in a single datagram, which could be unintentionally split on path",
      "id": "089afbdf59e3f0c4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1288,
      "quote": "A server MAY also immediately close the connection by sending a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame with an error code of PROTOCOL_VIOLATION; see Section 10.2.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "39c9e42b4943f075",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1304,
      "quote": "Invalid packets that lack strong integrity protection, such as Initial, Retry, or Version Negotiation, MAY be discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "tracking_issue": "336",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "0977e2c2749798d3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1311,
      "quote": "This token MUST be repeated by the client in all Initial packets it sends for that connection after it receives the Retry packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "tracking_issue": "385",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "3225a655ed087d90",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1363,
      "quote": "The client MAY drop these packets, or it MAY buffer them in anticipation of later packets that allow it to compute the key.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.1",
      "tracking_issue": "337",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "806530a9c43476b6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1369,
      "quote": "Clients are not able to send Handshake packets prior to receiving a server response, so servers SHOULD ignore any such packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "tracking_issue": "340",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f89616d6c43513a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1376,
      "quote": "Except for Initial and Stateless Resets, an endpoint only accepts packets that include a Destination Connection ID field that matches a value the endpoint previously chose.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c038cebdbdc01b4c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1423,
      "quote": "a server MUST discard Initial keys when it first successfully processes a Handshake packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8cde0c84996160c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1433,
      "quote": "Once an endpoint has successfully processed a Handshake packet from the peer, it can consider the peer address to have been validated.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb0e5ebcd57e9903",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1468,
      "quote": "Endpoints in either role MUST NOT decrypt 1-RTT packets from their peer prior to completing the handshake.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c9839dfbc3a8995a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1472,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT process incoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is complete.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e4a2fe383a627047",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1477,
      "quote": "Even if it has 1-RTT secrets, a client MUST NOT process incoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is complete.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "490de747181773fa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1493,
      "quote": "Except for Initial and Stateless Resets, an endpoint only accepts packets that include a Destination Connection ID field that matches a value the endpoint previously chose.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Version negotiation handler",
      "id": "c00c8b528159cef2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1585,
      "quote": "A client that supports only this version of QUIC MUST abandon the current connection attempt if it receives a Version Negotiation packet, with the following two exceptions.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "tracking_issue": "349",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Version negotiation handler",
      "id": "eed21c5d5e4d9feb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1593,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard any Version Negotiation packet if it has received and successfully processed any other packet, including an earlier Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "tracking_issue": "349",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Version negotiation handler",
      "id": "2cbde06950629d56",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1602,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard a Version Negotiation packet that lists the QUIC version selected by the client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "tracking_issue": "349",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "9cf59dbb6be870c5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1609,
      "quote": "Except for Initial and Stateless Resets, an endpoint only accepts packets that include a Destination Connection ID field that matches a value the endpoint previously chose.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b0606190cc087654",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1648,
      "quote": "If the packet is a 0-RTT packet, the server MAY buffer a limited number of these packets in anticipation of a late-arriving Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "tracking_issue": "339",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "aaa2cfbf95a7ecd1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1685,
      "quote": "A client MUST accept and process at most one Retry packet for each connection attempt.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6556c83cefd81536",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1699,
      "quote": "After the client has received and processed an Initial or Retry packet from the server, it MUST discard any subsequent Retry packets that it receives.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7b29aadd5fd5e946",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1714,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard a Retry packet that contains a Source Connection ID field that is identical to the Destination Connection ID field of its Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "664e71049f747416",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1735,
      "quote": "Retry packets (see Section 17.2.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) carry a Retry Integrity Tag that provides two properties: it allows the discarding of packets that have accidentally been corrupted by the network, and only an entity that observes an Initial packet can send a valid Retry packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.8",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ebcc210d68a79953",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1759,
      "quote": "The client MUST use the value from the Source Connection ID field of the Retry packet in the Destination Connection ID field of subsequent packets that it sends.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ebbc4090f691ac03",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1764,
      "quote": "A client MUST change the Destination Connection ID it uses for sending packets in response to only the first received Initial or Retry packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aca79d8decdaae1f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1827,
      "quote": "While otherwise identical to the closing state, an endpoint in the draining state MUST NOT send any packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b66cd9f00fa6096",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "An endpoint also restarts its idle timer when sending an ack-eliciting packet if no other ack- eliciting packets have been sent since last receiving and processing a packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_timers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4f0219cfe199dff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 244,
      "quote": "If a client receives a packet that uses a different version than it initially selected, it MUST discard that packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_trait.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "70382cc8764cdd2f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 257,
      "quote": "Senders MUST NOT coalesce QUIC packets with different connection IDs into a single UDP datagram.  Receivers SHOULD ignore any subsequent packets with a different Destination Connection ID than the first packet in the datagram.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_trait.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dd8533a789ef98bf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 272,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD continue to respond to packets that can be processed during this time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_trait.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "790e3e2def69a985",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 332,
      "quote": "An endpoint that is closing is not required to process any received frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_trait.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "55335982bfc864aa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 344,
      "quote": "Due to packet reordering or loss, a client might receive packets for a connection that are encrypted with a key it has not yet computed. The client MAY drop these packets, or it MAY buffer them in anticipation of later packets that allow it to compute the key.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_trait.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e8e922821caf70bf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 352,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY skip this check if any packet from a datagram is successfully processed.  However, the comparison MUST be performed when the first packet in an incoming datagram either cannot be associated with a connection, or cannot be decrypted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_trait.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "94151aa34ed286a2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 407,
      "quote": "Every QUIC packet that is coalesced into a single UDP datagram is separate and complete.  The receiver of coalesced QUIC packets MUST individually process each QUIC packet and separately acknowledge them, as if they were received as the payload of different UDP datagrams.  For example, if decryption fails (because the keys are not available or for any other reason), the receiver MAY either discard or buffer the packet for later processing and MUST attempt to process the remaining packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/connection_trait.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "07085cfa119ac10d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "As a trivial example, this means the same connection ID MUST NOT be issued more than once on the same connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "cd7939cd7111da92",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "The sequence number on each newly issued connection ID MUST increase by 1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8e623f9de67c5d59",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 275,
      "quote": "Receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame containing a sequence number greater than any previously sent to the peer MUST be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d697ecea7f56dff0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 292,
      "quote": "The sequence number specified in a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST NOT refer to the Destination Connection ID field of the packet in which the frame is contained.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7cc0082cc88df396",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 298,
      "quote": "The peer MAY treat this as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "82ecef3831ac2a2b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 321,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD supply a new connection ID when the peer retires a connection ID.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d9bd3405663ee929",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 330,
      "quote": "When an endpoint issues a connection ID, it MUST accept packets that carry this connection ID for the duration of the connection or until its peer invalidates the connection ID via a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame (Section 19.16).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ecf3e465f6417e06",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 337,
      "quote": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to accept the previously issued connection IDs until they are retired by the peer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "6fe0222326c3960c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 388,
      "quote": "An endpoint that initiates migration and requires non-zero-length connection IDs SHOULD ensure that the pool of connection IDs available to its peer allows the peer to use a new connection ID on migration, as the peer will be unable to respond if the pool is exhausted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "dbe5be269ef8738d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 396,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD ensure that its peer has a sufficient number of available and unused connection IDs.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "fe18182bc8e123a6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 401,
      "quote": "To ensure that migration is possible and packets sent on different paths cannot be correlated, endpoints SHOULD provide new connection IDs before peers migrate; see Section 5.1.1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "dbba1a6a97af78dc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 450,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT provide more connection IDs than the peer's limit.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c24fe07bcc4978ae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 478,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send connection IDs that temporarily exceed a peer's limit if the NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame also requires the retirement of any excess, by including a sufficiently large value in the Retire Prior To field.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "6d52f6c28b4d9ed3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 516,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY also limit the issuance of connection IDs to reduce the amount of per-path state it maintains, such as path validation status, as its peer might interact with it over as many paths as there are issued connection IDs.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2ef6ac9b313c645b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "An endpoint that initiates migration and requires non-zero-length connection IDs SHOULD ensure that the pool of connection IDs available to its peer allows the peer to use a new connection ID on migration, as the peer will be unable to respond if the pool is exhausted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aeff65c18a218201",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "Each Connection ID has an associated sequence number to assist in detecting when NEW_CONNECTION_ID or RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames refer to the same value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "84d338000469cc68",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 306,
      "quote": "The sequence number of the initial connection ID is 0.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "12a867b1d94a0d36",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 322,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY also limit the issuance of connection IDs to reduce the amount of per-path state it maintains, such as path validation status, as its peer might interact with it over as many paths as there are issued connection IDs.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1a9c49243cf4d64d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 343,
      "quote": "As a trivial example, this means the same connection ID MUST NOT be issued more than once on the same connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0897e9f8327c0fcc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 373,
      "quote": "The sequence number on each newly issued connection ID MUST increase by 1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2316958eebeca8fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 420,
      "quote": "When an endpoint issues a connection ID, it MUST accept packets that carry this connection ID for the duration of the connection or until its peer invalidates the connection ID via a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame (Section 19.16).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b7b53591e3f97fe9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 426,
      "quote": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to accept the previously issued connection IDs until they are retired by the peer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a95a74f12dc1b290",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 438,
      "quote": "Receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame containing a sequence number greater than any previously sent to the peer MUST be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f753bac8e2fbb454",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 456,
      "quote": "The sequence number specified in a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST NOT refer to the Destination Connection ID field of the packet in which the frame is contained.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4973d38de9e9c4a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 461,
      "quote": "The peer MAY treat this as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/local_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb6e5238aeda2dba",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 490,
