    },
    {
      "id": "4aafd39bc8fccf57",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 496,
      "quote": "After processing a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame and adding and retiring active connection IDs, if the number of active connection IDs exceeds the value advertised in its active_connection_id_limit transport parameter, an endpoint MUST close the connection with an error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8061f11d34d8a0c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 509,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT forget a connection ID without retiring it, though it MAY choose to treat having connection IDs in need of retirement that exceed this limit as a connection error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bb73aac7171f8307",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "This is an integer value specifying the maximum number of connection IDs from the peer that an endpoint is willing to store.  This value includes the connection ID received during the handshake, that received in the preferred_address transport parameter, and those received in NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames.  The value of the active_connection_id_limit parameter MUST be at least 2.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5c6e768543175d5c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD allow for sending and tracking a number of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames of at least twice the value of the active_connection_id_limit transport parameter.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4b906cea5178a09",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "Each Connection ID has an associated sequence number to assist in detecting when NEW_CONNECTION_ID or RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames refer to the same value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9cde603b10ec5dab",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "A 128-bit value that will be used for a stateless reset when the associated connection ID is used.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a7964905f1372b94",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame that repeats a previously issued connection ID with a different Stateless Reset Token field value or a different Sequence Number field value, or if a sequence number is used for different connection IDs, the endpoint MAY treat that receipt as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
