      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d92961ee53f39fc0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 390,
      "quote": "Receipt of the same frame multiple times MUST NOT be treated as a connection error.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0dfb890a1a0afec1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 401,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame with a sequence number smaller than the Retire Prior To field of a previously received NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST send a corresponding RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame that retires the newly received connection ID, unless it has already done so for that sequence number.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "248728abd3ae3fd7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 490,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT check for any stateless reset tokens associated with connection IDs it has not used or for connection IDs that have been retired.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2a9dcc05e15d9d1a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 499,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT forget a connection ID without retiring it",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a16fe2ddf32e7eaa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 547,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT check for any stateless reset tokens associated with connection IDs it has not used or for connection IDs that have been retired.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "00c902e8cb986195",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 607,
      "quote": "After processing a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame and adding and retiring active connection IDs, if the number of active connection IDs exceeds the value advertised in its active_connection_id_limit transport parameter, an endpoint MUST close the connection with an error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4846a13fe993a830",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 633,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD limit the number of connection IDs it has retired locally for which RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames have not yet been acknowledged.  An endpoint SHOULD allow for sending and tracking a number of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames of at least twice the value of the active_connection_id_limit transport parameter.  An endpoint MUST NOT forget a connection ID without retiring it, though it MAY choose to treat having connection IDs in need of retirement that exceed this limit as a connection error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/peer_id_registry.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "61dc3581ae6950c6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a packet if it would cause bytes_in_flight (see Appendix B.2) to be larger than the congestion window, unless the packet is sent on a PTO timer expiration (see Section 6.2) or when entering recovery (see Section 7.3.2).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "741ded0fe9dcca22",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "When a PTO timer expires, a sender MUST send at least one ack- eliciting packet in the packet number space as a probe.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6517fc9046ac8de",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD include new data in packets that are sent on PTO expiration.  Previously sent data MAY be sent if no new data can be sent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fc84900fa484f2c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 134,
      "quote": "Probe packets MUST NOT be blocked by the congestion controller.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba8283bee7a8ed18",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 156,
      "quote": "In addition to sending data in the packet number space for which the timer expired, the sender SHOULD send ack-eliciting packets from other packet number spaces with in-flight data, coalescing packets if possible.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e739fb20de3e6577",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 162,
      "quote": "A client MUST expand the payload of all UDP datagrams carrying Initial packets to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes by adding PADDING frames to the Initial packet or by coalescing the Initial packet; see Section 12.2.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "70ab4a9822ece151",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "Similarly, a server MUST expand the payload of all UDP datagrams carrying ack- eliciting Initial packets to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0b3f8278c55d0240",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 193,
      "quote": "These packets MAY also include PADDING frames.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3e971c797bc251ea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 199,
      "quote": "When packets of different types need to be sent, endpoints SHOULD use coalesced packets to send them in the same UDP datagram.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae6830965af01f60",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 226,
      "quote": "Similarly, a server MUST expand the payload of all UDP datagrams carrying ack- eliciting Initial packets to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7b80423a10d3d896",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 296,
      "quote": "a client MUST discard Initial keys when it first sends a Handshake packet",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8f9fccd266b916c5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 307,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST discard its handshake keys when the TLS handshake is confirmed (Section 4.1.2).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fbb16ce258921092",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 317,
      "quote": "Though an endpoint might retain older keys, new data MUST be sent at the highest currently-available encryption level.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba021aaa35b3b94c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 334,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST expand datagrams that contain a PATH_CHALLENGE frame to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "800939e821c69448",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 338,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST expand datagrams that contain a PATH_RESPONSE frame to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/connection/transmission.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "825e6e6afb4d4e7d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "A client MUST expand the payload of all UDP datagrams carrying Initial packets to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0bf3f367d952f584",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "A server MUST discard an Initial packet that is carried in a UDP datagram with a payload that is smaller than the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "43093a82e36c1559",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "First, the packet containing a ClientHello MUST be padded to a minimum size.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5210a302a4e0cbfb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "When an Initial packet is sent by a client that has not previously received an Initial or Retry packet from the server, the client populates the Destination Connection ID field with an unpredictable value.  This Destination Connection ID MUST be at least 8 bytes in length.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "db442ee8bfbf7636",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9359508c7528f8d8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 104,
      "quote": "Changing the Destination Connection ID field also results in a change to the keys used to protect the Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8093560131a1fa04",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 175,
      "quote": "A server includes the Destination Connection ID field from the first Initial packet it received from the client in the original_destination_connection_id transport parameter; if the server sent a Retry packet, this refers to the first Initial packet received before sending the Retry packet.  If it sends a Retry packet, a server also includes the Source Connection ID field from the Retry packet in the retry_source_connection_id transport parameter.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e393a09e3b498b10",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 197,
      "quote": "Each endpoint includes the value of the Source Connection ID field from the first Initial packet it sent in the initial_source_connection_id transport parameter",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "349a88a6b74d7ef7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 208,
      "quote": "active_connection_id_limit (0x0e):  This is an integer value specifying the maximum number of connection IDs from the peer that an endpoint is willing to store.  This value includes the connection ID received during the handshake, that received in the preferred_address transport parameter, and those received in NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5875646c7325a607",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 301,
      "quote": "A server MUST set the Destination Connection ID it uses for sending packets based on the first received Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1c4563fafea83efb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 409,
      "quote": "If the ClientHello spans multiple Initial packets, such servers would need to buffer the first received fragments, which could consume excessive resources if the client's address has not yet been validated.  To avoid this, servers MAY use the Retry feature (see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) to only buffer partial ClientHello messages from clients with a validated address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "tracking_issue": "299",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "80c3c18db520d059",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 358,
      "quote": "A server can also use a Retry packet to defer the state and processing costs of connection establishment.  Requiring the server to provide a different connection ID, along with the original_destination_connection_id transport parameter defined in Section 18.2, forces the server to demonstrate that it, or an entity it cooperates with, received the original Initial packet from the client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "01e0460e0be9271b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 385,
      "quote": "If a server refuses to accept a new connection, it SHOULD send an Initial packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame with error code CONNECTION_REFUSED.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "tracking_issue": "270",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "eec53c089fc4f709",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 462,
      "quote": "Servers MUST drop incoming packets under all other circumstances.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "df7bdc553d627866",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 465,
      "quote": "However, endpoints MUST treat any packet ending in a valid stateless reset token as a Stateless Reset, as other QUIC versions might allow the use of a long header.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "86f7ef2a7404d8a9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 596,
      "quote": "An endpoint that is closing is not required to process any received frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "17209f6810911223",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 622,
      "quote": "An endpoint that is closing is not required to process any received frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f358ba6cbd26a532",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 663,
      "quote": "Additionally, an endpoint MAY consider the peer address validated if the peer uses a connection ID chosen by the endpoint and the connection ID contains at least 64 bits of entropy",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "tracking_issue": "140",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a6d6dd469eb11f6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 670,
      "quote": "In response to processing an Initial packet containing a token that was provided in a Retry packet, a server cannot send another Retry packet; it can only refuse the connection or permit it to proceed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "797eed39bbbc5f71",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 686,
      "quote": "If the token is invalid, then the server SHOULD proceed as if the client did not have a validated address, including potentially sending a Retry packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "tracking_issue": "344",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "f65434525636c2d3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 693,
      "quote": "Instead, the server SHOULD immediately close (Section 10.2) the connection with an INVALID_TOKEN error.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "tracking_issue": "344",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "489475a9aa3acc0c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 706,
      "quote": "Servers MAY discard any Initial packet that does not carry the expected token.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fd44dc126964f41f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 712,
      "quote": "If the validation succeeds, the server SHOULD then allow the handshake to proceed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "be5cf89eb19c4a0e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 717,
      "quote": "Upon receiving the client's Initial packet, the server can request address validation by sending a Retry packet (Section 17.2.5) containing a token.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ee1085a6d69698ad",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 725,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT send more than one Retry packet in response to a single UDP datagram.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dbfe9cfc7a4aaa8a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 775,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY skip this check if any packet from a datagram is successfully processed.  However, the comparison MUST be performed when the first packet in an incoming datagram either cannot be associated with a connection, or cannot be decrypted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5608ad47e17282db",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 781,
      "quote": "However, endpoints MUST treat any packet ending in a valid stateless reset token as a Stateless Reset, as other QUIC versions might allow the use of a long header.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa1cfb9c3142fa83",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 789,
      "quote": "For instance, an endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to any further incoming packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "17956cca0be67f22",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 793,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to receiving a packet that it cannot associate with an active connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6c6a07cff1181e36",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 797,
      "quote": "Because the stateless reset token is not available until connection establishment is complete or near completion, ignoring an unknown packet with a long header might be as effective as sending a Stateless Reset.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "78272bbc0b78862f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 851,
      "quote": "The endpoint identifies a received datagram as a Stateless Reset by comparing the last 16 bytes of the datagram with all stateless reset tokens associated with the remote address on which the datagram was received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4f51437d5e969329",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 880,
      "quote": "If the last 16 bytes of the datagram are identical in value to a stateless reset token, the endpoint MUST enter the draining period and not send any further packets on this connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "294439d25310309d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1049,
      "quote": "When an Initial packet is sent by a client that has not previously received an Initial or Retry packet from the server, the client populates the Destination Connection ID field with an unpredictable value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6e6ef780f6b3c0c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1062,
      "quote": "Note that clients cannot use the stateless_reset_token transport parameter because their transport parameters do not have confidentiality protection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7a2445ba52a1de29",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1074,
      "quote": "This version of the specification is identified by the number 0x00000001.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-15",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb6511423fb856f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1158,
      "quote": "The Destination Connection ID field from the first Initial packet sent by a client is used to determine packet protection keys for Initial packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "87c8d3757465fa79",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a client initial with a supported version, the server logs this event with server_versions and chosen_version set",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-marx-qlog-event-definitions-quic-h3-02",
      "target_section": "5.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7527c98fa608d63",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a client initial with an unsupported version, the server logs this event with server_versions set and client_versions to the single-element array containing the client's attempted version.  The absence of chosen_version implies no overlap was found.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://tools.ietf.org/id/draft-marx-qlog-event-definitions-quic-h3-02",
      "target_section": "5.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9ded591be206ec6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "a server that is able to recognize packets as 0-RTT might choose not to send Version Negotiation packets in response to 0-RTT packets with the expectation that it will eventually receive an Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4490087acf47658b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a Version Negotiation packet in response to receiving a Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1ba21cce65a48a70",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 122,
      "quote": "If a server receives a packet that indicates an unsupported version and if the packet is large enough to initiate a new connection for any supported version, the server SHOULD send a Version Negotiation packet as described in Section 6.1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1ca3810aedb9e16",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "A server might not send a Version Negotiation packet if the datagram it receives is smaller than the minimum size specified in a different version;",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fbe2a83cbcc02fba",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "Servers MUST drop smaller packets that specify unsupported versions.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "133b67e545fd98e0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "A server MAY limit the number of packets to which it responds with a Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4035eae20cc53e5c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "A server MAY limit the number of Version Negotiation packets it sends.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "33b84784416b56b3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD respond with a Version Negotiation packet, provided that the datagram is sufficiently long.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0cb7b3b01d70dc6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 285,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY add reserved versions to any field where unknown or unsupported versions are ignored to test that a peer correctly ignores the value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bdbb260175b6c284",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 290,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY send packets with a reserved version to test that a peer correctly discards the packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "49020306a16820c8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 294,
      "quote": "For a server to use a new version in the future, clients need to correctly handle unsupported versions.  Some version numbers (0x?a?a?a?a as defined in Section 15) are reserved for inclusion in fields that contain version numbers.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/endpoint/version.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "33f6cf477122cae7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD NOT probe a new path with packets containing a PATH_CHALLENGE frame more frequently than it would send an Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/challenge.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a355fa946706a455",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send multiple PATH_CHALLENGE frames to guard against packet loss.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/challenge.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b9c2641b4e603aee",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "However, an endpoint SHOULD NOT send multiple PATH_CHALLENGE frames in a single packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/challenge.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7e42fa7a8de2da0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 217,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send multiple PATH_CHALLENGE frames to guard against packet loss.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/challenge.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a479346f412d9bed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 234,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD NOT probe a new path with packets containing a PATH_CHALLENGE frame more frequently than it would send an Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/challenge.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "26d9fc3e4651bba4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 257,
      "quote": "However, an endpoint SHOULD NOT send multiple PATH_CHALLENGE frames in a single packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/challenge.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c269842555830298",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "To protect the connection from failing due to such a spurious migration, an endpoint MUST revert to using the last validated peer address when validation of a new peer address fails.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7a4d45df60d14941",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 348,
      "quote": "This requirement MUST NOT be enforced by the endpoint that initiates path validation, as that would enable an attack on migration; see Section 9.3.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bdbd5356dd349972",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 354,
      "quote": "A PATH_RESPONSE frame received on any network path validates the path on which the PATH_CHALLENGE was sent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8e7e077eca149af0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 411,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD abandon path validation based on a timer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7b16f873602062fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 441,
      "quote": "If the recipient permits the migration, it MUST send subsequent packets to the new peer address and MUST initiate path validation (Section 8.2) to verify the peer's ownership of the address if validation is not already underway.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fef7f9afda65e6c7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 478,
      "quote": "When an endpoint has no validated path on which to send packets, it MAY discard connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "fe46ae0c22ac8c51",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 483,
      "quote": "If an endpoint has no state about the last validated peer address, it MUST close the connection silently by discarding all connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "74d55e94ddfe1077",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 489,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY discard connection state if it does not have a validated path on which it can send packets; see Section 8.2",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "20a99187c357b639",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 546,
      "quote": "After changing the address to which it sends non-probing packets, an endpoint can abandon any path validation for other addresses.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0f80c183ec9b9cb5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 634,
      "quote": "An endpoint can migrate a connection to a new local address by sending packets containing non-probing frames from that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a02c18f4b0766d0e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 664,
      "quote": "An endpoint can migrate a connection to a new local address by sending packets containing non-probing frames from that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1dd82a4107182a34",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 820,
      "quote": "If a client receives packets from an unknown server address, the client MUST discard these packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7bb26e93271f022d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 883,
      "quote": "Until a packet is received from the server, the client MUST use the same Destination Connection ID value on all packets in this connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "6c0afdbaf06bf079",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1152,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST perform path validation (Section 8.2) if it detects any change to a peer's address, unless it has previously validated that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "225f1c04d74312ea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1159,
      "quote": "The endpoint MUST use unpredictable data in every PATH_CHALLENGE frame so that it can associate the peer's response with the corresponding PATH_CHALLENGE.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "83bdbc7a678eab51",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1170,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST perform path validation (Section 8.2) if it detects any change to a peer's address, unless it has previously validated that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4110ca08436066e7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1356,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD abandon path validation based on a timer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d8e8ef19040b5380",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1360,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD abandon path validation based on a timer.  When setting this timer, implementations are cautioned that the new path could have a longer round-trip time than the original.  A value of three times the larger of the current PTO or the PTO for the new path (using kInitialRtt, as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY]) is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "853259a0df8cb519",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1390,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of an increased Retire Prior To field, the peer MUST stop using the corresponding connection IDs and retire them with RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames before adding the newly provided connection ID to the set of active connection IDs.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c6bebe1a51cfbdf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "In response to an apparent migration, endpoints MUST validate the previously active path using a PATH_CHALLENGE frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "70c25af876aad01e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY skip validation of a peer address if that address has been seen recently.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "tracking_issue": "714",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "7158d4cbd3a99ba5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 258,
      "quote": "Once a client has received a valid Initial packet from the server, it MUST discard any subsequent packet it receives on that connection with a different Source Connection ID.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7a928f1da652bce3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 263,
      "quote": "Any further changes to the Destination Connection ID are only permitted if the values are taken from NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames; if subsequent Initial packets include a different Source Connection ID, they MUST be discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "69fc84a005e41196",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 279,
      "quote": "If a client receives packets from an unknown server address, the client MUST discard these packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cffa5d5c47ea29d4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 286,
      "quote": "The design of QUIC relies on endpoints retaining a stable address for the duration of the handshake.  An endpoint MUST NOT initiate connection migration before the handshake is confirmed, as defined in section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8dbb4ff6931e38e8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 295,
      "quote": "If the peer violates this requirement, the endpoint MUST either drop the incoming packets on that path without generating a Stateless Reset or proceed with path validation and allow the peer to migrate.  Generating a Stateless Reset or closing the connection would allow third parties in the network to cause connections to close by spoofing or otherwise manipulating observed traffic.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1661f08a9f08403c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 325,
      "quote": "Clients are responsible for initiating all migrations.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d9e2a83045fc13e8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 398,
      "quote": "Because port-only changes are commonly the result of NAT rebinding or other middlebox activity, the endpoint MAY instead retain its congestion control state and round-trip estimate in those cases instead of reverting to initial values.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "1e7f321b68583075",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 405,
      "quote": "On confirming a peer's ownership of its new address, an endpoint MUST immediately reset the congestion controller and round-trip time estimator for the new path to initial values (see Appendices A.3 and B.3 of [QUIC-RECOVERY]) unless the only change in the peer's address is its port number.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "541334e7451fe1c4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 431,
      "quote": "Similarly, an endpoint MUST NOT reuse a connection ID when sending to more than one destination address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7454ee80e6875e8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 440,
      "quote": "Due to network changes outside the control of its peer, an endpoint might receive packets from a new source address with the same Destination Connection ID field value, in which case it MAY continue to use the current connection ID with the new remote address while still sending from the same local address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "20ded7a6f621cb66",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 451,
      "quote": "Until a peer's address is deemed valid, an endpoint limits the amount of data it sends to that address; see Section 8.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e557d4386f5dbc92",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 455,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send data to an unvalidated peer address, but it MUST protect against potential attacks as described in Sections 9.3.1 and 9.3.2.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef4aa6a485c5190a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 499,
      "quote": "The endpoint MUST use unpredictable data in every PATH_CHALLENGE frame so that it can associate the peer's response with the corresponding PATH_CHALLENGE.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8df9bb9b92b415fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 506,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD abandon path validation based on a timer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "13cb65a0584d8f1c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 509,
      "quote": "When setting this timer, implementations are cautioned that the new path could have a longer round-trip time than the original.  A value of three times the larger of the current PTO or the PTO for the new path (using kInitialRtt, as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY]) is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "81a1561553c3f33a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 521,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST perform path validation (Section 8.2) if it detects any change to a peer's address, unless it has previously validated that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8af166bda7f04855",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 526,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD initiate path validation to the client's new address upon receiving a probe packet from a different address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "681a82b174950300",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 578,
      "quote": "Path validation succeeds when a PATH_RESPONSE frame is received that contains the data that was sent in a previous PATH_CHALLENGE frame. A PATH_RESPONSE frame received on any network path validates the path on which the PATH_CHALLENGE was sent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0cec248892911ce4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 589,
      "quote": "A PATH_RESPONSE frame MUST be sent on the network path where the PATH_CHALLENGE frame was received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d874e0dfaa3c1bb5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 593,
      "quote": "This requirement MUST NOT be enforced by the endpoint that initiates path validation, as that would enable an attack on migration; see Section 9.3.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1276303e20382f41",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 603,
      "quote": "A PATH_RESPONSE frame received on any network path validates the path on which the PATH_CHALLENGE was sent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "43815835494d3ffb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 649,
      "quote": "A client MUST change the Destination Connection ID it uses for sending packets in response to only the first received Initial or Retry packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0453b999e03c45c5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 654,
      "quote": "Until a packet is received from the server, the client MUST use the same Destination Connection ID value on all packets in this connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5b82ed9e3cf7e9a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 679,
      "quote": "An endpoint can migrate a connection to a new local address by sending packets containing non-probing frames from that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf9d84362af9c7bb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 685,
      "quote": "After changing the address to which it sends non-probing packets, an endpoint can abandon any path validation for other addresses.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "24422ceb78370171",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 694,
      "quote": "If the recipient permits the migration, it MUST send subsequent packets to the new peer address and MUST initiate path validation (Section 8.2) to verify the peer's ownership of the address if validation is not already underway.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b86f685de7a79c46",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 716,
      "quote": "Tokens are invalidated when their associated connection ID is retired via a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame (Section 19.16).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4080e5954ce4d91e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 741,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of an increased Retire Prior To field, the peer MUST stop using the corresponding connection IDs and retire them with RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames before adding the newly provided connection ID to the set of active connection IDs.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "00124cef4d057cbe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 785,
      "quote": "To protect the connection from failing due to such a spurious migration, an endpoint MUST revert to using the last validated peer address when validation of a new peer address fails.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cbfbff5f672b1cae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 796,
      "quote": "When an endpoint has no validated path on which to send packets, it MAY discard connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "985e97380e714018",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 800,
      "quote": "An endpoint capable of connection migration MAY wait for a new path to become available before discarding connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "tracking_issue": "713",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "c102c5835f4f45d7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 807,
      "quote": "If an endpoint has no state about the last validated peer address, it MUST close the connection silently by discarding all connection state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cd4d9e8b02eaebdd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 812,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY discard connection state if it does not have a validated path on which it can send packets; see Section 8.2",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "84d64ae8937ea9cd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "If the client IP address has changed, the server MUST adhere to the anti-amplification limit; see Section 8.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "36471cf7b4e35a75",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "Clients are only constrained by the congestion controller.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e12d371ed8e7c309",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 208,
      "quote": "For the purposes of avoiding amplification prior to address validation, servers MUST count all of the payload bytes received in datagrams that are uniquely attributed to a single connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "455cc33b7752c76a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 214,
      "quote": "Prior to validating the client address, servers MUST NOT send more than three times as many bytes as the number of bytes they have received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fa0ce56b79306eea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 265,
      "quote": "A PATH_RESPONSE frame MUST be sent on the network path where the PATH_CHALLENGE frame was received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "92bf244cd5e03f23",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 273,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send more than one PATH_RESPONSE frame in response to one PATH_CHALLENGE frame; see Section 13.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3777d0f6ebe999c8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 304,
      "quote": "On receiving a PATH_CHALLENGE frame, an endpoint MUST respond by echoing the data contained in the PATH_CHALLENGE frame in a PATH_RESPONSE frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "af63b9b1618ff18e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 320,
      "quote": "After verifying a new client address, the server SHOULD send new address validation tokens (Section 8) to the client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "c60c84a98715819c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 432,
      "quote": "The server MUST also limit the number of bytes it sends before validating the address of the client; see Section 8.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf3daddda5799920",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 436,
      "quote": "All QUIC packets that are not sent in a PMTU probe SHOULD be sized to fit within the maximum datagram size to avoid the datagram being fragmented or dropped [RFC8085].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d694f76bdb18ba96",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 442,
      "quote": "A PL MUST NOT send a datagram (other than a probe packet) with a size at the PL that is larger than the current PLPMTU.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1477ffdeb88b13d4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 469,
      "quote": "Prior to validating the client address, servers MUST NOT send more than three times as many bytes as the number of bytes they have received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0aadc8a133af1132",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 476,
      "quote": "If the congestion window is reduced immediately, a single packet can be sent prior to reduction.  This speeds up loss recovery if the data in the lost packet is retransmitted and is similar to TCP as described in Section 5 of [RFC6675].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa4c13ec7b14a05e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 483,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a packet if it would cause bytes_in_flight (see Appendix B.2) to be larger than the congestion window, unless the packet is sent on a PTO timer expiration (see Section 6.2) or when entering recovery (see Section 7.3.2).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "341905c3b7567338",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 502,
      "quote": "Prior to validating the client address, servers MUST NOT send more than three times as many bytes as the number of bytes they have received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9ce99b8d640ebd83",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 578,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT delay transmission of a packet containing a PATH_RESPONSE frame unless constrained by congestion control.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "07965663aea5bebd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 701,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send more than one PATH_RESPONSE frame in response to one PATH_CHALLENGE frame; see Section 13.3.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b9b0f7225ae8f086",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 849,
      "quote": "On receiving a PATH_CHALLENGE frame, an endpoint MUST respond by echoing the data contained in the PATH_CHALLENGE frame in a PATH_RESPONSE frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
