    },
    {
      "id": "db45e6c9228908ef",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1019,
      "quote": "A PL MUST NOT send a datagram (other than a probe packet) with a size at the PL that is larger than the current PLPMTU.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/path/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "17f5cad1156001bd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "When no previous RTT is available, the initial RTT SHOULD be set to 333 milliseconds.  This results in handshakes starting with a PTO of 1 second, as recommended for TCP's initial RTO; see Section 2 of [RFC6298].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "50be5a04ecc6c37c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7ffe428365623743",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0ac7f0a3f344961f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 256,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "32f851e8865a9486",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 301,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "351ce80820e67067",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 308,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.7",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "11166da2d2bfe684",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 390,
      "quote": "An RTT sample MUST NOT be generated on receiving an ACK frame that does not newly acknowledge at least one ack-eliciting packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "922584cf16c40dd9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1196,
      "quote": "Validating ECN counts from reordered ACK frames can result in failure. An endpoint MUST NOT fail ECN validation as a result of processing an ACK frame that does not increase the largest acknowledged packet number.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d561c2a6971145fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1286,
      "quote": "To avoid generating multiple RTT samples for a single packet, an ACK frame SHOULD NOT be used to update RTT estimates if it does not newly acknowledge the largest acknowledged packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "18f001264a42af56",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1380,
      "quote": "Packets sent on the old path MUST NOT contribute to congestion control or RTT estimation for the new path.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "91d8eaa3376eeb72",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1588,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.10",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "43001241a1e625f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1693,
      "quote": "Once a later packet within the same packet number space has been acknowledged, an endpoint SHOULD declare an earlier packet lost if it was sent a threshold amount of time in the past.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "2082ecfda240a082",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1724,
      "quote": "If packets sent prior to the largest acknowledged packet cannot yet be declared lost, then a timer SHOULD be set for the remaining time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d45397aced5a93c7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2058,
      "quote": "Loss of a QUIC packet that is carried in a PMTU probe is therefore not a reliable indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction; see Item 7 in Section 3 of [DPLPMTUD].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "c81990c71b7ae9e5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2064,
      "quote": "Loss of a probe packet SHOULD NOT be treated as an indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction [RFC4821] because this could result in unnecessary reduction of the sending rate.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "67e35b18116074f2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2192,
      "quote": "A sender that does not have state for all packet number spaces or an implementation that cannot compare send times across packet number spaces MAY use state for just the packet number space that was acknowledged.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "7da947407a7d1da6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2310,
      "quote": "Packets 2 through 8 are declared lost when the acknowledgment for packet 9 is received at \"t = 12.2\".",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4bb13ff9bd12dab",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2315,
      "quote": "The congestion period is calculated as the time between the oldest and newest lost packets: \"8 - 1 = 7\".",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7ce5d2f26e71341e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2354,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD set the min_rtt to the newest RTT sample after persistent congestion is established.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "395ace7bd1bef4c3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2368,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "75477eae2a666ae2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2501,
      "quote": "The persistent congestion period SHOULD NOT start until there is at least one RTT sample.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a46172fe6a1c7a7e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2578,
      "quote": "These two packets MUST be ack-eliciting, since a receiver is required to acknowledge only ack-eliciting packets within its maximum acknowledgment delay; see Section 13.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "813a74249548647e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2666,
      "quote": "Loss of a QUIC packet that is carried in a PMTU probe is therefore not a reliable indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction; see Item 7 in Section 3 of [DPLPMTUD].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "05a59fe13e24dd70",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2752,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "b7d4d021df1dad35",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2788,
      "quote": "If no additional data can be sent, the server's PTO timer MUST NOT be armed until datagrams have been received from the client, because packets sent on PTO count against the anti-amplification limit.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "36a04f484d1d2b61",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2832,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data packet number space until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4d218ad71c593273",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2878,
      "quote": "When an ack-eliciting packet is transmitted, the sender schedules a timer for the PTO period as follows: PTO = smoothed_rtt + max(4*rttvar, kGranularity) + max_ack_delay",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c89e671c8f6045ce",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2893,
      "quote": "That is, the client MUST set the PTO timer if the client has not received an acknowledgment for any of its Handshake packets and the handshake is not confirmed (see Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), even if there are no packets in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e4b0cd8fe7ad3df2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2927,
      "quote": "The PTO period MUST be at least kGranularity, to avoid the timer expiring immediately.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bd367de6306830d0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2965,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "910fc4ea30db54d7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 2988,
      "quote": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold loss detection; see Section 6.1.2.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "156e9ee025f41d35",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3017,
      "quote": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold loss detection; see Section 6.1.2.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "27c80f23a520b367",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3046,
      "quote": "When a PTO timer expires, the PTO backoff MUST be increased, resulting in the PTO period being set to twice its current value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ac15b86678539649",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3071,
      "quote": "When a PTO timer expires, a sender MUST send at least one ack- eliciting packet in the packet number space as a probe.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "653b3e8a33f0e3c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3076,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send up to two full-sized datagrams containing ack-eliciting packets to avoid an expensive consecutive PTO expiration due to a single lost datagram or to transmit data from multiple packet number spaces.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "619f4e4b5888fc3c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3085,
      "quote": "A PTO timer expiration event does not indicate packet loss and MUST NOT cause prior unacknowledged packets to be marked as lost.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "4e741b0bce1bf664",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3342,
      "quote": "A sender MUST however count these packets as being additionally in flight, since these packets add network load without establishing packet loss.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8c65e31fd2d6f493",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "The largest packet number acknowledged in the packet number space so far.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ffcbb43b23f5825f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "An association of packet numbers in a packet number space to information about them.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf411599b8e09400",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "A Probe Timeout (PTO) triggers the sending of one or two probe datagrams when ack-eliciting packets are not acknowledged within the expected period of time or the server may not have validated the client's address.  A PTO enables a connection to recover from loss of tail packets or acknowledgments.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "86afd2b98717ed11",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "The time the most recent ack-eliciting packet was sent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1266287e0b2528e4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 187,
      "quote": "A PTO timer expiration event does not indicate packet loss and MUST NOT cause prior unacknowledged packets to be marked as lost.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f281291316da23ed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 191,
      "quote": "When a PTO timer expires, the PTO backoff MUST be increased, resulting in the PTO period being set to twice its current value.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "86f89011c2900bd5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 212,
      "quote": "After a packet is sent, information about the packet is stored.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7f637543b076917",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 225,
      "quote": "Similar to TCP, packets containing only ACK frames do not count towards bytes in flight and are not congestion controlled.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7ef3df077344ba7d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 230,
      "quote": "A sender MUST however count these packets as being additionally in flight, since these packets add network load without establishing packet loss.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b965610601ca5c57",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 269,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent or acknowledged,",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6fa1e580d96cff4c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 305,
      "quote": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold loss detection; see Section 6.1.2.  A timer that is set for time threshold loss detection will expire earlier than the PTO timer in most cases and is less likely to spuriously retransmit data.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6f23233b2035ddaa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 314,
      "quote": "If no additional data can be sent, the server's PTO timer MUST NOT be armed until datagrams have been received from the client, because packets sent on PTO count against the anti-amplification limit.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5c8b70b076afa1db",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 324,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data packet number space until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cab1c729d210e177",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 337,
      "quote": "it is the client's responsibility to send packets to unblock the server until it is certain that the server has finished its address validation",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "24fb183b0139ee65",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 353,
      "quote": "That is, the client MUST set the PTO timer if the client has not received an acknowledgment for any of its Handshake packets and the handshake is not confirmed (see Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), even if there are no packets in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "06be693fbf3aa30c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 446,
      "quote": "An endpoint generates an RTT sample on receiving an ACK frame that meets the following two conditions: *  the largest acknowledged packet number is newly acknowledged, and *  at least one of the newly acknowledged packets was ack-eliciting.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4b5faa5381e3d05",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 579,
      "quote": "Packets sent on the old path MUST NOT contribute to congestion control or RTT estimation for the new path.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0e771eb4dbe72cf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 584,
      "quote": "To avoid generating multiple RTT samples for a single packet, an ACK frame SHOULD NOT be used to update RTT estimates if it does not newly acknowledge the largest acknowledged packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bec31b36bba0fe18",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 590,
      "quote": "An RTT sample MUST NOT be generated on receiving an ACK frame that does not newly acknowledge at least one ack-eliciting packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "70405a31ed5d8975",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 634,
      "quote": "Once a later packet within the same packet number space has been acknowledged, an endpoint SHOULD declare an earlier packet lost if it was sent a threshold amount of time in the past.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "88d051a46b631aaa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 673,
      "quote": "The PTO backoff factor is reset when an acknowledgment is received, except in the following case.  A server might take longer to respond to packets during the handshake than otherwise.  To protect such a server from repeated client probes, the PTO backoff is not reset at a client that is not yet certain that the server has finished validating the client's address.  That is, a client does not reset the PTO backoff factor on receiving acknowledgments in Initial packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3cfc936925268a57",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 687,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent or acknowledged,",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4ba41dc2b1e3fe54",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 703,
      "quote": "Validating ECN counts from reordered ACK frames can result in failure. An endpoint MUST NOT fail ECN validation as a result of processing an ACK frame that does not increase the largest acknowledged packet number.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d6e8edb576f8824",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 756,
      "quote": "If a path has been validated to support Explicit Congestion Notification (ECN) [RFC3168] [RFC8311], QUIC treats a Congestion Experienced (CE) codepoint in the IP header as a signal of congestion.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "564e3b1aca782b6f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 786,
      "quote": "When Initial or Handshake keys are discarded, packets sent in that space no longer count toward bytes in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-B.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6473ae225238a17a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 817,
      "quote": "DetectAndRemoveLostPackets is called every time an ACK is received or the time threshold loss detection timer expires. This function operates on the sent_packets for that packet number space and returns a list of packets newly detected as lost.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c5f974e5584f76f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 900,
      "quote": "If packets sent prior to the largest acknowledged packet cannot yet be declared lost, then a timer SHOULD be set for the remaining time.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6d7dda14ee9a081e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 909,
      "quote": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold loss detection; see Section 6.1.2.  A timer that is set for time threshold loss detection will expire earlier than the PTO timer in most cases and is less likely to spuriously retransmit data.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3d79640708b15dc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 954,
      "quote": "A sender that does not have state for all packet number spaces or an implementation that cannot compare send times across packet number spaces MAY use state for just the packet number space that was acknowledged.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6d1cb17c91b96072",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 969,
      "quote": "Loss of a QUIC packet that is carried in a PMTU probe is therefore not a reliable indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction; see Item 7 in Section 3 of [DPLPMTUD].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "911294979d5faab3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 974,
      "quote": "Loss of a probe packet SHOULD NOT be treated as an indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction [RFC4821] because this could result in unnecessary reduction of the sending rate.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5cd63a12e5a6236",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1018,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD set the min_rtt to the newest RTT sample after persistent congestion is established.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dedff4a41954610e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1065,
      "quote": "it is the client's responsibility to send packets to unblock the server until it is certain that the server has finished its address validation",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a00e94f75ab1120",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1070,
      "quote": "If no additional data can be sent, the server's PTO timer MUST NOT be armed until datagrams have been received from the client, because packets sent on PTO count against the anti-amplification limit.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2ab1e0ec916091fa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1076,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data packet number space until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d714b384eb870b8b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1095,
      "quote": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold loss detection; see Section 6.1.2.  A timer that is set for time threshold loss detection will expire earlier than the PTO timer in most cases and is less likely to spuriously retransmit data.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/recovery/manager.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "91e61e47318bcc37",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "For this reason, endpoints MUST be able to retain two sets of packet protection keys for receiving packets: the current and the next.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1d2cfb4c5d3d2a7b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate a key update prior to having confirmed the handshake (Section 4.1.2).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2fcd2d32fb6c1a4f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 171,
      "quote": "If the sender wants to elicit a faster acknowledgement on PTO, it can skip a packet number to eliminate the acknowledgment delay.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "be3a6794015ec967",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 182,
      "quote": "An endpoint that acknowledges packets it has not received might cause a congestion controller to permit sending at rates beyond what the network supports.  An endpoint MAY skip packet numbers when sending packets to detect this behavior.  An endpoint can then immediately close the connection with a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f00244a4dff09344",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 437,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent or acknowledged, or when Initial or Handshake keys are discarded (Section 4.9 of [QUIC-TLS]).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "093b17cbceb9e8d4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 442,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data packet number space until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "25add3573021acbb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 615,
      "quote": "For a short period after a key update completes, up to the PTO, endpoints MAY defer generation of the next set of receive packet protection keys.  This allows endpoints to retain only two sets of receive keys; see Section 6.5.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3fde51f9b7de0bbe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 621,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY allow a period of approximately the Probe Timeout (PTO; see [QUIC-RECOVERY]) after promoting the next set of receive keys to be current before it creates the subsequent set of packet protection keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0920eed442940b3d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 648,
      "quote": "For authentication to be free from side channels, the entire process of header protection removal, packet number recovery, and packet protection removal MUST be applied together without timing and other side channels.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ab9f0fb0cf321c1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 836,
      "quote": "When a server is blocked by anti-amplification limits, receiving a datagram unblocks it, even if none of the packets in the datagram are successfully processed.  In such a case, the PTO timer will need to be re-armed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ab474a75f1720b7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 964,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat receipt of a NEW_TOKEN frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d311e90f98957b20",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 985,
      "quote": "An endpoint that is sending packets with a zero-length Destination Connection ID MUST treat receipt of a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5040c615a7f26d99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1028,
      "quote": "The sequence number specified in a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST NOT refer to the Destination Connection ID field of the packet in which the frame is contained.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e4b69adbdaec1095",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1033,
      "quote": "The peer MAY treat this as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ba5d564bdf8b3191",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1037,
      "quote": "Receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame containing a sequence number greater than any previously sent to the peer MUST be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d92158911cc1cdb2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1089,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat receipt of a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.20",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3c25dd3f1c84e32f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1102,
      "quote": "At the client, the handshake is considered confirmed when a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame is received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "45f55875d21ff494",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "When TLS provides keys for a higher encryption level, if there is data from a previous encryption level that TLS has not consumed, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/crypto_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "57854e1f88a1d9be",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "*  If the packet is from a previously installed encryption level, it MUST NOT contain data that extends past the end of previously received data in that flow.  Implementations MUST treat any violations of this requirement as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/crypto_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Crypto buffer limits",
      "id": "3d3191b378c5373d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST support buffering at least 4096 bytes of data received in out-of-order CRYPTO frames.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/crypto_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "tracking_issue": "356",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Crypto buffer limits",
      "id": "db97e23e689311b1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY choose to allow more data to be buffered during the handshake.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/crypto_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "tracking_issue": "356",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "6b9c83d6e70e838f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "If an endpoint does not expand its buffer, it MUST close the connection with a CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED error code.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/crypto_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "62822a8f8fb4c37d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "If QUIC needs to retransmit that data, it MUST use the same keys even if TLS has already updated to newer keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9634b11acf975237",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "If packets from a lower encryption level contain CRYPTO frames, frames that retransmit that data MUST be sent at the same encryption level.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "043671e0e3d8e7ce",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 119,
      "quote": "If the sender wants to elicit a faster acknowledgement on PTO, it can skip a packet number to eliminate the acknowledgment delay.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1f926a0db764279",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 507,
      "quote": "The payload of this packet contains CRYPTO frames and could contain PING, PADDING, or ACK frames.  Handshake packets MAY contain CONNECTION_CLOSE frames of type 0x1c.  Endpoints MUST treat receipt of Handshake packets with other frames as a connection error.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f28362e7bf516b58",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 526,
      "quote": "When a server is blocked by anti-amplification limits, receiving a datagram unblocks it, even if none of the packets in the datagram are successfully processed.  In such a case, the PTO timer will need to be re-armed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "238bd34f10309d73",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 578,
      "quote": "Handshake packets MAY contain CONNECTION_CLOSE frames of type 0x1c.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "522ae9597d9555fe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 198,
      "quote": "The HANDSHAKE_DONE frame MUST be retransmitted until it is acknowledged.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake_status/fuzz_target.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e40900b4ec58047e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "the TLS handshake is considered confirmed at the server when the handshake completes",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake_status.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "263348d9dc02b987",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "At the client, the handshake is considered confirmed when a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame is received.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake_status.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a103e4165f1b0a99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "The server MUST send a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame as soon as the handshake is complete.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake_status.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "04ab829dbf990865",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 157,
      "quote": "The HANDSHAKE_DONE frame MUST be retransmitted until it is acknowledged.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake_status.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "863ea3e7cc0d9ec5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 171,
      "quote": "A HANDSHAKE_DONE frame can only be sent by the server.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake_status.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.20",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2ce02182b723912b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 242,
      "quote": "the TLS handshake is considered confirmed at the server when the handshake completes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/handshake_status.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1bc29c0e219c09e0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "If QUIC needs to retransmit that data, it MUST use the same keys even if TLS has already updated to newer keys.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c4c46c02cc63bd35",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "If packets from a lower encryption level contain CRYPTO frames, frames that retransmit that data MUST be sent at the same encryption level.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f9cf8edf7e586edd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Subsequent Initial packets from the client include the connection ID and token values from the Retry packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7234a23e783bb5ca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "Changing the Destination Connection ID field also results in a change to the keys used to protect the Initial packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dfab72de44bbf83a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 112,
      "quote": "Other than updating the Destination Connection ID and Token fields, the Initial packet sent by the client is subject to the same restrictions as the first Initial packet.  A client MUST use the same cryptographic handshake message it included in this packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c6729db755f29f44",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "If the sender wants to elicit a faster acknowledgement on PTO, it can skip a packet number to eliminate the acknowledgment delay.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cded1b19c48bebd5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 425,
      "quote": "Initial packets sent by the server MUST set the Token Length field to 0; clients that receive an Initial packet with a non-zero Token Length field MUST either discard the packet or generate a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "847223e87e93d050",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 631,
      "quote": "The payload of an Initial packet includes a CRYPTO frame (or frames) containing a cryptographic handshake message, ACK frames, or both. PING, PADDING, and CONNECTION_CLOSE frames of type 0x1c are also permitted.  An endpoint that receives an Initial packet containing other frames can either discard the packet as spurious or treat it as a connection error.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "91b12d5568204d99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 654,
      "quote": "When a server is blocked by anti-amplification limits, receiving a datagram unblocks it, even if none of the packets in the datagram are successfully processed.  In such a case, the PTO timer will need to be re-armed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "appendix-A.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "51272c9d0f5a5518",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 716,
      "quote": "CONNECTION_CLOSE frames of type 0x1c are also permitted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/initial.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "83d5bfdbef37d74b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "A connection will time out if no packets are sent or received for a period longer than the time negotiated using the max_idle_timeout transport parameter; see Section 10.  However, state in middleboxes might time out earlier than that.  Though REQ-5 in [RFC4787] recommends a 2-minute timeout interval, experience shows that sending packets every 30 seconds is necessary to prevent the majority of middleboxes from losing state for UDP flows [GATEWAY].",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/keep_alive.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0e7529d90593e83d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST explicitly negotiate an application protocol.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2da524ff2f98f915",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "Unless another mechanism is used for agreeing on an application protocol, endpoints MUST use ALPN for this purpose.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "37a240fa3c9a3568",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "When Initial or Handshake keys are discarded, the PTO and loss detection timers MUST be reset, because discarding keys indicates forward progress and the loss detection timer might have been set for a now discarded packet number space.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ed62d0996c28ea0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 174,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent or acknowledged, or when Initial or Handshake keys are discarded (Section 4.9 of [QUIC-TLS]).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d1290cf82b38685",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "Since the server could be blocked until more datagrams are received from the client, it is the client's responsibility to send packets to unblock the server until it is certain that the server has finished its address validation",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ace332f699397066",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 191,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT send Initial packets after this point.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa4b3332be67a74b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 209,
      "quote": "When Initial or Handshake keys are discarded, the PTO and loss detection timers MUST be reset, because discarding keys indicates forward progress and the loss detection timer might have been set for a now discarded packet number space.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8d39e13aa49a1896",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 222,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data packet number space until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a242f9da661b7562",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 475,
      "quote": "When sending a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame, the goal is to ensure that the peer will process the frame.  Generally, this means sending the frame in a packet with the highest level of packet protection to avoid the packet being discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6010523178d9c15a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 484,
      "quote": "After the handshake is confirmed (see Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), an endpoint MUST send any CONNECTION_CLOSE frames in a 1-RTT packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1abfd2fd2c22a55e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 497,
      "quote": "A client will always know whether the server has Handshake keys (see Section 17.2.2.1), but it is possible that a server does not know whether the client has Handshake keys.  Under these circumstances, a server SHOULD send a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in both Handshake and Initial packets to ensure that at least one of them is processable by the client.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5783ff2e2d9b75c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 576,
      "quote": "A CONNECTION_CLOSE frame causes all streams to immediately become closed; open streams can be assumed to be implicitly reset.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6f252e25e8dea1ef",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 599,
      "quote": "When ack-eliciting packets in multiple packet number spaces are in flight, the timer MUST be set to the earlier value of the Initial and Handshake packet number spaces.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "25b9b5560c9fae5c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 895,
      "quote": "A PADDING frame (type=0x00) has no semantic value.  PADDING frames can be used to increase the size of a packet.  Padding can be used to increase an Initial packet to the minimum required size or to provide protection against traffic analysis for protected packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a95bcddddb0d5864",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 903,
      "quote": "Endpoints can use PING frames (type=0x01) to verify that their peers are still alive or to check reachability to the peer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae5492c2f08aa429",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 911,
      "quote": "Packets containing discarded CRYPTO frames MUST be acknowledged because the packet has been received and processed by the transport even though the CRYPTO frame was discarded.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "323d17267e58b592",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1021,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a PATH_CHALLENGE on an active path SHOULD send a non-probing packet in response.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4ba0e824087040bf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1064,
      "quote": "The payload of a packet that contains frames MUST contain at least one frame, and MAY contain multiple frames and multiple frame types. An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a packet containing no frames as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fbc0ebf9a740c98b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1091,
      "quote": "A packet MUST NOT be acknowledged until packet protection has been successfully removed and all frames contained in the packet have been processed.  For STREAM frames, this means the data has been enqueued in preparation to be received by the application protocol, but it does not require that data be delivered and consumed. Once the packet has been fully processed, a receiver acknowledges receipt by sending one or more ACK frames containing the packet number of the received packet.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/mod.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6063b23f72e317a6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of duplicate transport parameters as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "37de9585550d319c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat the following as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR or PROTOCOL_VIOLATION:",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4254ae43bb4dcfe6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "*  absence of the retry_source_connection_id transport parameter from the server after receiving a Retry packet,",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bb5569200f072fa4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "*  presence of the retry_source_connection_id transport parameter when no Retry packet was received, or",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "810c287809fe8b73",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "The values provided by a peer for these transport parameters MUST match the values that an endpoint used in the Destination and Source Connection ID fields of Initial packets that it sent (and received, for servers).  Endpoints MUST validate that received transport parameters match received connection ID values.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cbdc5cb94e4492d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 164,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat the absence of the initial_source_connection_id transport parameter from either endpoint or the absence of the original_destination_connection_id transport parameter from the server as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f704d073bd2b7766",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 174,
      "quote": "Servers can also issue a stateless_reset_token transport parameter during the handshake that applies to the connection ID that it selected during the handshake.  These exchanges are protected by encryption, so only client and server know their value.  Note that clients cannot use the stateless_reset_token transport parameter because their transport parameters do not have confidentiality protection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bc9ee53ab114d8da",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 233,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of duplicate transport parameters as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "115ef4adec296e38",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 248,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat the following as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR or PROTOCOL_VIOLATION:",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "df59bd4b6ae44bf1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 281,
      "quote": "Each endpoint includes the value of the Source Connection ID field from the first Initial packet it sent in the initial_source_connection_id transport parameter",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c29e43d66280155e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 295,
      "quote": "* a mismatch between values received from a peer in these transport parameters and the value sent in the corresponding Destination or Source Connection ID fields of Initial packets.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8576357164c9ca01",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 300,
      "quote": "The values provided by a peer for these transport parameters MUST match the values that an endpoint used in the Destination and Source Connection ID fields of Initial packets that it sent (and received, for servers).  Endpoints MUST validate that received transport parameters match received connection ID values.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7ad0e64859de8ae3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 311,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat the absence of the initial_source_connection_id transport parameter from either endpoint or the absence of the original_destination_connection_id transport parameter from the server as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b5dee0b238d917b7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 396,
      "quote": "Therefore, a client SHOULD discard 0-RTT keys as soon as it installs 1-RTT keys as they have no use after that moment.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bd4b99188979d27a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 546,
      "quote": "When using ALPN, endpoints MUST immediately close a connection (see Section 10.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) with a no_application_protocol TLS alert (QUIC error code 0x178; see Section 4.8) if an application protocol is not negotiated.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9fe60922f02a56b5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 552,
      "quote": "While [ALPN] only specifies that servers use this alert, QUIC clients MUST use error 0x178 to terminate a connection when ALPN negotiation fails.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c94a79b672019aa1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 570,
      "quote": "the TLS handshake is considered confirmed at the server when the handshake completes.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "464b20a0040be30c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 684,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of duplicate transport parameters as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/session_context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "695c4b8157e4ff92",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of an acknowledgment for a packet it did not send as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, if it is able to detect the condition.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/tx_packet_numbers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5393047672012cba",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "An endpoint that acknowledges packets it has not received might cause a congestion controller to permit sending at rates beyond what the network supports.  An endpoint MAY skip packet numbers when sending packets to detect this behavior.  An endpoint can then immediately close the connection with a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/tx_packet_numbers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7879c41e9d96a1be",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "A QUIC endpoint MUST NOT reuse a packet number within the same packet number space in one connection.  If the packet number for sending reaches 2^62-1, the sender MUST close the connection without sending a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame or any further packets; an endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset (Section 10.3) in response to further packets that it receives.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/space/tx_packet_numbers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3407ab21f14b990b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "MAX_STREAMS frames that do not increase the stream limit MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/local_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8f172bfd7f29baff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "MAX_STREAMS frames that do not increase the stream limit MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/local_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e93b258033f0a8ff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 111,
      "quote": "An endpoint that is unable to open a new stream due to the peer's limits SHOULD send a STREAMS_BLOCKED frame (Section 19.14).",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/local_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2533e31aa8e96d43",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAMS_BLOCKED frame (type=0x16 or 0x17) when it wishes to open a stream but is unable to do so due to the maximum stream limit set by its peer; see Section 19.11.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/local_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.14",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "403e6d8c705c908b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 227,
      "quote": "To keep the connection from closing, a sender that is flow control limited SHOULD periodically send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame when it has no ack-eliciting packets in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/local_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "79f3f088264fd8c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT wait to receive this signal before advertising additional credit, since doing so will mean that the peer will be blocked for at least an entire round trip",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/remote_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6a9036bb0c417178",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "Maximum Streams:  A count of the cumulative number of streams of the corresponding type that can be opened over the lifetime of the connection.  This value cannot exceed 2^60, as it is not possible to encode stream IDs larger than 2^62-1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/remote_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a6605a74b5f3e91",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT exceed the limit set by their peer.  An endpoint that receives a frame with a stream ID exceeding the limit it has sent MUST treat this as a connection error of type STREAM_LIMIT_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/remote_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2de49f147ce9b6de",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST terminate a connection with an error of type STREAM_LIMIT_ERROR if a peer opens more streams than was permitted.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/controller/remote_initiated.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.11",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0d84397f4d340388",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST close the connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if the sender violates the advertised connection or stream data limits; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/incoming_connection_flow_controller.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e151665a6c720d45",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 655,
      "quote": "MAX_STREAMS frames that do not increase the stream limit MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/manager/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
