    },
    {
      "id": "6efd9ad39ca6a07f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "o | Recv STREAM / STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED / RESET_STREAM | Create Bidirectional Stream (Sending) | Recv MAX_STREAM_DATA / STOP_SENDING (Bidirectional) | Create Higher-Numbered Stream v +-------+ | Recv  | Recv RESET_STREAM |       |-----------------------. +-------+                       | |                           | | Recv STREAM + FIN         | v                           | +-------+                       | | Size  | Recv RESET_STREAM     | | Known |---------------------->| +-------+                       | |                           | | Recv All Data             | v                           v +-------+ Recv RESET_STREAM +-------+ | Data  |--- (optional) --->| Reset | | Recvd |  Recv All Data    | Recvd | +-------+<-- (optional) ----+-------+ |                           | | App Read All Data         | App Read Reset v                           v +-------+                   +-------+ | Data  |                   | Reset | | Read  |                   | Read  | +-------+                   +-------+",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "00f272e98156ea11",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 218,
      "quote": "The data sent on a stream MUST NOT exceed the largest maximum stream data value advertised by the receiver.  An endpoint MUST terminate a connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if it receives more data than the largest maximum stream data that it has sent for the affected stream.  This includes violations of remembered limits in Early Data; see Section 7.4.1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f9b25d75b429d43e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 226,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST close the connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if the sender violates the advertised connection or stream data limits; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "758b001e494f0a51",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 254,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST close the connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if the sender violates the advertised connection or stream data limits; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5dd8415ed22c4f79",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "Therefore, a receiver MUST NOT wait for a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame before sending a MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frame; doing so could result in the sender being blocked for the rest of the connection.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f28f9b9871bd6f4e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 437,
      "quote": "The receiver MUST use the final size of the stream to account for all bytes sent on the stream in its connection level flow controller.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "adef24b0501443a1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 456,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST terminate a connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if it receives more data than the maximum data value that it has sent.  This includes violations of remembered limits in Early Data; see Section 7.4.1.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fdd7c09bd2d8841c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 462,
      "quote": "Once a final size for a stream is known, it cannot change.  If a RESET_STREAM or STREAM frame is received indicating a change in the final size for the stream, an endpoint SHOULD respond with an error of type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3fab040bd3aacc64",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 509,
      "quote": "When a STREAM frame with a FIN bit is received, the final size of the stream is known; see Section 4.5.  The receiving part of the stream then enters the \"Size Known\" state.  In this state, the endpoint no longer needs to send MAX_STREAM_DATA frames, it only receives any retransmissions of stream data.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It's simpler to accept any RESET_STREAM frame instead of ignore",
      "id": "55573b21cbda9c69",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 580,
      "quote": "An endpoint that sends a STOP_SENDING frame MAY ignore the error code in any RESET_STREAM frames subsequently received for that stream.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4d223abcc4ff0f5d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 607,
      "quote": "An implementation MAY interrupt delivery of stream data, discard any data that was not consumed, and signal the receipt of the RESET_STREAM.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c11dcc7d907f992b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 623,
      "quote": "Once a final size for a stream is known, it cannot change.  If a RESET_STREAM or STREAM frame is received indicating a change in the final size for the stream, an endpoint SHOULD respond with an error of type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error handling.  A receiver SHOULD treat receipt of data at or beyond the final size as an error of type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR, even after a stream is closed.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "05ccca8b42d82220",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 707,
      "quote": "To avoid blocking a sender, a receiver MAY send a MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frame multiple times within a round trip or send it early enough to allow time for loss of the frame and subsequent recovery.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "tracking_issue": "334",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "45c93449d9656473",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 748,
      "quote": "A receiver MAY send a STOP_SENDING frame in any state where it has not received a RESET_STREAM frame -- that is, states other than \"Reset Recvd\" or \"Reset Read\".",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2b7a198260b838fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 753,
      "quote": "STOP_SENDING SHOULD only be sent for a stream that has not been reset by the peer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc1dc458c925066",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 774,
      "quote": "If the stream is in the \"Recv\" or \"Size Known\" states, the transport SHOULD signal this by sending a STOP_SENDING frame to prompt closure of the stream in the opposite direction.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/receive_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2703176a0c77004f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 873,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame to indicate to the receiver that it has data to write but is blocked by flow control limits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1403bd14b132a299",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 879,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame (type=0x15) when it wishes to send data, but is unable to do so due to stream-level flow control.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.13",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "da74ade93153479d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1056,
      "quote": "A sender MUST ignore any MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frames that do not increase flow control limits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "21b760bf006d4a05",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1063,
      "quote": "A sender MUST ignore any MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frames that do not increase flow control limits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream/tests.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9cd8598f6e19b731",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "o | Create Stream (Sending) | Peer Creates Bidirectional Stream v +-------+ | Ready | Send RESET_STREAM |       |-----------------------. +-------+                       | |                           | | Send STREAM /             | |      STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED  | v                           | +-------+                       | | Send  | Send RESET_STREAM     | |       |---------------------->| +-------+                       | |                           | | Send STREAM + FIN         | v                           v +-------+                   +-------+ | Data  | Send RESET_STREAM | Reset | | Sent  |------------------>| Sent  | +-------+                   +-------+ |                           | | Recv All ACKs             | Recv ACK v                           v +-------+                   +-------+ | Data  |                   | Reset | | Recvd |                   | Recvd | +-------+                   +-------+",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "23758e8545f92cb3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 220,
      "quote": "A sender MUST ignore any MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frames that do not increase flow control limits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5f8ef8741ac12aca",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 306,
      "quote": "To keep the connection from closing, a sender that is flow control limited SHOULD periodically send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame when it has no ack-eliciting packets in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c120f9deadab5323",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 361,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame to indicate to the receiver that it has data to write but is blocked by flow control limits.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa7fb66ee9ed619c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 366,
      "quote": "To keep the connection from closing, a sender that is flow control limited SHOULD periodically send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame when it has no ack-eliciting packets in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "82aa70f8fc1eb52f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 372,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame (type=0x15) when it wishes to send data, but is unable to do so due to stream-level flow control.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.13",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "7e38dd5cb42b9d5d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 415,
      "quote": "A sender MUST NOT send a STREAM or STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame for a stream in the \"Reset Sent\" state or any terminal state -- that is, after sending a RESET_STREAM frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ed758483a6e111aa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 544,
      "quote": "A STOP_SENDING frame requests that the receiving endpoint send a RESET_STREAM frame.  An endpoint that receives a STOP_SENDING frame MUST send a RESET_STREAM frame if the stream is in the \"Ready\" or \"Send\" state.  If the stream is in the \"Data Sent\" state, the endpoint MAY defer sending the RESET_STREAM frame until the packets containing outstanding data are acknowledged or declared lost.  If any outstanding data is declared lost, the endpoint SHOULD send a RESET_STREAM frame instead of retransmitting the data.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "94602a514e7159d8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 564,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD copy the error code from the STOP_SENDING frame to the RESET_STREAM frame it sends, but it can use any application error code.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f03e388cbe2f00e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 979,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send a RESET_STREAM as the first frame that mentions a stream; this causes the sending part of that stream to open and then immediately transition to the \"Reset Sent\" state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "667990a0e42b1dd5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1032,
      "quote": "A sender MUST NOT send any of these frames from a terminal state (\"Data Recvd\" or \"Reset Recvd\").",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b1c96e70e24d7655",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1043,
      "quote": "A sender MUST NOT send a STREAM or STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame for a stream in the \"Reset Sent\" state or any terminal state -- that is, after sending a RESET_STREAM frame.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/send_stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ee479cc85a64a4fa",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 258,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a MAX_STREAM_DATA frame for a receive-only stream MUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/stream/stream_impl.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.10",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "08439cf0c6a97b70",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Both endpoints MUST maintain flow control state for the stream in the unterminated direction until that direction enters a terminal state.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/sync/data_sender/transmissions.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "615237ca7e9be4fd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send data on any stream without ensuring that it is within the flow control limits set by its peer.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/sync/data_sender/transmissions.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef0a69079d49b0da",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "Senders MUST NOT send data in excess of either limit.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/sync/data_sender/transmissions.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e19d3e2b6f5ea2c6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "The stream does not have an explicit end, so CRYPTO frames do not have a FIN bit.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/sync/data_sender/writer.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8948368fa6d90183",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD include new data in packets that are sent on PTO expiration.  Previously sent data MAY be sent if no new data can be sent.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/sync/data_sender/writer.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3ee20c367b665f9b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "The stream does not have an explicit end, so CRYPTO frames do not have a FIN bit.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/sync/data_sender/writer.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d8f3a28f908b2f81",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 248,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send data on a stream at or beyond the final size.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/sync/data_sender.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1f5f8fe973259e73",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "DATAGRAM frames cannot be fragmented;",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/transmission/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9221",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "83035544fa1aedcc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 183,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY include other frames with the PATH_CHALLENGE and PATH_RESPONSE frames used for path validation.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/transmission/application.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "558f55d751b2367e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "Packets containing frames besides ACK or CONNECTION_CLOSE frames count toward congestion control limits and are considered to be in flight.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/transmission/connection_close.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "017b3a57f738e845",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "Servers do not send non- probing packets (see Section 9.1) toward a client address until they see a non-probing packet from that address.",
      "source": "quic/s2n-quic-transport/src/transmission/context.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "There isn't much benefit from doing this since the initial RTT is\ndiscarded after the first RTT sample.\n",
      "id": "51545b329595ac1a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A connection MAY use the delay between sending a PATH_CHALLENGE and receiving a PATH_RESPONSE to set the initial RTT (see kInitialRtt in Appendix A.2) for a new path, but the delay SHOULD NOT be considered an RTT sample.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This increases the risk that loss is\ndeclared too aggressively, resulting in an unnecessary rate reduction\nby the congestion controller.\n",
      "id": "6e1ca500203f749c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Alternatively, instead of sending an ack-eliciting packet, the sender MAY mark any packets still in flight as lost.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "There isn't much benefit from doing this since the initial RTT is\ndiscarded after the first RTT sample.\n",
      "id": "7d3b1c2e86bb0eed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The client MAY compute an RTT estimate to the server as the time period from when the first Initial packet was sent to when a Retry or a Version Negotiation packet is received.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "There isn't much benefit from doing this since the initial RTT is\ndiscarded after the first RTT sample.\n",
      "id": "6927a5ab7f017c99",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "The client MAY use this value in place of its default for the initial RTT estimate.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since the default congestion controller is CUBIC and not NewReno,\nthe slow start threshold is set to congestion window * beta_cubic.\n",
      "id": "6bbf5fb72d9d569e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "On entering a recovery period, a sender MUST set the slow start threshold to half the value of the congestion window when loss is detected.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/7.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since the default congestion controller is CUBIC and not NewReno,\nthe congestion window is set to congestion window * beta_cubic.\n",
      "id": "c9f2a2cb541b8640",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "The congestion window MUST be set to the reduced value of the slow start threshold before exiting the recovery period.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/7.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The default congestion controller is CUBIC and not NewReno,\nand CUBIC does not specify this limit. However, the Linux implementation\nof CUBIC does limit the congestion window increase to 1 packet for\n2 packets acked. The s2n-QUIC implementation of CUBIC follows the Linux\nimplementation by limiting the increase on each ACK to half the acked bytes.\n",
      "id": "d7350ae80e110b45",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A sender in congestion avoidance uses an Additive Increase Multiplicative Decrease (AIMD) approach that MUST limit the increase to the congestion window to at most one maximum datagram size for each congestion window that is acknowledged.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/7.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This would require a large refactor to enable comparing sent packets\nacross all packet number spaces. The benefit is minimal, since it would\njust allow for persistent congestion while the handshake is still underway.\n",
      "id": "9e4fd98a92068f05",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Since network congestion is not affected by packet number spaces, persistent congestion SHOULD consider packets sent across packet number spaces.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/7.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The default CUBIC congestion controller is similar to the NewReno controller\nspecified. Alternative congestion controllers can be provided and should\nconform to the guidelines. Ultimately, this means this requirement cannot\nbe guaranteed by s2n-quic alone.\n",
      "id": "c4348552ae1ccdb1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If a sender uses a different controller than that specified in this document, the chosen controller MUST conform to the congestion control guidelines specified in Section 3.1 of [RFC8085].",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/recovery/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-QUIC is unlikely to be used in networks with only a single connection, so\nthere isn't much benefit from making this configurable.\n",
      "id": "746d426a8b07ac5f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "In network environments with only a single CUBIC flow and without any other traffic, the fast convergence SHOULD be disabled.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8312/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement is from a referenced RFC and is provided for context.\n",
      "id": "3cfe936f7369dd7b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The message size guidelines in Section 3.2 of the UDP Usage Guidelines [BCP145] state that \"an application SHOULD either use the Path MTU information provided by the IP layer or implement Path MTU Discovery (PMTUD)\" but do not provide a mechanism for discovering the largest size of unfragmented datagram that can be used on a network path.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-1.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement is from a referenced RFC and is provided for context.\n",
      "id": "185227d6e4a29dbb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "The Datagram Congestion Control Protocol (DCCP) [RFC4340] requires implementations to support Classical PMTUD and states that a DCCP sender \"MUST maintain the MPS allowed for each active DCCP session\".",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-1.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic cannot enforce the packet delivery behavior of links.\n",
      "id": "5b958354f6ee11fd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "This specification continues the requirement in [RFC4821] that states, \"All links MUST enforce their MTU: links that might non-deterministically deliver packets that are larger than their rated MTU MUST consistently discard such packets.\"",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement pertains to the network interface s2n-quic uses,\nnot s2n-quic itself.\n",
      "id": "c165022420f41fbe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Probe packets: The network interface below the PL is REQUIRED to provide a way to transmit a probe packet that is larger than the PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol fulfills this requirement via ACK frames.\n",
      "id": "93ddaf67502d96d2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "Reception feedback: The destination PL endpoint is REQUIRED to provide a feedback method that indicates to the DPLPMTUD sender when a probe packet has been received by the destination PL endpoint.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic PMTU probe packets do not contain user data.\n",
      "id": "9f419a58ce7eaa3a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "If a probe packet contains user data requiring retransmission in case of loss, the PL (or layers above) is REQUIRED to arrange any retransmission and/or repair of any resulting loss.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Flow control only applies to STREAM frames in QUIC.\n",
      "id": "f3d476a1f857ad0a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Flow control SHOULD NOT apply to DPLPMTU when probe packets use a design that does not carry user data to the remote application.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not control the IP layer cache.\n",
      "id": "e8b6b52b16f48d53",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "Shared PLPMTU state: The PMTU value calculated from the PLPMTU MAY also be stored with the corresponding entry associated with the destination in the IP layer cache and used by other PL instances.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol is designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS\ninto multiple datagrams.\n",
      "id": "f1d59d96d26a1a05",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "*  A PL MAY be designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS into multiple datagrams.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol supports segmenting data blocks and thus does not\nforce the application to use any particular data block size.\n",
      "id": "e5dabaf3b888778c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED that methods avoid forcing an application to use an arbitrary small MPS for transmission while the method is searching for the currently supported PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol supports segmenting data blocks and thus does not\nto assist the application in choosing any particular data block size.\n",
      "id": "135a13e13b5177e9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "*  To assist applications in choosing a suitable data block size, the PL is RECOMMENDED to provide a primitive that returns the MPS derived from the PLPMTU to the higher layer using the PL.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not receive any information about the maximum size of packet\na receiver can accept.\n",
      "id": "66a76c8070c1b7a6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "A PL sender MAY utilize similar information about the maximum size of network-layer packet that a receiver can accept when this is supplied (note this could be less than EMTU_R).",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The transmission of PMTU probe packets is controlled by the congestion\ncontroller.\n",
      "id": "ae3ae4e0d4eddef5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "When the transmission of probe packets is not controlled by the congestion controller, the interval between probe packets MUST be at least one RTT.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol fulfills this requirement via explicit PADDING frames.\n",
      "id": "61c37faa467dbbce",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A receiver is REQUIRED to be able to distinguish an in-band data block from any added padding.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol fulfills this requirement via packet numbers.\n",
      "id": "cc5fcba4e5aa6efc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Probe messages sent by a PL MUST contain enough information to uniquely identify the probe within the Maximum Segment Lifetime (e.g., including a unique identifier from the PL or the DPLPMTUD implementation), while being robust to reordering and replay of probe response and PTB messages.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol is designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS\ninto multiple datagrams.\n",
      "id": "056fba8c94846841",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "To avoid this, a PL MAY be designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS into multiple datagrams.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol supports segmenting data blocks and thus does not\nlimit the application to any particular data block size.\n",
      "id": "8dcdb4647905a55f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "To determine the largest data block that can be sent, a PL SHOULD provide applications with a primitive that returns the MPS, derived from the current PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic reconstructs lost packets by notifying each component of the\nlost packet number and retransmitting with newly written frames. This\nwill result in a new packet that is clamped to the new MPS.\n",
      "id": "e9046ea2621cb697",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "If these packets are lost, the PL MAY segment the data using the new MPS.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not use the probe timer.\n",
      "id": "0ff663e296433054",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "This value MUST NOT be smaller than 1 second and SHOULD be larger than 15 seconds.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "From the perspective of DPLPMTUD, QUIC can function as an acknowledged PL.\n",
      "id": "938b5b17604ba34e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "CONFIRMATION_TIMER:  When an acknowledged PL is used, this timer MUST NOT be used.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The QUIC protocol supports segmenting data blocks and thus does not\nuse input from the application on maximum data block size.\n",
      "id": "073e16f69441fd86",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The MAX_PLPMTU MAY be reduced by an application that sets a maximum to the size of datagrams it will send.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/5.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement applies only to applications\nbuilt directly or indirectly on UDP or UDP-Lite\n",
      "id": "ddb5be798773b38d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The method SHOULD allow the sender to check the value returned in the response to provide additional protection from off-path insertion of data [BCP145].",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement applies only to applications\nbuilt directly or indirectly on UDP or UDP-Lite\n",
      "id": "a1cea93debaa2bd2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An application that does not have other higher-layer information confirming connectivity with the remote peer SHOULD implement a connectivity mechanism using acknowledged probe packets before entering the BASE state.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement applies only to applications\nbuilt directly or indirectly on UDP or UDP-Lite\n",
      "id": "c15a1f07f3205081",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An application that does not have other higher-layer information confirming correct delivery of datagrams SHOULD implement the CONFIRMATION_TIMER to periodically send probe packets while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.1.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.5",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement applies only to applications\nbuilt directly or indirectly on UDP or UDP-Lite\n",
      "id": "98ee9db6841aa130",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An application that is able and wishes to receive PTB messages MUST perform ICMP validation as specified in Section 5.2 of [BCP145].",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.1.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement applies only to applications\nbuilt directly or indirectly on UDP or UDP-Lite\n",
      "id": "fef6b6b901c70a53",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "A validated PTB message MAY be used as input to the DPLPMTUD algorithm but MUST NOT be used directly to set the PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.1.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-QUIC acts as the Packetization Layer (PL) for applications using\nit, so the application will not be able to implement DPLPMTUD itself.\n",
      "id": "9bc7a23f59fbaa7c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An application SHOULD avoid using DPLPMTUD when the underlying transport system provides this capability.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "300d4b40171ade07",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Since SCTP provides an acknowledged PL, a sender MUST NOT implement the CONFIRMATION_TIMER while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "e284ffe046ecf226",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Normal ICMP validation MUST be performed as specified in Appendix C of [RFC4960].",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "e9fcf735bfb79764",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "When a PTB message has been validated, the PL_PTB_SIZE calculated from the PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message SHOULD be used with the DPLPMTUD algorithm, provided that the reported PL_PTB_SIZE is less than the current probe size (see Section 4.6).",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "0ccc45a92216d4ff",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "ICMP validation MUST be performed for PTB messages as specified in Appendix C of [RFC4960].",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "e3a89512f87bddb3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "When the validation is completed, the PL_PTB_SIZE calculated from the PTB_SIZE in the PTB message SHOULD be used with the DPLPMTUD providing that the reported PL_PTB_SIZE is less than the current probe size.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "2004dbe66d912671",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "|  The RECOMMENDED method for determining the MTU of the path is |  specified in RFC 8899.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "6b3c7b82f723e1c9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Since SCTP provides an acknowledged PL, a sender MUST NOT implement the CONFIRMATION_TIMER while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "aeee2bf1bbf6e0bd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The specification for DPLPMTUD continues the practice of using the PL to discover the PMTU but updates RFC4960 with a recommendation to use the method specified in this document: The RECOMMENDED method for generating probes is to add a chunk consisting only of padding to an SCTP message.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement only applies to SCTP.\n",
      "id": "f4aa57a4b792883a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "The PAD chunk defined in [RFC4820] SHOULD be attached to a minimum-length HEARTBEAT (HB) chunk to build a probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/rfc8899/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The optional requirement would not yield much benefits and require expensive\nchecks per packet received in the 1-RTT space.\n\nThe benefits would result in a quicker transition to the Handshake-confirmed\nstate for a Client endpoint in the event of packet loss. However, the delay\nin transitioning to the Handshake-confirmed state doesn't prevent the Client\nfrom making progress (sending application data); so the advantage is small.\n",
      "id": "4115fc0f9a430f14",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Additionally, a client MAY consider the handshake to be confirmed when it receives an acknowledgment for a 1-RTT packet.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirements for client\nauthentication vary based on application protocol and deployment.\n\ns2n-quic doesn't need to do anything specific, as this is only handled\nin the application layer.\n",
      "id": "10911a7e2758f207",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A server MAY request that the client authenticate during the handshake.  A server MAY refuse a connection if the client is unable to authenticate when requested.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic doesn't actually inspect any TLS messages so this will need\nto be enforced by the TLS layer.\n",
      "id": "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT use post-handshake client authentication (as defined in Section 4.6.2 of [TLS13]) because the multiplexing offered by QUIC prevents clients from correlating the certificate request with the application-level event that triggered it (see [HTTP2-TLS13]).  More specifically, servers MUST NOT send post- handshake TLS CertificateRequest messages, and clients MUST treat receipt of such messages as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because session resumption tickets are handled outside of s2n-quic,\nthere's no way for us to reliably enforce this and should be handled\nat the application/integration layer.\n",
      "id": "dd659fe2b23d5ab8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD NOT reuse tickets as that allows entities other than the server to correlate connections; see Appendix C.4 of [TLS13].",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The TLS layer is responsible for sending/not sending this message.\ns2n-quic cannot enforce this requirement on its own.\n",
      "id": "9e0e815522bde54a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Although it is in principle possible to use this feature for address verification, QUIC implementations SHOULD instead use the Retry feature; see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.7",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS support is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable by\ns2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "8e367be82e4c560f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Other versions of TLS MUST provide a similar function in order to be used with QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This only applies to future definitions of QUIC, not implementations.\n",
      "id": "684ca41db0d4b592",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Future versions of QUIC SHOULD generate a new salt value, thus ensuring that the keys are different for each version of QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic only offers TLS 1.3\n",
      "id": "65a4e70ffeb030f8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "The HKDF-Expand-Label function defined in TLS 1.3 MUST be used for Initial packets even where the TLS versions offered do not include TLS 1.3.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not implement TLS and isn't able to ensure this holds\n",
      "id": "72b4bdd84640af61",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT reject a ClientHello that offers a cipher suite that it does not support, or it would be impossible to deploy a new cipher suite.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic delegates ciphersuite selection to the TLS provider and is unable to\nenforce this.\n",
      "id": "ec03f4619272e58d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Before a TLS cipher suite can be used with QUIC, a header protection algorithm MUST be specified for the AEAD used with that cipher suite.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/5.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Returning this error would indicate that a key update is in progress, revealing information about the state of the connection.\n",
      "id": "cd12f67be6ced3d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY treat such consecutive key updates as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "We allow packets protected with older keys to be received for 1 PTO, then we derive a new key which prevents us from decrypting the old packets.\n",
      "id": "4c446bf8d17454af",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives an acknowledgement that is carried in a packet protected with old keys where any acknowledged packet was protected with newer keys MAY treat that as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "We are not performing key generations as part of packet processing, so we do not\nexpose any timing signal to an attacker. Therefore this MAY does not apply to our\nimplementation.\n",
      "id": "694e44bb6acc2636",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY generate new keys as part of packet processing, but this creates a timing signal that could be used by an attacker to learn when key updates happen and thus leak the value of the Key Phase bit.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To reduce the possibility of a timing side channel, we do not attempt to remove protection from packets with old keys if the initial attempt failed.\n",
      "id": "0674dec53d6bcf1b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1,
      "quote": "An endpoint that successfully removes protection with old keys when newer keys were used for packets with lower packet numbers MUST treat this as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/6.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not define any cipher suites beyond what is available in the\nTLS provider. In the end this means it is unenforceable by s2n-quic itself.\n",
      "id": "b62620fd58b9ddf7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Any TLS cipher suite that is specified for use with QUIC MUST define limits on the use of the associated AEAD function that preserves margins for confidentiality and integrity. That is, limits MUST be specified for the number of packets that can be authenticated and for the number of packets that can fail authentication.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "No plans to implement until said future analyses have been written and evaluated.\n",
      "id": "176b1f914604de67",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Future analyses and specifications MAY relax confidentiality or integrity limits for an AEAD.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not define any application protocols so this does not apply\n",
      "id": "a043e1c8b3823930",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An application protocol MAY restrict the QUIC versions that it can operate over.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS support is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable by\ns2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "dcce37975c44f791",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT send this extension in a TLS connection that does not use QUIC (such as the use of TLS with TCP defined in [TLS13]). A fatal unsupported_extension alert MUST be sent by an implementation that supports this extension if the extension is received when the transport is not QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS support is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable by\ns2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "63fafd04034871c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT send the EndOfEarlyData message.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/8.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS support is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable by\ns2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "ececce7ea36caa8b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT request the use of the TLS 1.3 compatibility mode.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/8.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS support is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable by\ns2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "c5a319c10e01f136",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD treat the receipt of a TLS ClientHello with a non-empty legacy_session_id field as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/8.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS support is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable by\ns2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "32dd7dcb761ae45e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "These MUST NOT be used to communicate application semantics between endpoints; clients MUST treat them as opaque values.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not define any additional extensions\n",
      "id": "560ef9d48a202672",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "QUIC extensions MUST either describe how replay attacks affect their operation or prohibit the use of the extension in 0-RTT.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not define any application protocols\n",
      "id": "d76c21602a655134",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Application protocols MUST either prohibit the use of extensions that carry application semantics in 0-RTT or provide replay mitigation strategies.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not use or define any additional header protection variants\n",
      "id": "13a726ded1b484d0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Future header protection variants based on this construction MUST use a PRF to ensure equivalent security guarantees.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not define any additional versions of QUIC.\n",
      "id": "a4fea428cdb7f3e2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "To preserve this separation, a new version of QUIC SHOULD define new labels for key derivation for packet protection key and IV, plus the header protection keys.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/9.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not define any additional versions of QUIC.\n",
      "id": "6b9c791d85e5d9f9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "New QUIC versions SHOULD define a new salt value used in calculating initial secrets.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/tls/9.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic maintains a hash map of all Stateless Reset Tokens to the connection\nthey are associated with. Since the hash map provides constant time lookups by\nusing SipHash initialized with random state, it is not necessary to use remote\naddress to reduce the potential pool of matching Stateless Reset Tokens before\nperforming the comparison. In addition, validating the remote address matches the\nremote address associated with the Stateless Reset Token provides minimal additional\nsecurity benefit given the ease of spoofing remote addresses and the difficult of\nforging a valid Stateless Reset Token.\n",
      "id": "4467ef220f9463f3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The endpoint identifies a received datagram as a Stateless Reset by comparing the last 16 bytes of the datagram with all stateless reset tokens associated with the remote address on which the datagram was received.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/10.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The stateless reset token is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable\nby s2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "8df72261e76d15ae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The stateless reset token MUST be difficult to guess.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The stateless reset token is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable\nby s2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "a252e9e4d82385de",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "The same stateless reset token MUST NOT be used for multiple connection IDs.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic always requests a new connection ID for each connection, but since\nconnection IDs are implemented through a provider this requirement is\nunenforceable.\n",
      "id": "a5b99874916cdb3b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "This method for choosing the stateless reset token means that the combination of connection ID and static key MUST NOT be used for another connection.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic always requests a new connection ID for each connection, but since\nconnection IDs are implemented through a provider this requirement is\nunenforceable.\n",
      "id": "5c8fcde14e74ba7e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "A connection ID from a connection that is reset by revealing the stateless reset token MUST NOT be reused for new connections at nodes that share a static key.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because the stateless reset token is not available\nuntil connection establishment is complete or near completion,\nignoring an unknown packet with a long header might be as effective\nas sending a stateless reset.\n",
      "id": "6697c4179935374a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to a packet with a long header.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The stateless resets that s2n-quic sends are always smaller than the packet\nit responds to. The size is randomly determined between the smallest value\nthat is indistinguishable from a valid short packet and the size of the triggering\npacket. This is sufficient to prevent stateless reset looping.\n",
      "id": "1d9a0b31b9fb4ced",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "An endpoint that sends a Stateless Reset in response to a packet that is 43 bytes or shorter SHOULD send a Stateless Reset that is one byte shorter than the packet it responds to.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic never requires the peer to send zero-length Destination Connection ID",
      "id": "7606a81dc73c7b34",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send this frame if it currently requires that its peer send packets with a zero-length Destination Connection ID.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-QUIC does not provide zero-length connection IDs",
      "id": "17fa259b1b17515d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An endpoint that provides a zero- length connection ID MUST treat receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/19.16.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This isn't something that would be used in HTTP/3 so we see little benefit\nin doing it currently.\n",
      "id": "1a7afe25df116fe4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "However, implementations MAY choose to offer the ability to deliver data out of order to a receiving application.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This would require comparing every single byte that a peer sends, which would\nbe quite costly and not add much value.\n\nMaybe in the future, we would include an option to enable it but it should not\nbe the default, as it would not be realistic for a production workload.\n",
      "id": "e2c7efdfeb58f8cd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "; an endpoint MAY treat receipt of different data at the same offset within a stream as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic proactively supplies connection IDs up to the minimum of the\npeer's active_connection_id_limit and a hardcoded MAX_ACTIVE_CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT,\nso the maximum amount of  connection IDs will already be issued by the time a\npeer uses them.\n",
      "id": "eb58bcf8296f30d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If an endpoint provided fewer connection IDs than the peer's active_connection_id_limit, it MAY supply a new connection ID when it receives a packet with a previously unused connection ID.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic requires connection ID providers to provide connection IDs of at\nleast 4 bytes in length, which allows for at least 4 billion possible connection\nIDs. s2n-quic allows limits the number of concurrent connection IDs issued,\nas well as their minimum lifetime, so the risk of running out of connection IDs\nis sufficiently mitigated.\n",
      "id": "dba7e21daadccf13",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY limit the total number of connection IDs issued for each connection to avoid the risk of running out of connection IDs; see Section 10.3.2.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Before removing a retired connection ID, s2n-quic gives the peer time to\nstop using the connection ID. If after that time the peer is still using\nthe connection ID, s2n-quic will respond with a stateless reset instead of\nclosing the connection. Therefore, there is no need to proactively close the\nconnection when a connection ID is removed.\n",
      "id": "c0299440fdad3cb8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If the endpoint can no longer process the indicated connection IDs, it MAY close the connection.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While the default provider in s2n-quic generates completely random connection IDs,\nan alternative provider can be provided and should ensure this is true. Ultimately,\nthis means this requirement cannot be guaranteed by s2n-quic alone.\n",
      "id": "358ba3db0d1b42bc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Connection IDs MUST NOT contain any information that can be used by an external observer (that is, one that does not cooperate with the issuer) to correlate them with other connection IDs for the same connection.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Zero-length connection IDs generated on an s2n-QUIC endpoint are not supported\n",
      "id": "3059124a8788357c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT use the same IP address and port for multiple concurrent connections with zero-length connection IDs, unless it is certain that those protocol features are not in use.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not require a particular deployment strategy, which makes\nthis requirement unenforceable.\n",
      "id": "857f17c739bb20b6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A server in a deployment that does not implement a solution to maintain connection continuity when the client address changes SHOULD indicate that migration is not supported by using the disable_active_migration transport parameter.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/5.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Both the connection ID and retry tokens are implemented through providers\nwhich means this requirement is unenforceable by s2n-quic alone.\n",
      "id": "fbedb1a658792af9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Server deployments that use this simple form of load balancing MUST avoid the creation of a stateless reset oracle; see Section 21.10.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/5.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not define or implement any additional transport parameters\n",
      "id": "ebb06409f1d11d58",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The definition of a new transport parameter (Section 7.4.2) MUST specify whether storing the transport parameter for 0-RTT is mandatory, optional, or prohibited.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TLS support is implemented through a provider and is unenforceable by\ns2n-quic.\n",
      "id": "859013f112b9ab1b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The cryptographic handshake MUST provide the following properties:",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic rounds up path validation frames to 1200 bytes so MTU is\nalways validated as part of path validation.\n",
      "id": "9d089ac61fd70e11",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "However, the endpoint MUST initiate another path validation with an expanded datagram to verify that the path supports the required MTU.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/8.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The text was updated in draft 34:\nA value of\nthree times the larger of the current Probe Timeout (PTO) or the PTO\nfor the new path (that is, using kInitialRtt as defined in\n[QUIC-RECOVERY]) is RECOMMENDED.\n",
      "id": "b1b2bb0203113d6c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A value of three times the larger of the current PTO or the PTO for the new path (using kInitialRtt, as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY]) is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/8.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic creates a new congestion controller for each path so there\nis no need to reset to initial values after path validation.\n",
      "id": "7ce2d348a3598fe3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "On confirming a peer's ownership of its new address, an endpoint MUST immediately reset the congestion controller and round-trip time estimator for the new path to initial values (see Appendices A.3 and B.3 of [QUIC-RECOVERY]) unless the only change in the peer's address is its port number.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "We create a new congestion controller for each path. At this time an\nunintentional rebind will cause the CC to start from an initial state.\nThe path is amplification limited anyway, so there will always be a\nshort drop in performance during a rebind.\n",
      "id": "92849d2bd646eef1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Because port-only changes are commonly the result of NAT rebinding or other middlebox activity, the endpoint MAY instead retain its congestion control state and round-trip estimate in those cases instead of reverting to initial values.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "s2n-quic does not use a timer for re-transmitting the PATH_CHALLENGE.\n\nInstead of using a timer, the PATH_CHALLENGE holds state to transmit\ntwice in the `on_tranmit` function.\n",
      "id": "38ab7e4621cc84ed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "This timer SHOULD be set as described in Section 6.2.1 of [QUIC-RECOVERY] and MUST NOT be more aggressive.",
      "source": "specs/exceptions/transport/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Re-establishing min_rtt",
      "id": "4b463d78740c1506",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY reestablish the min_rtt at other times in the connection, such as when traffic volume is low and an acknowledgment is received with a low acknowledgment delay.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "tracking_issue": "249",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Re-establishing min_rtt",
      "id": "3770d887cc5c0992",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD NOT refresh the min_rtt value too often, since the actual minimum RTT of the path is not frequently observable.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "tracking_issue": "249",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Local delays in RTT",
      "id": "e15246eb8affcaad",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "In such cases, an endpoint SHOULD subtract such local delays from its RTT sample until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "tracking_issue": "251",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Adaptive loss thresholds",
      "id": "3e1caec4bd859f4e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY experiment with absolute thresholds, thresholds from previous connections, adaptive thresholds, or the including of RTT variation.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/6.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "tracking_issue": "252",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Adaptive loss thresholds",
      "id": "65ea1316449b5532",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Implementations with adaptive time thresholds MAY choose to start with smaller initial reordering thresholds to minimize recovery latency.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "tracking_issue": "252",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Resumed connection RTT",
      "id": "499745d6365282d7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Resumed connections over the same network MAY use the previous connection's final smoothed RTT value as the resumed connection's initial RTT.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "tracking_issue": "144",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Speeding up handshake completion",
      "id": "0fa5b3588139e100",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "To speed up handshake completion under these conditions, an endpoint MAY, for a limited number of times per connection, send a packet containing unacknowledged CRYPTO data earlier than the PTO expiry, subject to the address validation limits in Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/6.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "tracking_issue": "253",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Probe packet configuration",
      "id": "a584ee87d1f9d50d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY use alternative strategies for determining the content of probe packets, including sending new or retransmitted data based on the application's priorities.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "tracking_issue": "254",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Ignoring loss of undecryptable packets",
      "id": "8aef9dcf5a49752a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY ignore the loss of Handshake, 0-RTT, and 1-RTT packets that might have arrived before the peer had packet protection keys to process those packets.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "tracking_issue": "149",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Ignoring loss of undecryptable packets",
      "id": "71e4d5d7c44f1d9e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT ignore the loss of packets that were sent after the earliest acknowledged packet in a given packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "tracking_issue": "149",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Packet pacing",
      "id": "dffab42ec48fcc47",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "To avoid delaying their delivery to the peer, packets containing only ACK frames SHOULD therefore not be paced.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/7.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "tracking_issue": "1072",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Packet pacing",
      "id": "da3d60441b578dde",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD NOT consider itself application limited if it would have fully utilized the congestion window without pacing delay.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/7.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.8",
      "tracking_issue": "146",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Detect loss of ack-only packets",
      "id": "7a55ddc680046ce0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Unlike TCP, QUIC can detect the loss of these packets and MAY use that information to adjust the congestion controller or the rate of ACK- only packets being sent, but this document does not describe a mechanism for doing so.",
      "source": "specs/todos/recovery/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "tracking_issue": "255",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "03b6701f5031c875",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Processing PTB messages: A DPLPMTUD sender MAY optionally utilize PTB messages received from the network layer to help identify when a network path does not support the current size of probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "a94bf4c168ec723c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "Any received PTB message MUST be validated before it is used to update the PLPMTU discovery information [RFC8201].",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "b003c020a0cd6de7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "A PTB message MUST NOT be used to increase the PLPMTU [RFC8201] but could trigger a probe to test for a larger PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "1d0008202f369ee9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "A PL_PTB_SIZE that is greater than that currently probed SHOULD be ignored.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "d562f1a81afe066f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A DPLPMTUD method MUST NOT rely solely on this method.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "53331f33173c045d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "*  A PL that supports PTB messages MUST validate these messages before they are further processed.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "1561c30caed90cb6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "The PL MUST check the protocol information in the quoted packet carried in an ICMP PTB message payload to validate the message originated from the sending node.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "f306cd2dd2cb8e6e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "The validation SHOULD utilize information that is not simple for an off-path attacker to determine [BCP145].",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "e42111a22f752596",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "A PTB message that does not complete the validation MUST NOT be further utilized by the DPLPMTUD method, as discussed in the Security Considerations section (Section 8).",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "c33e92573724fa1c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "PTB messages that have been validated MAY be utilized by the DPLPMTUD algorithm but MUST NOT be used directly to set the PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "eb5d8fb4374d2a25",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "MIN_PLPMTU < PL_PTB_SIZE < BASE_PLPMTU *  A robust PL MAY enter an error state (see Section 5.2) for an IPv4 path when the PL_PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message is larger than or equal to 68 bytes [RFC0791] and when this is less than the BASE_PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "2cc74846a65bf143",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "*  A robust PL MAY enter an error state (see Section 5.2) for an IPv6 path when the PL_PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message is larger than or equal to 1280 bytes [RFC8200] and when this is less than the BASE_PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "088edb8a66b5762c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "The PLPMTU SHOULD be set to BASE_PLPMTU (the PLPMTU is reduced to the BASE_PLPMTU to avoid unnecessary packet loss when a black hole is encountered).",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "c3969d0f3b94c1cc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A node supporting DPLPMTUD MUST therefore appropriately validate the payload of PTB messages to ensure these are received in response to transmitted traffic (i.e., a reported error condition that corresponds to a datagram actually sent by the path layer, see Section 4.6.1).",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Incorporate PTB messages into DPLPMTUD",
      "id": "4efd935261b6f218",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "This processing SHOULD be limited to avoid a denial-of-service attack when arbitrary headers are included.",
      "source": "specs/todos/rfc8899/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "tracking_issue": "628",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "Async handshake",
      "id": "83a09f7d66603ba9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "While waiting for TLS processing to complete, an endpoint SHOULD buffer received packets if they might be processed using keys that are not yet available.",
      "source": "specs/todos/tls/4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "tracking_issue": "298",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "0-RTT",
      "id": "e78f71c7fa7ac313",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send the early_data extension with a max_early_data_size field set to any value other than 0xffffffff.",
      "source": "specs/todos/tls/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "tracking_issue": "300",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "0-RTT",
      "id": "bcd2ce0383a4f57c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a NewSessionTicket that contains an early_data extension with any other value as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/todos/tls/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "tracking_issue": "300",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "0-RTT",
      "id": "8a691f2136953be6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "When rejecting 0-RTT, a server MUST NOT process any 0-RTT packets, even if it could.",
      "source": "specs/todos/tls/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "0-RTT",
      "id": "819f38a82b2d22a6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "When 0-RTT was rejected, a client SHOULD treat receipt of an acknowledgement for a 0-RTT packet as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, if it is able to detect the condition.",
      "source": "specs/todos/tls/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "feature": "0-RTT",
      "id": "3590e715ce241d7f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 19,
