    {
      "comment": "Parameter beta_cubic SHOULD be set to\n0.7.\n",
      "id": "e270957f979e22e8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Parameter beta_cubic SHOULD be set to 0.7.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To speed up this bandwidth release by\nexisting flows, the following mechanism called \"fast convergence\"\nSHOULD be implemented.\n",
      "id": "d789bc49189042a0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "To speed up this bandwidth release by existing flows, the following mechanism called \"fast convergence\" SHOULD be implemented.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In network environments with only a single\nCUBIC flow and without any other traffic, the fast convergence SHOULD\nbe disabled.\n",
      "id": "5185db15499d919f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "In network environments with only a single CUBIC flow and without any other traffic, the fast convergence SHOULD be disabled.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "CUBIC MUST employ a slow-start algorithm, when the cwnd is no more\nthan ssthresh.\n",
      "id": "bc116027539d9608",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "CUBIC MUST employ a slow-start algorithm, when the cwnd is no more than ssthresh.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312/4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Among the slow-start algorithms, CUBIC MAY choose the\nstandard TCP slow start [RFC5681] in general networks, or the limited\nslow start [RFC3742] or hybrid slow start [HR08] for fast and long-\ndistance networks.\n",
      "id": "037cfe3a85694a82",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Among the slow-start algorithms, CUBIC MAY choose the standard TCP slow start [RFC5681] in general networks, or the limited slow start [RFC3742] or hybrid slow start [HR08] for fast and long- distance networks.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312/4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, C\nSHOULD be set to 0.4.\n",
      "id": "885b001d92e1a386",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Therefore, C SHOULD be set to 0.4.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "1 MUST\nNOT include these periods; otherwise, W_cubic(t) might be very high\nafter restarting from these periods.\n",
      "id": "0afe37db1f74f6ee",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "1 MUST NOT include these periods; otherwise, W_cubic(t) might be very high after restarting from these periods.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312/5.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8312",
      "target_section": "section-5.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The message size guidelines in Section 3.2 of the UDP Usage\nGuidelines [BCP145] state that \"an application SHOULD either use the\nPath MTU information provided by the IP layer or implement Path MTU\nDiscovery (PMTUD)\" but do not provide a mechanism for discovering the\nlargest size of unfragmented datagram that can be used on a network\npath.\n",
      "id": "533a06857bc92c57",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "The message size guidelines in Section 3.2 of the UDP Usage Guidelines [BCP145] state that \"an application SHOULD either use the Path MTU information provided by the IP layer or implement Path MTU Discovery (PMTUD)\" but do not provide a mechanism for discovering the largest size of unfragmented datagram that can be used on a network path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The Datagram Congestion Control Protocol (DCCP) [RFC4340] requires\nimplementations to support Classical PMTUD and states that a DCCP\nsender \"MUST maintain the MPS allowed for each active DCCP session\".\n",
      "id": "c37766668f25c2ef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "The Datagram Congestion Control Protocol (DCCP) [RFC4340] requires implementations to support Classical PMTUD and states that a DCCP sender \"MUST maintain the MPS allowed for each active DCCP session\".",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This specification continues the requirement in\n[RFC4821] that states, \"All links MUST enforce their MTU: links\nthat might non-deterministically deliver packets that are larger\nthan their rated MTU MUST consistently discard such packets.\"\n",
      "id": "2f9bcbbe1c57e4a9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "This specification continues the requirement in [RFC4821] that states, \"All links MUST enforce their MTU: links that might non-deterministically deliver packets that are larger than their rated MTU MUST consistently discard such packets.\"",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This specification continues the requirement in\n[RFC4821] that states, \"All links MUST enforce their MTU: links\nthat might non-deterministically deliver packets that are larger\nthan their rated MTU MUST consistently discard such packets.\"\n",
      "id": "ad385674e63b6d20",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "This specification continues the requirement in [RFC4821] that states, \"All links MUST enforce their MTU: links that might non-deterministically deliver packets that are larger than their rated MTU MUST consistently discard such packets.\"",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL MUST NOT send a datagram (other than a probe\npacket) with a size at the PL that is larger than the current\nPLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "d1f76ae1413ac88a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "A PL MUST NOT send a datagram (other than a probe packet) with a size at the PL that is larger than the current PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Probe packets: The network interface below the PL is REQUIRED to\nprovide a way to transmit a probe packet that is larger than the\nPLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "f48f38c51da2f45b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "Probe packets: The network interface below the PL is REQUIRED to provide a way to transmit a probe packet that is larger than the PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In IPv4, a probe packet MUST be sent with the Don't\nFragment (DF) bit set in the IP header and without network layer\nendpoint fragmentation.\n",
      "id": "f258bdd2ee54607c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "In IPv4, a probe packet MUST be sent with the Don't Fragment (DF) bit set in the IP header and without network layer endpoint fragmentation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Reception feedback: The destination PL endpoint is REQUIRED to\nprovide a feedback method that indicates to the DPLPMTUD sender\nwhen a probe packet has been received by the destination PL\nendpoint.\n",
      "id": "c117c34087ea0b44",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 168,
      "quote": "Reception feedback: The destination PL endpoint is REQUIRED to provide a feedback method that indicates to the DPLPMTUD sender when a probe packet has been received by the destination PL endpoint.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Probe loss recovery: It is RECOMMENDED to use probe packets that\ndo not carry any user data that would require retransmission if\nlost.\n",
      "id": "b6748f375789b030",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 177,
      "quote": "Probe loss recovery: It is RECOMMENDED to use probe packets that do not carry any user data that would require retransmission if lost.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a probe packet\ncontains user data requiring retransmission in case of loss, the\nPL (or layers above) is REQUIRED to arrange any retransmission\nand/or repair of any resulting loss.\n",
      "id": "9a06aa84b14bf137",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "If a probe packet contains user data requiring retransmission in case of loss, the PL (or layers above) is REQUIRED to arrange any retransmission and/or repair of any resulting loss.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The PL is REQUIRED to be\nrobust in the case where probe packets are lost due to other\nreasons (including link transmission error, congestion).\n",
      "id": "06a684502cb64031",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 194,
      "quote": "The PL is REQUIRED to be robust in the case where probe packets are lost due to other reasons (including link transmission error, congestion).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "PMTU parameters: A DPLPMTUD sender is RECOMMENDED to utilize\ninformation about the maximum size of packet that can be\ntransmitted by the sender on the local link (e.g., the local link\nMTU).\n",
      "id": "1af555cbc9eceaab",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 202,
      "quote": "PMTU parameters: A DPLPMTUD sender is RECOMMENDED to utilize information about the maximum size of packet that can be transmitted by the sender on the local link (e.g., the local link MTU).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL sender MAY utilize similar information about the\nmaximum size of network-layer packet that a receiver can accept\nwhen this is supplied (note this could be less than EMTU_R).\n",
      "id": "57cb087ad1b5a267",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 211,
      "quote": "A PL sender MAY utilize similar information about the maximum size of network-layer packet that a receiver can accept when this is supplied (note this could be less than EMTU_R).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Processing PTB messages: A DPLPMTUD sender MAY optionally utilize\nPTB messages received from the network layer to help identify\nwhen a network path does not support the current size of probe\npacket.\n",
      "id": "08c5cc3f5c793d1f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 219,
      "quote": "Processing PTB messages: A DPLPMTUD sender MAY optionally utilize PTB messages received from the network layer to help identify when a network path does not support the current size of probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any received PTB message MUST be validated before it is\nused to update the PLPMTU discovery information [RFC8201].\n",
      "id": "1f53a553b5240377",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 228,
      "quote": "Any received PTB message MUST be validated before it is used to update the PLPMTU discovery information [RFC8201].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nPTB message MUST NOT be used to increase the PLPMTU [RFC8201] but\ncould trigger a probe to test for a larger PLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "ec42d96b7b9f6691",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 235,
      "quote": "A PTB message MUST NOT be used to increase the PLPMTU [RFC8201] but could trigger a probe to test for a larger PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL_PTB_SIZE that is greater than\nthat currently probed SHOULD be ignored.\n",
      "id": "e50b5f42b2553276",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 243,
      "quote": "A PL_PTB_SIZE that is greater than that currently probed SHOULD be ignored.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Probing and congestion control: A PL MAY use a congestion\ncontroller to decide when to send a probe packet.\n",
      "id": "82c23699dff3b912",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 250,
      "quote": "Probing and congestion control: A PL MAY use a congestion controller to decide when to send a probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the\ntransmission of probe packets is not controlled by the congestion\ncontroller, the interval between probe packets MUST be at least\none RTT.\n",
      "id": "9db6422dd55dc3cd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 257,
      "quote": "When the transmission of probe packets is not controlled by the congestion controller, the interval between probe packets MUST be at least one RTT.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Loss of a probe packet SHOULD NOT be treated as an\nindication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion\ncontrol reaction [RFC4821] because this could result in\nunnecessary reduction of the sending rate.\n",
      "id": "82e10bbb87ce7815",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 266,
      "quote": "Loss of a probe packet SHOULD NOT be treated as an indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction [RFC4821] because this could result in unnecessary reduction of the sending rate.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Loss of a probe packet SHOULD NOT be treated as an\nindication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion\ncontrol reaction [RFC4821] because this could result in\nunnecessary reduction of the sending rate.\n",
      "id": "0a7680592ffec265",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 275,
      "quote": "Loss of a probe packet SHOULD NOT be treated as an indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction [RFC4821] because this could result in unnecessary reduction of the sending rate.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An update to the\nPLPMTU (or MPS) MUST NOT increase the congestion window measured\nin bytes [RFC4821].\n",
      "id": "5266645dd73b6b4d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 284,
      "quote": "An update to the PLPMTU (or MPS) MUST NOT increase the congestion window measured in bytes [RFC4821].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL that maintains the congestion window in terms of a limit to\nthe number of outstanding fixed-size packets SHOULD adapt this\nlimit to compensate for the size of the actual packets.\n",
      "id": "05c35f4b9bb24e3c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 292,
      "quote": "A PL that maintains the congestion window in terms of a limit to the number of outstanding fixed-size packets SHOULD adapt this limit to compensate for the size of the actual packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Flow control\nSHOULD NOT apply to DPLPMTU when probe packets use a design that\ndoes not carry user data to the remote application.\n",
      "id": "f3f6965aebeac1b0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 300,
      "quote": "Flow control SHOULD NOT apply to DPLPMTU when probe packets use a design that does not carry user data to the remote application.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Shared PLPMTU state: The PMTU value calculated from the PLPMTU\nMAY also be stored with the corresponding entry associated with\nthe destination in the IP layer cache and used by other PL\ninstances.\n",
      "id": "ead4541b92904138",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 308,
      "quote": "Shared PLPMTU state: The PMTU value calculated from the PLPMTU MAY also be stored with the corresponding entry associated with the destination in the IP layer cache and used by other PL instances.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The specification of PLPMTUD [RFC4821] states, \"If\nPLPMTUD updates the MTU for a particular path, all Packetization\nLayer sessions that share the path representation (as described\nin Section 5.2) SHOULD be notified to make use of the new MTU\".\n",
      "id": "7e22457c52ddeedc",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 317,
      "quote": "The specification of PLPMTUD [RFC4821] states, \"If PLPMTUD updates the MTU for a particular path, all Packetization Layer sessions that share the path representation (as described in Section 5.2) SHOULD be notified to make use of the new MTU\".",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Such methods MUST be robust to the wide variety of underlying\nnetwork forwarding behaviors.\n",
      "id": "89900fd27032ce14",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 326,
      "quote": "Such methods MUST be robust to the wide variety of underlying network forwarding behaviors.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  A PL MAY be designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS\ninto multiple datagrams.\n",
      "id": "7d2b4f9768a4a09e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 333,
      "quote": "*  A PL MAY be designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS into multiple datagrams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It is RECOMMENDED that methods avoid\nforcing an application to use an arbitrary small MPS for\ntransmission while the method is searching for the currently\nsupported PLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "369227d795aa7b34",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 340,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED that methods avoid forcing an application to use an arbitrary small MPS for transmission while the method is searching for the currently supported PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  To assist applications in choosing a suitable data block size, the\nPL is RECOMMENDED to provide a primitive that returns the MPS\nderived from the PLPMTU to the higher layer using the PL.\n",
      "id": "d739b605a8fc12cd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 349,
      "quote": "*  To assist applications in choosing a suitable data block size, the PL is RECOMMENDED to provide a primitive that returns the MPS derived from the PLPMTU to the higher layer using the PL.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  Path validation: It is RECOMMENDED that methods are robust to path\nchanges that could have occurred since the path characteristics\nwere last confirmed and to the possibility of inconsistent path\ninformation being received.\n",
      "id": "df4ba794a2835d68",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 357,
      "quote": "*  Path validation: It is RECOMMENDED that methods are robust to path changes that could have occurred since the path characteristics were last confirmed and to the possibility of inconsistent path information being received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  Datagram reordering: A method is REQUIRED to be robust to the\npossibility that a flow encounters reordering or that the traffic\n(including probe packets) is divided over more than one network\npath.\n",
      "id": "96ae7063b87d2800",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 366,
      "quote": "*  Datagram reordering: A method is REQUIRED to be robust to the possibility that a flow encounters reordering or that the traffic (including probe packets) is divided over more than one network path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  Datagram delay and duplication: The feedback mechanism is REQUIRED\nto be robust to the possibility that packets could be\nsignificantly delayed or duplicated along a network path.\n",
      "id": "f825adf1fa7c9e2c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 375,
      "quote": "*  Datagram delay and duplication: The feedback mechanism is REQUIRED to be robust to the possibility that packets could be significantly delayed or duplicated along a network path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  When to probe: It is RECOMMENDED that methods determine whether\nthe path has changed since it last measured the path.\n",
      "id": "a29f8a4442a4206b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 383,
      "quote": "*  When to probe: It is RECOMMENDED that methods determine whether the path has changed since it last measured the path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver is REQUIRED to be able to distinguish an in-band data\nblock from any added padding.\n",
      "id": "b776d711d76eb315",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "A receiver is REQUIRED to be able to distinguish an in-band data block from any added padding.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DPLPMTUD MAY choose to use only one of these methods to simplify the\nimplementation.\n",
      "id": "c0b53fcb9c8be717",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "DPLPMTUD MAY choose to use only one of these methods to simplify the implementation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Probe messages sent by a PL MUST contain enough information to\nuniquely identify the probe within the Maximum Segment Lifetime\n(e.g., including a unique identifier from the PL or the DPLPMTUD\nimplementation), while being robust to reordering and replay of probe\nresponse and PTB messages.\n",
      "id": "ec7391363b9a607e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "Probe messages sent by a PL MUST contain enough information to uniquely identify the probe within the Maximum Segment Lifetime (e.g., including a unique identifier from the PL or the DPLPMTUD implementation), while being robust to reordering and replay of probe response and PTB messages.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When\nsupported, this mechanism MAY also be used by DPLPMTUD to acknowledge\nreception of a probe packet.\n",
      "id": "d94b4cee295add10",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "When supported, this mechanism MAY also be used by DPLPMTUD to acknowledge reception of a probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A DPLPMTUD method MUST\nNOT rely solely on this method.\n",
      "id": "c5bd299e7ff838d0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "A DPLPMTUD method MUST NOT rely solely on this method.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL MAY inhibit sending probe packets when no application data has\nbeen sent since the previous probe packet.\n",
      "id": "22b63b1edcfd7068",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "A PL MAY inhibit sending probe packets when no application data has been sent since the previous probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL that resumes sending\nuser data MAY continue PLPMTU discovery for each path.\n",
      "id": "f04063ac36d458ac",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "A PL that resumes sending user data MAY continue PLPMTU discovery for each path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid\nthis, a PL MAY be designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS\ninto multiple datagrams.\n",
      "id": "28a00cba4c8560d1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "To avoid this, a PL MAY be designed to segment data blocks larger than the MPS into multiple datagrams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the largest data block that can be sent,\na PL SHOULD provide applications with a primitive that returns the\nMPS, derived from the current PLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "0ef4872dde1a2719",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "To determine the largest data block that can be sent, a PL SHOULD provide applications with a primitive that returns the MPS, derived from the current PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If these packets are lost, the PL MAY segment\nthe data using the new MPS.\n",
      "id": "cb516fe18a43f17a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If these packets are lost, the PL MAY segment the data using the new MPS.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL implementing this specification MUST suspend network layer\nprocessing of outgoing packets that enforces a PMTU\n[RFC1191][RFC8201] for each flow utilizing DPLPMTUD and instead use\nDPLPMTUD to control the size of packets that are sent by a flow.\n",
      "id": "9095083e1c85d23e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "A PL implementing this specification MUST suspend network layer processing of outgoing packets that enforces a PMTU [RFC1191][RFC8201] for each flow utilizing DPLPMTUD and instead use DPLPMTUD to control the size of packets that are sent by a flow.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  A simple implementation MAY ignore received PTB messages, and in\nthis case, the PLPMTU is not updated when a PTB message is\nreceived.\n",
      "id": "a991e413992ccefc",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "*  A simple implementation MAY ignore received PTB messages, and in this case, the PLPMTU is not updated when a PTB message is received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  A PL that supports PTB messages MUST validate these messages\nbefore they are further processed.\n",
      "id": "5139c8528ba5282d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "*  A PL that supports PTB messages MUST validate these messages before they are further processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The PL MUST check the protocol information in the quoted packet\ncarried in an ICMP PTB message payload to validate the message\noriginated from the sending node.\n",
      "id": "03472eef86aa2b14",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "The PL MUST check the protocol information in the quoted packet carried in an ICMP PTB message payload to validate the message originated from the sending node.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The validation SHOULD utilize information that is not simple for an\noff-path attacker to determine [BCP145].\n",
      "id": "84df4d6ffb6bb7d7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "The validation SHOULD utilize information that is not simple for an off-path attacker to determine [BCP145].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PTB message\nthat does not complete the validation MUST NOT be further utilized by\nthe DPLPMTUD method, as discussed in the Security Considerations\nsection (Section 8).\n",
      "id": "d120bf079dabc7f5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "A PTB message that does not complete the validation MUST NOT be further utilized by the DPLPMTUD method, as discussed in the Security Considerations section (Section 8).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "PTB messages that have been validated MAY be utilized by the DPLPMTUD\nalgorithm but MUST NOT be used directly to set the PLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "6c70c9a938b64056",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "PTB messages that have been validated MAY be utilized by the DPLPMTUD algorithm but MUST NOT be used directly to set the PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "MIN_PLPMTU < PL_PTB_SIZE < BASE_PLPMTU\n*  A robust PL MAY enter an error state (see Section 5.2) for an\nIPv4 path when the PL_PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message is\nlarger than or equal to 68 bytes [RFC0791] and when this is\nless than the BASE_PLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "6690481086c8b59c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "MIN_PLPMTU < PL_PTB_SIZE < BASE_PLPMTU *  A robust PL MAY enter an error state (see Section 5.2) for an IPv4 path when the PL_PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message is larger than or equal to 68 bytes [RFC0791] and when this is less than the BASE_PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  A robust PL MAY enter an error state (see Section 5.2) for an\nIPv6 path when the PL_PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message is\nlarger than or equal to 1280 bytes [RFC8200] and when this is\nless than the BASE_PLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "a4db5fb9fae3dbbf",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "*  A robust PL MAY enter an error state (see Section 5.2) for an IPv6 path when the PL_PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message is larger than or equal to 1280 bytes [RFC8200] and when this is less than the BASE_PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The PLPMTU SHOULD\nbe set to BASE_PLPMTU (the PLPMTU is reduced to the BASE_PLPMTU\nto avoid unnecessary packet loss when a black hole is\nencountered).\n",
      "id": "33b7c17fbf7f55e8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "The PLPMTU SHOULD be set to BASE_PLPMTU (the PLPMTU is reduced to the BASE_PLPMTU to avoid unnecessary packet loss when a black hole is encountered).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This value MUST NOT be smaller than 1 second and\nSHOULD be larger than 15 seconds.\n",
      "id": "28327ed3ab1771d5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "This value MUST NOT be smaller than 1 second and SHOULD be larger than 15 seconds.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DPLPMTUD MAY inhibit sending probe packets when no application\ndata has been sent since the previous probe packet.\n",
      "id": "7a682f3323178bd7",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "DPLPMTUD MAY inhibit sending probe packets when no application data has been sent since the previous probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "CONFIRMATION_TIMER:  When an acknowledged PL is used, this timer MUST\nNOT be used.\n",
      "id": "c6a36726d813e53e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "CONFIRMATION_TIMER:  When an acknowledged PL is used, this timer MUST NOT be used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DPLPMTUD MAY inhibit sending probe packets when no application\ndata has been sent since the previous probe packet.\n",
      "id": "d372cdda6d729c52",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "DPLPMTUD MAY inhibit sending probe packets when no application data has been sent since the previous probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application, or PL, MAY\nchoose a smaller MAX_PLPMTU when there is no need to send packets\nlarger than a specific size.\n",
      "id": "948a64a0fac86eac",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "An application, or PL, MAY choose a smaller MAX_PLPMTU when there is no need to send packets larger than a specific size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When using\nIPv4, there is no currently equivalent size specified, and a\ndefault BASE_PLPMTU of 1200 bytes is RECOMMENDED.\n",
      "id": "68fdffb028135e39",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "When using IPv4, there is no currently equivalent size specified, and a default BASE_PLPMTU of 1200 bytes is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When used with an\nacknowledged PL (e.g., SCTP), DPLPMTUD SHOULD NOT continue to\ngenerate PLPMTU probes in this state.\n",
      "id": "5327a5235b534f9b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "When used with an acknowledged PL (e.g., SCTP), DPLPMTUD SHOULD NOT continue to generate PLPMTU probes in this state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nMAX_PLPMTU MAY be reduced by an application that sets a maximum to\nthe size of datagrams it will send.\n",
      "id": "9d44647fccc5ee7a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "The MAX_PLPMTU MAY be reduced by an application that sets a maximum to the size of datagrams it will send.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD select the set of probe packet sizes to\nmaximize the gain in PLPMTU from each search step.\n",
      "id": "e7ad900547fe5183",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD select the set of probe packet sizes to maximize the gain in PLPMTU from each search step.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DPLPMTUD SHOULD only be performed at one layer between a pair of\nendpoints.\n",
      "id": "38b5303dad958518",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "DPLPMTUD SHOULD only be performed at one layer between a pair of endpoints.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PL MUST\nadjust the MPS indicated by DPLPMTUD to account for any additional\noverhead introduced by the PL.\n",
      "id": "47629f24e6d420d0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "A PL MUST adjust the MPS indicated by DPLPMTUD to account for any additional overhead introduced by the PL.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The method SHOULD allow the sender to check\nthe value returned in the response to provide additional protection\nfrom off-path insertion of data [BCP145].\n",
      "id": "941ab7b173c52b72",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "The method SHOULD allow the sender to check the value returned in the response to provide additional protection from off-path insertion of data [BCP145].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application that does not have other higher-layer information\nconfirming connectivity with the remote peer SHOULD implement a\nconnectivity mechanism using acknowledged probe packets before\nentering the BASE state.\n",
      "id": "a82a3d2b82a00784",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "An application that does not have other higher-layer information confirming connectivity with the remote peer SHOULD implement a connectivity mechanism using acknowledged probe packets before entering the BASE state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application that does not have other higher-layer information\nconfirming correct delivery of datagrams SHOULD implement the\nCONFIRMATION_TIMER to periodically send probe packets while in the\nSEARCH_COMPLETE state.\n",
      "id": "e87e24f057def0a5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "An application that does not have other higher-layer information confirming correct delivery of datagrams SHOULD implement the CONFIRMATION_TIMER to periodically send probe packets while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.1.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application that is able and wishes to receive PTB messages MUST\nperform ICMP validation as specified in Section 5.2 of [BCP145].\n",
      "id": "578a3d618baf0b52",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "An application that is able and wishes to receive PTB messages MUST perform ICMP validation as specified in Section 5.2 of [BCP145].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.1.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A validated PTB message MAY be used\nas input to the DPLPMTUD algorithm but MUST NOT be used directly to\nset the PLPMTU.\n",
      "id": "86b8d1fab60c0c16",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "A validated PTB message MAY be used as input to the DPLPMTUD algorithm but MUST NOT be used directly to set the PLPMTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.1.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application SHOULD avoid using\nDPLPMTUD when the underlying transport system provides this\ncapability.\n",
      "id": "a3c17c0d4bc44fd6",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "An application SHOULD avoid using DPLPMTUD when the underlying transport system provides this capability.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since SCTP provides an acknowledged PL, a sender MUST NOT implement\nthe CONFIRMATION_TIMER while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.\n",
      "id": "07f56ff4469f6f9e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 8,
      "quote": "Since SCTP provides an acknowledged PL, a sender MUST NOT implement the CONFIRMATION_TIMER while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Normal ICMP validation MUST be performed as specified in Appendix C\nof [RFC4960].\n",
      "id": "ce332b3c0716ad75",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Normal ICMP validation MUST be performed as specified in Appendix C of [RFC4960].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a PTB message has been validated, the PL_PTB_SIZE calculated\nfrom the PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message SHOULD be used with the\nDPLPMTUD algorithm, provided that the reported PL_PTB_SIZE is less\nthan the current probe size (see Section 4.6).\n",
      "id": "cfa0a47d08a494f7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "When a PTB message has been validated, the PL_PTB_SIZE calculated from the PTB_SIZE reported in the PTB message SHOULD be used with the DPLPMTUD algorithm, provided that the reported PL_PTB_SIZE is less than the current probe size (see Section 4.6).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ICMP validation MUST be performed for PTB messages as specified in\nAppendix C of [RFC4960].\n",
      "id": "c74c52a9794b5ea3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "ICMP validation MUST be performed for PTB messages as specified in Appendix C of [RFC4960].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the\nvalidation is completed, the PL_PTB_SIZE calculated from the PTB_SIZE\nin the PTB message SHOULD be used with the DPLPMTUD providing that\nthe reported PL_PTB_SIZE is less than the current probe size.\n",
      "id": "20200b62c9ffc867",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "When the validation is completed, the PL_PTB_SIZE calculated from the PTB_SIZE in the PTB message SHOULD be used with the DPLPMTUD providing that the reported PL_PTB_SIZE is less than the current probe size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "|  The RECOMMENDED method for determining the MTU of the path is\n|  specified in RFC 8899.\n",
      "id": "0b41803ac4064430",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "|  The RECOMMENDED method for determining the MTU of the path is |  specified in RFC 8899.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since SCTP provides an acknowledged PL, a sender MUST NOT implement\nthe CONFIRMATION_TIMER while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.\n",
      "id": "0bc7290c8fb66ac8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 8,
      "quote": "Since SCTP provides an acknowledged PL, a sender MUST NOT implement the CONFIRMATION_TIMER while in the SEARCH_COMPLETE state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The specification for DPLPMTUD continues the practice of using the PL\nto discover the PMTU but updates RFC4960 with a recommendation to use\nthe method specified in this document: The RECOMMENDED method for\ngenerating probes is to add a chunk consisting only of padding to an\nSCTP message.\n",
      "id": "295dba840b599b42",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "The specification for DPLPMTUD continues the practice of using the PL to discover the PMTU but updates RFC4960 with a recommendation to use the method specified in this document: The RECOMMENDED method for generating probes is to add a chunk consisting only of padding to an SCTP message.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The PAD chunk defined in [RFC4820] SHOULD be attached\nto a minimum-length HEARTBEAT (HB) chunk to build a probe packet.\n",
      "id": "611a41e15f45aa51",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "The PAD chunk defined in [RFC4820] SHOULD be attached to a minimum-length HEARTBEAT (HB) chunk to build a probe packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid excessive load, the interval between individual probe\npackets MUST be at least one RTT, and the interval between rounds of\nprobing is determined by the PMTU_RAISE_TIMER.\n",
      "id": "9fab7c291d85a49e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "To avoid excessive load, the interval between individual probe packets MUST be at least one RTT, and the interval between rounds of probing is determined by the PMTU_RAISE_TIMER.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A node supporting DPLPMTUD\nMUST therefore appropriately validate the payload of PTB messages to\nensure these are received in response to transmitted traffic (i.e., a\nreported error condition that corresponds to a datagram actually sent\nby the path layer, see Section 4.6.1).\n",
      "id": "79e9cc7c3c156ef5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "A node supporting DPLPMTUD MUST therefore appropriately validate the payload of PTB messages to ensure these are received in response to transmitted traffic (i.e., a reported error condition that corresponds to a datagram actually sent by the path layer, see Section 4.6.1).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This processing\nSHOULD be limited to avoid a denial-of-service attack when arbitrary\nheaders are included.\n",
      "id": "0e2cd8d506a237a6",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "This processing SHOULD be limited to avoid a denial-of-service attack when arbitrary headers are included.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\ndesign of a PLPMTUD implementation SHOULD consider how to mitigate\nthe effects of varying path information.\n",
      "id": "536fc1b8f5566060",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "The design of a PLPMTUD implementation SHOULD consider how to mitigate the effects of varying path information.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8899",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Application protocols that use QUIC SHOULD provide guidance on when\ndeferring an idle timeout is appropriate.\n",
      "id": "44627613b95e2cf4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "Application protocols that use QUIC SHOULD provide guidance on when deferring an idle timeout is appropriate.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid excessively small idle timeout periods, endpoints MUST\nincrease the idle timeout period to be at least three times the\ncurrent Probe Timeout (PTO).\n",
      "id": "0b3307cdfba94a32",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "To avoid excessively small idle timeout periods, endpoints MUST increase the idle timeout period to be at least three times the current Probe Timeout (PTO).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD limit the rate at which it generates packets in\nthe closing state.\n",
      "id": "8d14dba9d4ae43a9",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD limit the rate at which it generates packets in the closing state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint's selected connection ID and the QUIC version are\nsufficient information to identify packets for a closing connection;\nthe endpoint MAY discard all other connection state.\n",
      "id": "5f539564bdd36e2d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "An endpoint's selected connection ID and the QUIC version are sufficient information to identify packets for a closing connection; the endpoint MAY discard all other connection state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint MAY retain packet protection keys for incoming packets to\nallow it to read and process a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame.\n",
      "id": "2c6d429cf7816984",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY retain packet protection keys for incoming packets to allow it to read and process a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY drop packet protection keys when entering the closing\nstate and send a packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in\nresponse to any UDP datagram that is received.\n",
      "id": "41bad1443b771c47",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY drop packet protection keys when entering the closing state and send a packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in response to any UDP datagram that is received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid being used for an amplification attack,\nsuch endpoints MUST limit the cumulative size of packets it sends to\nthree times the cumulative size of the packets that are received and\nattributed to the connection.\n",
      "id": "1d761ac8bfe1dc8f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "To avoid being used for an amplification attack, such endpoints MUST limit the cumulative size of packets it sends to three times the cumulative size of the packets that are received and attributed to the connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To minimize the state that an endpoint\nmaintains for a closing connection, endpoints MAY send the exact same\npacket in response to any received packet.\n",
      "id": "1ae6a2f1dc8366bd",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "To minimize the state that an endpoint maintains for a closing connection, endpoints MAY send the exact same packet in response to any received packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint in the closing state MUST either discard\npackets received from an unvalidated address or limit the cumulative\nsize of packets it sends to an unvalidated address to three times the\nsize of packets it receives from that address.\n",
      "id": "e825b24467f1ba69",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "An endpoint in the closing state MUST either discard packets received from an unvalidated address or limit the cumulative size of packets it sends to an unvalidated address to three times the size of packets it receives from that address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While otherwise identical to the closing state, an\nendpoint in the draining state MUST NOT send any packets.\n",
      "id": "67c05da063e0b92d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "While otherwise identical to the closing state, an endpoint in the draining state MUST NOT send any packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame MAY send a single\npacket containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame before entering the\ndraining state, using a NO_ERROR code if appropriate.\n",
      "id": "0a48c1a971d3a227",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame MAY send a single packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame before entering the draining state, using a NO_ERROR code if appropriate.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint\nMUST NOT send further packets.\n",
      "id": "4a76e834880c4198",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send further packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY enter the draining state from the closing state if it\nreceives a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame, which indicates that the peer is\nalso closing or draining.\n",
      "id": "10c1bd877ec6e935",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY enter the draining state from the closing state if it receives a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame, which indicates that the peer is also closing or draining.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After the handshake is confirmed (see\nSection 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), an endpoint MUST send any\nCONNECTION_CLOSE frames in a 1-RTT packet.\n",
      "id": "8f9a2bf6f1053e4f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "After the handshake is confirmed (see Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), an endpoint MUST send any CONNECTION_CLOSE frames in a 1-RTT packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, prior to\nconfirming the handshake, it is possible that more advanced packet\nprotection keys are not available to the peer, so another\nCONNECTION_CLOSE frame MAY be sent in a packet that uses a lower\npacket protection level.\n",
      "id": "0f0732486f25819a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "However, prior to confirming the handshake, it is possible that more advanced packet protection keys are not available to the peer, so another CONNECTION_CLOSE frame MAY be sent in a packet that uses a lower packet protection level.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Under these\ncircumstances, a server SHOULD send a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in\nboth Handshake and Initial packets to ensure that at least one of\nthem is processable by the client.\n",
      "id": "e9df32821f4c71cb",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "Under these circumstances, a server SHOULD send a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in both Handshake and Initial packets to ensure that at least one of them is processable by the client.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  Prior to confirming the handshake, a peer might be unable to\nprocess 1-RTT packets, so an endpoint SHOULD send a\nCONNECTION_CLOSE frame in both Handshake and 1-RTT packets.\n",
      "id": "fd95d60eec6c962d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "*  Prior to confirming the handshake, a peer might be unable to process 1-RTT packets, so an endpoint SHOULD send a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in both Handshake and 1-RTT packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nserver SHOULD also send a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in an Initial\npacket.\n",
      "id": "bf4286125401b7dd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD also send a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame in an Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1d MUST be replaced by a\nCONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1c when sending the frame in Initial or\nHandshake packets.\n",
      "id": "046cdacc40a27a85",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "A CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1d MUST be replaced by a CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1c when sending the frame in Initial or Handshake packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST clear the value of the\nReason Phrase field and SHOULD use the APPLICATION_ERROR code when\nconverting to a CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1c.\n",
      "id": "112388f08907f460",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST clear the value of the Reason Phrase field and SHOULD use the APPLICATION_ERROR code when converting to a CONNECTION_CLOSE of type 0x1c.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For this\nreason, endpoints MAY discard packets rather than immediately close\nif errors are detected in packets that lack authentication.\n",
      "id": "39a14a133ff52bcf",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "For this reason, endpoints MAY discard packets rather than immediately close if errors are detected in packets that lack authentication.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These states SHOULD persist for at least three\ntimes the current PTO interval as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY].\n",
      "id": "f5177e72b112b986",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "These states SHOULD persist for at least three times the current PTO interval as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints that have some alternative means to ensure that late-\narriving packets do not induce a response, such as those that are\nable to close the UDP socket, MAY end these states earlier to allow\nfor faster resource recovery.\n",
      "id": "4392b1b054c7fe62",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Endpoints that have some alternative means to ensure that late- arriving packets do not induce a response, such as those that are able to close the UDP socket, MAY end these states earlier to allow for faster resource recovery.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers that retain an open socket for\naccepting new connections SHOULD NOT end the closing or draining\nstate early.\n",
      "id": "2fe7d4209354393c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "Servers that retain an open socket for accepting new connections SHOULD NOT end the closing or draining state early.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once its closing or draining state ends, an endpoint SHOULD discard\nall connection state.\n",
      "id": "5d9ec33ac77943c1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "Once its closing or draining state ends, an endpoint SHOULD discard all connection state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in\nresponse to any further incoming packets belonging to this\nconnection.\n",
      "id": "4ca28b0171ff7324",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "The endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to any further incoming packets belonging to this connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY skip this check if any packet from a datagram is\nsuccessfully processed.\n",
      "id": "d0e30ee6f9db55ef",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY skip this check if any packet from a datagram is successfully processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, the comparison MUST be performed\nwhen the first packet in an incoming datagram either cannot be\nassociated with a connection or cannot be decrypted.\n",
      "id": "d2adcfa52fb2ee35",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "However, the comparison MUST be performed when the first packet in an incoming datagram either cannot be associated with a connection or cannot be decrypted.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT check for any stateless reset tokens associated\nwith connection IDs it has not used or for connection IDs that have\nbeen retired.\n",
      "id": "a4e61df46283768d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT check for any stateless reset tokens associated with connection IDs it has not used or for connection IDs that have been retired.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When comparing a datagram to stateless reset token values, endpoints\nMUST perform the comparison without leaking information about the\nvalue of the token.\n",
      "id": "bc919b414dd7f3a2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "When comparing a datagram to stateless reset token values, endpoints MUST perform the comparison without leaking information about the value of the token.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the last 16 bytes of the datagram are identical in value to a\nstateless reset token, the endpoint MUST enter the draining period\nand not send any further packets on this connection.\n",
      "id": "4f192a1373346f03",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "If the last 16 bytes of the datagram are identical in value to a stateless reset token, the endpoint MUST enter the draining period and not send any further packets on this connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The stateless reset token MUST be difficult to guess.\n",
      "id": "1b1544dce205ff50",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "The stateless reset token MUST be difficult to guess.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that uses this design MUST\neither use the same connection ID length for all connections or\nencode the length of the connection ID such that it can be recovered\nwithout state.\n",
      "id": "71fb3b8b4f3f0976",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "An endpoint that uses this design MUST either use the same connection ID length for all connections or encode the length of the connection ID such that it can be recovered without state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This method for\nchoosing the stateless reset token means that the combination of\nconnection ID and static key MUST NOT be used for another connection.\n",
      "id": "5ae68823a27a9cb2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "This method for choosing the stateless reset token means that the combination of connection ID and static key MUST NOT be used for another connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A connection ID from a connection\nthat is reset by revealing the stateless reset token MUST NOT be\nreused for new connections at nodes that share a static key.\n",
      "id": "40d93bee906c33a7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "A connection ID from a connection that is reset by revealing the stateless reset token MUST NOT be reused for new connections at nodes that share a static key.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The same stateless reset token MUST NOT be used for multiple\nconnection IDs.\n",
      "id": "9e77284acc696c60",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "The same stateless reset token MUST NOT be used for multiple connection IDs.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints are not required to compare new values\nagainst all previous values, but a duplicate value MAY be treated as\na connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "2295b7ab5640552a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "Endpoints are not required to compare new values against all previous values, but a duplicate value MAY be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST ensure that every Stateless Reset that it sends is\nsmaller than the packet that triggered it, unless it maintains state\nsufficient to prevent looping.\n",
      "id": "0b802499a0d09048",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST ensure that every Stateless Reset that it sends is smaller than the packet that triggered it, unless it maintains state sufficient to prevent looping.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to receiving a packet\nthat it cannot associate with an active connection.\n",
      "id": "2969e01135d76d7e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to receiving a packet that it cannot associate with an active connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that wishes to communicate a fatal\nconnection error MUST use a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame if it is able.\n",
      "id": "9bae62a78dfbc091",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "An endpoint that wishes to communicate a fatal connection error MUST use a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame if it is able.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The remainder of the first byte\nand an arbitrary number of bytes following it are set to values that\nSHOULD be indistinguishable from random.\n",
      "id": "0ad177a32e4a89f7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "The remainder of the first byte and an arbitrary number of bytes following it are set to values that SHOULD be indistinguishable from random.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To achieve that end,\nthe endpoint SHOULD ensure that all packets it sends are at least 22\nbytes longer than the minimum connection ID length that it requests\nthe peer to include in its packets, adding PADDING frames as\nnecessary.\n",
      "id": "e897e633e355bf3f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "To achieve that end, the endpoint SHOULD ensure that all packets it sends are at least 22 bytes longer than the minimum connection ID length that it requests the peer to include in its packets, adding PADDING frames as necessary.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint that sends a Stateless Reset in response to a packet that is\n43 bytes or shorter SHOULD send a Stateless Reset that is one byte\nshorter than the packet it responds to.\n",
      "id": "ef7878b7d9f7dd1e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 169,
      "quote": "An endpoint that sends a Stateless Reset in response to a packet that is 43 bytes or shorter SHOULD send a Stateless Reset that is one byte shorter than the packet it responds to.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a Stateless Reset that is three times or\nmore larger than the packet it receives to avoid being used for\namplification.\n",
      "id": "d0c38dd3fc97ca60",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 178,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a Stateless Reset that is three times or more larger than the packet it receives to avoid being used for amplification.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST discard packets that are too small to be valid QUIC\npackets.\n",
      "id": "5585bb546cb2d213",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 186,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST discard packets that are too small to be valid QUIC packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST send Stateless Resets formatted as a packet with a\nshort header.\n",
      "id": "7ab7c9678b3a4715",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 193,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST send Stateless Resets formatted as a packet with a short header.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, endpoints MUST treat any packet ending in a\nvalid stateless reset token as a Stateless Reset, as other QUIC\nversions might allow the use of a long header.\n",
      "id": "b62bbc555f50f04a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "However, endpoints MUST treat any packet ending in a valid stateless reset token as a Stateless Reset, as other QUIC versions might allow the use of a long header.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to a packet with a\nlong header.\n",
      "id": "afa9c12b9e90b922",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 208,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to a packet with a long header.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY discard connection state if it does not have a\nvalidated path on which it can send packets; see Section 8.2.\n",
      "id": "ffe4a1daea6133b1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY discard connection state if it does not have a validated path on which it can send packets; see Section 8.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Errors that result in the connection being unusable, such as an\nobvious violation of protocol semantics or corruption of state that\naffects an entire connection, MUST be signaled using a\nCONNECTION_CLOSE frame (Section 19.19).\n",
      "id": "a97212b8bde7b75a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "Errors that result in the connection being unusable, such as an obvious violation of protocol semantics or corruption of state that affects an entire connection, MUST be signaled using a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame (Section 19.19).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint SHOULD be prepared to retransmit a packet containing a\nCONNECTION_CLOSE frame if it receives more packets on a terminated\nconnection.\n",
      "id": "5c2c98c926f30700",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD be prepared to retransmit a packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame if it receives more packets on a terminated connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As the AEAD for Initial packets does not provide strong\nauthentication, an endpoint MAY discard an invalid Initial packet.\n",
      "id": "abc116b96cbf731e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "As the AEAD for Initial packets does not provide strong authentication, an endpoint MAY discard an invalid Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "RESET_STREAM MUST only be instigated by the\napplication protocol that uses QUIC.\n",
      "id": "0fd96d89d90290cb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "RESET_STREAM MUST only be instigated by the application protocol that uses QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Application protocols SHOULD define rules for handling streams that\nare prematurely canceled by either endpoint.\n",
      "id": "cd19b17307068d73",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Application protocols SHOULD define rules for handling streams that are prematurely canceled by either endpoint.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that detects an error SHOULD signal the existence of that\nerror to its peer.\n",
      "id": "d443e28b6f43ba03",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "An endpoint that detects an error SHOULD signal the existence of that error to its peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The most appropriate error code (Section 20) SHOULD be included in\nthe frame that signals the error.\n",
      "id": "4e87d964447c43eb",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "The most appropriate error code (Section 20) SHOULD be included in the frame that signals the error.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, an endpoint MAY use any applicable error\ncode when it detects an error condition; a generic error code (such\nas PROTOCOL_VIOLATION or INTERNAL_ERROR) can always be used in place\nof specific error codes.\n",
      "id": "4851646b57ece490",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "In particular, an endpoint MAY use any applicable error code when it detects an error condition; a generic error code (such as PROTOCOL_VIOLATION or INTERNAL_ERROR) can always be used in place of specific error codes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nstateless reset MUST NOT be used by an endpoint that has the state\nnecessary to send a frame on the connection.\n",
      "id": "47df2f0ddbb1541c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "A stateless reset MUST NOT be used by an endpoint that has the state necessary to send a frame on the connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receivers MUST be able to\nprocess coalesced packets.\n",
      "id": "096995d733046340",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Receivers MUST be able to process coalesced packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD include multiple frames in a single packet if they\nare to be sent at the same encryption level, instead of coalescing\nmultiple packets at the same encryption level.\n",
      "id": "bdf8dbf5bd174d7f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD include multiple frames in a single packet if they are to be sent at the same encryption level, instead of coalescing multiple packets at the same encryption level.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receivers MAY route based on the information in the first packet\ncontained in a UDP datagram.\n",
      "id": "74d27e5d76a69ce4",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "Receivers MAY route based on the information in the first packet contained in a UDP datagram.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Senders MUST NOT coalesce QUIC packets\nwith different connection IDs into a single UDP datagram.\n",
      "id": "2ddaf28f87de81dc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Senders MUST NOT coalesce QUIC packets with different connection IDs into a single UDP datagram.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receivers\nSHOULD ignore any subsequent packets with a different Destination\nConnection ID than the first packet in the datagram.\n",
      "id": "a2b493ace874f9d7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "Receivers SHOULD ignore any subsequent packets with a different Destination Connection ID than the first packet in the datagram.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The receiver of coalesced QUIC packets MUST\nindividually process each QUIC packet and separately acknowledge\nthem, as if they were received as the payload of different UDP\ndatagrams.\n",
      "id": "5497024bdee02670",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "The receiver of coalesced QUIC packets MUST individually process each QUIC packet and separately acknowledge them, as if they were received as the payload of different UDP datagrams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For example, if decryption fails (because the keys are\nnot available or for any other reason), the receiver MAY either\ndiscard or buffer the packet for later processing and MUST attempt to\nprocess the remaining packets.\n",
      "id": "b2f62b954c93758e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "For example, if decryption fails (because the keys are not available or for any other reason), the receiver MAY either discard or buffer the packet for later processing and MUST attempt to process the remaining packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Subsequent packets sent in the same packet\nnumber space MUST increase the packet number by at least one.\n",
      "id": "2ab17ec3d5552d8f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "Subsequent packets sent in the same packet number space MUST increase the packet number by at least one.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A QUIC endpoint MUST NOT reuse a packet number within the same packet\nnumber space in one connection.\n",
      "id": "ae02d5e1facba69b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "A QUIC endpoint MUST NOT reuse a packet number within the same packet number space in one connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the packet number for sending\nreaches 2^62-1, the sender MUST close the connection without sending\na CONNECTION_CLOSE frame or any further packets; an endpoint MAY send\na Stateless Reset (Section 10.3) in response to further packets that\nit receives.\n",
      "id": "de7948abd33ab26e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "If the packet number for sending reaches 2^62-1, the sender MUST close the connection without sending a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame or any further packets; an endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset (Section 10.3) in response to further packets that it receives.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MUST discard a newly unprotected packet unless it is\ncertain that it has not processed another packet with the same packet\nnumber from the same packet number space.\n",
      "id": "2299fefbe8438be1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST discard a newly unprotected packet unless it is certain that it has not processed another packet with the same packet number from the same packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Duplicate suppression MUST\nhappen after removing packet protection for the reasons described in\nSection 9.5 of [QUIC-TLS].\n",
      "id": "05a3fbf24fae034d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "Duplicate suppression MUST happen after removing packet protection for the reasons described in Section 9.5 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The payload of a packet that contains frames MUST contain at least\none frame, and MAY contain multiple frames and multiple frame types.\n",
      "id": "3fea2267a4ed4acc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "The payload of a packet that contains frames MUST contain at least one frame, and MAY contain multiple frames and multiple frame types.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a packet containing no frames as a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "8bf875fa01f65359",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 158,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a packet containing no frames as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST treat\nreceipt of a frame in a packet type that is not permitted as a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "c31deb3361ccc09d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a frame in a packet type that is not permitted as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST treat the receipt of a frame of unknown type as a\nconnection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "7fa35a10de132b74",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 173,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat the receipt of a frame of unknown type as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To ensure simple and efficient\nimplementations of frame parsing, a frame type MUST use the shortest\npossible encoding.\n",
      "id": "1587d38fd5f2a692",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "To ensure simple and efficient implementations of frame parsing, a frame type MUST use the shortest possible encoding.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY treat the\nreceipt of a frame type that uses a longer encoding than necessary as\na connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "77a062f7e8eddafa",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY treat the receipt of a frame type that uses a longer encoding than necessary as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  PADDING, PING, and CRYPTO frames MAY appear in any packet number\nspace.\n",
      "id": "96e6cfb24e89a5cb",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "*  PADDING, PING, and CRYPTO frames MAY appear in any packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  CONNECTION_CLOSE frames signaling errors at the QUIC layer (type\n0x1c) MAY appear in any packet number space.\n",
      "id": "d13adf1d8ad9d3f0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "*  CONNECTION_CLOSE frames signaling errors at the QUIC layer (type 0x1c) MAY appear in any packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "CONNECTION_CLOSE\nframes signaling application errors (type 0x1d) MUST only appear\nin the application data packet number space.\n",
      "id": "aecc66925f70e3a6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "CONNECTION_CLOSE frames signaling application errors (type 0x1d) MUST only appear in the application data packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  ACK frames MAY appear in any packet number space but can only\nacknowledge packets that appeared in that packet number space.\n",
      "id": "4a4e246d4f4a04eb",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "*  ACK frames MAY appear in any packet number space but can only acknowledge packets that appeared in that packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  All other frame types MUST only be sent in the application data\npacket number space.\n",
      "id": "e4361354d7929b13",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "*  All other frame types MUST only be sent in the application data packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY treat receipt\nof these frames in 0-RTT packets as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "c997b4b4e691e176",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "A server MAY treat receipt of these frames in 0-RTT packets as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/12.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-12.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A packet MUST NOT be acknowledged until packet protection has been\nsuccessfully removed and all frames contained in the packet have been\nprocessed.\n",
      "id": "3aeadc07c91094af",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "A packet MUST NOT be acknowledged until packet protection has been successfully removed and all frames contained in the packet have been processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of an acknowledgment for a packet it\ndid not send as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, if it\nis able to detect the condition.\n",
      "id": "6a86f74e109e20e7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of an acknowledgment for a packet it did not send as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, if it is able to detect the condition.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Every packet SHOULD be acknowledged at least once, and ack-eliciting\npackets MUST be acknowledged at least once within the maximum delay\nan endpoint communicated using the max_ack_delay transport parameter;\nsee Section 18.2.\n",
      "id": "624bf1d4ec9659de",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Every packet SHOULD be acknowledged at least once, and ack-eliciting packets MUST be acknowledged at least once within the maximum delay an endpoint communicated using the max_ack_delay transport parameter; see Section 18.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST acknowledge all ack-eliciting Initial and Handshake\npackets immediately and all ack-eliciting 0-RTT and 1-RTT packets\nwithin its advertised max_ack_delay, with the following exception.\n",
      "id": "7510ff8cb2a15d34",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST acknowledge all ack-eliciting Initial and Handshake packets immediately and all ack-eliciting 0-RTT and 1-RTT packets within its advertised max_ack_delay, with the following exception.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since packets containing only ACK frames are not congestion\ncontrolled, an endpoint MUST NOT send more than one such packet in\nresponse to receiving an ack-eliciting packet.\n",
      "id": "a49840b2bcb6a47c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Since packets containing only ACK frames are not congestion controlled, an endpoint MUST NOT send more than one such packet in response to receiving an ack-eliciting packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a non-ack-eliciting packet in response to a\nnon-ack-eliciting packet, even if there are packet gaps that precede\nthe received packet.\n",
      "id": "8e51930e72aef839",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a non-ack-eliciting packet in response to a non-ack-eliciting packet, even if there are packet gaps that precede the received packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD\nsend an ACK frame with other frames when there are new ack-eliciting\npackets to acknowledge.\n",
      "id": "a0b28d7fd0268253",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD send an ACK frame with other frames when there are new ack-eliciting packets to acknowledge.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When only non-ack-eliciting packets need to\nbe acknowledged, an endpoint MAY choose not to send an ACK frame with\noutgoing frames until an ack-eliciting packet has been received.\n",
      "id": "7b5ff51fc5772ac6",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "When only non-ack-eliciting packets need to be acknowledged, an endpoint MAY choose not to send an ACK frame with outgoing frames until an ack-eliciting packet has been received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In\nthat case, an endpoint MUST NOT send an ack-eliciting frame in all\npackets that would otherwise be non-ack-eliciting, to avoid an\ninfinite feedback loop of acknowledgments.\n",
      "id": "d805d94f04eedb05",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "In that case, an endpoint MUST NOT send an ack-eliciting frame in all packets that would otherwise be non-ack-eliciting, to avoid an infinite feedback loop of acknowledgments.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to assist loss detection at the sender, an endpoint SHOULD\ngenerate and send an ACK frame without delay when it receives an ack-\neliciting packet either:\n",
      "id": "a0a2ad035e109503",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 130,
      "quote": "In order to assist loss detection at the sender, an endpoint SHOULD generate and send an ACK frame without delay when it receives an ack- eliciting packet either:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Similarly, packets marked with the ECN Congestion Experienced (CE)\ncodepoint in the IP header SHOULD be acknowledged immediately, to\nreduce the peer's response time to congestion events.\n",
      "id": "4c8e5eaf0e401d5b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "Similarly, packets marked with the ECN Congestion Experienced (CE) codepoint in the IP header SHOULD be acknowledged immediately, to reduce the peer's response time to congestion events.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver SHOULD send an ACK frame after receiving at least two ack-\neliciting packets.\n",
      "id": "2068ec42a8a04be5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "A receiver SHOULD send an ACK frame after receiving at least two ack- eliciting packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MAY process multiple available packets before determining\nwhether to send an ACK frame in response.\n",
      "id": "70e9680900d746f6",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "A receiver MAY process multiple available packets before determining whether to send an ACK frame in response.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ACK frames SHOULD always acknowledge the most recently received\npackets, and the more out of order the packets are, the more\nimportant it is to send an updated ACK frame quickly, to prevent the\npeer from declaring a packet as lost and spuriously retransmitting\nthe frames it contains.\n",
      "id": "baea631b6a5a87fd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "ACK frames SHOULD always acknowledge the most recently received packets, and the more out of order the packets are, the more important it is to send an updated ACK frame quickly, to prevent the peer from declaring a packet as lost and spuriously retransmitting the frames it contains.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After receiving\nacknowledgments for an ACK frame, the receiver SHOULD stop tracking\nthose acknowledged ACK Ranges.\n",
      "id": "e953848e7c0495f0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "After receiving acknowledgments for an ACK frame, the receiver SHOULD stop tracking those acknowledged ACK Ranges.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receivers MAY also limit ACK\nframe size further to preserve space for other frames or to limit the\ncapacity that acknowledgments consume.\n",
      "id": "6bb7789727babc35",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "Receivers MAY also limit ACK frame size further to preserve space for other frames or to limit the capacity that acknowledgments consume.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MUST retain an ACK Range unless it can ensure that it will\nnot subsequently accept packets with numbers in that range.\n",
      "id": "aa6fdf392b1160b6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST retain an ACK Range unless it can ensure that it will not subsequently accept packets with numbers in that range.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receivers can discard all ACK Ranges, but they MUST retain the\nlargest packet number that has been successfully processed, as that\nis used to recover packet numbers from subsequent packets; see\nSection 17.1.\n",
      "id": "e832b381dd522a53",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "Receivers can discard all ACK Ranges, but they MUST retain the largest packet number that has been successfully processed, as that is used to recover packet numbers from subsequent packets; see Section 17.1.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver SHOULD include an ACK Range containing the largest\nreceived packet number in every ACK frame.\n",
      "id": "664a97448c32bc77",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "A receiver SHOULD include an ACK Range containing the largest received packet number in every ACK frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT include delays that it\ndoes not control when populating the ACK Delay field in an ACK frame.\n",
      "id": "e4e06b69acc0b3d2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT include delays that it does not control when populating the ACK Delay field in an ACK frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, endpoints SHOULD include buffering delays caused by\nunavailability of decryption keys, since these delays can be large\nand are likely to be non-repeating.\n",
      "id": "76e91969a60b2a96",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "However, endpoints SHOULD include buffering delays caused by unavailability of decryption keys, since these delays can be large and are likely to be non-repeating.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the measured acknowledgment delay is larger than its\nmax_ack_delay, an endpoint SHOULD report the measured delay.\n",
      "id": "d3db2eaac21becd9",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "When the measured acknowledgment delay is larger than its max_ack_delay, an endpoint SHOULD report the measured delay.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ACK frames MUST only be carried in a packet that has the same packet\nnumber space as the packet being acknowledged; see Section 12.1.\n",
      "id": "8b32ad028401db4e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "ACK frames MUST only be carried in a packet that has the same packet number space as the packet being acknowledged; see Section 12.1.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For\ninstance, packets that are protected with 1-RTT keys MUST be\nacknowledged in packets that are also protected with 1-RTT keys.\n",
      "id": "2f6a8178daf9b2f8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "For instance, packets that are protected with 1-RTT keys MUST be acknowledged in packets that are also protected with 1-RTT keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Packets that a client sends with 0-RTT packet protection MUST be\nacknowledged by the server in packets protected by 1-RTT keys.\n",
      "id": "4bc37bcedec36d19",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Packets that a client sends with 0-RTT packet protection MUST be acknowledged by the server in packets protected by 1-RTT keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To\navoid a deadlock, a sender SHOULD ensure that other frames are sent\nperiodically in addition to PADDING frames to elicit acknowledgments\nfrom the receiver.\n",
      "id": "80824d603ba82977",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "To avoid a deadlock, a sender SHOULD ensure that other frames are sent periodically in addition to PADDING frames to elicit acknowledgments from the receiver.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When sending a packet for any reason, an endpoint SHOULD attempt to\ninclude an ACK frame if one has not been sent recently.\n",
      "id": "e340f9bc61c4f8d8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "When sending a packet for any reason, an endpoint SHOULD attempt to include an ACK frame if one has not been sent recently.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The content of a RESET_STREAM frame MUST NOT change when it is\nsent again.\n",
      "id": "b0c97c0e57703bcc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "The content of a RESET_STREAM frame MUST NOT change when it is sent again.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD stop sending\nMAX_STREAM_DATA frames when the receiving part of the stream\nenters a \"Size Known\" or \"Reset Recvd\" state.\n",
      "id": "efac6a875879dd5a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD stop sending MAX_STREAM_DATA frames when the receiving part of the stream enters a \"Size Known\" or \"Reset Recvd\" state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  The HANDSHAKE_DONE frame MUST be retransmitted until it is\nacknowledged.\n",
      "id": "8fa2d270bb2a5baf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "*  The HANDSHAKE_DONE frame MUST be retransmitted until it is acknowledged.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD prioritize retransmission of data over sending new\ndata, unless priorities specified by the application indicate\notherwise; see Section 2.3.\n",
      "id": "48b434ccf3946eb0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 157,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD prioritize retransmission of data over sending new data, unless priorities specified by the application indicate otherwise; see Section 2.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MUST accept packets containing an\noutdated frame, such as a MAX_DATA frame carrying a smaller maximum\ndata value than one found in an older packet.\n",
      "id": "584bccb28ddec537",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST accept packets containing an outdated frame, such as a MAX_DATA frame carrying a smaller maximum data value than one found in an older packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD avoid retransmitting information from packets once\nthey are acknowledged.\n",
      "id": "31df123045bb9162",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 173,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD avoid retransmitting information from packets once they are acknowledged.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon detecting losses, a sender MUST take appropriate congestion\ncontrol action.\n",
      "id": "c0775727c71e2380",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "Upon detecting losses, a sender MUST take appropriate congestion control action.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Even if an endpoint does not set an ECT field in packets it sends,\nthe endpoint MUST provide feedback about ECN markings it receives, if\nthese are accessible.\n",
      "id": "9ef49545a257a1f9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Even if an endpoint does not set an ECT field in packets it sends, the endpoint MUST provide feedback about ECN markings it receives, if these are accessible.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT fail ECN validation as a result of\nprocessing an ACK frame that does not increase the largest\nacknowledged packet number.\n",
      "id": "56ab6d07a112cea4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT fail ECN validation as a result of processing an ACK frame that does not increase the largest acknowledged packet number.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If validation fails, then the endpoint MUST disable ECN.\n",
      "id": "5c8fae2c42619812",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "If validation fails, then the endpoint MUST disable ECN.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Even if validation fails, an endpoint MAY revalidate ECN for the same\npath at any later time in the connection.\n",
      "id": "b96a93169bb27707",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Even if validation fails, an endpoint MAY revalidate ECN for the same path at any later time in the connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon successful validation, an endpoint MAY continue to set an ECT\ncodepoint in subsequent packets it sends, with the expectation that\nthe path is ECN capable.\n",
      "id": "cf3efff22840c957",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Upon successful validation, an endpoint MAY continue to set an ECT codepoint in subsequent packets it sends, with the expectation that the path is ECN capable.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Network routing and path elements can\nchange mid-connection; an endpoint MUST disable ECN if validation\nlater fails.\n",
      "id": "db406a7f5a9f72f8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "Network routing and path elements can change mid-connection; an endpoint MUST disable ECN if validation later fails.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MAY use other methods\ndefined in RFCs; see [RFC8311].\n",
      "id": "133a9699048fcb5c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY use other methods defined in RFCs; see [RFC8311].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender\nMAY wait for a short period of time to collect multiple frames before\nsending a packet that is not maximally packed, to avoid sending out\nlarge numbers of small packets.\n",
      "id": "48397a861d02ef05",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "A sender MAY wait for a short period of time to collect multiple frames before sending a packet that is not maximally packed, to avoid sending out large numbers of small packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An implementation MAY use knowledge\nabout application sending behavior or heuristics to determine whether\nand for how long to wait.\n",
      "id": "c0bce6195ef87f33",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "An implementation MAY use knowledge about application sending behavior or heuristics to determine whether and for how long to wait.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/13.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-13",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST expand the payload of all UDP datagrams carrying\nInitial packets to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram\nsize of 1200 bytes by adding PADDING frames to the Initial packet or\nby coalescing the Initial packet; see Section 12.2.\n",
      "id": "5adfe775da303680",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "A client MUST expand the payload of all UDP datagrams carrying Initial packets to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes by adding PADDING frames to the Initial packet or by coalescing the Initial packet; see Section 12.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Similarly, a server MUST expand the payload of all UDP\ndatagrams carrying ack-eliciting Initial packets to at least the\nsmallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.\n",
      "id": "a62fc545d8528f00",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Similarly, a server MUST expand the payload of all UDP datagrams carrying ack-eliciting Initial packets to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Datagrams containing Initial packets MAY exceed 1200 bytes if the\nsender believes that the network path and peer both support the size\nthat it chooses.\n",
      "id": "b6a82e793b248221",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Datagrams containing Initial packets MAY exceed 1200 bytes if the sender believes that the network path and peer both support the size that it chooses.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST discard an Initial packet that is carried in a UDP\ndatagram with a payload that is smaller than the smallest allowed\nmaximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.\n",
      "id": "4bf0821ec968fed9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "A server MUST discard an Initial packet that is carried in a UDP datagram with a payload that is smaller than the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY also immediately\nclose the connection by sending a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame with an\nerror code of PROTOCOL_VIOLATION; see Section 10.2.3.\n",
      "id": "8609e6a275962356",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "A server MAY also immediately close the connection by sending a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame with an error code of PROTOCOL_VIOLATION; see Section 10.2.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST also limit the number of bytes it sends before\nvalidating the address of the client; see Section 8.\n",
      "id": "81bd28cf220efd1b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "The server MUST also limit the number of bytes it sends before validating the address of the client; see Section 8.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST ignore an ICMP message that claims the PMTU has\ndecreased below QUIC's smallest allowed maximum datagram size.\n",
      "id": "92fbed1cb9a61e8a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST ignore an ICMP message that claims the PMTU has decreased below QUIC's smallest allowed maximum datagram size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC endpoints using PMTUD SHOULD validate ICMP messages to protect\nfrom packet injection as specified in [RFC8201] and Section 5.2 of\n[RFC8085].\n",
      "id": "77fb50c4e403f1a0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "QUIC endpoints using PMTUD SHOULD validate ICMP messages to protect from packet injection as specified in [RFC8201] and Section 5.2 of [RFC8085].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This validation SHOULD use the quoted packet supplied in\nthe payload of an ICMP message to associate the message with a\ncorresponding transport connection (see Section 4.6.1 of [DPLPMTUD]).\n",
      "id": "36650dd545d6d8f9",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "This validation SHOULD use the quoted packet supplied in the payload of an ICMP message to associate the message with a corresponding transport connection (see Section 4.6.1 of [DPLPMTUD]).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "ICMP message validation MUST include matching IP addresses and UDP\nports [RFC8085] and, when possible, connection IDs to an active QUIC\nsession.\n",
      "id": "52d8fe8c43d7a52e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "ICMP message validation MUST include matching IP addresses and UDP ports [RFC8085] and, when possible, connection IDs to an active QUIC session.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The endpoint SHOULD ignore all ICMP messages that fail\nvalidation.\n",
      "id": "fb3ebb8acb482d53",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "The endpoint SHOULD ignore all ICMP messages that fail validation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT increase the PMTU based on ICMP messages; see\nItem 6 in Section 3 of [DPLPMTUD].\n",
      "id": "681b8bb874170dcc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT increase the PMTU based on ICMP messages; see Item 6 in Section 3 of [DPLPMTUD].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any reduction in QUIC's maximum\ndatagram size in response to ICMP messages MAY be provisional until\nQUIC's loss detection algorithm determines that the quoted packet has\nactually been lost.\n",
      "id": "d458f880a1611a92",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Any reduction in QUIC's maximum datagram size in response to ICMP messages MAY be provisional until QUIC's loss detection algorithm determines that the quoted packet has actually been lost.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD use DPLPMTUD (Section 14.3) or PMTUD\n(Section 14.2.1) to determine whether the path to a destination will\nsupport a desired maximum datagram size without fragmentation.\n",
      "id": "cd3f6fe45abb0cbd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD use DPLPMTUD (Section 14.3) or PMTUD (Section 14.2.1) to determine whether the path to a destination will support a desired maximum datagram size without fragmentation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In\nthe absence of these mechanisms, QUIC endpoints SHOULD NOT send\ndatagrams larger than the smallest allowed maximum datagram size.\n",
      "id": "2b7605d6acde88e5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "In the absence of these mechanisms, QUIC endpoints SHOULD NOT send datagrams larger than the smallest allowed maximum datagram size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All QUIC\npackets that are not sent in a PMTU probe SHOULD be sized to fit\nwithin the maximum datagram size to avoid the datagram being\nfragmented or dropped [RFC8085].\n",
      "id": "1a5bd900f7e8bcc0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "All QUIC packets that are not sent in a PMTU probe SHOULD be sized to fit within the maximum datagram size to avoid the datagram being fragmented or dropped [RFC8085].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a QUIC endpoint determines that the PMTU between any pair of local\nand remote IP addresses cannot support the smallest allowed maximum\ndatagram size of 1200 bytes, it MUST immediately cease sending QUIC\npackets, except for those in PMTU probes or those containing\nCONNECTION_CLOSE frames, on the affected path.\n",
      "id": "eff7744f4f0bb3ea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "If a QUIC endpoint determines that the PMTU between any pair of local and remote IP addresses cannot support the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes, it MUST immediately cease sending QUIC packets, except for those in PMTU probes or those containing CONNECTION_CLOSE frames, on the affected path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY\nterminate the connection if an alternative path cannot be found.\n",
      "id": "81a7bca2532b8271",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY terminate the connection if an alternative path cannot be found.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC implementations that implement any kind of PMTU discovery\ntherefore SHOULD maintain a maximum datagram size for each\ncombination of local and remote IP addresses.\n",
      "id": "e1743da042875f27",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "QUIC implementations that implement any kind of PMTU discovery therefore SHOULD maintain a maximum datagram size for each combination of local and remote IP addresses.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A QUIC implementation MAY be more conservative in computing the\nmaximum datagram size to allow for unknown tunnel overheads or IP\nheader options/extensions.\n",
      "id": "3493f26cdd4f8806",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "A QUIC implementation MAY be more conservative in computing the maximum datagram size to allow for unknown tunnel overheads or IP header options/extensions.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD set the initial value of BASE_PLPMTU (Section 5.1 of\n[DPLPMTUD]) to be consistent with QUIC's smallest allowed maximum\ndatagram size.\n",
      "id": "7db5417fdee39a66",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD set the initial value of BASE_PLPMTU (Section 5.1 of [DPLPMTUD]) to be consistent with QUIC's smallest allowed maximum datagram size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Loss of\na QUIC packet that is carried in a PMTU probe is therefore not a\nreliable indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion\ncontrol reaction; see Item 7 in Section 3 of [DPLPMTUD].\n",
      "id": "b1813910ffb33996",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Loss of a QUIC packet that is carried in a PMTU probe is therefore not a reliable indication of congestion and SHOULD NOT trigger a congestion control reaction; see Item 7 in Section 3 of [DPLPMTUD].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC MUST NOT be used if the network path cannot support a\nmaximum datagram size of at least 1200 bytes.\n",
      "id": "70c522927b702ef2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "QUIC MUST NOT be used if the network path cannot support a maximum datagram size of at least 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "UDP datagrams MUST NOT be fragmented at the IP layer.\n",
      "id": "9941291c1e8f31ca",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "UDP datagrams MUST NOT be fragmented at the IP layer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In IPv4\n[IPv4], the Don't Fragment (DF) bit MUST be set if possible, to\nprevent fragmentation on the path.\n",
      "id": "99543ea46bd4a090",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "In IPv4 [IPv4], the Don't Fragment (DF) bit MUST be set if possible, to prevent fragmentation on the path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, an endpoint MUST NOT close a connection\nwhen it receives a datagram that does not meet size constraints; the\nendpoint MAY discard such datagrams.\n",
      "id": "10080a643f3bc955",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "Therefore, an endpoint MUST NOT close a connection when it receives a datagram that does not meet size constraints; the endpoint MAY discard such datagrams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/14.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-14",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nclient or server MAY advertise support for any of these reserved\nversions.\n",
      "id": "940c9fdf86b20935",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "A client or server MAY advertise support for any of these reserved versions.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Reserved version numbers will never represent a real protocol; a\nclient MAY use one of these version numbers with the expectation that\nthe server will initiate version negotiation; a server MAY advertise\nsupport for one of these versions and can expect that clients ignore\nthe value.\n",
      "id": "606a62f6580eecee",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Reserved version numbers will never represent a real protocol; a client MAY use one of these version numbers with the expectation that the server will initiate version negotiation; a server MAY advertise support for one of these versions and can expect that clients ignore the value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Reserved version numbers will never represent a real protocol; a\nclient MAY use one of these version numbers with the expectation that\nthe server will initiate version negotiation; a server MAY advertise\nsupport for one of these versions and can expect that clients ignore\nthe value.\n",
      "id": "22e54a07e2384465",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Reserved version numbers will never represent a real protocol; a client MAY use one of these version numbers with the expectation that the server will initiate version negotiation; a server MAY advertise support for one of these versions and can expect that clients ignore the value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Prior to receiving an acknowledgment for a packet number space, the\nfull packet number MUST be included; it is not to be truncated, as\ndescribed below.\n",
      "id": "b7db0289e531e76c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Prior to receiving an acknowledgment for a packet number space, the full packet number MUST be included; it is not to be truncated, as described below.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After an acknowledgment is received for a packet number space, the\nsender MUST use a packet number size able to represent more than\ntwice as large a range as the difference between the largest\nacknowledged packet number and the packet number being sent.\n",
      "id": "1d04012921950b69",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "After an acknowledgment is received for a packet number space, the sender MUST use a packet number size able to represent more than twice as large a range as the difference between the largest acknowledged packet number and the packet number being sent.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD\nuse a large enough packet number encoding to allow the packet number\nto be recovered even if the packet arrives after packets that are\nsent afterwards.\n",
      "id": "4950db9faa790a25",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD use a large enough packet number encoding to allow the packet number to be recovered even if the packet arrives after packets that are sent afterwards.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST ignore the value of this field.\n",
      "id": "53cf34f256293c7c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Clients MUST ignore the value of this field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Where QUIC\nmight be multiplexed with other protocols (see [RFC7983]), servers\nSHOULD set the most significant bit of this field (0x40) to 1 so that\nVersion Negotiation packets appear to have the Fixed Bit field.\n",
      "id": "68995a51b8e3322e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Where QUIC might be multiplexed with other protocols (see [RFC7983]), servers SHOULD set the most significant bit of this field (0x40) to 1 so that Version Negotiation packets appear to have the Fixed Bit field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The Version field of a Version Negotiation packet MUST be set to\n0x00000000.\n",
      "id": "21fc6e16ad3f6684",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "The Version field of a Version Negotiation packet MUST be set to 0x00000000.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST include the value from the Source Connection ID field\nof the packet it receives in the Destination Connection ID field.\n",
      "id": "bd2f795259e48b7c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "The server MUST include the value from the Source Connection ID field of the packet it receives in the Destination Connection ID field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value for Source Connection ID MUST be copied from the\nDestination Connection ID of the received packet, which is initially\nrandomly selected by a client.\n",
      "id": "f8773f72f2ef9b77",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "The value for Source Connection ID MUST be copied from the Destination Connection ID of the received packet, which is initially randomly selected by a client.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Version-\nspecific rules for the connection ID therefore MUST NOT influence a\ndecision about whether to send a Version Negotiation packet.\n",
      "id": "a39b31f347560ea9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "Version- specific rules for the connection ID therefore MUST NOT influence a decision about whether to send a Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST NOT send more than one Version Negotiation packet in\nresponse to a single UDP datagram.\n",
      "id": "0bb0e9a87b01eca8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT send more than one Version Negotiation packet in response to a single UDP datagram.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Initial packets sent by the server MUST set the Token Length field\nto 0; clients that receive an Initial packet with a non-zero Token\nLength field MUST either discard the packet or generate a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "9e8414e5b278cf98",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "Initial packets sent by the server MUST set the Token Length field to 0; clients that receive an Initial packet with a non-zero Token Length field MUST either discard the packet or generate a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Initial packets sent by the server MUST set the Token Length field\nto 0; clients that receive an Initial packet with a non-zero Token\nLength field MUST either discard the packet or generate a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "99462de191887864",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "Initial packets sent by the server MUST set the Token Length field to 0; clients that receive an Initial packet with a non-zero Token Length field MUST either discard the packet or generate a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY send multiple Initial packets.\n",
      "id": "48be3420319a4537",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "A server MAY send multiple Initial packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client SHOULD attempt\nto resend data in 0-RTT packets after it sends a new Initial packet.\n",
      "id": "f975fea46f3ad398",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "A client SHOULD attempt to resend data in 0-RTT packets after it sends a new Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "New packet numbers MUST be used for any new packets that are sent; as\ndescribed in Section 17.2.5.3, reusing packet numbers could\ncompromise packet protection.\n",
      "id": "e3d9214884bd4684",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "New packet numbers MUST be used for any new packets that are sent; as described in Section 17.2.5.3, reusing packet numbers could compromise packet protection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT send 0-RTT packets once it starts processing 1-RTT\npackets from the server.\n",
      "id": "43c5421c0f1bf751",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT send 0-RTT packets once it starts processing 1-RTT packets from the server.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An acknowledgment for a 1-RTT\npacket MUST be carried in a 1-RTT packet.\n",
      "id": "2031d7444b40120f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "An acknowledgment for a 1-RTT packet MUST be carried in a 1-RTT packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server SHOULD treat a violation of remembered limits\n(Section 7.4.1) as a connection error of an appropriate type (for\ninstance, a FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR for exceeding stream data limits).\n",
      "id": "46d96be58e64d790",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD treat a violation of remembered limits (Section 7.4.1) as a connection error of an appropriate type (for instance, a FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR for exceeding stream data limits).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Handshake packets MAY contain\nCONNECTION_CLOSE frames of type 0x1c.\n",
      "id": "fb228f61a6faa9f9",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Handshake packets MAY contain CONNECTION_CLOSE frames of type 0x1c.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST treat receipt\nof Handshake packets with other frames as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "b176adab8dd1cc6a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST treat receipt of Handshake packets with other frames as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This value MUST NOT be equal to the Destination\nConnection ID field of the packet sent by the client.\n",
      "id": "77c827c165dc4208",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "This value MUST NOT be equal to the Destination Connection ID field of the packet sent by the client.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST\ndiscard a Retry packet that contains a Source Connection ID field\nthat is identical to the Destination Connection ID field of its\nInitial packet.\n",
      "id": "7532b9f6f2be3932",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard a Retry packet that contains a Source Connection ID field that is identical to the Destination Connection ID field of its Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST use the value from the Source\nConnection ID field of the Retry packet in the Destination Connection\nID field of subsequent packets that it sends.\n",
      "id": "00486010e978d5ea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "The client MUST use the value from the Source Connection ID field of the Retry packet in the Destination Connection ID field of subsequent packets that it sends.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY send Retry packets in response to Initial and 0-RTT\npackets.\n",
      "id": "b0f75b91ed138c42",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "A server MAY send Retry packets in response to Initial and 0-RTT packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST NOT send more than one Retry\npacket in response to a single UDP datagram.\n",
      "id": "06b3d523682a2174",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT send more than one Retry packet in response to a single UDP datagram.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST accept and process at most one Retry packet for each\nconnection attempt.\n",
      "id": "f251a47e1738a9e6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "A client MUST accept and process at most one Retry packet for each connection attempt.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After the client has received and processed an\nInitial or Retry packet from the server, it MUST discard any\nsubsequent Retry packets that it receives.\n",
      "id": "319a0a4edd982b95",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "After the client has received and processed an Initial or Retry packet from the server, it MUST discard any subsequent Retry packets that it receives.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST discard Retry packets that have a Retry Integrity Tag\nthat cannot be validated; see Section 5.8 of [QUIC-TLS].\n",
      "id": "5f17309ba827a886",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Clients MUST discard Retry packets that have a Retry Integrity Tag that cannot be validated; see Section 5.8 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client\nMUST discard a Retry packet with a zero-length Retry Token field.\n",
      "id": "ad9263d94bdced62",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard a Retry packet with a zero-length Retry Token field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nclient MUST NOT change the Source Connection ID because the server\ncould include the connection ID as part of its token validation\nlogic; see Section 8.1.4.\n",
      "id": "64330e47a19227fa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "The client MUST NOT change the Source Connection ID because the server could include the connection ID as part of its token validation logic; see Section 8.1.4.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST use the same\ncryptographic handshake message it included in this packet.\n",
      "id": "3dc1972002816b5e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "A client MUST use the same cryptographic handshake message it included in this packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server\nMAY treat a packet that contains a different cryptographic handshake\nmessage as a connection error or discard it.\n",
      "id": "12b2ce770930b41d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "A server MAY treat a packet that contains a different cryptographic handshake message as a connection error or discard it.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MAY attempt 0-RTT after receiving a Retry packet by sending\n0-RTT packets to the connection ID provided by the server.\n",
      "id": "b199e06d7b06763c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "A client MAY attempt 0-RTT after receiving a Retry packet by sending 0-RTT packets to the connection ID provided by the server.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT reset the packet number for any packet number space\nafter processing a Retry packet.\n",
      "id": "f7fe7b1c78d29ffe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT reset the packet number for any packet number space after processing a Retry packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY abort the connection if it\ndetects that the client reset the packet number.\n",
      "id": "63d7fc7e14356d18",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "A server MAY abort the connection if it detects that the client reset the packet number.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value in\nthe Unused field is set to an arbitrary value by the server; a client\nMUST ignore these bits.\n",
      "id": "7c944cd058b84aeb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "The value in the Unused field is set to an arbitrary value by the server; a client MUST ignore these bits.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Packets containing a zero\nvalue for this bit are not valid packets in this version and MUST\nbe discarded.\n",
      "id": "eda972c6e9080d51",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 137,
      "quote": "Packets containing a zero value for this bit are not valid packets in this version and MUST be discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In QUIC version 1, this value MUST NOT exceed\n20 bytes.\n",
      "id": "7c31be37ed24b7ba",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 145,
      "quote": "In QUIC version 1, this value MUST NOT exceed 20 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a\nvalue larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.\n",
      "id": "fd8f469451e48c1e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to properly\nform a Version Negotiation packet, servers SHOULD be able to read\nlonger connection IDs from other QUIC versions.\n",
      "id": "8cf958d23f7e3cdd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "In order to properly form a Version Negotiation packet, servers SHOULD be able to read longer connection IDs from other QUIC versions.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In QUIC version 1, this value MUST NOT\nexceed 20 bytes.\n",
      "id": "e63ee70e7d857272",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "In QUIC version 1, this value MUST NOT exceed 20 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header\nwith a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.\n",
      "id": "2680f24e55c07ebe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 174,
      "quote": "Endpoints that receive a version 1 long header with a value larger than 20 MUST drop the packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to\nproperly form a Version Negotiation packet, servers SHOULD be able\nto read longer connection IDs from other QUIC versions.\n",
      "id": "dd2fdc039d73d9da",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 181,
      "quote": "In order to properly form a Version Negotiation packet, servers SHOULD be able to read longer connection IDs from other QUIC versions.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value\nincluded prior to protection MUST be set to 0.\n",
      "id": "7cdea2ae79ca2372",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 189,
      "quote": "The value included prior to protection MUST be set to 0.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST\ntreat receipt of a packet that has a non-zero value for these bits\nafter removing both packet and header protection as a connection\nerror of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "bd20adee52052fbe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 196,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a packet that has a non-zero value for these bits after removing both packet and header protection as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Packets\ncontaining a zero value for this bit are not valid packets in this\nversion and MUST be discarded.\n",
      "id": "b52d95f1aef97c69",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "Packets containing a zero value for this bit are not valid packets in this version and MUST be discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value included prior to\nprotection MUST be set to 0.\n",
      "id": "d4fea002e72ef642",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "The value included prior to protection MUST be set to 0.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a\npacket that has a non-zero value for these bits, after removing\nboth packet and header protection, as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "3f504f667262e178",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a packet that has a non-zero value for these bits, after removing both packet and header protection, as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The spin bit is an OPTIONAL feature of this version of QUIC.\n",
      "id": "961973c87db708f0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "The spin bit is an OPTIONAL feature of this version of QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint that does not support this feature MUST disable it, as\ndefined below.\n",
      "id": "3c418f0ac6ee1c96",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "An endpoint that does not support this feature MUST disable it, as defined below.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST allow administrators\nof clients and servers to disable the spin bit either globally or on\na per-connection basis.\n",
      "id": "94e8c23f6ceeb003",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST allow administrators of clients and servers to disable the spin bit either globally or on a per-connection basis.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Even when the spin bit is not disabled by\nthe administrator, endpoints MUST disable their use of the spin bit\nfor a random selection of at least one in every 16 network paths, or\nfor one in every 16 connection IDs, in order to ensure that QUIC\nconnections that disable the spin bit are commonly observed on the\nnetwork.\n",
      "id": "3c95b5224834fa84",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Even when the spin bit is not disabled by the administrator, endpoints MUST disable their use of the spin bit for a random selection of at least one in every 16 network paths, or for one in every 16 connection IDs, in order to ensure that QUIC connections that disable the spin bit are commonly observed on the network.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the spin bit is disabled, endpoints MAY set the spin bit to any\nvalue and MUST ignore any incoming value.\n",
      "id": "e067280d653368f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "When the spin bit is disabled, endpoints MAY set the spin bit to any value and MUST ignore any incoming value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It is RECOMMENDED that\nendpoints set the spin bit to a random value either chosen\nindependently for each packet or chosen independently for each\nconnection ID.\n",
      "id": "a1eeb8e7ece9f56b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED that endpoints set the spin bit to a random value either chosen independently for each packet or chosen independently for each connection ID.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/17.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-17.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This transport parameter MUST NOT be sent\nby a client but MAY be sent by a server.\n",
      "id": "c0906d958d1a4455",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 208,
      "quote": "This transport parameter MUST NOT be sent by a client but MAY be sent by a server.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This value\nSHOULD include the receiver's expected delays in alarms firing.\n",
      "id": "3a65da04bbbb6eb3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 215,
      "quote": "This value SHOULD include the receiver's expected delays in alarms firing.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives this transport\nparameter MUST NOT use a new local address when sending to the\naddress that the peer used during the handshake.\n",
      "id": "5963c5878d887035",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 222,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives this transport parameter MUST NOT use a new local address when sending to the address that the peer used during the handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY choose to only send a preferred address\nof one address family by sending an all-zero address and port\n(0.0.0.0:0 or [::]:0) for the other family.\n",
      "id": "2d26d297d22ef4d0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 230,
      "quote": "Servers MAY choose to only send a preferred address of one address family by sending an all-zero address and port (0.0.0.0:0 or [::]:0) for the other family.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server\nthat chooses a zero-length connection ID MUST NOT provide a\npreferred address.\n",
      "id": "6f8d83a905c19b08",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 238,
      "quote": "A server that chooses a zero-length connection ID MUST NOT provide a preferred address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Similarly, a server MUST NOT include a zero-\nlength connection ID in this transport parameter.\n",
      "id": "85b5b7d4b9ddc733",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 246,
      "quote": "Similarly, a server MUST NOT include a zero- length connection ID in this transport parameter.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST\ntreat a violation of these requirements as a connection error of\ntype TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "a4b3a3578baac8b5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 253,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat a violation of these requirements as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of the\nactive_connection_id_limit parameter MUST be at least 2.\n",
      "id": "214d85c3c94ea9f2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 261,
      "quote": "The value of the active_connection_id_limit parameter MUST be at least 2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint that receives a value less than 2 MUST close the\nconnection with an error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "f2e19c5ca62c87df",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 268,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a value less than 2 MUST close the connection with an error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT include any server-only transport parameter:\noriginal_destination_connection_id, preferred_address,\nretry_source_connection_id, or stateless_reset_token.\n",
      "id": "981c2c2990df14b6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 276,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT include any server-only transport parameter: original_destination_connection_id, preferred_address, retry_source_connection_id, or stateless_reset_token.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST\ntreat receipt of any of these transport parameters as a connection\nerror of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "0a5bc3b881201331",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 284,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat receipt of any of these transport parameters as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/18.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-18.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receiving a MAX_STREAM_DATA frame for a locally\ninitiated stream that has not yet been created MUST be treated as a\nconnection error of type STREAM_STATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "638b0962e1f0e445",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "Receiving a MAX_STREAM_DATA frame for a locally initiated stream that has not yet been created MUST be treated as a connection error of type STREAM_STATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that\nreceives a MAX_STREAM_DATA frame for a receive-only stream MUST\nterminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "31bb7b372eff6f20",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a MAX_STREAM_DATA frame for a receive-only stream MUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The data sent on a stream MUST NOT exceed the largest maximum stream\ndata value advertised by the receiver.\n",
      "id": "0254f2bf49b2228f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "The data sent on a stream MUST NOT exceed the largest maximum stream data value advertised by the receiver.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST terminate a\nconnection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if it receives\nmore data than the largest maximum stream data that it has sent for\nthe affected stream.\n",
      "id": "9fb05320603e10d5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST terminate a connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if it receives more data than the largest maximum stream data that it has sent for the affected stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.10.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.10",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt of a frame that\npermits opening of a stream larger than this limit MUST be treated\nas a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "9ef31dcec7c4d8ab",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Receipt of a frame that permits opening of a stream larger than this limit MUST be treated as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "MAX_STREAMS frames that do not increase the stream limit MUST be\nignored.\n",
      "id": "08fa12fc8c5a2c86",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "MAX_STREAMS frames that do not increase the stream limit MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT open more streams than permitted by the current\nstream limit set by its peer.\n",
      "id": "318f52f4afd35820",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT open more streams than permitted by the current stream limit set by its peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST terminate a connection\nwith an error of type STREAM_LIMIT_ERROR if a peer opens more streams\nthan was permitted.\n",
      "id": "a28c7fbbcbd5c77b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST terminate a connection with an error of type STREAM_LIMIT_ERROR if a peer opens more streams than was permitted.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD send a DATA_BLOCKED frame (type=0x14) when it wishes\nto send data but is unable to do so due to connection-level flow\ncontrol; see Section 4.\n",
      "id": "e9eced689e4aad19",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a DATA_BLOCKED frame (type=0x14) when it wishes to send data but is unable to do so due to connection-level flow control; see Section 4.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.12.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.12",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame (type=0x15) when it\nwishes to send data but is unable to do so due to stream-level flow\ncontrol.\n",
      "id": "924c82ed1bb7cf63",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame (type=0x15) when it wishes to send data but is unable to do so due to stream-level flow control.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.13.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.13",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame for a send-only\nstream MUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "74f7c5148ea2e2bb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame for a send-only stream MUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.13.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.13",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAMS_BLOCKED frame (type=0x16 or 0x17) when\nit wishes to open a stream but is unable to do so due to the maximum\nstream limit set by its peer; see Section 19.11.\n",
      "id": "6a243a43a0107b34",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAMS_BLOCKED frame (type=0x16 or 0x17) when it wishes to open a stream but is unable to do so due to the maximum stream limit set by its peer; see Section 19.11.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.14.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.14",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt of a frame that encodes a larger\nstream ID MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nSTREAM_LIMIT_ERROR or FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "67306cb455da9997",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Receipt of a frame that encodes a larger stream ID MUST be treated as a connection error of type STREAM_LIMIT_ERROR or FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.14.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.14",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Values less than 1 and greater than 20 are invalid\nand MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nFRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "ea84b8e420be738f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "Values less than 1 and greater than 20 are invalid and MUST be treated as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send this frame if it currently requires that\nits peer send packets with a zero-length Destination Connection ID.\n",
      "id": "48ee6ac897287dda",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send this frame if it currently requires that its peer send packets with a zero-length Destination Connection ID.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that is sending packets with a zero-length Destination\nConnection ID MUST treat receipt of a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame as a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "6233dd3eb0b7fc97",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "An endpoint that is sending packets with a zero-length Destination Connection ID MUST treat receipt of a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt\nof the same frame multiple times MUST NOT be treated as a connection\nerror.\n",
      "id": "198218462724e69b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "Receipt of the same frame multiple times MUST NOT be treated as a connection error.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an endpoint receives a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame that repeats a\npreviously issued connection ID with a different Stateless Reset\nToken field value or a different Sequence Number field value, or if a\nsequence number is used for different connection IDs, the endpoint\nMAY treat that receipt as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "81a3dc1b2f852b42",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame that repeats a previously issued connection ID with a different Stateless Reset Token field value or a different Sequence Number field value, or if a sequence number is used for different connection IDs, the endpoint MAY treat that receipt as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value in the Retire Prior To field\nMUST be less than or equal to the value in the Sequence Number field.\n",
      "id": "fc6dd938659ee64e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "The value in the Retire Prior To field MUST be less than or equal to the value in the Sequence Number field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receiving a value in the Retire Prior To field that is greater than\nthat in the Sequence Number field MUST be treated as a connection\nerror of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "5364fbe0f3d2754a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "Receiving a value in the Retire Prior To field that is greater than that in the Sequence Number field MUST be treated as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver\nMUST ignore any Retire Prior To fields that do not increase the\nlargest received Retire Prior To value.\n",
      "id": "ca2bdd29147f0cd5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST ignore any Retire Prior To fields that do not increase the largest received Retire Prior To value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame with a sequence\nnumber smaller than the Retire Prior To field of a previously\nreceived NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST send a corresponding\nRETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame that retires the newly received connection\nID, unless it has already done so for that sequence number.\n",
      "id": "b9fdd533fa0708ad",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 148,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame with a sequence number smaller than the Retire Prior To field of a previously received NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST send a corresponding RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame that retires the newly received connection ID, unless it has already done so for that sequence number.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.15.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.15",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame containing a sequence number\ngreater than any previously sent to the peer MUST be treated as a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "8846fd20551610df",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame containing a sequence number greater than any previously sent to the peer MUST be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.16.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sequence number specified in a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST\nNOT refer to the Destination Connection ID field of the packet in\nwhich the frame is contained.\n",
      "id": "f6f4f1c750733f3e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "The sequence number specified in a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame MUST NOT refer to the Destination Connection ID field of the packet in which the frame is contained.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.16.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The peer MAY treat this as a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "9495fb37a31499ed",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "The peer MAY treat this as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.16.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that provides a zero-\nlength connection ID MUST treat receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID\nframe as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "adbee28bcbdda392",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "An endpoint that provides a zero- length connection ID MUST treat receipt of a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.16.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.16",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The recipient of this frame MUST generate a PATH_RESPONSE frame\n(Section 19.18) containing the same Data value.\n",
      "id": "14fbfda4dd5655a1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "The recipient of this frame MUST generate a PATH_RESPONSE frame (Section 19.18) containing the same Data value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.17.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.17",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the content of a PATH_RESPONSE frame does not match the content of\na PATH_CHALLENGE frame previously sent by the endpoint, the endpoint\nMAY generate a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "9e451ef7e7400a0c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "If the content of a PATH_RESPONSE frame does not match the content of a PATH_CHALLENGE frame previously sent by the endpoint, the endpoint MAY generate a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.18.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.18",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This SHOULD be a UTF-8 encoded\nstring [RFC3629], though the frame does not carry information,\nsuch as language tags, that would aid comprehension by any entity\nother than the one that created the text.\n",
      "id": "bdb1386b53f55e52",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "This SHOULD be a UTF-8 encoded string [RFC3629], though the frame does not carry information, such as language tags, that would aid comprehension by any entity other than the one that created the text.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.19.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.19",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST\nNOT send a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame before completing the handshake.\n",
      "id": "49098b523f8eb4b0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame before completing the handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.20.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.20",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nserver MUST treat receipt of a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame as a connection\nerror of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "b9a09cef0113408b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat receipt of a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.20.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.20",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An extension to QUIC that wishes to use a new type of frame MUST\nfirst ensure that a peer is able to understand the frame.\n",
      "id": "ee65cf1d92ba3e96",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "An extension to QUIC that wishes to use a new type of frame MUST first ensure that a peer is able to understand the frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.21.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.21",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Such extensions\nSHOULD define their interaction with previously defined extensions\nmodifying the same protocol components.\n",
      "id": "7e702e9ddf991805",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "Such extensions SHOULD define their interaction with previously defined extensions modifying the same protocol components.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.21.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.21",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Extension frames MUST be congestion controlled and MUST cause an ACK\nframe to be sent.\n",
      "id": "54a9ec55f6b24e36",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Extension frames MUST be congestion controlled and MUST cause an ACK frame to be sent.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.21.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.21",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Extension frames MUST be congestion controlled and MUST cause an ACK\nframe to be sent.\n",
      "id": "a7acfeed97922052",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Extension frames MUST be congestion controlled and MUST cause an ACK frame to be sent.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.21.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.21",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If any computed packet number is negative, an endpoint MUST generate\na connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "b3e143e567183bec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "If any computed packet number is negative, an endpoint MUST generate a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC implementations MUST properly handle both\ntypes, and, if they have enabled ECN for packets they send, they\nSHOULD use the information in the ECN section to manage their\ncongestion state.\n",
      "id": "7ed99c1b1e7726ef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "QUIC implementations MUST properly handle both types, and, if they have enabled ECN for packets they send, they SHOULD use the information in the ECN section to manage their congestion state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a RESET_STREAM frame for a send-only stream\nMUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "10270cc91771ca1a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a RESET_STREAM frame for a send-only stream MUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receiving a STOP_SENDING frame for a\nlocally initiated stream that has not yet been created MUST be\ntreated as a connection error of type STREAM_STATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "bc862f05dfe4fb8f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Receiving a STOP_SENDING frame for a locally initiated stream that has not yet been created MUST be treated as a connection error of type STREAM_STATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint that receives a STOP_SENDING frame for a receive-only stream\nMUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "97dde5d724e76890",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a STOP_SENDING frame for a receive-only stream MUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt of a frame that exceeds\nthis limit MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nFRAME_ENCODING_ERROR or CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED.\n",
      "id": "c7f4122ac9b7608d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Receipt of a frame that exceeds this limit MUST be treated as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR or CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The token MUST NOT be empty.\n",
      "id": "4dc1da7770966ec5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "The token MUST NOT be empty.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST treat receipt\nof a NEW_TOKEN frame with an empty Token field as a connection\nerror of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "537fcd2680d4c808",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a NEW_TOKEN frame with an empty Token field as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT send NEW_TOKEN frames.\n",
      "id": "13d72ee35416c06d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT send NEW_TOKEN frames.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST treat receipt\nof a NEW_TOKEN frame as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "f6ec6de0ac5a1343",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat receipt of a NEW_TOKEN frame as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST terminate the connection with error\nSTREAM_STATE_ERROR if it receives a STREAM frame for a locally\ninitiated stream that has not yet been created, or for a send-only\nstream.\n",
      "id": "eb5ca35112c5ebaf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST terminate the connection with error STREAM_STATE_ERROR if it receives a STREAM frame for a locally initiated stream that has not yet been created, or for a send-only stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt of a frame that exceeds this limit\nMUST be treated as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR or\nFLOW_CONTROL_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "41cfe8d66b3d6fc2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "Receipt of a frame that exceeds this limit MUST be treated as a connection error of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR or FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sum of\nthe final sizes on all streams -- including streams in terminal\nstates -- MUST NOT exceed the value advertised by a receiver.\n",
      "id": "f813d00c91f31db4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "The sum of the final sizes on all streams -- including streams in terminal states -- MUST NOT exceed the value advertised by a receiver.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint MUST terminate a connection with an error of type\nFLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if it receives more data than the maximum data\nvalue that it has sent.\n",
      "id": "ce82af2a4883a01f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST terminate a connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if it receives more data than the maximum data value that it has sent.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/19.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-19.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A QUIC\nendpoint MUST NOT reuse a stream ID within a connection.\n",
      "id": "45729960425b3047",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "A QUIC endpoint MUST NOT reuse a stream ID within a connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST be able to deliver stream data to an application as an\nordered byte stream.\n",
      "id": "fe917a179d39ef91",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST be able to deliver stream data to an application as an ordered byte stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, implementations MAY choose to offer the ability to\ndeliver data out of order to a receiving application.\n",
      "id": "1a3fa56cbbbb26e1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "However, implementations MAY choose to offer the ability to deliver data out of order to a receiving application.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The data at a given offset MUST NOT change if it is sent\nmultiple times; an endpoint MAY treat receipt of different data at\nthe same offset within a stream as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "d186d84723170ac4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "The data at a given offset MUST NOT change if it is sent multiple times; an endpoint MAY treat receipt of different data at the same offset within a stream as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send data on any stream without ensuring that it\nis within the flow control limits set by its peer.\n",
      "id": "7ef6831409f851e0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send data on any stream without ensuring that it is within the flow control limits set by its peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A QUIC implementation SHOULD provide ways in which an application can\nindicate the relative priority of streams.\n",
      "id": "0db6dc381feb676e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "A QUIC implementation SHOULD provide ways in which an application can indicate the relative priority of streams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To defend\nagainst this style of denial of service, endpoints that share a\nstatic key for stateless resets (see Section 10.3.2) MUST be arranged\nso that packets with a given connection ID always arrive at an\ninstance that has connection state, unless that connection is no\nlonger active.\n",
      "id": "29029dd7158cc9d3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "To defend against this style of denial of service, endpoints that share a static key for stateless resets (see Section 10.3.2) MUST be arranged so that packets with a given connection ID always arrive at an instance that has connection state, unless that connection is no longer active.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "More generally, servers MUST NOT generate a stateless reset if a\nconnection with the corresponding connection ID could be active on\nany endpoint using the same static key.\n",
      "id": "525437d8c697fc6d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "More generally, servers MUST NOT generate a stateless reset if a connection with the corresponding connection ID could be active on any endpoint using the same static key.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.11.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.11",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Future\nversions of QUIC that use Version Negotiation packets MUST define a\nmechanism that is robust against version downgrade attacks.\n",
      "id": "9931f61b1565ceef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "Future versions of QUIC that use Version Negotiation packets MUST define a mechanism that is robust against version downgrade attacks.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.12.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.12",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD provide mitigations for this attack by limiting the\nusage and lifetime of address validation tokens; see Section 8.1.3.\n",
      "id": "b31944c393726521",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD provide mitigations for this attack by limiting the usage and lifetime of address validation tokens; see Section 8.1.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY skip packet numbers when sending\npackets to detect this behavior.\n",
      "id": "bead5d8d4d74d692",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY skip packet numbers when sending packets to detect this behavior.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT send non-probing frames to a preferred address\nprior to validating that address; see Section 8.\n",
      "id": "04508122535bcaf1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT send non-probing frames to a preferred address prior to validating that address; see Section 8.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY prevent connection attempts or\nmigration to a loopback address.\n",
      "id": "ed3820c5af6eb45a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY prevent connection attempts or migration to a loopback address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT allow\nconnections or migration to a loopback address if the same service\nwas previously available at a different interface or if the address\nwas provided by a service at a non-loopback address.\n",
      "id": "ee0e69f5e78af374",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT allow connections or migration to a loopback address if the same service was previously available at a different interface or if the address was provided by a service at a non-loopback address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT refuse to use\nan address unless they have specific knowledge about the network\nindicating that sending datagrams to unvalidated addresses in a given\nrange is not safe.\n",
      "id": "89192a54330ac791",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT refuse to use an address unless they have specific knowledge about the network indicating that sending datagrams to unvalidated addresses in a given range is not safe.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY choose to reduce the risk of request forgery by not\nincluding values from NEW_TOKEN frames in Initial packets or by only\nsending probing frames in packets prior to completing address\nvalidation.\n",
      "id": "31fbf47356b6614f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY choose to reduce the risk of request forgery by not including values from NEW_TOKEN frames in Initial packets or by only sending probing frames in packets prior to completing address validation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY\nchoose to avoid sending datagrams to these ports or not send\ndatagrams that match these patterns prior to validating the\ndestination address.\n",
      "id": "103ace4872ab593d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY choose to avoid sending datagrams to these ports or not send datagrams that match these patterns prior to validating the destination address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY retire connection IDs containing\npatterns known to be problematic without using them.\n",
      "id": "da1e4cb13727028f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY retire connection IDs containing patterns known to be problematic without using them.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC\nservers SHOULD NOT be deployed in networks that do not deploy ingress\nfiltering [BCP38] and also have inadequately secured UDP endpoints.\n",
      "id": "f990ac5c67f836a7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "QUIC servers SHOULD NOT be deployed in networks that do not deploy ingress filtering [BCP38] and also have inadequately secured UDP endpoints.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any future extension that allows server migration MUST\nalso define countermeasures for forgery attacks.\n",
      "id": "8780b6d6e501df3c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Any future extension that allows server migration MUST also define countermeasures for forgery attacks.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC deployments SHOULD provide mitigations for the Slowloris\nattacks, such as increasing the maximum number of clients the server\nwill allow, limiting the number of connections a single IP address is\nallowed to make, imposing restrictions on the minimum transfer speed\na connection is allowed to have, and restricting the length of time\nan endpoint is allowed to stay connected.\n",
      "id": "7589d399cacdef66",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "QUIC deployments SHOULD provide mitigations for the Slowloris attacks, such as increasing the maximum number of clients the server will allow, limiting the number of connections a single IP address is allowed to make, imposing restrictions on the minimum transfer speed a connection is allowed to have, and restricting the length of time an endpoint is allowed to stay connected.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC deployments SHOULD provide mitigations for stream fragmentation\nattacks.\n",
      "id": "bd2260a8f7d68d16",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "QUIC deployments SHOULD provide mitigations for stream fragmentation attacks.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While there are legitimate uses for all messages, implementations\nSHOULD track cost of processing relative to progress and treat\nexcessive quantities of any non-productive packets as indicative of\nan attack.\n",
      "id": "a3ab765581b8aca4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "While there are legitimate uses for all messages, implementations SHOULD track cost of processing relative to progress and treat excessive quantities of any non-productive packets as indicative of an attack.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY respond to this condition with a connection\nerror or by dropping packets.\n",
      "id": "b924522dbd9b7178",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY respond to this condition with a connection error or by dropping packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/21.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-21.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Provisional registrations MAY omit the Specification and Notes\nfields, plus any additional fields that might be required for a\npermanent registration.\n",
      "id": "9d49661b577b0eb3",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Provisional registrations MAY omit the Specification and Notes fields, plus any additional fields that might be required for a permanent registration.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "New requests for codepoints from QUIC registries SHOULD use a\nrandomly selected codepoint that excludes both existing allocations\nand the first unallocated codepoint in the selected space.\n",
      "id": "ada749584fbd42d8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "New requests for codepoints from QUIC registries SHOULD use a randomly selected codepoint that excludes both existing allocations and the first unallocated codepoint in the selected space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Requests\nfor multiple codepoints MAY use a contiguous range.\n",
      "id": "114bc9d02e309cfd",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Requests for multiple codepoints MAY use a contiguous range.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For codepoints that are encoded in variable-length integers\n(Section 16), such as frame types, codepoints that encode to four or\neight bytes (that is, values 2^14 and above) SHOULD be used unless\nthe usage is especially sensitive to having a longer encoding.\n",
      "id": "9f200d95e11f81db",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "For codepoints that are encoded in variable-length integers (Section 16), such as frame types, codepoints that encode to four or eight bytes (that is, values 2^14 and above) SHOULD be used unless the usage is especially sensitive to having a longer encoding.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Applications to register codepoints in QUIC registries MAY include a\nrequested codepoint as part of the registration.\n",
      "id": "74fe40bdb796e06f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Applications to register codepoints in QUIC registries MAY include a requested codepoint as part of the registration.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "IANA MUST allocate\nthe selected codepoint if the codepoint is unassigned and the\nrequirements of the registration policy are met.\n",
      "id": "b0620f9f3938c982",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "IANA MUST allocate the selected codepoint if the codepoint is unassigned and the requirements of the registration policy are met.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This SHOULD be done only for the\ncodepoints with the earliest recorded date, and entries that have\nbeen updated less than a year prior SHOULD NOT be reclaimed.\n",
      "id": "227b064788dfee47",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "This SHOULD be done only for the codepoints with the earliest recorded date, and entries that have been updated less than a year prior SHOULD NOT be reclaimed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This SHOULD be done only for the\ncodepoints with the earliest recorded date, and entries that have\nbeen updated less than a year prior SHOULD NOT be reclaimed.\n",
      "id": "6b434ffb869392d8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "This SHOULD be done only for the codepoints with the earliest recorded date, and entries that have been updated less than a year prior SHOULD NOT be reclaimed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A request to remove a codepoint MUST be reviewed by the designated\nexperts.\n",
      "id": "ec069554546ae279",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "A request to remove a codepoint MUST be reviewed by the designated experts.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The experts MUST attempt to determine whether the codepoint\nis still in use.\n",
      "id": "a25ab39e3b4204ea",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "The experts MUST attempt to determine whether the codepoint is still in use.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If any use of the codepoints is identified by this search or a\nrequest to update the registration is made, the codepoint MUST NOT be\nreclaimed.\n",
      "id": "8cd25006cde42c2c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If any use of the codepoints is identified by this search or a request to update the registration is made, the codepoint MUST NOT be reclaimed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If no use of the codepoint was identified and no request was made to\nupdate the registration, the codepoint MAY be removed from the\nregistry.\n",
      "id": "e6e18dfd21f8f555",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "If no use of the codepoint was identified and no request was made to update the registration, the codepoint MAY be removed from the registry.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The creation of a registry\nMAY specify additional constraints on permanent registrations.\n",
      "id": "db2ed77c21ad5f9e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "The creation of a registry MAY specify additional constraints on permanent registrations.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The creation of a registry MAY identify a range of codepoints where\nregistrations are governed by a different registration policy.\n",
      "id": "3af4389a5a62e401",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "The creation of a registry MAY identify a range of codepoints where registrations are governed by a different registration policy.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All registrations made by Standards Track publications MUST be\npermanent.\n",
      "id": "aeda192bdd8e1b6f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "All registrations made by Standards Track publications MUST be permanent.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All codepoints that follow the pattern 0x?a?a?a?a are reserved, MUST\nNOT be assigned by IANA, and MUST NOT appear in the listing of\nassigned values.\n",
      "id": "3ebb0db94cebfb82",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "All codepoints that follow the pattern 0x?a?a?a?a are reserved, MUST NOT be assigned by IANA, and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All codepoints that follow the pattern 0x?a?a?a?a are reserved, MUST\nNOT be assigned by IANA, and MUST NOT appear in the listing of\nassigned values.\n",
      "id": "ffb51e436599aaf7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "All codepoints that follow the pattern 0x?a?a?a?a are reserved, MUST NOT be assigned by IANA, and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to the fields listed in Section 22.1.1, permanent\nregistrations in this registry MUST include the following field:\n",
      "id": "a429a3c174e6ee72",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "In addition to the fields listed in Section 22.1.1, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following field:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each value of the form \"31 * N + 27\" for integer values of N (that\nis, 27, 58, 89, ...) are reserved; these values MUST NOT be assigned\nby IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.\n",
      "id": "e46baf014d21fabe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "Each value of the form \"31 * N + 27\" for integer values of N (that is, 27, 58, 89, ...) are reserved; these values MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each value of the form \"31 * N + 27\" for integer values of N (that\nis, 27, 58, 89, ...) are reserved; these values MUST NOT be assigned\nby IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.\n",
      "id": "728592f750827071",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "Each value of the form \"31 * N + 27\" for integer values of N (that is, 27, 58, 89, ...) are reserved; these values MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to the fields listed in Section 22.1.1, permanent\nregistrations in this registry MUST include the following field:\n",
      "id": "b0aa7dd0848f35c6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "In addition to the fields listed in Section 22.1.1, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following field:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to the advice in Section 22.1, specifications for new\npermanent registrations SHOULD describe the means by which an\nendpoint might determine that it can send the identified type of\nframe.\n",
      "id": "ccff55d143903824",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "In addition to the advice in Section 22.1, specifications for new permanent registrations SHOULD describe the means by which an endpoint might determine that it can send the identified type of frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to the fields listed in Section 22.1.1, permanent\nregistrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:\n",
      "id": "25ca8a0e478da5d8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "In addition to the fields listed in Section 22.1.1, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Description:  A brief description of the error code semantics, which\nMAY be a summary if a specification reference is provided.\n",
      "id": "f5942c9258ebe823",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "Description:  A brief description of the error code semantics, which MAY be a summary if a specification reference is provided.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/22.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-22.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY send a RESET_STREAM as the first frame that mentions\na stream; this causes the sending part of that stream to open and\nthen immediately transition to the \"Reset Sent\" state.\n",
      "id": "aab3dc3829ee601d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send a RESET_STREAM as the first frame that mentions a stream; this causes the sending part of that stream to open and then immediately transition to the \"Reset Sent\" state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Before a stream is created, all streams of the same type with lower-\nnumbered stream IDs MUST be created.\n",
      "id": "ce8ca832c7ba75ec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 119,
      "quote": "Before a stream is created, all streams of the same type with lower- numbered stream IDs MUST be created.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nimplementation MAY interrupt delivery of stream data, discard any\ndata that was not consumed, and signal the receipt of the\nRESET_STREAM.\n",
      "id": "08f787cf4fe2072e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 126,
      "quote": "An implementation MAY interrupt delivery of stream data, discard any data that was not consumed, and signal the receipt of the RESET_STREAM.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender MUST NOT send any of these frames from a terminal state\n(\"Data Recvd\" or \"Reset Recvd\").\n",
      "id": "b7baec6e43dd5deb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "A sender MUST NOT send any of these frames from a terminal state (\"Data Recvd\" or \"Reset Recvd\").",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender MUST NOT send a STREAM or\nSTREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame for a stream in the \"Reset Sent\" state or\nany terminal state -- that is, after sending a RESET_STREAM frame.\n",
      "id": "c7b385879ed05fa3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "A sender MUST NOT send a STREAM or STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED frame for a stream in the \"Reset Sent\" state or any terminal state -- that is, after sending a RESET_STREAM frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MAY send a STOP_SENDING frame in any state where it has\nnot received a RESET_STREAM frame -- that is, states other than\n\"Reset Recvd\" or \"Reset Read\".\n",
      "id": "350715e3f86deafc",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "A receiver MAY send a STOP_SENDING frame in any state where it has not received a RESET_STREAM frame -- that is, states other than \"Reset Recvd\" or \"Reset Read\".",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the stream is in the \"Recv\" or \"Size Known\" state, the transport\nSHOULD signal this by sending a STOP_SENDING frame to prompt closure\nof the stream in the opposite direction.\n",
      "id": "63a976cdf78f5991",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "If the stream is in the \"Recv\" or \"Size Known\" state, the transport SHOULD signal this by sending a STOP_SENDING frame to prompt closure of the stream in the opposite direction.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a STOP_SENDING frame\nMUST send a RESET_STREAM frame if the stream is in the \"Ready\" or\n\"Send\" state.\n",
      "id": "5e03b5408ef33589",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a STOP_SENDING frame MUST send a RESET_STREAM frame if the stream is in the \"Ready\" or \"Send\" state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the stream is in the \"Data Sent\" state, the\nendpoint MAY defer sending the RESET_STREAM frame until the packets\ncontaining outstanding data are acknowledged or declared lost.\n",
      "id": "24e0260ac13b0486",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If the stream is in the \"Data Sent\" state, the endpoint MAY defer sending the RESET_STREAM frame until the packets containing outstanding data are acknowledged or declared lost.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nany outstanding data is declared lost, the endpoint SHOULD send a\nRESET_STREAM frame instead of retransmitting the data.\n",
      "id": "1b8169a84b5fce4b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "If any outstanding data is declared lost, the endpoint SHOULD send a RESET_STREAM frame instead of retransmitting the data.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD copy the error code from the STOP_SENDING frame to\nthe RESET_STREAM frame it sends, but it can use any application error\ncode.\n",
      "id": "58008e9519dd7c64",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD copy the error code from the STOP_SENDING frame to the RESET_STREAM frame it sends, but it can use any application error code.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that sends a STOP_SENDING frame MAY ignore the\nerror code in any RESET_STREAM frames subsequently received for that\nstream.\n",
      "id": "ca94d1fe95c7fdc5",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "An endpoint that sends a STOP_SENDING frame MAY ignore the error code in any RESET_STREAM frames subsequently received for that stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "STOP_SENDING SHOULD only be sent for a stream that has not been reset\nby the peer.\n",
      "id": "576925622deb731d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "STOP_SENDING SHOULD only be sent for a stream that has not been reset by the peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/3.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-3.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Senders MUST NOT send data in excess of either limit.\n",
      "id": "a4a23092edf91a31",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "Senders MUST NOT send data in excess of either limit.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MUST close the connection with an error of type\nFLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if the sender violates the advertised connection\nor stream data limits; see Section 11 for details on error handling.\n",
      "id": "eca346fa50c98657",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST close the connection with an error of type FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR if the sender violates the advertised connection or stream data limits; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender MUST ignore any MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frames that do\nnot increase flow control limits.\n",
      "id": "5825974d6488b37e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "A sender MUST ignore any MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frames that do not increase flow control limits.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD send a\nSTREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame to indicate to the receiver\nthat it has data to write but is blocked by flow control limits.\n",
      "id": "4050eb5088365906",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame to indicate to the receiver that it has data to write but is blocked by flow control limits.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To keep the\nconnection from closing, a sender that is flow control limited SHOULD\nperiodically send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame when it\nhas no ack-eliciting packets in flight.\n",
      "id": "dcad2862e413ef4f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "To keep the connection from closing, a sender that is flow control limited SHOULD periodically send a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame when it has no ack-eliciting packets in flight.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid blocking a sender, a receiver MAY send a MAX_STREAM_DATA or\nMAX_DATA frame multiple times within a round trip or send it early\nenough to allow time for loss of the frame and subsequent recovery.\n",
      "id": "011426e106b5440c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "To avoid blocking a sender, a receiver MAY send a MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frame multiple times within a round trip or send it early enough to allow time for loss of the frame and subsequent recovery.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, a receiver MUST NOT wait for a\nSTREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame before sending a\nMAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frame; doing so could result in the\nsender being blocked for the rest of the connection.\n",
      "id": "6d19c2e47eea218d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Therefore, a receiver MUST NOT wait for a STREAM_DATA_BLOCKED or DATA_BLOCKED frame before sending a MAX_STREAM_DATA or MAX_DATA frame; doing so could result in the sender being blocked for the rest of the connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Both endpoints MUST maintain flow control state\nfor the stream in the unterminated direction until that direction\nenters a terminal state.\n",
      "id": "4a6ee3b14d7ff726",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "Both endpoints MUST maintain flow control state for the stream in the unterminated direction until that direction enters a terminal state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The receiver MUST use the final size of the stream to\naccount for all bytes sent on the stream in its connection-level flow\ncontroller.\n",
      "id": "edb1ef634f0f23f1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "The receiver MUST use the final size of the stream to account for all bytes sent on the stream in its connection-level flow controller.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send data on a stream at or beyond the final\nsize.\n",
      "id": "d7efc72d52171ea2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send data on a stream at or beyond the final size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a\nRESET_STREAM or STREAM frame is received indicating a change in the\nfinal size for the stream, an endpoint SHOULD respond with an error\nof type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error\nhandling.\n",
      "id": "c221797d6218ff2e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "If a RESET_STREAM or STREAM frame is received indicating a change in the final size for the stream, an endpoint SHOULD respond with an error of type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver SHOULD treat receipt of data at or beyond the\nfinal size as an error of type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR, even after a stream\nis closed.\n",
      "id": "ec413ad2fe1a80ef",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "A receiver SHOULD treat receipt of data at or beyond the final size as an error of type FINAL_SIZE_ERROR, even after a stream is closed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If either is received, the connection MUST be closed\nimmediately with a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR\nif the offending value was received in a transport parameter or of\ntype FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR if it was received in a frame; see\nSection 10.2.\n",
      "id": "4ce3523ca69e5eff",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "If either is received, the connection MUST be closed immediately with a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR if the offending value was received in a transport parameter or of type FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR if it was received in a frame; see Section 10.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT exceed the limit set by their peer.\n",
      "id": "a308be0bbc7f31d0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT exceed the limit set by their peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint\nthat receives a frame with a stream ID exceeding the limit it has\nsent MUST treat this as a connection error of type\nSTREAM_LIMIT_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error handling.\n",
      "id": "2cfa7e13fb1b98b9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a frame with a stream ID exceeding the limit it has sent MUST treat this as a connection error of type STREAM_LIMIT_ERROR; see Section 11 for details on error handling.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "MAX_STREAMS frames\nthat do not increase the stream limit MUST be ignored.\n",
      "id": "7e88f1d8de2e54f7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "MAX_STREAMS frames that do not increase the stream limit MUST be ignored.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that is unable to open a new stream due to the peer's\nlimits SHOULD send a STREAMS_BLOCKED frame (Section 19.14).\n",
      "id": "4c40ba00125d32b8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "An endpoint that is unable to open a new stream due to the peer's limits SHOULD send a STREAMS_BLOCKED frame (Section 19.14).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT wait\nto receive this signal before advertising additional credit, since\ndoing so will mean that the peer will be blocked for at least an\nentire round trip, and potentially indefinitely if the peer chooses\nnot to send STREAMS_BLOCKED frames.\n",
      "id": "2a734467a0b996a6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT wait to receive this signal before advertising additional credit, since doing so will mean that the peer will be blocked for at least an entire round trip, and potentially indefinitely if the peer chooses not to send STREAMS_BLOCKED frames.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid excessive buffering at multiple layers, QUIC implementations\nSHOULD provide an interface for the cryptographic protocol\nimplementation to communicate its buffering limits.\n",
      "id": "297ab0e4d35bd8fd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "To avoid excessive buffering at multiple layers, QUIC implementations SHOULD provide an interface for the cryptographic protocol implementation to communicate its buffering limits.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sequence number on\neach newly issued connection ID MUST increase by 1.\n",
      "id": "e4ca95f625cac82c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "The sequence number on each newly issued connection ID MUST increase by 1.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an endpoint issues a connection ID, it MUST accept packets that\ncarry this connection ID for the duration of the connection or until\nits peer invalidates the connection ID via a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID\nframe (Section 19.16).\n",
      "id": "c504d86a23d81914",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "When an endpoint issues a connection ID, it MUST accept packets that carry this connection ID for the duration of the connection or until its peer invalidates the connection ID via a RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frame (Section 19.16).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD ensure that its peer has a sufficient number of\navailable and unused connection IDs.\n",
      "id": "dfb766af79decaea",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD ensure that its peer has a sufficient number of available and unused connection IDs.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT\nprovide more connection IDs than the peer's limit.\n",
      "id": "0b305f4db3933c4e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT provide more connection IDs than the peer's limit.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY\nsend connection IDs that temporarily exceed a peer's limit if the\nNEW_CONNECTION_ID frame also requires the retirement of any excess,\nby including a sufficiently large value in the Retire Prior To field.\n",
      "id": "6d1e2574cbc0a3cd",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send connection IDs that temporarily exceed a peer's limit if the NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame also requires the retirement of any excess, by including a sufficiently large value in the Retire Prior To field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After processing a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame and\nadding and retiring active connection IDs, if the number of active\nconnection IDs exceeds the value advertised in its\nactive_connection_id_limit transport parameter, an endpoint MUST\nclose the connection with an error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "7cd217d509209af0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "After processing a NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame and adding and retiring active connection IDs, if the number of active connection IDs exceeds the value advertised in its active_connection_id_limit transport parameter, an endpoint MUST close the connection with an error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD supply a new connection ID when the peer retires a\nconnection ID.\n",
      "id": "7ba1664bf8584203",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD supply a new connection ID when the peer retires a connection ID.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an endpoint provided fewer connection IDs than the\npeer's active_connection_id_limit, it MAY supply a new connection ID\nwhen it receives a packet with a previously unused connection ID.\n",
      "id": "f5e55d24cd90cbeb",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "If an endpoint provided fewer connection IDs than the peer's active_connection_id_limit, it MAY supply a new connection ID when it receives a packet with a previously unused connection ID.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint MAY limit the total number of connection IDs issued for each\nconnection to avoid the risk of running out of connection IDs; see\nSection 10.3.2.\n",
      "id": "186192f920dba4fe",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY limit the total number of connection IDs issued for each connection to avoid the risk of running out of connection IDs; see Section 10.3.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY also limit the issuance of\nconnection IDs to reduce the amount of per-path state it maintains,\nsuch as path validation status, as its peer might interact with it\nover as many paths as there are issued connection IDs.\n",
      "id": "b2f5e6001acbd51a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY also limit the issuance of connection IDs to reduce the amount of per-path state it maintains, such as path validation status, as its peer might interact with it over as many paths as there are issued connection IDs.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that initiates migration and requires non-zero-length\nconnection IDs SHOULD ensure that the pool of connection IDs\navailable to its peer allows the peer to use a new connection ID on\nmigration, as the peer will be unable to respond if the pool is\nexhausted.\n",
      "id": "8f29adec6f95432a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 151,
      "quote": "An endpoint that initiates migration and requires non-zero-length connection IDs SHOULD ensure that the pool of connection IDs available to its peer allows the peer to use a new connection ID on migration, as the peer will be unable to respond if the pool is exhausted.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD retire connection IDs when\nthey are no longer actively using either the local or destination\naddress for which the connection ID was used.\n",
      "id": "b560b90634e051a0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD retire connection IDs when they are no longer actively using either the local or destination address for which the connection ID was used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to\naccept the previously issued connection IDs until they are retired by\nthe peer.\n",
      "id": "b3f665a2703b19e7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to accept the previously issued connection IDs until they are retired by the peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the endpoint can no longer process the indicated\nconnection IDs, it MAY close the connection.\n",
      "id": "7b1ea521f5f8c992",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "If the endpoint can no longer process the indicated connection IDs, it MAY close the connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receipt of an increased Retire Prior To field, the peer MUST\nstop using the corresponding connection IDs and retire them with\nRETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames before adding the newly provided\nconnection ID to the set of active connection IDs.\n",
      "id": "a3253938be9247f0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of an increased Retire Prior To field, the peer MUST stop using the corresponding connection IDs and retire them with RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames before adding the newly provided connection ID to the set of active connection IDs.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD limit the number of connection IDs it has retired\nlocally for which RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames have not yet been\nacknowledged.\n",
      "id": "942d5f416807725d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD limit the number of connection IDs it has retired locally for which RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames have not yet been acknowledged.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD allow for sending and tracking a\nnumber of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames of at least twice the value of\nthe active_connection_id_limit transport parameter.\n",
      "id": "e4d485ce35b55e7c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD allow for sending and tracking a number of RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames of at least twice the value of the active_connection_id_limit transport parameter.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST\nNOT forget a connection ID without retiring it, though it MAY choose\nto treat having connection IDs in need of retirement that exceed this\nlimit as a connection error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "62d1491d583221ec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT forget a connection ID without retiring it, though it MAY choose to treat having connection IDs in need of retirement that exceed this limit as a connection error of type CONNECTION_ID_LIMIT_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT issue updates of the Retire Prior To field\nbefore receiving RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames that retire all\nconnection IDs indicated by the previous Retire Prior To value.\n",
      "id": "70e6a9456cb8df96",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD NOT issue updates of the Retire Prior To field before receiving RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID frames that retire all connection IDs indicated by the previous Retire Prior To value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Connection IDs MUST NOT contain any information that can be used by\nan external observer (that is, one that does not cooperate with the\nissuer) to correlate them with other connection IDs for the same\nconnection.\n",
      "id": "66442f51d27db163",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "Connection IDs MUST NOT contain any information that can be used by an external observer (that is, one that does not cooperate with the issuer) to correlate them with other connection IDs for the same connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As a trivial example, this means the same connection ID\nMUST NOT be issued more than once on the same connection.\n",
      "id": "70e97e7add68f081",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "As a trivial example, this means the same connection ID MUST NOT be issued more than once on the same connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint MUST NOT use the same IP address and port for multiple\nconcurrent connections with zero-length connection IDs, unless it is\ncertain that those protocol features are not in use.\n",
      "id": "11241d5ca4b36c1e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT use the same IP address and port for multiple concurrent connections with zero-length connection IDs, unless it is certain that those protocol features are not in use.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MAY drop these packets, or it MAY buffer them in\nanticipation of later packets that allow it to compute the key.\n",
      "id": "b07a6a42c7f780ae",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "The client MAY drop these packets, or it MAY buffer them in anticipation of later packets that allow it to compute the key.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MAY drop these packets, or it MAY buffer them in\nanticipation of later packets that allow it to compute the key.\n",
      "id": "60695a7b42f716d1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "The client MAY drop these packets, or it MAY buffer them in anticipation of later packets that allow it to compute the key.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a client receives a packet that uses a different version than it\ninitially selected, it MUST discard that packet.\n",
      "id": "078563bc05171225",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "If a client receives a packet that uses a different version than it initially selected, it MUST discard that packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server receives a packet that indicates an unsupported version\nand if the packet is large enough to initiate a new connection for\nany supported version, the server SHOULD send a Version Negotiation\npacket as described in Section 6.1.\n",
      "id": "a297bb8e26f02475",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "If a server receives a packet that indicates an unsupported version and if the packet is large enough to initiate a new connection for any supported version, the server SHOULD send a Version Negotiation packet as described in Section 6.1.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY limit the number of\npackets to which it responds with a Version Negotiation packet.\n",
      "id": "20eaf6a007f2d625",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "A server MAY limit the number of packets to which it responds with a Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST drop smaller packets that specify unsupported versions.\n",
      "id": "a529a990e7258848",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "Servers MUST drop smaller packets that specify unsupported versions.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD respond with a Version\nNegotiation packet, provided that the datagram is sufficiently long.\n",
      "id": "ff909e9d153e9689",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD respond with a Version Negotiation packet, provided that the datagram is sufficiently long.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server refuses to accept a new connection, it SHOULD send an\nInitial packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame with error code\nCONNECTION_REFUSED.\n",
      "id": "bdfbe0b55ecccd2f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "If a server refuses to accept a new connection, it SHOULD send an Initial packet containing a CONNECTION_CLOSE frame with error code CONNECTION_REFUSED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the packet is a 0-RTT packet, the server MAY buffer a limited\nnumber of these packets in anticipation of a late-arriving Initial\npacket.\n",
      "id": "ed97fbfba65a5967",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "If the packet is a 0-RTT packet, the server MAY buffer a limited number of these packets in anticipation of a late-arriving Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients are not able to send Handshake packets prior to\nreceiving a server response, so servers SHOULD ignore any such\npackets.\n",
      "id": "24c44b0b58cb54c0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "Clients are not able to send Handshake packets prior to receiving a server response, so servers SHOULD ignore any such packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST drop incoming packets under all other circumstances.\n",
      "id": "b771992b1a35b745",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "Servers MUST drop incoming packets under all other circumstances.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server in a deployment that does not implement a solution to\nmaintain connection continuity when the client address changes SHOULD\nindicate that migration is not supported by using the\ndisable_active_migration transport parameter.\n",
      "id": "7ab2e87df2c85969",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "A server in a deployment that does not implement a solution to maintain connection continuity when the client address changes SHOULD indicate that migration is not supported by using the disable_active_migration transport parameter.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Server deployments that use this simple form of load balancing MUST\navoid the creation of a stateless reset oracle; see Section 21.11.\n",
      "id": "7a148ad0da8e486f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Server deployments that use this simple form of load balancing MUST avoid the creation of a stateless reset oracle; see Section 21.11.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Invalid packets that lack strong integrity protection, such as\nInitial, Retry, or Version Negotiation, MAY be discarded.\n",
      "id": "30d0026e849fd1e7",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "Invalid packets that lack strong integrity protection, such as Initial, Retry, or Version Negotiation, MAY be discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nendpoint MUST generate a connection error if processing the contents\nof these packets prior to discovering an error, or fully revert any\nchanges made during that processing.\n",
      "id": "e9e5bc9da9683ae8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST generate a connection error if processing the contents of these packets prior to discovering an error, or fully revert any changes made during that processing.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a Version Negotiation packet\nin response to receiving a Version Negotiation packet.\n",
      "id": "87532235eb7274fa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a Version Negotiation packet in response to receiving a Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY limit the number of Version Negotiation packets it\nsends.\n",
      "id": "492f50ea5bc46a5e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "A server MAY limit the number of Version Negotiation packets it sends.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that supports only this version of QUIC MUST abandon the\ncurrent connection attempt if it receives a Version Negotiation\npacket, with the following two exceptions.\n",
      "id": "5d35591abe9b608f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "A client that supports only this version of QUIC MUST abandon the current connection attempt if it receives a Version Negotiation packet, with the following two exceptions.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST discard any\nVersion Negotiation packet if it has received and successfully\nprocessed any other packet, including an earlier Version Negotiation\npacket.\n",
      "id": "bb9f0aff35056ada",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard any Version Negotiation packet if it has received and successfully processed any other packet, including an earlier Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST discard a Version Negotiation packet that\nlists the QUIC version selected by the client.\n",
      "id": "1c29b18a059a082e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "A client MUST discard a Version Negotiation packet that lists the QUIC version selected by the client.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY add reserved versions to any field where unknown or\nunsupported versions are ignored to test that a peer correctly\nignores the value.\n",
      "id": "f8042919b511a6dd",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY add reserved versions to any field where unknown or unsupported versions are ignored to test that a peer correctly ignores the value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY send packets with a reserved version to test that a\npeer correctly discards the packet.\n",
      "id": "9cf44770bc6dc4b2",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY send packets with a reserved version to test that a peer correctly discards the packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients that support\nmultiple QUIC versions SHOULD ensure that the first UDP datagram they\nsend is sized to the largest of the minimum datagram sizes from all\nversions they support, using PADDING frames (Section 19.1) as\nnecessary.\n",
      "id": "c39307444a2b54ae",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "Clients that support multiple QUIC versions SHOULD ensure that the first UDP datagram they send is sized to the largest of the minimum datagram sizes from all versions they support, using PADDING frames (Section 19.1) as necessary.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This Destination Connection ID MUST be at least 8 bytes in\nlength.\n",
      "id": "970d75b6584425db",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "This Destination Connection ID MUST be at least 8 bytes in length.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Until a packet is received from the server, the client MUST\nuse the same Destination Connection ID value on all packets in this\nconnection.\n",
      "id": "adb5ea7cad6df481",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "Until a packet is received from the server, the client MUST use the same Destination Connection ID value on all packets in this connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a\nclient has received a valid Initial packet from the server, it MUST\ndiscard any subsequent packet it receives on that connection with a\ndifferent Source Connection ID.\n",
      "id": "c44be17cf0437812",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "Once a client has received a valid Initial packet from the server, it MUST discard any subsequent packet it receives on that connection with a different Source Connection ID.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST change the Destination Connection ID it uses for\nsending packets in response to only the first received Initial or\nRetry packet.\n",
      "id": "b6395c2c8f4e3168",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "A client MUST change the Destination Connection ID it uses for sending packets in response to only the first received Initial or Retry packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST set the Destination Connection ID it\nuses for sending packets based on the first received Initial packet.\n",
      "id": "812745265173298a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "A server MUST set the Destination Connection ID it uses for sending packets based on the first received Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any further changes to the Destination Connection ID are only\npermitted if the values are taken from NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames; if\nsubsequent Initial packets include a different Source Connection ID,\nthey MUST be discarded.\n",
      "id": "166315b0224ddb65",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "Any further changes to the Destination Connection ID are only permitted if the values are taken from NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames; if subsequent Initial packets include a different Source Connection ID, they MUST be discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The values provided by a peer for these transport parameters MUST\nmatch the values that an endpoint used in the Destination and Source\nConnection ID fields of Initial packets that it sent (and received,\nfor servers).\n",
      "id": "7ceca0776e47c543",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "The values provided by a peer for these transport parameters MUST match the values that an endpoint used in the Destination and Source Connection ID fields of Initial packets that it sent (and received, for servers).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST validate that received transport\nparameters match received connection ID values.\n",
      "id": "6435d7ba06e49242",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST validate that received transport parameters match received connection ID values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST treat the absence of the\ninitial_source_connection_id transport parameter from either endpoint\nor the absence of the original_destination_connection_id transport\nparameter from the server as a connection error of type\nTRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "deffd4d73cfe4d4e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat the absence of the initial_source_connection_id transport parameter from either endpoint or the absence of the original_destination_connection_id transport parameter from the server as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST treat the following as a connection error of type\nTRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR or PROTOCOL_VIOLATION:\n",
      "id": "0f627866d552858f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat the following as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR or PROTOCOL_VIOLATION:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The definition of a new transport parameter (Section 7.4.2) MUST\nspecify whether storing the transport parameter for 0-RTT is\nmandatory, optional, or prohibited.\n",
      "id": "862b0c8ce9f2e1a9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "The definition of a new transport parameter (Section 7.4.2) MUST specify whether storing the transport parameter for 0-RTT is mandatory, optional, or prohibited.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT use remembered values for the following parameters:\nack_delay_exponent, max_ack_delay, initial_source_connection_id,\noriginal_destination_connection_id, preferred_address,\nretry_source_connection_id, and stateless_reset_token.\n",
      "id": "ae6dac1934fa1c19",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 104,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT use remembered values for the following parameters: ack_delay_exponent, max_ack_delay, initial_source_connection_id, original_destination_connection_id, preferred_address, retry_source_connection_id, and stateless_reset_token.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client\nMUST use the server's new values in the handshake instead; if the\nserver does not provide new values, the default values are used.\n",
      "id": "188a3c4f6c92e011",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "The client MUST use the server's new values in the handshake instead; if the server does not provide new values, the default values are used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that attempts to send 0-RTT data MUST remember all other\ntransport parameters used by the server that it is able to process.\n",
      "id": "ec08d5bc9e1d585e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "A client that attempts to send 0-RTT data MUST remember all other transport parameters used by the server that it is able to process.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If 0-RTT data is accepted by the server, the server MUST NOT reduce\nany limits or alter any values that might be violated by the client\nwith its 0-RTT data.\n",
      "id": "faf830d34773918b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "If 0-RTT data is accepted by the server, the server MUST NOT reduce any limits or alter any values that might be violated by the client with its 0-RTT data.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, a server that accepts 0-RTT data\nMUST NOT set values for the following parameters (Section 18.2) that\nare smaller than the remembered values of the parameters.\n",
      "id": "315954f0ead4745a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "In particular, a server that accepts 0-RTT data MUST NOT set values for the following parameters (Section 18.2) that are smaller than the remembered values of the parameters.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The applicable\nsubset of transport parameters that permit the sending of application\ndata SHOULD be set to non-zero values for 0-RTT.\n",
      "id": "8e335eaf66161795",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "The applicable subset of transport parameters that permit the sending of application data SHOULD be set to non-zero values for 0-RTT.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY store and recover the previously sent values of the\nmax_idle_timeout, max_udp_payload_size, and disable_active_migration\nparameters and reject 0-RTT if it selects smaller values.\n",
      "id": "d5b0fd0684115e30",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 152,
      "quote": "A server MAY store and recover the previously sent values of the max_idle_timeout, max_udp_payload_size, and disable_active_migration parameters and reject 0-RTT if it selects smaller values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST reject 0-RTT data if the restored values for transport\nparameters cannot be supported.\n",
      "id": "d1f1148f9998baa7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "A server MUST reject 0-RTT data if the restored values for transport parameters cannot be supported.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When sending frames in 0-RTT packets, a client MUST only use\nremembered transport parameters; importantly, it MUST NOT use updated\nvalues that it learns from the server's updated transport parameters\nor from frames received in 1-RTT packets.\n",
      "id": "79efd0b0d80a2ca8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "When sending frames in 0-RTT packets, a client MUST only use remembered transport parameters; importantly, it MUST NOT use updated values that it learns from the server's updated transport parameters or from frames received in 1-RTT packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When sending frames in 0-RTT packets, a client MUST only use\nremembered transport parameters; importantly, it MUST NOT use updated\nvalues that it learns from the server's updated transport parameters\nor from frames received in 1-RTT packets.\n",
      "id": "2510c95c3460e386",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 176,
      "quote": "When sending frames in 0-RTT packets, a client MUST only use remembered transport parameters; importantly, it MUST NOT use updated values that it learns from the server's updated transport parameters or from frames received in 1-RTT packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nserver MAY treat the use of updated transport parameters in 0-RTT as\na connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "3968b54f2da889ec",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "A server MAY treat the use of updated transport parameters in 0-RTT as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST ignore transport parameters that it does\nnot support.\n",
      "id": "51936c9c2d59aea9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST ignore transport parameters that it does not support.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a transport parameter with an\ninvalid value as a connection error of type\nTRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "35952151362bf521",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST treat receipt of a transport parameter with an invalid value as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a parameter more than once in a given\ntransport parameters extension.\n",
      "id": "54c26ed8d46e0afc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a parameter more than once in a given transport parameters extension.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of\nduplicate transport parameters as a connection error of type\nTRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "465a4d3c37777e68",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD treat receipt of duplicate transport parameters as a connection error of type TRANSPORT_PARAMETER_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST support buffering at least 4096 bytes of data\nreceived in out-of-order CRYPTO frames.\n",
      "id": "7face8d5de0871a2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST support buffering at least 4096 bytes of data received in out-of-order CRYPTO frames.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY choose to\nallow more data to be buffered during the handshake.\n",
      "id": "5f9a64e6a8e9520f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY choose to allow more data to be buffered during the handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an endpoint does not expand its buffer, it MUST close\nthe connection with a CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED error code.\n",
      "id": "ca234ef0fdd304e3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "If an endpoint does not expand its buffer, it MUST close the connection with a CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED error code.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the handshake completes, if an endpoint is unable to buffer all\ndata in a CRYPTO frame, it MAY discard that CRYPTO frame and all\nCRYPTO frames received in the future, or it MAY close the connection\nwith a CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED error code.\n",
      "id": "d91119c5d7dd17cb",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Once the handshake completes, if an endpoint is unable to buffer all data in a CRYPTO frame, it MAY discard that CRYPTO frame and all CRYPTO frames received in the future, or it MAY close the connection with a CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED error code.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the handshake completes, if an endpoint is unable to buffer all\ndata in a CRYPTO frame, it MAY discard that CRYPTO frame and all\nCRYPTO frames received in the future, or it MAY close the connection\nwith a CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED error code.\n",
      "id": "00428dab814b2995",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "Once the handshake completes, if an endpoint is unable to buffer all data in a CRYPTO frame, it MAY discard that CRYPTO frame and all CRYPTO frames received in the future, or it MAY close the connection with a CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED error code.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Packets containing\ndiscarded CRYPTO frames MUST be acknowledged because the packet has\nbeen received and processed by the transport even though the CRYPTO\nframe was discarded.\n",
      "id": "db107f9862c3b493",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "Packets containing discarded CRYPTO frames MUST be acknowledged because the packet has been received and processed by the transport even though the CRYPTO frame was discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The cryptographic handshake MUST\nprovide the following properties:\n",
      "id": "3dff35df8971cbef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "The cryptographic handshake MUST provide the following properties:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST explicitly negotiate an application protocol.\n",
      "id": "0028db16a81e832d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST explicitly negotiate an application protocol.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A token sent in a NEW_TOKEN frame or a Retry packet MUST be\nconstructed in a way that allows the server to identify how it was\nprovided to a client.\n",
      "id": "71d3a7c6ce984ac1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "A token sent in a NEW_TOKEN frame or a Retry packet MUST be constructed in a way that allows the server to identify how it was provided to a client.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This token MUST be repeated by the client in all\nInitial packets it sends for that connection after it receives the\nRetry packet.\n",
      "id": "353d645ea4ce2f44",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "This token MUST be repeated by the client in all Initial packets it sends for that connection after it receives the Retry packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Instead, the\nserver SHOULD immediately close (Section 10.2) the connection with an\nINVALID_TOKEN error.\n",
      "id": "dbbe3928fca8abc3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Instead, the server SHOULD immediately close (Section 10.2) the connection with an INVALID_TOKEN error.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY provide clients with an address validation token during\none connection that can be used on a subsequent connection.\n",
      "id": "994fe138c7458c7c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "A server MAY provide clients with an address validation token during one connection that can be used on a subsequent connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client\nMUST include the token in all Initial packets it sends, unless a\nRetry replaces the token with a newer one.\n",
      "id": "0e7bcc54e42d9d64",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "The client MUST include the token in all Initial packets it sends, unless a Retry replaces the token with a newer one.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MUST NOT use\nthe token provided in a Retry for future connections.\n",
      "id": "0e5eba6339c834e3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "The client MUST NOT use the token provided in a Retry for future connections.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY\ndiscard any Initial packet that does not carry the expected token.\n",
      "id": "35d2dfe2e060b1e1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 131,
      "quote": "Servers MAY discard any Initial packet that does not carry the expected token.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Thus, a token SHOULD have an\nexpiration time, which could be either an explicit expiration time or\nan issued timestamp that can be used to dynamically calculate the\nexpiration time.\n",
      "id": "ed1a12bd47bc95c4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 138,
      "quote": "Thus, a token SHOULD have an expiration time, which could be either an explicit expiration time or an issued timestamp that can be used to dynamically calculate the expiration time.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A token issued with NEW_TOKEN MUST NOT include information that would\nallow values to be linked by an observer to the connection on which\nit was issued.\n",
      "id": "2bc71f468317fd7a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 147,
      "quote": "A token issued with NEW_TOKEN MUST NOT include information that would allow values to be linked by an observer to the connection on which it was issued.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST ensure that every NEW_TOKEN frame it sends\nis unique across all clients, with the exception of those sent to\nrepair losses of previously sent NEW_TOKEN frames.\n",
      "id": "b70bb6f5f1674cdb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "A server MUST ensure that every NEW_TOKEN frame it sends is unique across all clients, with the exception of those sent to repair losses of previously sent NEW_TOKEN frames.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Information that\nallows the server to distinguish between tokens from Retry and\nNEW_TOKEN MAY be accessible to entities other than the server.\n",
      "id": "303a6b1f2f346ea8",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "Information that allows the server to distinguish between tokens from Retry and NEW_TOKEN MAY be accessible to entities other than the server.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When connecting to a server for\nwhich the client retains an applicable and unused token, it SHOULD\ninclude that token in the Token field of its Initial packet.\n",
      "id": "60ecf92b3086cc0d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 171,
      "quote": "When connecting to a server for which the client retains an applicable and unused token, it SHOULD include that token in the Token field of its Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT include\na token that is not applicable to the server that it is connecting\nto, unless the client has the knowledge that the server that issued\nthe token and the server the client is connecting to are jointly\nmanaging the tokens.\n",
      "id": "8eb4aadbfdb643b5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT include a token that is not applicable to the server that it is connecting to, unless the client has the knowledge that the server that issued the token and the server the client is connecting to are jointly managing the tokens.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MAY use a token from any previous\nconnection to that server.\n",
      "id": "a1ca34ed499a3d44",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 189,
      "quote": "A client MAY use a token from any previous connection to that server.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In comparison, a\ntoken obtained in a Retry packet MUST be used immediately during the\nconnection attempt and cannot be used in subsequent connection\nattempts.\n",
      "id": "162bb9786dcca53c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 196,
      "quote": "In comparison, a token obtained in a Retry packet MUST be used immediately during the connection attempt and cannot be used in subsequent connection attempts.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client SHOULD NOT reuse a token from a NEW_TOKEN frame for\ndifferent connection attempts.\n",
      "id": "c0b7826069e6dbd3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 205,
      "quote": "A client SHOULD NOT reuse a token from a NEW_TOKEN frame for different connection attempts.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a server receives an Initial packet with an address validation\ntoken, it MUST attempt to validate the token, unless it has already\ncompleted address validation.\n",
      "id": "ae7144619ea50f7b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 212,
      "quote": "When a server receives an Initial packet with an address validation token, it MUST attempt to validate the token, unless it has already completed address validation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the token is invalid, then the\nserver SHOULD proceed as if the client did not have a validated\naddress, including potentially sending a Retry packet.\n",
      "id": "c1d8536d08994770",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 220,
      "quote": "If the token is invalid, then the server SHOULD proceed as if the client did not have a validated address, including potentially sending a Retry packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the validation succeeds, the server SHOULD then allow\nthe handshake to proceed.\n",
      "id": "e5c207b8e5cd98a8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 228,
      "quote": "If the validation succeeds, the server SHOULD then allow the handshake to proceed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MAY use tokens obtained on one connection for any connection\nattempt using the same version.\n",
      "id": "a218dedb5fb4ecba",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 235,
      "quote": "Clients MAY use tokens obtained on one connection for any connection attempt using the same version.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An address validation token MUST be difficult to guess.\n",
      "id": "9458a7be71207b56",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "An address validation token MUST be difficult to guess.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For this design to work,\nthe token MUST be covered by integrity protection against\nmodification or falsification by clients.\n",
      "id": "d85ca3aeedc41fe9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "For this design to work, the token MUST be covered by integrity protection against modification or falsification by clients.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tokens\nsent in Retry packets SHOULD include information that allows the\nserver to verify that the source IP address and port in client\npackets remain constant.\n",
      "id": "d92efa92267eb1f1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Tokens sent in Retry packets SHOULD include information that allows the server to verify that the source IP address and port in client packets remain constant.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tokens sent in NEW_TOKEN frames MUST include information that allows\nthe server to verify that the client IP address has not changed from\nwhen the token was issued.\n",
      "id": "67264e41f40aa2c9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "Tokens sent in NEW_TOKEN frames MUST include information that allows the server to verify that the client IP address has not changed from when the token was issued.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client IP address has changed, the\nserver MUST adhere to the anti-amplification limit; see Section 8.\n",
      "id": "31f64ea7b5010aac",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "If the client IP address has changed, the server MUST adhere to the anti-amplification limit; see Section 8.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To protect against such attacks, servers MUST ensure that\nreplay of tokens is prevented or limited.\n",
      "id": "5bb72c6c6bd2c9d8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 83,
      "quote": "To protect against such attacks, servers MUST ensure that replay of tokens is prevented or limited.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD ensure that\ntokens sent in Retry packets are only accepted for a short time, as\nthey are returned immediately by clients.\n",
      "id": "d4380ee653fd2948",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 90,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD ensure that tokens sent in Retry packets are only accepted for a short time, as they are returned immediately by clients.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tokens that are provided\nin NEW_TOKEN frames (Section 19.7) need to be valid for longer but\nSHOULD NOT be accepted multiple times.\n",
      "id": "1551c0de35aeab10",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "Tokens that are provided in NEW_TOKEN frames (Section 19.7) need to be valid for longer but SHOULD NOT be accepted multiple times.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers are encouraged to\nallow tokens to be used only once, if possible; tokens MAY include\nadditional information about clients to further narrow applicability\nor reuse.\n",
      "id": "dea05e639def30ca",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "Servers are encouraged to allow tokens to be used only once, if possible; tokens MAY include additional information about clients to further narrow applicability or reuse.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Additionally, an endpoint MAY consider the peer address validated if\nthe peer uses a connection ID chosen by the endpoint and the\nconnection ID contains at least 64 bits of entropy.\n",
      "id": "f73eb8758714ea1f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Additionally, an endpoint MAY consider the peer address validated if the peer uses a connection ID chosen by the endpoint and the connection ID contains at least 64 bits of entropy.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Prior to validating the client address, servers MUST NOT send more\nthan three times as many bytes as the number of bytes they have\nreceived.\n",
      "id": "aa37490c7b31a27e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Prior to validating the client address, servers MUST NOT send more than three times as many bytes as the number of bytes they have received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For the purposes of\navoiding amplification prior to address validation, servers MUST\ncount all of the payload bytes received in datagrams that are\nuniquely attributed to a single connection.\n",
      "id": "71cef84febf640e9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "For the purposes of avoiding amplification prior to address validation, servers MUST count all of the payload bytes received in datagrams that are uniquely attributed to a single connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST ensure that UDP datagrams containing Initial packets\nhave UDP payloads of at least 1200 bytes, adding PADDING frames as\nnecessary.\n",
      "id": "63020251b982e31c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Clients MUST ensure that UDP datagrams containing Initial packets have UDP payloads of at least 1200 bytes, adding PADDING frames as necessary.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To\nprevent this deadlock, clients MUST send a packet on a Probe Timeout\n(PTO); see Section 6.2 of [QUIC-RECOVERY].\n",
      "id": "a861ba0bc5031f59",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "To prevent this deadlock, clients MUST send a packet on a Probe Timeout (PTO); see Section 6.2 of [QUIC-RECOVERY].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Specifically, the client\nMUST send an Initial packet in a UDP datagram that contains at least\n1200 bytes if it does not have Handshake keys, and otherwise send a\nHandshake packet.\n",
      "id": "471714743cde72f3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "Specifically, the client MUST send an Initial packet in a UDP datagram that contains at least 1200 bytes if it does not have Handshake keys, and otherwise send a Handshake packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY send multiple PATH_CHALLENGE frames to guard against\npacket loss.\n",
      "id": "68ebca40f233f253",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send multiple PATH_CHALLENGE frames to guard against packet loss.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, an endpoint SHOULD NOT send multiple\nPATH_CHALLENGE frames in a single packet.\n",
      "id": "9bcfb9ac8715adc8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "However, an endpoint SHOULD NOT send multiple PATH_CHALLENGE frames in a single packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD NOT probe a new path with packets containing a\nPATH_CHALLENGE frame more frequently than it would send an Initial\npacket.\n",
      "id": "869624b5d1dad408",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD NOT probe a new path with packets containing a PATH_CHALLENGE frame more frequently than it would send an Initial packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The endpoint MUST use unpredictable data in every PATH_CHALLENGE\nframe so that it can associate the peer's response with the\ncorresponding PATH_CHALLENGE.\n",
      "id": "31fb0d42d34f03b7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "The endpoint MUST use unpredictable data in every PATH_CHALLENGE frame so that it can associate the peer's response with the corresponding PATH_CHALLENGE.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST expand datagrams that contain a PATH_CHALLENGE frame\nto at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes,\nunless the anti-amplification limit for the path does not permit\nsending a datagram of this size.\n",
      "id": "5bf05284a438ffd6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST expand datagrams that contain a PATH_CHALLENGE frame to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes, unless the anti-amplification limit for the path does not permit sending a datagram of this size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To ensure that the path MTU is large enough, the endpoint\nMUST perform a second path validation by sending a PATH_CHALLENGE\nframe in a datagram of at least 1200 bytes.\n",
      "id": "91275876ee69469c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "To ensure that the path MTU is large enough, the endpoint MUST perform a second path validation by sending a PATH_CHALLENGE frame in a datagram of at least 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Unlike other cases where datagrams are expanded, endpoints MUST NOT\ndiscard datagrams that appear to be too small when they contain\nPATH_CHALLENGE or PATH_RESPONSE.\n",
      "id": "9442f5dc21bc8054",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Unlike other cases where datagrams are expanded, endpoints MUST NOT discard datagrams that appear to be too small when they contain PATH_CHALLENGE or PATH_RESPONSE.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On receiving a PATH_CHALLENGE frame, an endpoint MUST respond by\nechoing the data contained in the PATH_CHALLENGE frame in a\nPATH_RESPONSE frame.\n",
      "id": "e0e967a79ae160d6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "On receiving a PATH_CHALLENGE frame, an endpoint MUST respond by echoing the data contained in the PATH_CHALLENGE frame in a PATH_RESPONSE frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT delay transmission of a\npacket containing a PATH_RESPONSE frame unless constrained by\ncongestion control.\n",
      "id": "0904410647db60de",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT delay transmission of a packet containing a PATH_RESPONSE frame unless constrained by congestion control.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PATH_RESPONSE frame MUST be sent on the network path where the\nPATH_CHALLENGE frame was received.\n",
      "id": "290b31ae636afef9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "A PATH_RESPONSE frame MUST be sent on the network path where the PATH_CHALLENGE frame was received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This requirement MUST NOT be enforced by the endpoint that initiates\npath validation, as that would enable an attack on migration; see\nSection 9.3.3.\n",
      "id": "1736796599e785ed",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "This requirement MUST NOT be enforced by the endpoint that initiates path validation, as that would enable an attack on migration; see Section 9.3.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST expand datagrams that contain a PATH_RESPONSE frame\nto at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.\n",
      "id": "61cf6b3f122a21ca",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST expand datagrams that contain a PATH_RESPONSE frame to at least the smallest allowed maximum datagram size of 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, an endpoint MUST NOT expand the\ndatagram containing the PATH_RESPONSE if the resulting data exceeds\nthe anti-amplification limit.\n",
      "id": "a6d00323eeb43c59",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "However, an endpoint MUST NOT expand the datagram containing the PATH_RESPONSE if the resulting data exceeds the anti-amplification limit.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send more than one PATH_RESPONSE frame in\nresponse to one PATH_CHALLENGE frame; see Section 13.3.\n",
      "id": "6aa1749e019817a0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send more than one PATH_RESPONSE frame in response to one PATH_CHALLENGE frame; see Section 13.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, the endpoint MUST initiate\nanother path validation with an expanded datagram to verify that the\npath supports the required MTU.\n",
      "id": "fe11b8c8134adfb3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "However, the endpoint MUST initiate another path validation with an expanded datagram to verify that the path supports the required MTU.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD abandon path validation based on a timer.\n",
      "id": "100b5091d7f70f06",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD abandon path validation based on a timer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A value of\nthree times the larger of the current PTO or the PTO for the new path\n(using kInitialRtt, as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY]) is RECOMMENDED.\n",
      "id": "5f4be7f04310051b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "A value of three times the larger of the current PTO or the PTO for the new path (using kInitialRtt, as defined in [QUIC-RECOVERY]) is RECOMMENDED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint\nthat has no valid network path to its peer MAY signal this using the\nNO_VIABLE_PATH connection error, noting that this is only possible if\nthe network path exists but does not support the required MTU\n(Section 14).\n",
      "id": "a2bdbd91fddf6376",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "An endpoint that has no valid network path to its peer MAY signal this using the NO_VIABLE_PATH connection error, noting that this is only possible if the network path exists but does not support the required MTU (Section 14).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY include other frames with the PATH_CHALLENGE and\nPATH_RESPONSE frames used for path validation.\n",
      "id": "b17f91b513819600",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY include other frames with the PATH_CHALLENGE and PATH_RESPONSE frames used for path validation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, after receiving packets from an address that is\nnot yet validated, an endpoint MUST limit the amount of data it sends\nto the unvalidated address to three times the amount of data received\nfrom that address.\n",
      "id": "759f1f4b47b5789b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Therefore, after receiving packets from an address that is not yet validated, an endpoint MUST limit the amount of data it sends to the unvalidated address to three times the amount of data received from that address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY probe for peer reachability from a new local address\nusing path validation (Section 8.2) prior to migrating the connection\nto the new local address.\n",
      "id": "885b6a6aeedda490",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY probe for peer reachability from a new local address using path validation (Section 8.2) prior to migrating the connection to the new local address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY defer path\nvalidation until after a peer sends the next non-probing frame to its\nnew address.\n",
      "id": "66f02df4c13c55eb",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY defer path validation until after a peer sends the next non-probing frame to its new address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To protect the connection from failing due to such a spurious\nmigration, an endpoint MUST revert to using the last validated peer\naddress when validation of a new peer address fails.\n",
      "id": "7f3e3dcd7fdfa85f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "To protect the connection from failing due to such a spurious migration, an endpoint MUST revert to using the last validated peer address when validation of a new peer address fails.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an endpoint has no state about the last validated peer address, it\nMUST close the connection silently by discarding all connection\nstate.\n",
      "id": "2740d2ffe03aff97",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "If an endpoint has no state about the last validated peer address, it MUST close the connection silently by discarding all connection state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For instance, an endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in\nresponse to any further incoming packets.\n",
      "id": "2366df8c0ee515f8",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "For instance, an endpoint MAY send a Stateless Reset in response to any further incoming packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In response to an apparent migration, endpoints MUST validate the\npreviously active path using a PATH_CHALLENGE frame.\n",
      "id": "fca7f218db83bc78",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "In response to an apparent migration, endpoints MUST validate the previously active path using a PATH_CHALLENGE frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives a PATH_CHALLENGE on an active path SHOULD\nsend a non-probing packet in response.\n",
      "id": "048bf771ca8cb6b7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives a PATH_CHALLENGE on an active path SHOULD send a non-probing packet in response.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the recipient permits the migration, it MUST send subsequent\npackets to the new peer address and MUST initiate path validation\n(Section 8.2) to verify the peer's ownership of the address if\nvalidation is not already underway.\n",
      "id": "23330c3c17c05947",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "If the recipient permits the migration, it MUST send subsequent packets to the new peer address and MUST initiate path validation (Section 8.2) to verify the peer's ownership of the address if validation is not already underway.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the recipient permits the migration, it MUST send subsequent\npackets to the new peer address and MUST initiate path validation\n(Section 8.2) to verify the peer's ownership of the address if\nvalidation is not already underway.\n",
      "id": "a1a8e1f7ce6af81d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "If the recipient permits the migration, it MUST send subsequent packets to the new peer address and MUST initiate path validation (Section 8.2) to verify the peer's ownership of the address if validation is not already underway.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY send data to an unvalidated peer address, but it MUST\nprotect against potential attacks as described in Sections 9.3.1 and\n9.3.2.\n",
      "id": "33524d557d4d9b6f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send data to an unvalidated peer address, but it MUST protect against potential attacks as described in Sections 9.3.1 and 9.3.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY skip validation of a peer address if that\naddress has been seen recently.\n",
      "id": "0de57d94d3caa684",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY skip validation of a peer address if that address has been seen recently.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After verifying a new client address, the server SHOULD send new\naddress validation tokens (Section 8) to the client.\n",
      "id": "40f5d2ce5feaf1c6",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "After verifying a new client address, the server SHOULD send new address validation tokens (Section 8) to the client.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Packets sent on the old path MUST NOT contribute to\ncongestion control or RTT estimation for the new path.\n",
      "id": "38f86d165f49d4df",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "Packets sent on the old path MUST NOT contribute to congestion control or RTT estimation for the new path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On confirming a peer's ownership of its new address, an endpoint MUST\nimmediately reset the congestion controller and round-trip time\nestimator for the new path to initial values (see Appendices A.3 and\nB.3 of [QUIC-RECOVERY]) unless the only change in the peer's address\nis its port number.\n",
      "id": "5ce6760d617d2f29",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "On confirming a peer's ownership of its new address, an endpoint MUST immediately reset the congestion controller and round-trip time estimator for the new path to initial values (see Appendices A.3 and B.3 of [QUIC-RECOVERY]) unless the only change in the peer's address is its port number.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because port-only changes are commonly the\nresult of NAT rebinding or other middlebox activity, the endpoint MAY\ninstead retain its congestion control state and round-trip estimate\nin those cases instead of reverting to initial values.\n",
      "id": "39a02ba0dbe40d08",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "Because port-only changes are commonly the result of NAT rebinding or other middlebox activity, the endpoint MAY instead retain its congestion control state and round-trip estimate in those cases instead of reverting to initial values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This timer SHOULD be set as described in Section 6.2.1 of\n[QUIC-RECOVERY] and MUST NOT be more aggressive.\n",
      "id": "4ea778205eb31de6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "This timer SHOULD be set as described in Section 6.2.1 of [QUIC-RECOVERY] and MUST NOT be more aggressive.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "At any time, endpoints MAY change the Destination Connection ID they\ntransmit with to a value that has not been used on another path.\n",
      "id": "44ca2e476f1815c8",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "At any time, endpoints MAY change the Destination Connection ID they transmit with to a value that has not been used on another path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT reuse a connection ID when sending from more\nthan one local address -- for example, when initiating connection\nmigration as described in Section 9.2 or when probing a new network\npath as described in Section 9.1.\n",
      "id": "1678e937f7d9776e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT reuse a connection ID when sending from more than one local address -- for example, when initiating connection migration as described in Section 9.2 or when probing a new network path as described in Section 9.1.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Similarly, an endpoint MUST NOT reuse a connection ID when sending to\nmore than one destination address.\n",
      "id": "cca6f19c963cc67e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "Similarly, an endpoint MUST NOT reuse a connection ID when sending to more than one destination address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Due to network changes outside\nthe control of its peer, an endpoint might receive packets from a new\nsource address with the same Destination Connection ID field value,\nin which case it MAY continue to use the current connection ID with\nthe new remote address while still sending from the same local\naddress.\n",
      "id": "e16b0c11f199c92b",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "Due to network changes outside the control of its peer, an endpoint might receive packets from a new source address with the same Destination Connection ID field value, in which case it MAY continue to use the current connection ID with the new remote address while still sending from the same local address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD NOT initiate migration with a peer that has\nrequested a zero-length connection ID, because traffic over the new\npath might be trivially linkable to traffic over the old one.\n",
      "id": "2719d7d5fae72c78",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD NOT initiate migration with a peer that has requested a zero-length connection ID, because traffic over the new path might be trivially linkable to traffic over the old one.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Changing address\ncan cause a peer to reset its congestion control state (see\nSection 9.4), so addresses SHOULD only be changed infrequently.\n",
      "id": "791df8c9573a43ad",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "Changing address can cause a peer to reset its congestion control state (see Section 9.4), so addresses SHOULD only be changed infrequently.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To ensure that migration is possible and\npackets sent on different paths cannot be correlated, endpoints\nSHOULD provide new connection IDs before peers migrate; see\nSection 5.1.1.\n",
      "id": "5bb866d3bdeac482",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "To ensure that migration is possible and packets sent on different paths cannot be correlated, endpoints SHOULD provide new connection IDs before peers migrate; see Section 5.1.1.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY communicate a preferred address of each address family\n(IPv4 and IPv6) to allow clients to pick the one most suited to their\nnetwork attachment.\n",
      "id": "9e1e14961b306e42",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "Servers MAY communicate a preferred address of each address family (IPv4 and IPv6) to allow clients to pick the one most suited to their network attachment.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the handshake is confirmed, the client SHOULD select one of the\ntwo addresses provided by the server and initiate path validation\n(see Section 8.2).\n",
      "id": "1053c952956d53b7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Once the handshake is confirmed, the client SHOULD select one of the two addresses provided by the server and initiate path validation (see Section 8.2).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As soon as path validation succeeds, the client SHOULD begin sending\nall future packets to the new server address using the new connection\nID and discontinue use of the old server address.\n",
      "id": "6b07d7a264c4ed58",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "As soon as path validation succeeds, the client SHOULD begin sending all future packets to the new server address using the new connection ID and discontinue use of the old server address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If path validation\nfails, the client MUST continue sending all future packets to the\nserver's original IP address.\n",
      "id": "2d615fead0c955a0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "If path validation fails, the client MUST continue sending all future packets to the server's original IP address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that migrates to a preferred address MUST validate the\naddress it chooses before migrating; see Section 21.5.3.\n",
      "id": "89a7308c121814fd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "A client that migrates to a preferred address MUST validate the address it chooses before migrating; see Section 21.5.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST send non-\nprobing packets from its original address until it receives a non-\nprobing packet from the client at its preferred address and until the\nserver has validated the new path.\n",
      "id": "9a83dbaeebeda2eb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "The server MUST send non- probing packets from its original address until it receives a non- probing packet from the client at its preferred address and until the server has validated the new path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST probe on the path toward the client from its\npreferred address.\n",
      "id": "ac0055e3e734de3e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "The server MUST probe on the path toward the client from its preferred address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server SHOULD drop\nnewer packets for this connection that are received on the old IP\naddress.\n",
      "id": "359003a1776a0ed2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "The server SHOULD drop newer packets for this connection that are received on the old IP address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MAY continue to process delayed packets that are\nreceived on the old IP address.\n",
      "id": "097caac8c8a8e2b1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "The server MAY continue to process delayed packets that are received on the old IP address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT use these for other connections,\nincluding connections that are resumed from the current connection.\n",
      "id": "e554f66f4c330717",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT use these for other connections, including connections that are resumed from the current connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In this case, the client\nSHOULD perform path validation to both the original and preferred\nserver address from the client's new address concurrently.\n",
      "id": "783caea35edaa857",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "In this case, the client SHOULD perform path validation to both the original and preferred server address from the client's new address concurrently.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If path validation of the server's preferred address succeeds, the\nclient MUST abandon validation of the original address and migrate to\nusing the server's preferred address.\n",
      "id": "92de5eaf9f3bcfb8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 46,
      "quote": "If path validation of the server's preferred address succeeds, the client MUST abandon validation of the original address and migrate to using the server's preferred address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If path validation of the\nserver's preferred address fails but validation of the server's\noriginal address succeeds, the client MAY migrate to its new address\nand continue sending to the server's original address.\n",
      "id": "5603818ccabe2891",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "If path validation of the server's preferred address fails but validation of the server's original address succeeds, the client MAY migrate to its new address and continue sending to the server's original address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If packets received at the server's preferred address have a\ndifferent source address than observed from the client during the\nhandshake, the server MUST protect against potential attacks as\ndescribed in Sections 9.3.1 and 9.3.2.\n",
      "id": "e198ebb9b76f9dbb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "If packets received at the server's preferred address have a different source address than observed from the client during the handshake, the server MUST protect against potential attacks as described in Sections 9.3.1 and 9.3.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD initiate path validation to the client's new address\nupon receiving a probe packet from a different address; see\nSection 8.\n",
      "id": "3937a9db0453f5dd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD initiate path validation to the client's new address upon receiving a probe packet from a different address; see Section 8.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that migrates to a new address SHOULD use a preferred\naddress from the same address family for the server.\n",
      "id": "e24118c1d6142dee",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "A client that migrates to a new address SHOULD use a preferred address from the same address family for the server.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This\nconnection ID is provided to ensure that the client has a connection\nID available for migration, but the client MAY use this connection ID\non any path.\n",
      "id": "0ab3a3bccc9bd011",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "This connection ID is provided to ensure that the client has a connection ID available for migration, but the client MAY use this connection ID on any path.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a\nclient receives packets from a new server address when the client has\nnot initiated a migration to that address, the client SHOULD discard\nthese packets.\n",
      "id": "c797f84432fe40f5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "If a client receives packets from a new server address when the client has not initiated a migration to that address, the client SHOULD discard these packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints that send data using IPv6 SHOULD apply an IPv6 flow label\nin compliance with [RFC6437], unless the local API does not allow\nsetting IPv6 flow labels.\n",
      "id": "14fa71bef174fadd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Endpoints that send data using IPv6 SHOULD apply an IPv6 flow label in compliance with [RFC6437], unless the local API does not allow setting IPv6 flow labels.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The flow label generation MUST be designed to minimize the chances of\nlinkability with a previously used flow label, as a stable flow label\nwould enable correlating activity on multiple paths; see Section 9.5.\n",
      "id": "5a24c678de15bd85",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "The flow label generation MUST be designed to minimize the chances of linkability with a previously used flow label, as a stable flow label would enable correlating activity on multiple paths; see Section 9.5.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate\nconnection migration before the handshake is confirmed, as defined in\nSection 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS].\n",
      "id": "3754dd98dffda0b0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate connection migration before the handshake is confirmed, as defined in Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the peer sent the disable_active_migration transport parameter, an\nendpoint also MUST NOT send packets (including probing packets; see\nSection 9.1) from a different local address to the address the peer\nused during the handshake, unless the endpoint has acted on a\npreferred_address transport parameter from the peer.\n",
      "id": "62df56156fb6e4f5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "If the peer sent the disable_active_migration transport parameter, an endpoint also MUST NOT send packets (including probing packets; see Section 9.1) from a different local address to the address the peer used during the handshake, unless the endpoint has acted on a preferred_address transport parameter from the peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the peer\nviolates this requirement, the endpoint MUST either drop the incoming\npackets on that path without generating a Stateless Reset or proceed\nwith path validation and allow the peer to migrate.\n",
      "id": "9b878cf178d3c788",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "If the peer violates this requirement, the endpoint MUST either drop the incoming packets on that path without generating a Stateless Reset or proceed with path validation and allow the peer to migrate.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST\nperform path validation (Section 8.2) if it detects any change to a\npeer's address, unless it has previously validated that address.\n",
      "id": "7507d60274dec992",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST perform path validation (Section 8.2) if it detects any change to a peer's address, unless it has previously validated that address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an endpoint has no validated path on which to send packets, it\nMAY discard connection state.\n",
      "id": "4a92d5875474e5a5",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "When an endpoint has no validated path on which to send packets, it MAY discard connection state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint capable of connection\nmigration MAY wait for a new path to become available before\ndiscarding connection state.\n",
      "id": "5e2ac4c3ec8512b6",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "An endpoint capable of connection migration MAY wait for a new path to become available before discarding connection state.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a client receives\npackets from an unknown server address, the client MUST discard these\npackets.\n",
      "id": "f7cbeb6002b1a3bf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "If a client receives packets from an unknown server address, the client MUST discard these packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST send a\nHANDSHAKE_DONE frame as soon as the handshake is complete.\n",
      "id": "e26d8caf6fdd7308",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "The server MUST send a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame as soon as the handshake is complete.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Additionally, a client MAY consider the handshake to be confirmed\nwhen it receives an acknowledgment for a 1-RTT packet.\n",
      "id": "ac6a2d4ded35c580",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Additionally, a client MAY consider the handshake to be confirmed when it receives an acknowledgment for a 1-RTT packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  If the packet is from a previously installed encryption level, it\nMUST NOT contain data that extends past the end of previously\nreceived data in that flow.\n",
      "id": "dd3c75de6e238f50",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "*  If the packet is from a previously installed encryption level, it MUST NOT contain data that extends past the end of previously received data in that flow.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST treat any\nviolations of this requirement as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "104af49c55fd7002",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 107,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST treat any violations of this requirement as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When TLS\nprovides keys for a higher encryption level, if there is data from\na previous encryption level that TLS has not consumed, this MUST\nbe treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "44c23a453e527497",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "When TLS provides keys for a higher encryption level, if there is data from a previous encryption level that TLS has not consumed, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.1.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While waiting for TLS processing to\ncomplete, an endpoint SHOULD buffer received packets if they might be\nprocessed using keys that are not yet available.\n",
      "id": "80d45779e9fc63ca",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "While waiting for TLS processing to complete, an endpoint SHOULD buffer received packets if they might be processed using keys that are not yet available.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD\ncontinue to respond to packets that can be processed during this\ntime.\n",
      "id": "d658381659295dcf",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD continue to respond to packets that can be processed during this time.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.1.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT offer TLS versions older than 1.3.\n",
      "id": "511d57f420209d23",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT offer TLS versions older than 1.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST terminate the connection if a\nversion of TLS older than 1.3 is negotiated.\n",
      "id": "7a9f7f03ae812e2e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST terminate the connection if a version of TLS older than 1.3 is negotiated.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To\navoid this, servers MAY use the Retry feature (see Section 8.1 of\n[QUIC-TRANSPORT]) to only buffer partial ClientHello messages from\nclients with a validated address.\n",
      "id": "0b26957a366da714",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "To avoid this, servers MAY use the Retry feature (see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) to only buffer partial ClientHello messages from clients with a validated address.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST authenticate the identity of the server.\n",
      "id": "736d0ae1db312afa",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "A client MUST authenticate the identity of the server.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY request that the client authenticate during the\nhandshake.\n",
      "id": "60f61abdc28ce953",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "A server MAY request that the client authenticate during the handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY refuse a connection if the client is unable\nto authenticate when requested.\n",
      "id": "583726e720646243",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "A server MAY refuse a connection if the client is unable to authenticate when requested.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST NOT use post-handshake client authentication (as\ndefined in Section 4.6.2 of [TLS13]) because the multiplexing offered\nby QUIC prevents clients from correlating the certificate request\nwith the application-level event that triggered it (see\n[HTTP2-TLS13]).\n",
      "id": "5e6d99e00cf3be38",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT use post-handshake client authentication (as defined in Section 4.6.2 of [TLS13]) because the multiplexing offered by QUIC prevents clients from correlating the certificate request with the application-level event that triggered it (see [HTTP2-TLS13]).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "More specifically, servers MUST NOT send post-\nhandshake TLS CertificateRequest messages, and clients MUST treat\nreceipt of such messages as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "More specifically, servers MUST NOT send post- handshake TLS CertificateRequest messages, and clients MUST treat receipt of such messages as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "More specifically, servers MUST NOT send post-\nhandshake TLS CertificateRequest messages, and clients MUST treat\nreceipt of such messages as a connection error of type\nPROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "7331307381553d6f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "More specifically, servers MUST NOT send post- handshake TLS CertificateRequest messages, and clients MUST treat receipt of such messages as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD NOT reuse tickets as\nthat allows entities other than the server to correlate connections;\nsee Appendix C.4 of [TLS13].\n",
      "id": "6d8c284b4bfaa356",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD NOT reuse tickets as that allows entities other than the server to correlate connections; see Appendix C.4 of [TLS13].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT send the early_data extension with a\nmax_early_data_size field set to any value other than 0xffffffff.\n",
      "id": "8e34ffaa41163500",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT send the early_data extension with a max_early_data_size field set to any value other than 0xffffffff.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nclient MUST treat receipt of a NewSessionTicket that contains an\nearly_data extension with any other value as a connection error of\ntype PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "4eb8ad70446164db",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a NewSessionTicket that contains an early_data extension with any other value as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When rejecting 0-RTT, a server MUST NOT\nprocess any 0-RTT packets, even if it could.\n",
      "id": "fb566a2bc8f6302c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "When rejecting 0-RTT, a server MUST NOT process any 0-RTT packets, even if it could.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When 0-RTT was\nrejected, a client SHOULD treat receipt of an acknowledgment for a\n0-RTT packet as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, if it\nis able to detect the condition.\n",
      "id": "1f447322cb298a76",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "When 0-RTT was rejected, a client SHOULD treat receipt of an acknowledgment for a 0-RTT packet as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, if it is able to detect the condition.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client therefore MUST reset the state of all\nstreams, including application state bound to those streams.\n",
      "id": "714474469180745e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "The client therefore MUST reset the state of all streams, including application state bound to those streams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MAY reattempt 0-RTT if it receives a Retry or Version\nNegotiation packet.\n",
      "id": "20ce51973fbdc645",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "A client MAY reattempt 0-RTT if it receives a Retry or Version Negotiation packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although it is in principle possible to use this feature\nfor address verification, QUIC implementations SHOULD instead use the\nRetry feature; see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].\n",
      "id": "512e9116bca109fa",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "Although it is in principle possible to use this feature for address verification, QUIC implementations SHOULD instead use the Retry feature; see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As QUIC provides\nalternative mechanisms for connection termination and the TLS\nconnection is only closed if an error is encountered, a QUIC endpoint\nMUST treat any alert from TLS as if it were at the \"fatal\" level.\n",
      "id": "6abd3fb11212117b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "As QUIC provides alternative mechanisms for connection termination and the TLS connection is only closed if an error is encountered, a QUIC endpoint MUST treat any alert from TLS as if it were at the \"fatal\" level.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY use a generic\nerror code to avoid possibly exposing confidential information.\n",
      "id": "168ba8c6f079d159",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY use a generic error code to avoid possibly exposing confidential information.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Thus, a client MUST discard Initial keys when it first sends a\nHandshake packet and a server MUST discard Initial keys when it first\nsuccessfully processes a Handshake packet.\n",
      "id": "08c13935a12086c0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "Thus, a client MUST discard Initial keys when it first sends a Handshake packet and a server MUST discard Initial keys when it first successfully processes a Handshake packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Thus, a client MUST discard Initial keys when it first sends a\nHandshake packet and a server MUST discard Initial keys when it first\nsuccessfully processes a Handshake packet.\n",
      "id": "41d208e3a6ed32b5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "Thus, a client MUST discard Initial keys when it first sends a Handshake packet and a server MUST discard Initial keys when it first successfully processes a Handshake packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT send\nInitial packets after this point.\n",
      "id": "4cdcbeff17bf0b5d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT send Initial packets after this point.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST discard its Handshake keys when the TLS handshake is\nconfirmed (Section 4.1.2).\n",
      "id": "c15c15459c143973",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 8,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST discard its Handshake keys when the TLS handshake is confirmed (Section 4.1.2).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, a client SHOULD discard 0-RTT keys as soon as it installs\n1-RTT keys as they have no use after that moment.\n",
      "id": "1f873c82be82355f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Therefore, a client SHOULD discard 0-RTT keys as soon as it installs 1-RTT keys as they have no use after that moment.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Additionally, a server MAY discard 0-RTT keys as soon as it receives\na 1-RTT packet.\n",
      "id": "ffe98a460c92108f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "Additionally, a server MAY discard 0-RTT keys as soon as it receives a 1-RTT packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY temporarily retain\n0-RTT keys to allow decrypting reordered packets without requiring\ntheir contents to be retransmitted with 1-RTT keys.\n",
      "id": "46c4022250f4bfb0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Servers MAY temporarily retain 0-RTT keys to allow decrypting reordered packets without requiring their contents to be retransmitted with 1-RTT keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After receiving\na 1-RTT packet, servers MUST discard 0-RTT keys within a short time;\nthe RECOMMENDED time period is three times the Probe Timeout (PTO,\nsee [QUIC-RECOVERY]).\n",
      "id": "789c84b6cda0d53f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "After receiving a 1-RTT packet, servers MUST discard 0-RTT keys within a short time; the RECOMMENDED time period is three times the Probe Timeout (PTO, see [QUIC-RECOVERY]).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY discard 0-RTT keys earlier if it\ndetermines that it has received all 0-RTT packets, which can be done\nby keeping track of missing packet numbers.\n",
      "id": "05d25b3d18397669",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "A server MAY discard 0-RTT keys earlier if it determines that it has received all 0-RTT packets, which can be done by keeping track of missing packet numbers.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If packets from a lower encryption level contain\nCRYPTO frames, frames that retransmit that data MUST be sent at the\nsame encryption level.\n",
      "id": "17c261c7811f3ad9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "If packets from a lower encryption level contain CRYPTO frames, frames that retransmit that data MUST be sent at the same encryption level.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Though an endpoint might retain older keys, new data MUST be sent at\nthe highest currently available encryption level.\n",
      "id": "f1fb2b0613ada526",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Though an endpoint might retain older keys, new data MUST be sent at the highest currently available encryption level.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These packets MAY also include PADDING frames.\n",
      "id": "a5ecd973b6a49fff",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "These packets MAY also include PADDING frames.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If QUIC needs to retransmit that data, it MUST use\nthe same keys even if TLS has already updated to newer keys.\n",
      "id": "17207c41759e9b87",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "If QUIC needs to retransmit that data, it MUST use the same keys even if TLS has already updated to newer keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When packets of different types need to be sent,\nendpoints SHOULD use coalesced packets to send them in the same UDP\ndatagram.\n",
      "id": "4816853cb1241237",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "When packets of different types need to be sent, endpoints SHOULD use coalesced packets to send them in the same UDP datagram.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Other versions of TLS MUST provide a similar function in order to be\nused with QUIC.\n",
      "id": "e408c13ed2a103ed",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "Other versions of TLS MUST provide a similar function in order to be used with QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Future versions of QUIC SHOULD generate a new salt value, thus\nensuring that the keys are different for each version of QUIC.\n",
      "id": "77f809cab45640c5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "Future versions of QUIC SHOULD generate a new salt value, thus ensuring that the keys are different for each version of QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The HKDF-Expand-Label function defined in TLS 1.3 MUST be used for\nInitial packets even where the TLS versions offered do not include\nTLS 1.3.\n",
      "id": "9e77c0b9b84b3ebb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "The HKDF-Expand-Label function defined in TLS 1.3 MUST be used for Initial packets even where the TLS versions offered do not include TLS 1.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A cipher suite MUST NOT be\nnegotiated unless a header protection scheme is defined for the\ncipher suite.\n",
      "id": "54fd7c99b12900da",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "A cipher suite MUST NOT be negotiated unless a header protection scheme is defined for the cipher suite.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT reject a ClientHello that offers a cipher suite\nthat it does not support, or it would be impossible to deploy a new\ncipher suite.\n",
      "id": "82c52e4a7e587882",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT reject a ClientHello that offers a cipher suite that it does not support, or it would be impossible to deploy a new cipher suite.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST initiate a key update\n(Section 6) prior to exceeding any limit set for the AEAD that is in\nuse.\n",
      "id": "1fd7a4b503ba35ad",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST initiate a key update (Section 6) prior to exceeding any limit set for the AEAD that is in use.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Before a TLS cipher suite can be used with QUIC, a header protection\nalgorithm MUST be specified for the AEAD used with that cipher suite.\n",
      "id": "471701866ffdb361",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Before a TLS cipher suite can be used with QUIC, a header protection algorithm MUST be specified for the AEAD used with that cipher suite.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST discard packets that are not long enough to contain\na complete sample.\n",
      "id": "398241f624ccfe6d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST discard packets that are not long enough to contain a complete sample.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once an endpoint successfully receives a packet with a given packet\nnumber, it MUST discard all packets in the same packet number space\nwith higher packet numbers if they cannot be successfully unprotected\nwith either the same key, or -- if there is a key update -- a\nsubsequent packet protection key; see Section 6.\n",
      "id": "099fbeb3d5e5e361",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "Once an endpoint successfully receives a packet with a given packet number, it MUST discard all packets in the same packet number space with higher packet numbers if they cannot be successfully unprotected with either the same key, or -- if there is a key update -- a subsequent packet protection key; see Section 6.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Similarly, a packet\nthat appears to trigger a key update but cannot be unprotected\nsuccessfully MUST be discarded.\n",
      "id": "2f1142e99acbb2f4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "Similarly, a packet that appears to trigger a key update but cannot be unprotected successfully MUST be discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client\ntherefore MUST NOT use 0-RTT for application data unless specifically\nrequested by the application that is in use.\n",
      "id": "4f07b33fe5528a1e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "A client therefore MUST NOT use 0-RTT for application data unless specifically requested by the application that is in use.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application protocol that uses QUIC MUST include a profile that\ndefines acceptable use of 0-RTT; otherwise, 0-RTT can only be used to\ncarry QUIC frames that do not carry application data.\n",
      "id": "98def066aa0e9cb1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "An application protocol that uses QUIC MUST include a profile that defines acceptable use of 0-RTT; otherwise, 0-RTT can only be used to carry QUIC frames that do not carry application data.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MAY wish to apply additional restrictions on what data it\nsends prior to the completion of the TLS handshake.\n",
      "id": "ff5d76d27a1ba6b0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "A client MAY wish to apply additional restrictions on what data it sends prior to the completion of the TLS handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client SHOULD stop sending 0-RTT data\nif it receives an indication that 0-RTT data has been rejected.\n",
      "id": "1d667f7c2999d51c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "A client SHOULD stop sending 0-RTT data if it receives an indication that 0-RTT data has been rejected.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST NOT use 0-RTT keys to protect packets; it uses 1-RTT\nkeys to protect acknowledgments of 0-RTT packets.\n",
      "id": "cf8577a771718715",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT use 0-RTT keys to protect packets; it uses 1-RTT keys to protect acknowledgments of 0-RTT packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT\nattempt to decrypt 0-RTT packets it receives and instead MUST discard\nthem.\n",
      "id": "21bb3806e971bc47",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT attempt to decrypt 0-RTT packets it receives and instead MUST discard them.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT\nattempt to decrypt 0-RTT packets it receives and instead MUST discard\nthem.\n",
      "id": "062885a1f7e5d933",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT attempt to decrypt 0-RTT packets it receives and instead MUST discard them.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a client has installed 1-RTT keys, it MUST NOT send any more\n0-RTT packets.\n",
      "id": "2a51688a17ecb552",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 111,
      "quote": "Once a client has installed 1-RTT keys, it MUST NOT send any more 0-RTT packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints in either role MUST NOT decrypt 1-RTT packets from\ntheir peer prior to completing the handshake.\n",
      "id": "1bbeb270688617a7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "Endpoints in either role MUST NOT decrypt 1-RTT packets from their peer prior to completing the handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST NOT process\nincoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is\ncomplete.\n",
      "id": "182f07301f7d385b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT process incoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is complete.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Received\npackets protected with 1-RTT keys MAY be stored and later decrypted\nand used once the handshake is complete.\n",
      "id": "48e1933c20cf925a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "Received packets protected with 1-RTT keys MAY be stored and later decrypted and used once the handshake is complete.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MAY retain these packets for\nlater decryption in anticipation of receiving a ClientHello.\n",
      "id": "f3a8509be94bb311",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "The server MAY retain these packets for later decryption in anticipation of receiving a ClientHello.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Even if it has 1-RTT secrets, a client MUST NOT\nprocess incoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is\ncomplete.\n",
      "id": "0297a9b292a1e8d8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "Even if it has 1-RTT secrets, a client MUST NOT process incoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is complete.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/5.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-5.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate a key update prior to having confirmed\nthe handshake (Section 4.1.2).\n",
      "id": "2bea64447cf4e3b0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate a key update prior to having confirmed the handshake (Section 4.1.2).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate a\nsubsequent key update unless it has received an acknowledgment for a\npacket that was sent protected with keys from the current key phase.\n",
      "id": "3ad82f1956fef698",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate a subsequent key update unless it has received an acknowledgment for a packet that was sent protected with keys from the current key phase.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST retain old keys until it has successfully\nunprotected a packet sent using the new keys.\n",
      "id": "c09e8fafe3b815f3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST retain old keys until it has successfully unprotected a packet sent using the new keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD\nretain old keys for some time after unprotecting a packet sent using\nthe new keys.\n",
      "id": "3c7cebfbc7d3303d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old keys for some time after unprotecting a packet sent using the new keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The endpoint MUST update its\nsend keys to the corresponding key phase in response, as described in\nSection 6.1.\n",
      "id": "350a4f115e2ba3b3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "The endpoint MUST update its send keys to the corresponding key phase in response, as described in Section 6.1.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Sending keys MUST be updated before sending an\nacknowledgment for the packet that was received with updated keys.\n",
      "id": "6daf94142c799a6b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Sending keys MUST be updated before sending an acknowledgment for the packet that was received with updated keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint\nMAY treat such consecutive key updates as a connection error of type\nKEY_UPDATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "e30b25d33b7c41ab",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY treat such consecutive key updates as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that receives an acknowledgment that is carried in a\npacket protected with old keys where any acknowledged packet was\nprotected with newer keys MAY treat that as a connection error of\ntype KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "51e24a309f5e5b34",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "An endpoint that receives an acknowledgment that is carried in a packet protected with old keys where any acknowledged packet was protected with newer keys MAY treat that as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints responding to an apparent key update MUST NOT generate a\ntiming side-channel signal that might indicate that the Key Phase bit\nwas invalid (see Section 9.5).\n",
      "id": "589b56449b7d569d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Endpoints responding to an apparent key update MUST NOT generate a timing side-channel signal that might indicate that the Key Phase bit was invalid (see Section 9.5).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY\ngenerate new keys as part of packet processing, but this creates a\ntiming signal that could be used by an attacker to learn when key\nupdates happen and thus leak the value of the Key Phase bit.\n",
      "id": "246ace45610f51e2",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY generate new keys as part of packet processing, but this creates a timing signal that could be used by an attacker to learn when key updates happen and thus leak the value of the Key Phase bit.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For a short period after a key\nupdate completes, up to the PTO, endpoints MAY defer generation of\nthe next set of receive packet protection keys.\n",
      "id": "ff38c0324287dce0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "For a short period after a key update completes, up to the PTO, endpoints MAY defer generation of the next set of receive packet protection keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once generated, the next set of packet protection keys SHOULD be\nretained, even if the packet that was received was subsequently\ndiscarded.\n",
      "id": "f3a68a80a8ecf04b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "Once generated, the next set of packet protection keys SHOULD be retained, even if the packet that was received was subsequently discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For this reason, endpoints MUST be able to retain two sets of packet\nprotection keys for receiving packets: the current and the next.\n",
      "id": "62f608bc210cd886",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 70,
      "quote": "For this reason, endpoints MUST be able to retain two sets of packet protection keys for receiving packets: the current and the next.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Packets with higher packet numbers MUST be protected with either the\nsame or newer packet protection keys than packets with lower packet\nnumbers.\n",
      "id": "ff40a701e4f2b0e2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Packets with higher packet numbers MUST be protected with either the same or newer packet protection keys than packets with lower packet numbers.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that successfully removes protection with old\nkeys when newer keys were used for packets with lower packet numbers\nMUST treat this as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "ce6046b36f5547b5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "An endpoint that successfully removes protection with old keys when newer keys were used for packets with lower packet numbers MUST treat this as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY allow a period of approximately the Probe Timeout\n(PTO; see [QUIC-RECOVERY]) after promoting the next set of receive\nkeys to be current before it creates the subsequent set of packet\nprotection keys.\n",
      "id": "9af88fd84ea0aeb1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY allow a period of approximately the Probe Timeout (PTO; see [QUIC-RECOVERY]) after promoting the next set of receive keys to be current before it creates the subsequent set of packet protection keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These updated keys MAY replace the previous keys at\nthat time.\n",
      "id": "a5912ff6801cb849",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "These updated keys MAY replace the previous keys at that time.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD wait three times\nthe PTO before initiating a key update after receiving an\nacknowledgment that confirms that the previous key update was\nreceived.\n",
      "id": "359b8d76ccfb8e52",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD wait three times the PTO before initiating a key update after receiving an acknowledgment that confirms that the previous key update was received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old read keys for no more than three times\nthe PTO after having received a packet protected using the new keys.\n",
      "id": "fe38612b261d4850",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old read keys for no more than three times the PTO after having received a packet protected using the new keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After this period, old read keys and their corresponding secrets\nSHOULD be discarded.\n",
      "id": "6acffcbdcc4e3f9c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 85,
      "quote": "After this period, old read keys and their corresponding secrets SHOULD be discarded.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST count the number of encrypted packets for each set of\nkeys.\n",
      "id": "2770efe716ebe6f8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST count the number of encrypted packets for each set of keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the total number of encrypted packets with the same key\nexceeds the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint\nMUST stop using those keys.\n",
      "id": "0bcb268a49e6973e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "If the total number of encrypted packets with the same key exceeds the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST stop using those keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST initiate a key update\nbefore sending more protected packets than the confidentiality limit\nfor the selected AEAD permits.\n",
      "id": "7d78b881f55910c7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST initiate a key update before sending more protected packets than the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD permits.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a key update is not possible or\nintegrity limits are reached, the endpoint MUST stop using the\nconnection and only send stateless resets in response to receiving\npackets.\n",
      "id": "6bd50ae4311d8611",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "If a key update is not possible or integrity limits are reached, the endpoint MUST stop using the connection and only send stateless resets in response to receiving packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It is RECOMMENDED that endpoints immediately close the\nconnection with a connection error of type AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED before\nreaching a state where key updates are not possible.\n",
      "id": "7ac463fada73bbd8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "It is RECOMMENDED that endpoints immediately close the connection with a connection error of type AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED before reaching a state where key updates are not possible.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to counting packets sent, endpoints MUST count the number\nof received packets that fail authentication during the lifetime of a\nconnection.\n",
      "id": "6fe3e67c090b6ba1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "In addition to counting packets sent, endpoints MUST count the number of received packets that fail authentication during the lifetime of a connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the total number of received packets that fail\nauthentication within the connection, across all keys, exceeds the\nintegrity limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST immediately\nclose the connection with a connection error of type\nAEAD_LIMIT_REACHED and not process any more packets.\n",
      "id": "df1eb4146e3a5bda",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "If the total number of received packets that fail authentication within the connection, across all keys, exceeds the integrity limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST immediately close the connection with a connection error of type AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED and not process any more packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints that limit the size of packets MAY use higher\nconfidentiality and integrity limits; see Appendix B for details.\n",
      "id": "30aa8efed8eac449",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "Endpoints that limit the size of packets MAY use higher confidentiality and integrity limits; see Appendix B for details.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Future analyses and specifications MAY relax confidentiality or\nintegrity limits for an AEAD.\n",
      "id": "945d7661ab80386f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 142,
      "quote": "Future analyses and specifications MAY relax confidentiality or integrity limits for an AEAD.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any TLS cipher suite that is specified for use with QUIC MUST define\nlimits on the use of the associated AEAD function that preserves\nmargins for confidentiality and integrity.\n",
      "id": "ce750c73b5172e04",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 149,
      "quote": "Any TLS cipher suite that is specified for use with QUIC MUST define limits on the use of the associated AEAD function that preserves margins for confidentiality and integrity.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "That is, limits MUST be\nspecified for the number of packets that can be authenticated and for\nthe number of packets that can fail authentication.\n",
      "id": "a80853f16cf3fd95",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 157,
      "quote": "That is, limits MUST be specified for the number of packets that can be authenticated and for the number of packets that can fail authentication.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the handshake is confirmed (see Section 4.1.2), an endpoint MAY\ninitiate a key update.\n",
      "id": "6aae86c09b28a2ec",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "Once the handshake is confirmed (see Section 4.1.2), an endpoint MAY initiate a key update.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints\nMUST NOT send a TLS KeyUpdate message.\n",
      "id": "034f2d2b05a2f036",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT send a TLS KeyUpdate message.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST treat the\nreceipt of a TLS KeyUpdate message as a connection error of type\n0x010a, equivalent to a fatal TLS alert of unexpected_message; see\nSection 4.8.\n",
      "id": "2cb68bcd82b06b0d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST treat the receipt of a TLS KeyUpdate message as a connection error of type 0x010a, equivalent to a fatal TLS alert of unexpected_message; see Section 4.8.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations\nSHOULD use caution in relying on any data that is contained in\nInitial packets that is not otherwise authenticated.\n",
      "id": "ea1803fd8ec529a7",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD use caution in relying on any data that is contained in Initial packets that is not otherwise authenticated.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Unless another\nmechanism is used for agreeing on an application protocol, endpoints\nMUST use ALPN for this purpose.\n",
      "id": "039855da59c7f98e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "Unless another mechanism is used for agreeing on an application protocol, endpoints MUST use ALPN for this purpose.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When using ALPN, endpoints MUST immediately close a connection (see\nSection 10.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) with a no_application_protocol TLS\nalert (QUIC error code 0x0178; see Section 4.8) if an application\nprotocol is not negotiated.\n",
      "id": "1778b5465a3f5873",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "When using ALPN, endpoints MUST immediately close a connection (see Section 10.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) with a no_application_protocol TLS alert (QUIC error code 0x0178; see Section 4.8) if an application protocol is not negotiated.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While [ALPN] only specifies that servers\nuse this alert, QUIC clients MUST use error 0x0178 to terminate a\nconnection when ALPN negotiation fails.\n",
      "id": "23d56e364c31d5cf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "While [ALPN] only specifies that servers use this alert, QUIC clients MUST use error 0x0178 to terminate a connection when ALPN negotiation fails.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application protocol MAY restrict the QUIC versions that it can\noperate over.\n",
      "id": "5ed623961d875f12",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "An application protocol MAY restrict the QUIC versions that it can operate over.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST select an application protocol compatible\nwith the QUIC version that the client has selected.\n",
      "id": "ee9e684402018f09",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Servers MUST select an application protocol compatible with the QUIC version that the client has selected.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST\ntreat the inability to select a compatible application protocol as a\nconnection error of type 0x0178 (no_application_protocol).\n",
      "id": "cc28d7765c1cfff3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "The server MUST treat the inability to select a compatible application protocol as a connection error of type 0x0178 (no_application_protocol).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Similarly, a client MUST treat the selection of an incompatible\napplication protocol by a server as a connection error of type\n0x0178.\n",
      "id": "d91e15ff45d84f66",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "Similarly, a client MUST treat the selection of an incompatible application protocol by a server as a connection error of type 0x0178.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints\nMUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension; endpoints that\nreceive ClientHello or EncryptedExtensions messages without the\nquic_transport_parameters extension MUST close the connection with an\nerror of type 0x016d (equivalent to a fatal TLS missing_extension\nalert, see Section 4.8).\n",
      "id": "9dc6b60202f2921c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension; endpoints that receive ClientHello or EncryptedExtensions messages without the quic_transport_parameters extension MUST close the connection with an error of type 0x016d (equivalent to a fatal TLS missing_extension alert, see Section 4.8).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints\nMUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension; endpoints that\nreceive ClientHello or EncryptedExtensions messages without the\nquic_transport_parameters extension MUST close the connection with an\nerror of type 0x016d (equivalent to a fatal TLS missing_extension\nalert, see Section 4.8).\n",
      "id": "f4e3ebe2df46f85e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension; endpoints that receive ClientHello or EncryptedExtensions messages without the quic_transport_parameters extension MUST close the connection with an error of type 0x016d (equivalent to a fatal TLS missing_extension alert, see Section 4.8).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT send this extension in a TLS connection that does\nnot use QUIC (such as the use of TLS with TCP defined in [TLS13]).\n",
      "id": "ae4ac4230c4cd2f4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT send this extension in a TLS connection that does not use QUIC (such as the use of TLS with TCP defined in [TLS13]).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nfatal unsupported_extension alert MUST be sent by an implementation\nthat supports this extension if the extension is received when the\ntransport is not QUIC.\n",
      "id": "cf1c029210930bfe",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "A fatal unsupported_extension alert MUST be sent by an implementation that supports this extension if the extension is received when the transport is not QUIC.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT send the EndOfEarlyData message.\n",
      "id": "27408493e90d2af0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT send the EndOfEarlyData message.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST\ntreat receipt of a CRYPTO frame in a 0-RTT packet as a connection\nerror of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "943e7aa406a973c5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat receipt of a CRYPTO frame in a 0-RTT packet as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT request the use of the\nTLS 1.3 compatibility mode.\n",
      "id": "b008c9c12c477ce8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT request the use of the TLS 1.3 compatibility mode.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server SHOULD treat the receipt of a\nTLS ClientHello with a non-empty legacy_session_id field as a\nconnection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\n",
      "id": "d4805ded1c2ec3fa",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD treat the receipt of a TLS ClientHello with a non-empty legacy_session_id field as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/8.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-8.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST implement and use the replay protections described in\n[TLS13], however it is recognized that these protections are\nimperfect.\n",
      "id": "fcf570b91d5bdd84",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST implement and use the replay protections described in [TLS13], however it is recognized that these protections are imperfect.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These MUST NOT be\nused to communicate application semantics between endpoints; clients\nMUST treat them as opaque values.\n",
      "id": "55732214e6ed577f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "These MUST NOT be used to communicate application semantics between endpoints; clients MUST treat them as opaque values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These MUST NOT be\nused to communicate application semantics between endpoints; clients\nMUST treat them as opaque values.\n",
      "id": "9033644da74ed437",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "These MUST NOT be used to communicate application semantics between endpoints; clients MUST treat them as opaque values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An application\nprotocol that uses QUIC MUST describe how the protocol uses 0-RTT and\nthe measures that are employed to protect against replay attack.\n",
      "id": "18e8515012cacb42",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "An application protocol that uses QUIC MUST describe how the protocol uses 0-RTT and the measures that are employed to protect against replay attack.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "QUIC extensions MUST either describe how replay attacks affect their\noperation or prohibit the use of the extension in 0-RTT.\n",
      "id": "dda726d8a0439df1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "QUIC extensions MUST either describe how replay attacks affect their operation or prohibit the use of the extension in 0-RTT.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Application\nprotocols MUST either prohibit the use of extensions that carry\napplication semantics in 0-RTT or provide replay mitigation\nstrategies.\n",
      "id": "0c59a338ee91220b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "Application protocols MUST either prohibit the use of extensions that carry application semantics in 0-RTT or provide replay mitigation strategies.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "First, the packet\ncontaining a ClientHello MUST be padded to a minimum size.\n",
      "id": "bcea154c686257c3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "First, the packet containing a ClientHello MUST be padded to a minimum size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Future header protection variants based on this construction MUST use\na PRF to ensure equivalent security guarantees.\n",
      "id": "2c70cdac2be658ab",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "Future header protection variants based on this construction MUST use a PRF to ensure equivalent security guarantees.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For authentication to be\nfree from side channels, the entire process of header protection\nremoval, packet number recovery, and packet protection removal MUST\nbe applied together without timing and other side channels.\n",
      "id": "7005140a837b7a0b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "For authentication to be free from side channels, the entire process of header protection removal, packet number recovery, and packet protection removal MUST be applied together without timing and other side channels.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For the sending of packets, construction and protection of packet\npayloads and packet numbers MUST be free from side channels that\nwould reveal the packet number or its encoded size.\n",
      "id": "6b6ffff309f5c221",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "For the sending of packets, construction and protection of packet payloads and packet numbers MUST be free from side channels that would reveal the packet number or its encoded size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After\nreceiving a key update, an endpoint SHOULD generate and save the next\nset of receive packet protection keys, as described in Section 6.3.\n",
      "id": "4ca80978e16f737c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "After receiving a key update, an endpoint SHOULD generate and save the next set of receive packet protection keys, as described in Section 6.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To preserve this separation, a new version of QUIC SHOULD define new\nlabels for key derivation for packet protection key and IV, plus the\nheader protection keys.\n",
      "id": "4ec23e3f6de38651",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "To preserve this separation, a new version of QUIC SHOULD define new labels for key derivation for packet protection key and IV, plus the header protection keys.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "New QUIC versions SHOULD define a new salt value used in\ncalculating initial secrets.\n",
      "id": "ebf376eba13fb050",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "New QUIC versions SHOULD define a new salt value used in calculating initial secrets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001/9.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9001",
      "target_section": "section-9.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid generating multiple RTT samples for a single packet, an ACK\nframe SHOULD NOT be used to update RTT estimates if it does not newly\nacknowledge the largest acknowledged packet.\n",
      "id": "30366f5989233f4a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "To avoid generating multiple RTT samples for a single packet, an ACK frame SHOULD NOT be used to update RTT estimates if it does not newly acknowledge the largest acknowledged packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An RTT sample MUST NOT be generated on receiving an ACK frame that\ndoes not newly acknowledge at least one ack-eliciting packet.\n",
      "id": "a2caaec3050db9df",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "An RTT sample MUST NOT be generated on receiving an ACK frame that does not newly acknowledge at least one ack-eliciting packet.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "min_rtt MUST be set to the latest_rtt on the first RTT sample.\n",
      "id": "0ad1df424f066d8e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "min_rtt MUST be set to the latest_rtt on the first RTT sample.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "min_rtt MUST be set to the lesser of min_rtt and latest_rtt\n(Section 5.1) on all other samples.\n",
      "id": "dfbc703486f10bbf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "min_rtt MUST be set to the lesser of min_rtt and latest_rtt (Section 5.1) on all other samples.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD set the min_rtt to the newest RTT sample after\npersistent congestion is established.\n",
      "id": "3107573d5f2c1be9",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD set the min_rtt to the newest RTT sample after persistent congestion is established.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY reestablish the min_rtt at other times in the\nconnection, such as when traffic volume is low and an acknowledgment\nis received with a low acknowledgment delay.\n",
      "id": "0fc98c3b448b7dc0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY reestablish the min_rtt at other times in the connection, such as when traffic volume is low and an acknowledgment is received with a low acknowledgment delay.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD\nNOT refresh the min_rtt value too often since the actual minimum RTT\nof the path is not frequently observable.\n",
      "id": "0f18efeb842adc87",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD NOT refresh the min_rtt value too often since the actual minimum RTT of the path is not frequently observable.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To account for this, the endpoint SHOULD ignore\nmax_ack_delay until the handshake is confirmed, as defined in\nSection 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS].\n",
      "id": "297380de9761d246",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "To account for this, the endpoint SHOULD ignore max_ack_delay until the handshake is confirmed, as defined in Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, prior to handshake confirmation, an endpoint\nMAY ignore RTT samples if adjusting the RTT sample for acknowledgment\ndelay causes the sample to be less than the min_rtt.\n",
      "id": "4316cff8be451e7f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "Therefore, prior to handshake confirmation, an endpoint MAY ignore RTT samples if adjusting the RTT sample for acknowledgment delay causes the sample to be less than the min_rtt.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  MAY ignore the acknowledgment delay for Initial packets, since\nthese acknowledgments are not delayed by the peer (Section 13.2.1\nof [QUIC-TRANSPORT]);\n",
      "id": "078235cc849f37bc",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "*  MAY ignore the acknowledgment delay for Initial packets, since these acknowledgments are not delayed by the peer (Section 13.2.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]);",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  SHOULD ignore the peer's max_ack_delay until the handshake is\nconfirmed;\n",
      "id": "0e0430f6455f6ee4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "*  SHOULD ignore the peer's max_ack_delay until the handshake is confirmed;",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  MUST use the lesser of the acknowledgment delay and the peer's\nmax_ack_delay after the handshake is confirmed; and\n",
      "id": "78cbfd9c8f5b1bc0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "*  MUST use the lesser of the acknowledgment delay and the peer's max_ack_delay after the handshake is confirmed; and",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "*  MUST NOT subtract the acknowledgment delay from the RTT sample if\nthe resulting value is smaller than the min_rtt.\n",
      "id": "4162916a03fb1fb0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 143,
      "quote": "*  MUST NOT subtract the acknowledgment delay from the RTT sample if the resulting value is smaller than the min_rtt.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In such\ncases, an endpoint SHOULD subtract such local delays from its RTT\nsample until the handshake is confirmed.\n",
      "id": "860e6682ce4cedb4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "In such cases, an endpoint SHOULD subtract such local delays from its RTT sample until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The RECOMMENDED initial value for the packet reordering threshold\n(kPacketThreshold) is 3, based on best practices for TCP loss\ndetection [RFC5681] [RFC6675].\n",
      "id": "f2ab3eb9477c7f5a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "The RECOMMENDED initial value for the packet reordering threshold (kPacketThreshold) is 3, based on best practices for TCP loss detection [RFC5681] [RFC6675].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to remain similar to TCP,\nimplementations SHOULD NOT use a packet threshold less than 3; see\n[RFC5681].\n",
      "id": "d50ce1d23d0bd6a2",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "In order to remain similar to TCP, implementations SHOULD NOT use a packet threshold less than 3; see [RFC5681].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a later packet within the same packet number space has been\nacknowledged, an endpoint SHOULD declare an earlier packet lost if it\nwas sent a threshold amount of time in the past.\n",
      "id": "9a631063a214836a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Once a later packet within the same packet number space has been acknowledged, an endpoint SHOULD declare an earlier packet lost if it was sent a threshold amount of time in the past.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid declaring\npackets as lost too early, this time threshold MUST be set to at\nleast the local timer granularity, as indicated by the kGranularity\nconstant.\n",
      "id": "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "To avoid declaring packets as lost too early, this time threshold MUST be set to at least the local timer granularity, as indicated by the kGranularity constant.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If packets sent prior to the largest acknowledged packet cannot yet\nbe declared lost, then a timer SHOULD be set for the remaining time.\n",
      "id": "4a603cfeb1739748",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "If packets sent prior to the largest acknowledged packet cannot yet be declared lost, then a timer SHOULD be set for the remaining time.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The RECOMMENDED time threshold (kTimeThreshold), expressed as an RTT\nmultiplier, is 9/8.\n",
      "id": "5584ded4937204b8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "The RECOMMENDED time threshold (kTimeThreshold), expressed as an RTT multiplier, is 9/8.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The RECOMMENDED value of the timer granularity\n(kGranularity) is 1 millisecond.\n",
      "id": "debabb64eb1f6cb4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "The RECOMMENDED value of the timer granularity (kGranularity) is 1 millisecond.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MAY experiment with absolute thresholds, thresholds\nfrom previous connections, adaptive thresholds, or the including of\nRTT variation.\n",
      "id": "afbac7a0811efe43",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY experiment with absolute thresholds, thresholds from previous connections, adaptive thresholds, or the including of RTT variation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations with adaptive time\nthresholds MAY choose to start with smaller initial reordering\nthresholds to minimize recovery latency.\n",
      "id": "179dc30e32127dfe",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "Implementations with adaptive time thresholds MAY choose to start with smaller initial reordering thresholds to minimize recovery latency.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The PTO period MUST be at least kGranularity to avoid the timer\nexpiring immediately.\n",
      "id": "980f088aed264721",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "The PTO period MUST be at least kGranularity to avoid the timer expiring immediately.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When ack-eliciting packets in multiple packet number spaces are in\nflight, the timer MUST be set to the earlier value of the Initial and\nHandshake packet number spaces.\n",
      "id": "dcd7e7e320d3a9fb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 80,
      "quote": "When ack-eliciting packets in multiple packet number spaces are in flight, the timer MUST be set to the earlier value of the Initial and Handshake packet number spaces.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data\npacket number space until the handshake is confirmed.\n",
      "id": "570d2c57cab9aeb3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data packet number space until the handshake is confirmed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting\npacket is sent or acknowledged, or when Initial or Handshake keys are\ndiscarded (Section 4.9 of [QUIC-TLS]).\n",
      "id": "fea735ed6b114ce5",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting packet is sent or acknowledged, or when Initial or Handshake keys are discarded (Section 4.9 of [QUIC-TLS]).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a PTO timer expires, the PTO backoff MUST be increased,\nresulting in the PTO period being set to twice its current value.\n",
      "id": "68e2f3c0bb1cae13",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 103,
      "quote": "When a PTO timer expires, the PTO backoff MUST be increased, resulting in the PTO period being set to twice its current value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold\nloss detection; see Section 6.1.2.\n",
      "id": "b05fcb157378b39f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold loss detection; see Section 6.1.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\nno additional data can be sent, the server's PTO timer MUST NOT be\narmed until datagrams have been received from the client because\npackets sent on PTO count against the anti-amplification limit.\n",
      "id": "46037ed79a62ffec",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "If no additional data can be sent, the server's PTO timer MUST NOT be armed until datagrams have been received from the client because packets sent on PTO count against the anti-amplification limit.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "That is,\nthe client MUST set the PTO timer if the client has not received an\nacknowledgment for any of its Handshake packets and the handshake is\nnot confirmed (see Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), even if there are no\npackets in flight.\n",
      "id": "55cdc9e127aabb0e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "That is, the client MUST set the PTO timer if the client has not received an acknowledgment for any of its Handshake packets and the handshake is not confirmed (see Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), even if there are no packets in flight.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the PTO fires, the client MUST send a\nHandshake packet if it has Handshake keys, otherwise it MUST send an\nInitial packet in a UDP datagram with a payload of at least 1200\nbytes.\n",
      "id": "cf2b22526ff26305",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "When the PTO fires, the client MUST send a Handshake packet if it has Handshake keys, otherwise it MUST send an Initial packet in a UDP datagram with a payload of at least 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the PTO fires, the client MUST send a\nHandshake packet if it has Handshake keys, otherwise it MUST send an\nInitial packet in a UDP datagram with a payload of at least 1200\nbytes.\n",
      "id": "f98f6bfc990cd879",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "When the PTO fires, the client MUST send a Handshake packet if it has Handshake keys, otherwise it MUST send an Initial packet in a UDP datagram with a payload of at least 1200 bytes.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Resumed connections over the same network MAY use the previous\nconnection's final smoothed RTT value as the resumed connection's\ninitial RTT.\n",
      "id": "f1c9300306aae2f3",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "Resumed connections over the same network MAY use the previous connection's final smoothed RTT value as the resumed connection's initial RTT.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When no previous RTT is available, the initial RTT\nSHOULD be set to 333 milliseconds.\n",
      "id": "f3411d34ad8a5cbe",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "When no previous RTT is available, the initial RTT SHOULD be set to 333 milliseconds.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A connection MAY use the delay between sending a PATH_CHALLENGE and\nreceiving a PATH_RESPONSE to set the initial RTT (see kInitialRtt in\nAppendix A.2) for a new path, but the delay SHOULD NOT be considered\nan RTT sample.\n",
      "id": "5edb51b2f445fae0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "A connection MAY use the delay between sending a PATH_CHALLENGE and receiving a PATH_RESPONSE to set the initial RTT (see kInitialRtt in Appendix A.2) for a new path, but the delay SHOULD NOT be considered an RTT sample.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When\nInitial or Handshake keys are discarded, the PTO and loss detection\ntimers MUST be reset, because discarding keys indicates forward\nprogress and the loss detection timer might have been set for a now-\ndiscarded packet number space.\n",
      "id": "0e5a9d88bd0af789",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "When Initial or Handshake keys are discarded, the PTO and loss detection timers MUST be reset, because discarding keys indicates forward progress and the loss detection timer might have been set for a now- discarded packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To speed up handshake completion under these conditions, an endpoint\nMAY, for a limited number of times per connection, send a packet\ncontaining unacknowledged CRYPTO data earlier than the PTO expiry,\nsubject to the address validation limits in Section 8.1 of\n[QUIC-TRANSPORT].\n",
      "id": "7a175129504699e7",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "To speed up handshake completion under these conditions, an endpoint MAY, for a limited number of times per connection, send a packet containing unacknowledged CRYPTO data earlier than the PTO expiry, subject to the address validation limits in Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a PTO timer expires, a sender MUST send at least one ack-\neliciting packet in the packet number space as a probe.\n",
      "id": "69ca26bab0e3e3a3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "When a PTO timer expires, a sender MUST send at least one ack- eliciting packet in the packet number space as a probe.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint\nMAY send up to two full-sized datagrams containing ack-eliciting\npackets to avoid an expensive consecutive PTO expiration due to a\nsingle lost datagram or to transmit data from multiple packet number\nspaces.\n",
      "id": "05535811e1e743b3",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send up to two full-sized datagrams containing ack-eliciting packets to avoid an expensive consecutive PTO expiration due to a single lost datagram or to transmit data from multiple packet number spaces.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All probe packets sent on a PTO MUST be ack-eliciting.\n",
      "id": "b37fb0a44a754a58",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "All probe packets sent on a PTO MUST be ack-eliciting.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to sending data in the packet number space for which the\ntimer expired, the sender SHOULD send ack-eliciting packets from\nother packet number spaces with in-flight data, coalescing packets if\npossible.\n",
      "id": "5ab3137e80ed34ae",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "In addition to sending data in the packet number space for which the timer expired, the sender SHOULD send ack-eliciting packets from other packet number spaces with in-flight data, coalescing packets if possible.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint SHOULD include new data in packets that are sent on PTO\nexpiration.\n",
      "id": "6b76f132c56d3922",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 88,
      "quote": "An endpoint SHOULD include new data in packets that are sent on PTO expiration.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Previously sent data MAY be sent if no new data can be\nsent.\n",
      "id": "0ea8e25507365f90",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "Previously sent data MAY be sent if no new data can be sent.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MAY use alternative strategies for determining\nthe content of probe packets, including sending new or retransmitted\ndata based on the application's priorities.\n",
      "id": "32c5200d17b71a65",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY use alternative strategies for determining the content of probe packets, including sending new or retransmitted data based on the application's priorities.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When there is no data to send, the sender SHOULD send\na PING or other ack-eliciting frame in a single packet, rearming the\nPTO timer.\n",
      "id": "c8c6401ae082b878",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "When there is no data to send, the sender SHOULD send a PING or other ack-eliciting frame in a single packet, rearming the PTO timer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Alternatively, instead of sending an ack-eliciting packet, the sender\nMAY mark any packets still in flight as lost.\n",
      "id": "a0ab66bc3388b870",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "Alternatively, instead of sending an ack-eliciting packet, the sender MAY mark any packets still in flight as lost.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A PTO timer expiration event does not indicate packet loss and MUST\nNOT cause prior unacknowledged packets to be marked as lost.\n",
      "id": "96d4dd072e49509b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "A PTO timer expiration event does not indicate packet loss and MUST NOT cause prior unacknowledged packets to be marked as lost.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MAY compute an RTT estimate to the server as the time\nperiod from when the first Initial packet was sent to when a Retry or\na Version Negotiation packet is received.\n",
      "id": "6e7349279bb93031",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "The client MAY compute an RTT estimate to the server as the time period from when the first Initial packet was sent to when a Retry or a Version Negotiation packet is received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The client MAY use this\nvalue in place of its default for the initial RTT estimate.\n",
      "id": "939b44edeb923934",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "The client MAY use this value in place of its default for the initial RTT estimate.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sender MUST discard all recovery state\nassociated with those packets and MUST remove them from the count of\nbytes in flight.\n",
      "id": "711f3d0a6cdc09db",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "The sender MUST discard all recovery state associated with those packets and MUST remove them from the count of bytes in flight.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sender MUST discard all recovery state\nassociated with those packets and MUST remove them from the count of\nbytes in flight.\n",
      "id": "a447177add9f3a13",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "The sender MUST discard all recovery state associated with those packets and MUST remove them from the count of bytes in flight.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/6.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-6.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD use an initial congestion\nwindow of ten times the maximum datagram size (max_datagram_size),\nwhile limiting the window to the larger of 14,720 bytes or twice the\nmaximum datagram size.\n",
      "id": "1c60eb14e9787351",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 31,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD use an initial congestion window of ten times the maximum datagram size (max_datagram_size), while limiting the window to the larger of 14,720 bytes or twice the maximum datagram size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the maximum datagram size changes during the connection, the\ninitial congestion window SHOULD be recalculated with the new size.\n",
      "id": "d1110d44eb561ad1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "If the maximum datagram size changes during the connection, the initial congestion window SHOULD be recalculated with the new size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the maximum datagram size is decreased in order to complete the\nhandshake, the congestion window SHOULD be set to the new initial\ncongestion window.\n",
      "id": "fe7a094ef163db6a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "If the maximum datagram size is decreased in order to complete the handshake, the congestion window SHOULD be set to the new initial congestion window.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The RECOMMENDED\nvalue is 2 * max_datagram_size.\n",
      "id": "1caf21afbd22ac63",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "The RECOMMENDED value is 2 * max_datagram_size.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sender MUST exit slow start and enter a recovery period when a\npacket is lost or when the ECN-CE count reported by its peer\nincreases.\n",
      "id": "6faffbbdbddc00ef",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "The sender MUST exit slow start and enter a recovery period when a packet is lost or when the ECN-CE count reported by its peer increases.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On entering a recovery period, a sender MUST set the slow start\nthreshold to half the value of the congestion window when loss is\ndetected.\n",
      "id": "2b8da48fe292cff9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "On entering a recovery period, a sender MUST set the slow start threshold to half the value of the congestion window when loss is detected.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The congestion window MUST be set to the reduced value of\nthe slow start threshold before exiting the recovery period.\n",
      "id": "cf6da80a29e5304a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "The congestion window MUST be set to the reduced value of the slow start threshold before exiting the recovery period.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MAY reduce the congestion window immediately upon\nentering a recovery period or use other mechanisms, such as\nProportional Rate Reduction [PRR], to reduce the congestion window\nmore gradually.\n",
      "id": "992ba3a30bb896d5",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY reduce the congestion window immediately upon entering a recovery period or use other mechanisms, such as Proportional Rate Reduction [PRR], to reduce the congestion window more gradually.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender in congestion avoidance uses an Additive Increase\nMultiplicative Decrease (AIMD) approach that MUST limit the increase\nto the congestion window to at most one maximum datagram size for\neach congestion window that is acknowledged.\n",
      "id": "e2e05e0324a0b93a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "A sender in congestion avoidance uses an Additive Increase Multiplicative Decrease (AIMD) approach that MUST limit the increase to the congestion window to at most one maximum datagram size for each congestion window that is acknowledged.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MAY ignore the\nloss of Handshake, 0-RTT, and 1-RTT packets that might have arrived\nbefore the peer had packet protection keys to process those packets.\n",
      "id": "cc137cf78bfce47d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Endpoints MAY ignore the loss of Handshake, 0-RTT, and 1-RTT packets that might have arrived before the peer had packet protection keys to process those packets.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT ignore the loss of packets that were sent after\nthe earliest acknowledged packet in a given packet number space.\n",
      "id": "73eb1c087163c432",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT ignore the loss of packets that were sent after the earliest acknowledged packet in a given packet number space.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Probe packets MUST NOT be blocked by the congestion controller.\n",
      "id": "291d4e52691375ee",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "Probe packets MUST NOT be blocked by the congestion controller.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nsender MUST however count these packets as being additionally in\nflight, since these packets add network load without establishing\npacket loss.\n",
      "id": "e0cf357c5ebccf98",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "A sender MUST however count these packets as being additionally in flight, since these packets add network load without establishing packet loss.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The RECOMMENDED value for kPersistentCongestionThreshold is 3, which\nresults in behavior that is approximately equivalent to a TCP sender\ndeclaring an RTO after two TLPs.\n",
      "id": "b5b164874db0819b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "The RECOMMENDED value for kPersistentCongestionThreshold is 3, which results in behavior that is approximately equivalent to a TCP sender declaring an RTO after two TLPs.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These two packets MUST be ack-eliciting, since a receiver is required\nto acknowledge only ack-eliciting packets within its maximum\nacknowledgment delay; see Section 13.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].\n",
      "id": "77e29682ff6c7e87",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "These two packets MUST be ack-eliciting, since a receiver is required to acknowledge only ack-eliciting packets within its maximum acknowledgment delay; see Section 13.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The persistent congestion period SHOULD NOT start until there is at\nleast one RTT sample.\n",
      "id": "82f8fc86c740484e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "The persistent congestion period SHOULD NOT start until there is at least one RTT sample.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since network congestion is not affected by packet number spaces,\npersistent congestion SHOULD consider packets sent across packet\nnumber spaces.\n",
      "id": "c9e34257a277df4d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "Since network congestion is not affected by packet number spaces, persistent congestion SHOULD consider packets sent across packet number spaces.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender that does not have state for all packet\nnumber spaces or an implementation that cannot compare send times\nacross packet number spaces MAY use state for just the packet number\nspace that was acknowledged.\n",
      "id": "06bdae7ef5528bb2",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "A sender that does not have state for all packet number spaces or an implementation that cannot compare send times across packet number spaces MAY use state for just the packet number space that was acknowledged.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When persistent congestion is declared, the sender's congestion\nwindow MUST be reduced to the minimum congestion window\n(kMinimumWindow), similar to a TCP sender's response on an RTO\n[RFC5681].\n",
      "id": "cc0a7a6365d0ea10",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "When persistent congestion is declared, the sender's congestion window MUST be reduced to the minimum congestion window (kMinimumWindow), similar to a TCP sender's response on an RTO [RFC5681].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD pace sending of all in-flight packets based on input\nfrom the congestion controller.\n",
      "id": "627371eae1ad5e3a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD pace sending of all in-flight packets based on input from the congestion controller.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Senders MUST either use pacing or limit such bursts.\n",
      "id": "6ef71d6719880d8b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "Senders MUST either use pacing or limit such bursts.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Senders SHOULD limit bursts to the initial congestion window; see\nSection 7.2.\n",
      "id": "eced398c52b4e356",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Senders SHOULD limit bursts to the initial congestion window; see Section 7.2.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender with knowledge that the network path to the\nreceiver can absorb larger bursts MAY use a higher limit.\n",
      "id": "cd2dc0faa9d081d4",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "A sender with knowledge that the network path to the receiver can absorb larger bursts MAY use a higher limit.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To avoid delaying their delivery to the peer, packets\ncontaining only ACK frames SHOULD therefore not be paced.\n",
      "id": "69e44c4262e309dd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "To avoid delaying their delivery to the peer, packets containing only ACK frames SHOULD therefore not be paced.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When this occurs, the congestion window\nSHOULD NOT be increased in either slow start or congestion avoidance.\n",
      "id": "412c81ff8202b111",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "When this occurs, the congestion window SHOULD NOT be increased in either slow start or congestion avoidance.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender SHOULD NOT consider itself application limited if it\nwould have fully utilized the congestion window without pacing delay.\n",
      "id": "71a2485004a71caa",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "A sender SHOULD NOT consider itself application limited if it would have fully utilized the congestion window without pacing delay.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A sender MAY implement alternative mechanisms to update its\ncongestion window after periods of underutilization, such as those\nproposed for TCP in [RFC7661].\n",
      "id": "03a229c2334a2d5a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "A sender MAY implement alternative mechanisms to update its congestion window after periods of underutilization, such as those proposed for TCP in [RFC7661].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a sender uses a different controller than that specified in this\ndocument, the chosen controller MUST conform to the congestion\ncontrol guidelines specified in Section 3.1 of [RFC8085].\n",
      "id": "9d7f56e2dd823cde",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "If a sender uses a different controller than that specified in this document, the chosen controller MUST conform to the congestion control guidelines specified in Section 3.1 of [RFC8085].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Unlike\nTCP, QUIC can detect the loss of these packets and MAY use that\ninformation to adjust the congestion controller or the rate of ACK-\nonly packets being sent, but this document does not describe a\nmechanism for doing so.\n",
      "id": "6680c8afa985c409",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Unlike TCP, QUIC can detect the loss of these packets and MAY use that information to adjust the congestion controller or the rate of ACK- only packets being sent, but this document does not describe a mechanism for doing so.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a packet if it would cause bytes_in_flight\n(see Appendix B.2) to be larger than the congestion window, unless\nthe packet is sent on a PTO timer expiration (see Section 6.2) or\nwhen entering recovery (see Section 7.3.2).\n",
      "id": "5051ba9d620362f6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a packet if it would cause bytes_in_flight (see Appendix B.2) to be larger than the congestion window, unless the packet is sent on a PTO timer expiration (see Section 6.2) or when entering recovery (see Section 7.3.2).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002/7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9002",
      "target_section": "section-7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    }
  ],
