        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   The Internet has traditionally used loss-based congestion control",
            "   algorithms like Reno ([Jac88], [Jac90], [WS95] [RFC5681]) and CUBIC",
            "   ([HRX08], [RFC8312]).  These algorithms worked well for many years",
            "   because they were sufficiently well-matched to the prevalent range of",
            "   bandwidth-delay products and degrees of buffering in Internet paths.",
            "   As the Internet has evolved, loss-based congestion control is",
            "   increasingly problematic in several important scenarios:",
            "",
            "   1.  Shallow buffers: In shallow buffers, packet loss can happen even",
            "       when a link has low utilization.  With high-speed, long-haul",
            "       links employing commodity switches with shallow buffers, loss-",
            "       based congestion control can cause abysmal throughput because it",
            "       overreacts, multiplicatively decreasing the sending rate upon",
            "       packet loss, and only slowly growing its sending rate thereafter.",
            "       This can happen even if the packet loss arises from transient",
            "       traffic bursts when the link is mostly idle.",
            "",
            "   2.  Deep buffers: At the edge of today's Internet, loss-based",
            "       congestion control can cause the problem of \"bufferbloat\", by",
            "       repeatedly filling deep buffers in last-mile links and causing",
            "       high queuing delays.",
            "",
            "   3.  Dynamic traffic workloads: With buffers of any depth, dynamic",
            "       mixes of newly-entering flows or flights of data from recently",
            "       idle flows can cause frequent packet loss.  In such scenarios",
            "       loss-based congestion control can fail to maintain its fair share",
            "       of bandwidth, leading to poor application performance.",
            "",
            "   In both the shallow-buffer (1.) or dynamic-traffic (3.) scenarios",
            "   mentioned above it is difficult to achieve full throughput with loss-",
            "   based congestion control in practice: for CUBIC, sustaining 10Gbps",
            "   over 100ms RTT needs a packet loss rate below 0.000003% (i.e., more",
            "   than 40 seconds between packet losses), and over a 100ms RTT path a",
            "   more feasible loss rate like 1% can only sustain at most 3 Mbps",
            "   [RFC8312].  These limitations apply no matter what the bottleneck",
            "   link is capable of or what the connection's fair share is.",
            "   Furthermore, failure to reach the fair share can cause poor",
            "   throughpout and poor tail latency for latency-sensitive applications.",
            "",
            "   The BBR (\"Bottleneck Bandwidth and Round-trip propagation time\")",
            "   congestion control algorithm is a model-based algorithm that takes an",
            "   approach different from loss-based congestion control: BBR uses",
            "   recent measurements of a transport connection's delivery rate, round-",
            "   trip time, and packet loss rate to build an explicit model of the",
            "   network path, including its estimated available bandwidth, bandwidth-",
            "   delay product, and the maximum volume of data that the connection can",
            "   place in-flight in the network without causing excessive queue",
            "   pressure.  It then uses this model in order to guide its control",
            "   behavior in seeking high throughput and low queue pressure.",
            "",
            "   This document describes the current version of the BBR algorithm,",
            "   BBRv2.  The previous version of the algorithm, BBRv1, was described",
            "   previously at a high level [CCGHJ16][CCGHJ17].  The implications of",
            "   BBR in allowing high utilization of high-speed networks with shallow",
            "   buffers have been discussed in other work [MM19].  Active work on the",
            "   BBR algorithm is continuing.",
            "",
            "   This document is organized as follows.  Section 2 provides various",
            "   definitions that will be used throughout this document.  Section 3",
            "   provides an overview of the design of the BBR algorithm, and section",
            "   4 describes the BBR algorithm in detail, including BBR's network path",
            "   model, control parameters, and state machine.  Section 5 describes",
            "   the implementation status, section 6 describes security",
            "   considerations, section 7 notes that there are no IANA",
            "   considerations, and section 8 closes with Acknowledgments."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   This document defines state variables and constants for the BBR",
            "   algorithm.",
            "",
            "   The variables starting with C, P, or rs not defined below are defined",
            "   in [draft-cheng-iccrg-delivery-rate-estimation]."
          ],
          "title": "Terminology"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   C.delivered: The total amount of data (tracked in octets or in",
            "   packets) delivered so far over the lifetime of the transport",
            "   connection C.",
            "",
            "   SMSS: The Sender Maximum Segment Size.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   is_cwnd_limited: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13d9c383c286e33a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "True if the connection has fully utilized its cwnd"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13d9c383c286e33a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "at any point in the last packet-timed round trip."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   InitialCwnd: The initial congestion window set by the transport",
            "   protocol implementation for the connection at initialization time."
          ],
          "title": "Transport Connection State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   packet.delivered: C.delivered when the given packet was sent by",
            "   transport connection C.",
            "",
            "   packet.departure_time: The earliest pacing departure time for the",
            "   given packet.",
            "",
            "   packet.tx_in_flight: The volume of data that was estimated to be in",
            "   flight at the time of the transmission of the packet."
          ],
          "title": "Per-Packet State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   rs.delivered: The volume of data delivered between the transmission",
            "   of the packet that has just been ACKed and the current time.",
            "",
            "   rs.delivery_rate: The delivery rate (aka bandwidth) sample obtained",
            "   from the packet that has just been ACKed.",
            "",
            "   rs.rtt: The RTT sample calculated based on the most recently-sent",
            "   segment of the segments that have just been ACKed.",
            "",
            "   rs.newly_acked: The volume of data cumulatively or selectively",
            "   acknowledged upon the ACK that was just received.  (This quantity is",
            "   referred to as \"DeliveredData\" in [RFC6937].)",
            "",
            "   rs.newly_lost: The volume of data newly marked lost upon the ACK that",
            "   was just received.",
            "",
            "   rs.tx_in_flight: The volume of data that was estimated to be in",
            "   flight at the time of the transmission of the packet that has just",
            "   been ACKed (the most recently sent segment among segments ACKed by",
            "   the ACK that was just received).",
            "",
            "   rs.lost: The volume of data that was declared lost between the",
            "   transmission and acknowledgement of the packet that has just been",
            "   ACKed (the most recently sent segment among segments ACKed by the ACK",
            "   that was just received)."
          ],
          "title": "Per-ACK Rate Sample State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.4",
          "lines": [
            "   cwnd: The transport sender's congestion window, which limits the",
            "   amount of data in flight.",
            "",
            "   BBR.pacing_rate: The current pacing rate for a BBR flow, which",
            "   controls inter-packet spacing.",
            "",
            "   BBR.send_quantum: The maximum size of a data aggregate scheduled and",
            "   transmitted together."
          ],
          "title": "Output Control Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.5",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR.pacing_gain: The dynamic gain factor used to scale BBR.bw to",
            "   produce BBR.pacing_rate.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRPacingMarginPercent: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52cabf878af3e934"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The static discount factor of 1% used to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52cabf878af3e934"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "scale BBR.bw to produce BBR.pacing_rate."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   BBR.next_departure_time: The earliest pacing departure time for the",
            "   next packet BBR schedules for transmission."
          ],
          "title": "Pacing State and Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.6",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR.cwnd_gain: The dynamic gain factor used to scale the estimated",
            "   BDP to produce a congestion window (cwnd).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRStartupPacingGain: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "629f8f49796e7605",
                  "079c4aa37024c8a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A constant specifying the minimum gain value"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "629f8f49796e7605",
                  "079c4aa37024c8a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "for calculating the pacing rate that will allow the sending rate to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "629f8f49796e7605",
                  "079c4aa37024c8a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "double each round (4*ln(2) ~= 2.77)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " [BBRStartupPacingGain]; used in"
              }
            ],
            "   Startup mode for BBR.pacing_gain.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRStartupCwndGain: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5372c09911672676",
                  "153d58aef167eb8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A constant specifying the minimum gain value for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5372c09911672676",
                  "153d58aef167eb8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "calculating the cwnd that will allow the sending rate to double each"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5372c09911672676",
                  "153d58aef167eb8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "round (2.0)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "; used in Startup mode for BBR.cwnd_gain."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   BBR.packet_conservation: A boolean indicating whether BBR is",
            "   currently using packet conservation dynamics to bound cwnd."
          ],
          "title": "cwnd State and Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.7",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR.state: The current state of a BBR flow in the BBR state machine.",
            "",
            "   BBR.round_count: Count of packet-timed round trips elapsed so far.",
            "",
            "   BBR.round_start: A boolean that BBR sets to true once per packet-",
            "   timed round trip, on ACKs that advance BBR.round_count.",
            "",
            "   BBR.next_round_delivered: packet.delivered value denoting the end of",
            "   a packet-timed round trip.",
            "",
            "   BBR.idle_restart: A boolean that is true if and only if a connection",
            "   is restarting after being idle."
          ],
          "title": "General Algorithm State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.8",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRLossThresh: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e70cd9961b5ae2a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The maximum tolerated per-round-trip packet loss rate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e70cd9961b5ae2a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "when probing for bandwidth (the default is 2%)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRBeta: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "24438378d21af590"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The default multiplicative decrease to make upon each round"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "24438378d21af590"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "trip during which the connection detects packet loss (the value is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "24438378d21af590"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "0.7)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRHeadroom: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "faeb47cc5b0505ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The multiplicative factor to apply to BBR.inflight_hi"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "faeb47cc5b0505ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "when attempting to leave free headroom in the path (e.g. free space"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "faeb47cc5b0505ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "in the bottleneck buffer or free time slots in the bottleneck link)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "faeb47cc5b0505ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "that can be used by cross traffic (the value is 0.85)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRMinPipeCwnd: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b7d0ae0a2edf3cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The minimal cwnd value BBR targets, to allow"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b7d0ae0a2edf3cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "pipelining with TCP endpoints that follow an \"ACK every other packet\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b7d0ae0a2edf3cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "delayed-ACK policy: 4 * SMSS."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Core Algorithm Design Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.9",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Network Path Model Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.9.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d685ac88581071a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The data rate model parameters together estimate both the sending"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d685ac88581071a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "rate required to reach the full bandwidth available to the flow"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d685ac88581071a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(BBR.max_bw), and the maximum pacing rate control parameter that is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d685ac88581071a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "consistent with the queue pressure objective (BBR.bw)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.max_bw: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de60bc1312e93606"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The windowed maximum recent bandwidth sample - obtained"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de60bc1312e93606"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "using the BBR delivery rate sampling algorithm [draft-cheng-iccrg-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de60bc1312e93606"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "delivery-rate-estimation] - measured during the current or previous"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de60bc1312e93606"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "bandwidth probing cycle (or during Startup, if the flow is still in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de60bc1312e93606"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "that state)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  (Part of the long-term model.)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.bw_hi: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a356cd25f9016c90"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The long-term maximum sending bandwidth that the algorithm"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a356cd25f9016c90"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "estimates will produce acceptable queue pressure, based on signals in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a356cd25f9016c90"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the current or previous bandwidth probing cycle, as measured by loss."
              }
            ],
            "   (Part of the long-term model.)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.bw_lo: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e85e560495e8b57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The short-term maximum sending bandwidth that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e85e560495e8b57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "algorithm estimates is safe for matching the current network path"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e85e560495e8b57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "delivery rate, based on any loss signals in the current bandwidth"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e85e560495e8b57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "probing cycle.  This is generally lower than max_bw or bw_hi (thus"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e85e560495e8b57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the name)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  (Part of the short-term model.)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.bw: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b1f6d2835e3a967"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The maximum sending bandwidth that the algorithm estimates is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b1f6d2835e3a967"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "appropriate for matching the current network path delivery rate,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b1f6d2835e3a967"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "given all available signals in the model, at any time scale.  It is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b1f6d2835e3a967"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the min() of max_bw, bw_hi, and bw_lo."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Data Rate Network Path Model Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.9.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11fee86ab1eb45cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The data volume model parameters together estimate both the volume of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11fee86ab1eb45cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "in-flight data required to reach the full bandwidth available to the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11fee86ab1eb45cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "flow (BBR.max_inflight), and the maximum volume of data that is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11fee86ab1eb45cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "consistent with the queue pressure objective (cwnd)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.min_rtt: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "145cf41f5e32b935"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The windowed minimum round-trip time sample measured"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "145cf41f5e32b935"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "over the last MinRTTFilterLen = 10 seconds."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This attempts to"
              }
            ],
            "   estimate the two-way propagation delay of the network path when all",
            "   connections sharing a bottleneck are using BBR, but also allows BBR",
            "   to estimate the value required for a bdp estimate that allows full",
            "   throughput if there are legacy loss-based Reno or CUBIC flows sharing",
            "   the bottleneck.",
            "",
            "   BBR.bdp: The estimate of the network path's BDP (Bandwidth-Delay",
            "   Product), computed as: BBR.bdp = BBR.bw * BBR.min_rtt.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.extra_acked: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be409852d4adbb2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A volume of data that is the estimate of the recent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be409852d4adbb2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "degree of aggregation in the network path."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   BBR.offload_budget: The estimate of the minimum volume of data",
            "   necessary to achieve full throughput when using sender (TSO/GSO) and",
            "   receiver (LRO, GRO) host offload mechanisms.",
            "",
            "   BBR.max_inflight: The estimate of the volume of in-flight data",
            "   required to fully utilize the bottleneck bandwidth available to the",
            "   flow, based on the BDP estimate (BBR.bdp), the aggregation estimate",
            "   (BBR.extra_acked), the offload budget (BBR.offload_budget), and",
            "   BBRMinPipeCwnd.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.inflight_hi: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6057f9b2ecab59b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Analogous to BBR.bw_hi, the long-term maximum volume"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6057f9b2ecab59b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "of in-flight data that the algorithm estimates will produce"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6057f9b2ecab59b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "acceptable queue pressure, based on signals in the current or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6057f9b2ecab59b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "previous bandwidth probing cycle, as measured by loss."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  That is, if a"
              }
            ],
            "   flow is probing for bandwidth, and observes that sending a particular",
            "   volume of in-flight data causes a loss rate higher than the loss rate",
            "   objective, it sets inflight_hi to that volume of data.  (Part of the",
            "   long-term model.)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.inflight_lo: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1470954db9282be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Analogous to BBR.bw_lo, the short-term maximum"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1470954db9282be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "volume of in-flight data that the algorithm estimates is safe for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1470954db9282be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "matching the current network path delivery process, based on any loss"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b1470954db9282be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "signals in the current bandwidth probing cycle."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This is generally"
              }
            ],
            "   lower than max_inflight or inflight_hi (thus the name).  (Part of the",
            "   short-term model.)"
          ],
          "title": "Data Volume Network Path Model Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.10",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.bw_latest: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b8b55bcf1ace7d0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "a 1-round-trip max of delivered bandwidth"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3b8b55bcf1ace7d0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(rs.delivery_rate)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.inflight_latest: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9c4c36b9097a50f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "a 1-round-trip max of delivered volume of data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9c4c36b9097a50f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(rs.delivered)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "State for Responding to Congestion"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.11",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR.MaxBwFilter: The filter for tracking the maximum recent",
            "   rs.delivery_rate sample, for estimating BBR.max_bw.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   MaxBwFilterLen: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52faa1fa0bfe45a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The filter window length for BBR.MaxBwFilter = 2"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52faa1fa0bfe45a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(representing up to 2 ProbeBW cycles, the current cycle and the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52faa1fa0bfe45a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "previous full cycle)"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.cycle_count: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8406c81909cace0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The virtual time used by the BBR.max_bw filter"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8406c81909cace0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "window."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that BBR.cycle_count only needs to be tracked with a"
              }
            ],
            "   single bit, since the BBR.MaxBwFilter only needs to track samples",
            "   from two time slots: the previous ProbeBW cycle and the current",
            "   ProbeBW cycle."
          ],
          "title": "Estimating BBR.max_bw"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.12",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.extra_acked_interval_start: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ed0021015f826f3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the start of the time interval for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ed0021015f826f3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "estimating the excess amount of data acknowledged due to aggregation"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ed0021015f826f3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "effects."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.extra_acked_delivered: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2d5fab85ec506385"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the volume of data marked as delivered"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2d5fab85ec506385"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "since BBR.extra_acked_interval_start."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   BBR.ExtraACKedFilter: the max filter tracking the recent maximum",
            "   degree of aggregation in the path.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRExtraAckedFilterLen = "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74587199d171af15"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The window length of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74587199d171af15"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "BBR.ExtraACKedFilter max filter window: 10 (in units of packet-timed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "74587199d171af15"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "round trips)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Estimating BBR.extra_acked"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.13",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.filled_pipe: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7684d67ed9f3f49"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A boolean that records whether BBR estimates that it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f7684d67ed9f3f49"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "has ever fully utilized its available bandwidth (\"filled the pipe\")."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.full_bw: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0c160f67e8e2668d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A recent baseline BBR.max_bw to estimate if BBR has"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0c160f67e8e2668d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"filled the pipe\" in Startup."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.full_bw_count: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a19b2d1242630a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The number of non-app-limited round trips without"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a19b2d1242630a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "large increases in BBR.full_bw."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Startup Parameters and State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.14",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "ProbeRTT and min_rtt Parameters and State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.14.1",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR.min_rtt_stamp: The wall clock time at which the current",
            "   BBR.min_rtt sample was obtained.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   MinRTTFilterLen: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e06cf66ed7d0385"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A constant specifying the length of the BBR.min_rtt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e06cf66ed7d0385"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "min filter window, MinRTTFilterLen is 10 secs."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Parameters for Estimating BBR.min_rtt"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.14.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBRProbeRTTCwndGain = "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "07e746b180573afe",
                  "bf4e693d206021be"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A constant specifying the gain value for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "07e746b180573afe",
                  "bf4e693d206021be"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "calculating the cwnd during ProbeRTT: 0.5"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " (meaning that ProbeRTT"
              }
            ],
            "   attempts to reduce in-flight data to 50% of the estimated BDP).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ProbeRTTDuration: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0ae826e6c88df6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A constant specifying the minimum duration for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0ae826e6c88df6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "which ProbeRTT state holds inflight to BBRMinPipeCwnd or fewer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0ae826e6c88df6e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packets: 200 ms."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   ProbeRTTInterval: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "85fc26e3e97b4121"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A constant specifying the minimum time interval"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "85fc26e3e97b4121"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "between ProbeRTT states: 5 secs."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay: The minimum RTT sample recorded in the last",
            "   ProbeRTTInterval.",
            "",
            "   BBR.probe_rtt_min_stamp: The wall clock time at which the current",
            "   BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay sample was obtained.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   BBR.probe_rtt_expired: "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fee7bc33d5da5b2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A boolean recording whether the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fee7bc33d5da5b2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "BBR.probe_rtt_min_delay has expired and is due for a refresh with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fee7bc33d5da5b2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "application idle period or a transition into ProbeRTT state."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The keywords \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this",
            "   document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC2119]."
          ],
          "title": "Parameters for Scheduling ProbeRTT"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Design Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The high-level goal of BBR is to achieve both:",
            "",
            "   1.  The full throughput (or approximate fair share thereof) available",
            "       to a flow",
            "",
            "       *  Achieved in a fast and scalable manner (using bandwidth in",
            "          O(log(BDP)) time).",
            "",
            "       *  Achieved with average packet loss rates of up to 1%.",
            "",
            "   2.  Low queue pressure (low queuing delay and low packet loss).",
            "",
            "   These goals are in tension: sending faster improves the odds of",
            "   achieving (1) but reduces the odds of achieving (2), while sending",
            "   slower improves the odds of achieving (2) but reduces the odds of",
            "   achieving (1).  Thus the algorithm cannot maximize throughput or",
            "   minimize queue pressure independently, and must jointly optimize",
            "   both.",
            "",
            "   To try to achieve these goals, and seek an operating point with high",
            "   throughput and low delay [K79] [GK81], BBR aims to adapt its sending",
            "   process to match the network delivery process, in two dimensions:",
            "",
            "   1.  data rate: the rate at which the flow sends data should ideally",
            "       match the rate at which the network delivers the flow's data (the",
            "       available bottleneck bandwidth)",
            "",
            "   2.  data volume: the amount of unacknowledged data in flight in the",
            "       network should ideally match the bandwidth-delay product (BDP) of",
            "       the path",
            "",
            "   Both the control of the data rate (via the pacing rate) and data",
            "   volume (directly via the congestion window or cwnd; and indirectly",
            "   via the pacing rate) are important.  A mismatch in either dimension",
            "   can cause the sender to fail to meet its high-level design goals:",
            "",
            "   1.  volume mismatch: If a sender perfectly matches its sending rate",
            "       to the available bandwidth, but its volume of in-flight data",
            "       exceeds the BDP, then the sender can maintain a large standing",
            "       queue, increasing network latency and risking packet loss.",
            "",
            "   2.  rate mismatch: If a sender's volume of in-flight data matches the",
            "       BDP perfectly but its sending rate exceeds the available",
            "       bottleneck bandwidth (e.g. the sender transmits a BDP of data in",
            "       an unpaced fashion, at the sender's link rate), then up to a full",
            "       BDP of data can burst into the bottleneck queue, causing high",
            "       delay and/or high loss."
          ],
          "title": "High-Level Design Goals"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Based on the rationale above, BBR tries to spend most of its time",
            "   matching its sending process (data rate and data volume) to the",
            "   network path's delivery process.  To do this, it explores the",
            "   2-dimensional control parameter space of (1) data rate (\"bandwidth\"",
            "   or \"throughput\") and (2) data volume (\"in-flight data\"), with a goal",
            "   of finding the maximum values of each control parameter that are",
            "   consistent with its objective for queue pressure.",
            "",
            "   Depending on what signals a given network path manifests at a given",
            "   time, the objective for queue pressure is measured in terms of the",
            "   most strict among:",
            "",
            "   *  the amount of data that is estimated to be queued in the",
            "      bottleneck buffer (data_in_flight - estimated_BDP): the objective",
            "      is to maintain this amount at or below 1.5 * estimated_BDP",
            "",
            "   *  the packet loss rate: the objective is a maximum per-round-trip",
            "      packet loss rate of BBRLossThresh=2% (and an average packet loss",
            "      rate considerably lower)"
          ],
          "title": "Algorithm Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.3",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR varies its control parameters with a simple state machine that",
            "   aims for high throughput, low latency, and an approximately fair",
            "   sharing of bandwidth, while maintaining an up-to-date model of the",
            "   network path.",
            "",
            "   A BBR flow starts in the Startup state, and ramps up its sending rate",
            "   quickly, to rapidly estimate the maximum available bandwidth",
            "   (BBR.max_bw).  When it estimates the bottleneck bandwidth has been",
            "   fully utilized, it enters the Drain state to drain the estimated",
            "   queue.  In steady state a BBR flow mostly uses the ProbeBW states, to",
            "   periodically briefly send faster to probe for higher capacity and",
            "   then briefly send slower to try to drain any resulting queue.  If",
            "   needed, it briefly enters the ProbeRTT state, to lower the sending",
            "   rate to probe for lower BBR.min_rtt samples.  The detailed behavior",
            "   for each state is described below."
          ],
          "title": "State Machine Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Network Path Model Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   At a high level, the BBR model is trying to reflect two aspects of",
            "   the network path:",
            "",
            "   *  Model what's required for achieving full throughput: Estimate the",
            "      minimum data rate and data volume required to fully utilize the",
            "      fair share of the bottleneck bandwidth available to the flow.",
            "      This must incorporate estimates of the maximum available bandwidth",
            "      (BBR.max_bw), the BDP of the path (BBR.bdp), and the requirements",
            "      of any offload features on the end hosts or mechanisms on the",
            "      network path that produce aggregation effects (summing up to",
            "      BBR.max_inflight).",
            "",
            "   *  Model what's permitted for achieving low queue pressure: Estimate",
            "      the maximum data rate (BBR.bw) and data volume (cwnd) consistent",
            "      with the queue pressure objective, as measured by the estimated",
            "      degree of queuing and packet loss.",
            "",
            "   Note that those two aspects are in tension: the highest throughput is",
            "   available to the flow when it sends as fast as possible and occupies",
            "   as many bottleneck buffer slots as possible; the lowest que pressure",
            "   is achieved by the flow when it sends as slow as possible and",
            "   occupies as few bottleneck buffer slots as possible.  To resolve the",
            "   tension, the algorithm aims to achieve the maximum throughput",
            "   achievable while still meeting the queue pressure objective."
          ],
          "title": "High-Level Design Goals for the Network Path Model"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   At a high level, the BBR model is trying to reflect the properties of",
            "   the network path on two different time scales:"
          ],
          "title": "Time Scales for the Network Model"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   One goal is for BBR to maintain high average utilization of the fair",
            "   share of the available bandwidth, over long time intervals.  This",
            "   requires estimates of the path's data rate and volume capacities that",
            "   are robust over long time intervals.  This means being robust to",
            "   congestion signals that may be noisy or may reflect short-term",
            "   congestion that has already abated by the time an ACK arrives.  This",
            "   also means providing a robust history of the best recently-achievable",
            "   performance on the path so that the flow can quickly and robustly aim",
            "   to re-probe that level of performance whenever it decides to probe",
            "   the capacity of the path."
          ],
          "title": "Long-term model"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4.2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   A second goal of BBR is to react to every congestion signal,",
            "   including loss, as if it may indicate a persistent/long-term increase",
            "   in congestion and/or decrease in the bandwidth available to the flow,",
            "   because that may indeed be the case."
          ],
          "title": "Short-term model"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.4.2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR sequentially alternates between spending most of its time using",
            "   short-term models to conservatively respect all congestion signals in",
            "   case they represent persistent congestion, but periodically using its",
            "   long-term model to robustly probe the limits of the available path",
            "   capacity in case the congestion has abated and more capacity is",
            "   available."
          ],
          "title": "Time Scale Strategy"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.5",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR uses its model to control the connection's sending behavior.",
            "   Rather than using a single control parameter, like the cwnd parameter",
            "   that limits the volume of in-flight data in the Reno and CUBIC",
            "   congestion control algorithms, BBR uses three distinct control",
            "   parameters:",
            "",
            "   1.  pacing rate: the maximum rate at which BBR sends data.",
            "",
            "   2.  send quantum: the maximum size of any aggregate that the",
            "       transport sender implementation may need to transmit as a unit to",
            "       amortize per-packet transmission overheads.",
            "",
            "   3.  cwnd: the maximum volume of data BBR allows in-flight in the",
            "       network at any time."
          ],
          "title": "Control Parameter Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.6",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR is a congestion control algorithm that is agnostic to transport-",
            "   layer and link-layer technologies, requires only sender-side changes,",
            "   and does not require changes in the network.  Open source",
            "   implementations of BBR are available for the TCP [RFC793] and QUIC",
            "   [RFC9000] transport protocols, and these implementations have been",
            "   used in production for a large volume of Internet traffic.  An open",
            "   source implementation of BBR is also available for DCCP [RFC4340]",
            "   [draft-romo-iccrg-ccid5]."
          ],
          "title": "Environment and Usage"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Detailed Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   BBR implements a state machine that uses the network path model to",
            "   guide its decisions, and the control parameters to enact its",
            "   decisions."
          ],
          "title": "State Machine"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b068a126ff2ab86"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The following state transition diagram summarizes the flow of control"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b068a126ff2ab86"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "and the relationship between the different states:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "V"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b068a126ff2ab86"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+---> Startup  ------------+"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b068a126ff2ab86"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|        |                 |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b068a126ff2ab86"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|        V                 |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b068a126ff2ab86"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|     Drain  --------------+"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b068a126ff2ab86"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|        |                 |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
