        {
          "id": "appendix-A",
          "lines": [
            "   The pseudocode in this section describes sample algorithms.  These",
            "   algorithms are intended to be correct and clear, rather than being",
            "   optimally performant.",
            "",
            "   The pseudocode segments in this section are licensed as Code",
            "   Components; see the Copyright Notice."
          ],
          "title": "Pseudocode"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The pseudocode in Figure 45 shows how a variable-length integer can",
            "   be read from a stream of bytes.  The function ReadVarint takes a",
            "   single argument -- a sequence of bytes, which can be read in network",
            "   byte order.",
            "",
            "   ReadVarint(data):",
            "     // The length of variable-length integers is encoded in the",
            "     // first two bits of the first byte.",
            "     v = data.next_byte()",
            "     prefix = v >> 6",
            "     length = 1 << prefix",
            "",
            "     // Once the length is known, remove these bits and read any",
            "     // remaining bytes.",
            "     v = v & 0x3f",
            "     repeat length-1 times:",
            "       v = (v << 8) + data.next_byte()",
            "     return v",
            "",
            "        Figure 45: Sample Variable-Length Integer Decoding Algorithm",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69bb530980177fb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "For example, the eight-byte sequence 0xc2197c5eff14e88c decodes to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69bb530980177fb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the decimal value 151,288,809,941,952,652; the four-byte sequence"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69bb530980177fb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "0x9d7f3e7d decodes to 494,878,333; the two-byte sequence 0x7bbd"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69bb530980177fb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "decodes to 15,293; and the single byte 0x25 decodes to 37 (as does"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69bb530980177fb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the two-byte sequence 0x4025)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Sample Variable-Length Integer Decoding"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The pseudocode in Figure 46 shows how an implementation can select an",
            "   appropriate size for packet number encodings.",
            "",
            "   The EncodePacketNumber function takes two arguments:",
            "",
            "   *  full_pn is the full packet number of the packet being sent.",
            "",
            "   *  largest_acked is the largest packet number that has been",
            "      acknowledged by the peer in the current packet number space, if",
            "      any.",
            "",
            "   EncodePacketNumber(full_pn, largest_acked):",
            "",
            "     // The number of bits must be at least one more",
            "     // than the base-2 logarithm of the number of contiguous",
            "     // unacknowledged packet numbers, including the new packet.",
            "     if largest_acked is None:",
            "       num_unacked = full_pn + 1",
            "     else:",
            "       num_unacked = full_pn - largest_acked",
            "",
            "     min_bits = log(num_unacked, 2) + 1",
            "     num_bytes = ceil(min_bits / 8)",
            "",
            "     // Encode the integer value and truncate to",
            "     // the num_bytes least significant bytes.",
            "     return encode(full_pn, num_bytes)",
            "",
            "             Figure 46: Sample Packet Number Encoding Algorithm",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "For example, if an endpoint has received an acknowledgment for packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "0xabe8b3 and is sending a packet with a number of 0xac5c02, there are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "29,519 (0x734f) outstanding packet numbers.  In order to represent at"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "least twice this range (59,038 packets, or 0xe69e), 16 bits are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "required."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "In the same state, sending a packet with a number of 0xace8fe uses"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the 24-bit encoding, because at least 18 bits are required to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "763bf9c745dc66ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "represent twice the range (131,222 packets, or 0x020096)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Sample Packet Number Encoding Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The pseudocode in Figure 47 includes an example algorithm for",
            "   decoding packet numbers after header protection has been removed.",
            "",
            "   The DecodePacketNumber function takes three arguments:",
            "",
            "   *  largest_pn is the largest packet number that has been successfully",
            "      processed in the current packet number space.",
            "",
            "   *  truncated_pn is the value of the Packet Number field.",
            "",
            "   *  pn_nbits is the number of bits in the Packet Number field (8, 16,",
            "      24, or 32).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "DecodePacketNumber(largest_pn, truncated_pn, pn_nbits):"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "expected_pn  = largest_pn + 1"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "pn_win       = 1 << pn_nbits"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "pn_hwin      = pn_win / 2"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "pn_mask      = pn_win - 1"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// The incoming packet number should be greater than"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// expected_pn - pn_hwin and less than or equal to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// expected_pn + pn_hwin"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "//"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// This means we cannot just strip the trailing bits from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// expected_pn and add the truncated_pn because that might"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// yield a value outside the window."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "//"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// The following code calculates a candidate value and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// makes sure it's within the packet number window."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "// Note the extra checks to prevent overflow and underflow."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "candidate_pn = (expected_pn & ~pn_mask) | truncated_pn"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "if candidate_pn <= expected_pn - pn_hwin and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "candidate_pn < (1 << 62) - pn_win:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "return candidate_pn + pn_win"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "if candidate_pn > expected_pn + pn_hwin and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "candidate_pn >= pn_win:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "return candidate_pn - pn_win"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b6c04dc7ab3befbb",
                  "0d9f6a1122406686"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "return candidate_pn"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "             Figure 47: Sample Packet Number Decoding Algorithm",
            "",
            "   For example, if the highest successfully authenticated packet had a",
            "   packet number of 0xa82f30ea, then a packet containing a 16-bit value",
            "   of 0x9b32 will be decoded as 0xa82f9b32."
          ],
          "title": "Sample Packet Number Decoding Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.4",
          "lines": [
            "   Each time an endpoint commences sending on a new network path, it",
            "   determines whether the path supports ECN; see Section 13.4.  If the",
            "   path supports ECN, the goal is to use ECN.  Endpoints might also",
            "   periodically reassess a path that was determined to not support ECN.",
            "",
            "   This section describes one method for testing new paths.  This",
            "   algorithm is intended to show how a path might be tested for ECN",
            "   support.  Endpoints can implement different methods.",
            "",
            "   The path is assigned an ECN state that is one of \"testing\",",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   \"unknown\", \"failed\", or \"capable\".  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90f11eb804d90e07"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "On paths with a \"testing\" or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90f11eb804d90e07"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"capable\" state, the endpoint sends packets with an ECT marking --"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "90f11eb804d90e07"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ECT(0) by default; otherwise, the endpoint sends unmarked packets."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   To start testing a path, the ECN state is set to \"testing\", and",
            "   existing ECN counts are remembered as a baseline.",
            "",
            "   The testing period runs for a number of packets or a limited time, as",
            "   determined by the endpoint.  The goal is not to limit the duration of",
            "   the testing period but to ensure that enough marked packets are sent",
            "   for received ECN counts to provide a clear indication of how the path",
            "   treats marked packets.  Section 13.4.2 suggests limiting this to ten",
            "   packets or three times the PTO.",
            "",
            "   After the testing period ends, the ECN state for the path becomes",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   \"unknown\".  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be319e04503806ab",
                  "6e611df783e7c466"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "From the \"unknown\" state, successful validation of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be319e04503806ab",
                  "6e611df783e7c466"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "ECN counts in an ACK frame (see Section 13.4.2.1) causes the ECN"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be319e04503806ab",
                  "6e611df783e7c466"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "state for the path to become \"capable\", unless no marked packet has"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "be319e04503806ab",
                  "6e611df783e7c466"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "been acknowledged."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If validation of ECN counts fails at any time, the ECN state for the",
            "   affected path becomes \"failed\".  An endpoint can also mark the ECN",
            "   state for a path as \"failed\" if marked packets are all declared lost",
            "   or if they are all ECN-CE marked.",
            "",
            "   Following this algorithm ensures that ECN is rarely disabled for",
            "   paths that properly support ECN.  Any path that incorrectly modifies",
            "   markings will cause ECN to be disabled.  For those rare cases where",
            "   marked packets are discarded by the path, the short duration of the",
            "   testing period limits the number of losses incurred."
          ],
          "title": "Sample ECN Validation Algorithm"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-contributors",
          "lines": [
            "   The original design and rationale behind this protocol draw",
            "   significantly from work by Jim Roskind [EARLY-DESIGN].",
            "",
            "   The IETF QUIC Working Group received an enormous amount of support",
            "   from many people.  The following people provided substantive",
            "   contributions to this document:",
