            "   include Simplified BSD License text as described in Section 4.e of",
            "   the Trust Legal Provisions and are provided without warranty as",
            "   described in the Simplified BSD License."
          ],
          "title": "Copyright Notice"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-table-of-contents",
          "lines": [
            "   1.  Introduction",
            "   2.  Notational Conventions",
            "     2.1.  TLS Overview",
            "   3.  Protocol Overview",
            "   4.  Carrying TLS Messages",
            "     4.1.  Interface to TLS",
            "       4.1.1.  Handshake Complete",
            "       4.1.2.  Handshake Confirmed",
            "       4.1.3.  Sending and Receiving Handshake Messages",
            "       4.1.4.  Encryption Level Changes",
            "       4.1.5.  TLS Interface Summary",
            "     4.2.  TLS Version",
            "     4.3.  ClientHello Size",
            "     4.4.  Peer Authentication",
            "     4.5.  Session Resumption",
            "     4.6.  0-RTT",
            "       4.6.1.  Enabling 0-RTT",
            "       4.6.2.  Accepting and Rejecting 0-RTT",
            "       4.6.3.  Validating 0-RTT Configuration",
            "     4.7.  HelloRetryRequest",
            "     4.8.  TLS Errors",
            "     4.9.  Discarding Unused Keys",
            "       4.9.1.  Discarding Initial Keys",
            "       4.9.2.  Discarding Handshake Keys",
            "       4.9.3.  Discarding 0-RTT Keys",
            "   5.  Packet Protection",
            "     5.1.  Packet Protection Keys",
            "     5.2.  Initial Secrets",
            "     5.3.  AEAD Usage",
            "     5.4.  Header Protection",
            "       5.4.1.  Header Protection Application",
            "       5.4.2.  Header Protection Sample",
            "       5.4.3.  AES-Based Header Protection",
            "       5.4.4.  ChaCha20-Based Header Protection",
            "     5.5.  Receiving Protected Packets",
            "     5.6.  Use of 0-RTT Keys",
            "     5.7.  Receiving Out-of-Order Protected Packets",
            "     5.8.  Retry Packet Integrity",
            "   6.  Key Update",
            "     6.1.  Initiating a Key Update",
            "     6.2.  Responding to a Key Update",
            "     6.3.  Timing of Receive Key Generation",
            "     6.4.  Sending with Updated Keys",
            "     6.5.  Receiving with Different Keys",
            "     6.6.  Limits on AEAD Usage",
            "     6.7.  Key Update Error Code",
            "   7.  Security of Initial Messages",
            "   8.  QUIC-Specific Adjustments to the TLS Handshake",
            "     8.1.  Protocol Negotiation",
            "     8.2.  QUIC Transport Parameters Extension",
            "     8.3.  Removing the EndOfEarlyData Message",
            "     8.4.  Prohibit TLS Middlebox Compatibility Mode",
            "   9.  Security Considerations",
            "     9.1.  Session Linkability",
            "     9.2.  Replay Attacks with 0-RTT",
            "     9.3.  Packet Reflection Attack Mitigation",
            "     9.4.  Header Protection Analysis",
            "     9.5.  Header Protection Timing Side Channels",
            "     9.6.  Key Diversity",
            "     9.7.  Randomness",
            "   10. IANA Considerations",
            "   11. References",
            "     11.1.  Normative References",
            "     11.2.  Informative References",
            "   Appendix A.  Sample Packet Protection",
            "     A.1.  Keys",
            "     A.2.  Client Initial",
            "     A.3.  Server Initial",
            "     A.4.  Retry",
            "     A.5.  ChaCha20-Poly1305 Short Header Packet",
            "   Appendix B.  AEAD Algorithm Analysis",
            "     B.1.  Analysis of AEAD_AES_128_GCM and AEAD_AES_256_GCM Usage",
            "           Limits",
            "       B.1.1.  Confidentiality Limit",
            "       B.1.2.  Integrity Limit",
            "     B.2.  Analysis of AEAD_AES_128_CCM Usage Limits",
            "   Contributors",
            "   Authors' Addresses"
          ],
          "title": "Table of Contents"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   This document describes how QUIC [QUIC-TRANSPORT] is secured using",
            "   TLS [TLS13].",
            "",
            "   TLS 1.3 provides critical latency improvements for connection",
            "   establishment over previous versions.  Absent packet loss, most new",
            "   connections can be established and secured within a single round",
            "   trip; on subsequent connections between the same client and server,",
            "   the client can often send application data immediately, that is,",
            "   using a zero round-trip setup.",
            "",
            "   This document describes how TLS acts as a security component of QUIC."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"NOT RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and",
            "   \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP",
            "   14 [RFC2119] [RFC8174] when, and only when, they appear in all",
            "   capitals, as shown here.",
            "",
            "   This document uses the terminology established in [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   For brevity, the acronym TLS is used to refer to TLS 1.3, though a",
            "   newer version could be used; see Section 4.2."
          ],
          "title": "Notational Conventions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   TLS provides two endpoints with a way to establish a means of",
            "   communication over an untrusted medium (for example, the Internet).",
            "   TLS enables authentication of peers and provides confidentiality and",
            "   integrity protection for messages that endpoints exchange.",
            "",
            "   Internally, TLS is a layered protocol, with the structure shown in",
            "   Figure 1.",
            "",
            "             +-------------+------------+--------------+---------+",
            "   Content   |             |            |  Application |         |",
            "   Layer     |  Handshake  |   Alerts   |     Data     |   ...   |",
            "             |             |            |              |         |",
            "             +-------------+------------+--------------+---------+",
            "   Record    |                                                   |",
            "   Layer     |                      Records                      |",
            "             |                                                   |",
            "             +---------------------------------------------------+",
            "",
            "                            Figure 1: TLS Layers",
            "",
            "   Each content-layer message (e.g., handshake, alerts, and application",
            "   data) is carried as a series of typed TLS records by the record",
            "   layer.  Records are individually cryptographically protected and then",
            "   transmitted over a reliable transport (typically TCP), which provides",
            "   sequencing and guaranteed delivery.",
            "",
            "   The TLS authenticated key exchange occurs between two endpoints:",
            "   client and server.  The client initiates the exchange and the server",
            "   responds.  If the key exchange completes successfully, both client",
            "   and server will agree on a secret.  TLS supports both pre-shared key",
            "   (PSK) and Diffie-Hellman over either finite fields or elliptic curves",
            "   ((EC)DHE) key exchanges.  PSK is the basis for Early Data (0-RTT);",
            "   the latter provides forward secrecy (FS) when the (EC)DHE keys are",
            "   destroyed.  The two modes can also be combined to provide forward",
            "   secrecy while using the PSK for authentication.",
            "",
            "   After completing the TLS handshake, the client will have learned and",
            "   authenticated an identity for the server, and the server is",
            "   optionally able to learn and authenticate an identity for the client.",
            "   TLS supports X.509 [RFC5280] certificate-based authentication for",
            "   both server and client.  When PSK key exchange is used (as in",
            "   resumption), knowledge of the PSK serves to authenticate the peer.",
            "",
            "   The TLS key exchange is resistant to tampering by attackers, and it",
            "   produces shared secrets that cannot be controlled by either",
            "   participating peer.",
            "",
            "   TLS provides two basic handshake modes of interest to QUIC:",
            "",
            "   *  A full 1-RTT handshake, in which the client is able to send",
            "      application data after one round trip and the server immediately",
            "      responds after receiving the first handshake message from the",
            "      client.",
            "",
            "   *  A 0-RTT handshake, in which the client uses information it has",
            "      previously learned about the server to send application data",
            "      immediately.  This application data can be replayed by an",
            "      attacker, so 0-RTT is not suitable for carrying instructions that",
            "      might initiate any action that could cause unwanted effects if",
            "      replayed.",
            "",
            "   A simplified TLS handshake with 0-RTT application data is shown in",
            "   Figure 2.",
            "",
            "       Client                                             Server",
            "",
            "       ClientHello",
            "      (0-RTT Application Data)  -------->",
            "                                                     ServerHello",
            "                                            {EncryptedExtensions}",
            "                                                       {Finished}",
            "                                <--------      [Application Data]",
            "      {Finished}                -------->",
            "",
            "      [Application Data]        <------->      [Application Data]",
            "",
            "       () Indicates messages protected by Early Data (0-RTT) Keys",
            "       {} Indicates messages protected using Handshake Keys",
            "       [] Indicates messages protected using Application Data",
            "          (1-RTT) Keys",
            "",
            "                     Figure 2: TLS Handshake with 0-RTT",
            "",
            "   Figure 2 omits the EndOfEarlyData message, which is not used in QUIC;",
            "   see Section 8.3.  Likewise, neither ChangeCipherSpec nor KeyUpdate",
            "   messages are used by QUIC.  ChangeCipherSpec is redundant in TLS 1.3;",
            "   see Section 8.4.  QUIC has its own key update mechanism; see",
            "   Section 6.",
            "",
            "   Data is protected using a number of encryption levels:",
            "",
            "   *  Initial keys",
            "",
            "   *  Early data (0-RTT) keys",
            "",
            "   *  Handshake keys",
            "",
            "   *  Application data (1-RTT) keys",
            "",
            "   Application data can only appear in the early data and application",
            "   data levels.  Handshake and alert messages may appear in any level.",
            "",
            "   The 0-RTT handshake can be used if the client and server have",
            "   previously communicated.  In the 1-RTT handshake, the client is",
            "   unable to send protected application data until it has received all",
            "   of the handshake messages sent by the server."
          ],
          "title": "TLS Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC [QUIC-TRANSPORT] assumes responsibility for the confidentiality",
            "   and integrity protection of packets.  For this it uses keys derived",
            "   from a TLS handshake [TLS13], but instead of carrying TLS records",
            "   over QUIC (as with TCP), TLS handshake and alert messages are carried",
            "   directly over the QUIC transport, which takes over the",
            "   responsibilities of the TLS record layer, as shown in Figure 3.",
            "",
            "   +--------------+--------------+ +-------------+",
            "   |     TLS      |     TLS      | |    QUIC     |",
            "   |  Handshake   |    Alerts    | | Applications|",
            "   |              |              | |  (h3, etc.) |",
            "   +--------------+--------------+-+-------------+",
            "   |                                             |",
            "   |                QUIC Transport               |",
            "   |   (streams, reliability, congestion, etc.)  |",
            "   |                                             |",
            "   +---------------------------------------------+",
            "   |                                             |",
            "   |            QUIC Packet Protection           |",
            "   |                                             |",
            "   +---------------------------------------------+",
            "",
            "                           Figure 3: QUIC Layers",
            "",
            "   QUIC also relies on TLS for authentication and negotiation of",
            "   parameters that are critical to security and performance.",
            "",
            "   Rather than a strict layering, these two protocols cooperate: QUIC",
            "   uses the TLS handshake; TLS uses the reliability, ordered delivery,",
            "   and record layer provided by QUIC.",
            "",
            "   At a high level, there are two main interactions between the TLS and",
            "   QUIC components:",
            "",
            "   *  The TLS component sends and receives messages via the QUIC",
            "      component, with QUIC providing a reliable stream abstraction to",
            "      TLS.",
            "",
            "   *  The TLS component provides a series of updates to the QUIC",
            "      component, including (a) new packet protection keys to install and",
            "      (b) state changes such as handshake completion, the server",
            "      certificate, etc.",
            "",
            "   Figure 4 shows these interactions in more detail, with the QUIC",
            "   packet protection being called out specially.",
            "",
            "   +------------+                               +------------+",
            "   |            |<---- Handshake Messages ----->|            |",
            "   |            |<- Validate 0-RTT Parameters ->|            |",
            "   |            |<--------- 0-RTT Keys ---------|            |",
            "   |    QUIC    |<------- Handshake Keys -------|    TLS     |",
            "   |            |<--------- 1-RTT Keys ---------|            |",
            "   |            |<------- Handshake Done -------|            |",
            "   +------------+                               +------------+",
            "    |         ^",
            "    | Protect | Protected",
            "    v         | Packet",
            "   +------------+",
            "   |   QUIC     |",
            "   |  Packet    |",
            "   | Protection |",
            "   +------------+",
            "",
            "                    Figure 4: QUIC and TLS Interactions",
            "",
            "   Unlike TLS over TCP, QUIC applications that want to send data do not",
            "   send it using TLS Application Data records.  Rather, they send it as",
            "   QUIC STREAM frames or other frame types, which are then carried in",
            "   QUIC packets."
          ],
          "title": "Protocol Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC carries TLS handshake data in CRYPTO frames, each of which",
            "   consists of a contiguous block of handshake data identified by an",
            "   offset and length.  Those frames are packaged into QUIC packets and",
            "   encrypted under the current encryption level.  As with TLS over TCP,",
            "   once TLS handshake data has been delivered to QUIC, it is QUIC's",
            "   responsibility to deliver it reliably.  Each chunk of data that is",
            "   produced by TLS is associated with the set of keys that TLS is",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   currently using.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62822a8f8fb4c37d",
                  "1bc29c0e219c09e0",
                  "17207c41759e9b87"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If QUIC needs to retransmit that data, it MUST use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "62822a8f8fb4c37d",
                  "1bc29c0e219c09e0",
                  "17207c41759e9b87"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the same keys even if TLS has already updated to newer keys."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Each encryption level corresponds to a packet number space.  The",
            "   packet number space that is used determines the semantics of frames.",
            "   Some frames are prohibited in different packet number spaces; see",
            "   Section 12.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   Because packets could be reordered on the wire, QUIC uses the packet",
            "   type to indicate which keys were used to protect a given packet, as",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   shown in Table 1.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e971c797bc251ea",
                  "4816853cb1241237"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "When packets of different types need to be sent,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e971c797bc251ea",
                  "4816853cb1241237"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "endpoints SHOULD use coalesced packets to send them in the same UDP"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e971c797bc251ea",
                  "4816853cb1241237"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "datagram."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "       +=====================+=================+==================+",
            "       | Packet Type         | Encryption Keys | PN Space         |",
            "       +=====================+=================+==================+",
            "       | Initial             | Initial secrets | Initial          |",
            "       +=====================+-----------------+------------------+",
            "       | 0-RTT Protected     | 0-RTT           | Application data |",
            "       +=====================+-----------------+------------------+",
            "       | Handshake           | Handshake       | Handshake        |",
            "       +=====================+-----------------+------------------+",
            "       | Retry               | Retry           | N/A              |",
            "       +=====================+-----------------+------------------+",
            "       | Version Negotiation | N/A             | N/A              |",
            "       +=====================+-----------------+------------------+",
            "       | Short Header        | 1-RTT           | Application data |",
            "       +=====================+-----------------+------------------+",
            "",
            "                 Table 1: Encryption Keys by Packet Type",
            "",
            "   Section 17 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT] shows how packets at the various",
            "   encryption levels fit into the handshake process."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "17207c41759e9b87",
            "17207c41759e9b87",
            "4816853cb1241237",
            "4816853cb1241237",
            "4816853cb1241237"
          ],
          "title": "Carrying TLS Messages"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   As shown in Figure 4, the interface from QUIC to TLS consists of four",
            "   primary functions:",
            "",
            "   *  Sending and receiving handshake messages",
            "",
            "   *  Processing stored transport and application state from a resumed",
            "      session and determining if it is valid to generate or accept 0-RTT",
            "      data",
            "",
            "   *  Rekeying (both transmit and receive)",
            "",
            "   *  Updating handshake state",
            "",
            "   Additional functions might be needed to configure TLS.  In",
            "   particular, QUIC and TLS need to agree on which is responsible for",
            "   validation of peer credentials, such as certificate validation",
            "   [RFC5280]."
          ],
          "title": "Interface to TLS"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   In this document, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a0a0a90af49b4de"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the TLS handshake is considered complete when the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a0a0a90af49b4de"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "TLS stack has reported that the handshake is complete.  This happens"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a0a0a90af49b4de"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "when the TLS stack has both sent a Finished message and verified the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a0a0a90af49b4de"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "peer's Finished message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Verifying the peer's Finished message"
              }
            ],
            "   provides the endpoints with an assurance that previous handshake",
            "   messages have not been modified.  Note that the handshake does not",
            "   complete at both endpoints simultaneously.  Consequently, any",
            "   requirement that is based on the completion of the handshake depends",
            "   on the perspective of the endpoint in question."
          ],
          "title": "Handshake Complete"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   In this document, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e40900b4ec58047e",
                  "2ce02182b723912b",
                  "c94a79b672019aa1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "the TLS handshake is considered confirmed at the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e40900b4ec58047e",
                  "2ce02182b723912b",
                  "c94a79b672019aa1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "server when the handshake completes"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2ce02182b723912b",
                  "c94a79b672019aa1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a103e4165f1b0a99",
                  "e26d8caf6fdd7308"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The server MUST send a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a103e4165f1b0a99",
                  "e26d8caf6fdd7308"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "HANDSHAKE_DONE frame as soon as the handshake is complete."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c25dd3f1c84e32f",
                  "263348d9dc02b987"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "At the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c25dd3f1c84e32f",
                  "263348d9dc02b987"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "client, the handshake is considered confirmed when a HANDSHAKE_DONE"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c25dd3f1c84e32f",
                  "263348d9dc02b987"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "frame is received."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4115fc0f9a430f14",
                  "ac6a2d4ded35c580"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "Additionally, a client MAY consider the handshake to be confirmed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4115fc0f9a430f14",
                  "ac6a2d4ded35c580"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "when it receives an acknowledgment for a 1-RTT packet."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This can be"
              }
            ],
            "   implemented by recording the lowest packet number sent with 1-RTT",
            "   keys and comparing it to the Largest Acknowledged field in any",
            "   received 1-RTT ACK frame: once the latter is greater than or equal to",
            "   the former, the handshake is confirmed."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e26d8caf6fdd7308",
            "e26d8caf6fdd7308",
            "ac6a2d4ded35c580",
            "ac6a2d4ded35c580"
          ],
          "title": "Handshake Confirmed"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.3",
          "lines": [
            "   In order to drive the handshake, TLS depends on being able to send",
            "   and receive handshake messages.  There are two basic functions on",
            "   this interface: one where QUIC requests handshake messages and one",
            "   where QUIC provides bytes that comprise handshake messages.",
            "",
            "   Before starting the handshake, QUIC provides TLS with the transport",
            "   parameters (see Section 8.2) that it wishes to carry.",
            "",
            "   A QUIC client starts TLS by requesting TLS handshake bytes from TLS.",
            "   The client acquires handshake bytes before sending its first packet.",
            "   A QUIC server starts the process by providing TLS with the client's",
            "   handshake bytes.",
            "",
            "   At any time, the TLS stack at an endpoint will have a current sending",
            "   encryption level and a receiving encryption level.  TLS encryption",
            "   levels determine the QUIC packet type and keys that are used for",
            "   protecting data.",
            "",
            "   Each encryption level is associated with a different sequence of",
            "   bytes, which is reliably transmitted to the peer in CRYPTO frames.",
            "   When TLS provides handshake bytes to be sent, they are appended to",
            "   the handshake bytes for the current encryption level.  The encryption",
            "   level then determines the type of packet that the resulting CRYPTO",
            "   frame is carried in; see Table 1.",
            "",
            "   Four encryption levels are used, producing keys for Initial, 0-RTT,",
            "   Handshake, and 1-RTT packets.  CRYPTO frames are carried in just",
            "   three of these levels, omitting the 0-RTT level.  These four levels",
            "   correspond to three packet number spaces: Initial and Handshake",
            "   encrypted packets use their own separate spaces; 0-RTT and 1-RTT",
            "   packets use the application data packet number space.",
            "",
            "   QUIC takes the unprotected content of TLS handshake records as the",
            "   content of CRYPTO frames.  TLS record protection is not used by QUIC.",
            "   QUIC assembles CRYPTO frames into QUIC packets, which are protected",
            "   using QUIC packet protection.",
            "",
            "   QUIC CRYPTO frames only carry TLS handshake messages.  TLS alerts are",
            "   turned into QUIC CONNECTION_CLOSE error codes; see Section 4.8.  TLS",
            "   application data and other content types cannot be carried by QUIC at",
            "   any encryption level; it is an error if they are received from the",
            "   TLS stack.",
            "",
            "   When an endpoint receives a QUIC packet containing a CRYPTO frame",
            "   from the network, it proceeds as follows:",
            "",
            "   *  If the packet uses the current TLS receiving encryption level,",
            "      sequence the data into the input flow as usual.  As with STREAM",
            "      frames, the offset is used to find the proper location in the data",
            "      sequence.  If the result of this process is that new data is",
            "      available, then it is delivered to TLS in order.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "57854e1f88a1d9be",
                  "dd3c75de6e238f50"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "*  If the packet is from a previously installed encryption level, it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "57854e1f88a1d9be",
                  "dd3c75de6e238f50"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST NOT contain data that extends past the end of previously"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "57854e1f88a1d9be",
                  "dd3c75de6e238f50"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "received data in that flow."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "57854e1f88a1d9be"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "57854e1f88a1d9be",
                  "104af49c55fd7002"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Implementations MUST treat any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "57854e1f88a1d9be",
                  "104af49c55fd7002"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "violations of this requirement as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "57854e1f88a1d9be",
                  "104af49c55fd7002"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "PROTOCOL_VIOLATION."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   *  If the packet is from a new encryption level, it is saved for",
            "      later processing by TLS.  Once TLS moves to receiving from this",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      encryption level, saved data can be provided to TLS.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45f55875d21ff494",
                  "44c23a453e527497"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "When TLS"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45f55875d21ff494",
                  "44c23a453e527497"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "provides keys for a higher encryption level, if there is data from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45f55875d21ff494",
                  "44c23a453e527497"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "a previous encryption level that TLS has not consumed, this MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45f55875d21ff494",
                  "44c23a453e527497"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "be treated as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Each time that TLS is provided with new data, new handshake bytes are",
            "   requested from TLS.  TLS might not provide any bytes if the handshake",
            "   messages it has received are incomplete or it has no data to send.",
            "",
            "   The content of CRYPTO frames might either be processed incrementally",
            "   by TLS or buffered until complete messages or flights are available.",
            "   TLS is responsible for buffering handshake bytes that have arrived in",
            "   order.  QUIC is responsible for buffering handshake bytes that arrive",
            "   out of order or for encryption levels that are not yet ready.  QUIC",
            "   does not provide any means of flow control for CRYPTO frames; see",
            "   Section 7.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   Once the TLS handshake is complete, this is indicated to QUIC along",
            "   with any final handshake bytes that TLS needs to send.  At this",
            "   stage, the transport parameters that the peer advertised during the",
            "   handshake are authenticated; see Section 8.2.",
            "",
            "   Once the handshake is complete, TLS becomes passive.  TLS can still",
            "   receive data from its peer and respond in kind, but it will not need",
            "   to send more data unless specifically requested -- either by an",
            "   application or QUIC.  One reason to send data is that the server",
            "   might wish to provide additional or updated session tickets to a",
            "   client.",
            "",
            "   When the handshake is complete, QUIC only needs to provide TLS with",
            "   any data that arrives in CRYPTO streams.  In the same manner that is",
            "   used during the handshake, new data is requested from TLS after",
            "   providing received data."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "dd3c75de6e238f50",
            "dd3c75de6e238f50",
            "dd3c75de6e238f50",
            "104af49c55fd7002",
            "104af49c55fd7002",
            "104af49c55fd7002",
            "44c23a453e527497",
            "44c23a453e527497",
            "44c23a453e527497",
            "44c23a453e527497"
          ],
          "title": "Sending and Receiving Handshake Messages"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.4",
          "lines": [
            "   As keys at a given encryption level become available to TLS, TLS",
            "   indicates to QUIC that reading or writing keys at that encryption",
            "   level are available.",
            "",
            "   The availability of new keys is always a result of providing inputs",
            "   to TLS.  TLS only provides new keys after being initialized (by a",
            "   client) or when provided with new handshake data.",
            "",
            "   However, a TLS implementation could perform some of its processing",
            "   asynchronously.  In particular, the process of validating a",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   certificate can take some time.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83a09f7d66603ba9",
                  "80d45779e9fc63ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "While waiting for TLS processing to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83a09f7d66603ba9",
                  "80d45779e9fc63ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "complete, an endpoint SHOULD buffer received packets if they might be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83a09f7d66603ba9",
                  "80d45779e9fc63ca"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "processed using keys that are not yet available."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  These packets can"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   be processed once keys are provided by TLS.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd8533a789ef98bf",
                  "d658381659295dcf"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "An endpoint SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd8533a789ef98bf",
                  "d658381659295dcf"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "continue to respond to packets that can be processed during this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd8533a789ef98bf",
                  "d658381659295dcf"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "time."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   After processing inputs, TLS might produce handshake bytes, keys for",
            "   new encryption levels, or both.",
            "",
            "   TLS provides QUIC with three items as a new encryption level becomes",
            "   available:",
            "",
            "   *  A secret",
            "",
            "   *  An Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data (AEAD) function",
            "",
            "   *  A Key Derivation Function (KDF)",
            "",
            "   These values are based on the values that TLS negotiates and are used",
            "   by QUIC to generate packet and header protection keys; see Section 5",
            "   and Section 5.4.",
            "",
            "   If 0-RTT is possible, it is ready after the client sends a TLS",
            "   ClientHello message or the server receives that message.  After",
            "   providing a QUIC client with the first handshake bytes, the TLS stack",
            "   might signal the change to 0-RTT keys.  On the server, after",
            "   receiving handshake bytes that contain a ClientHello message, a TLS",
            "   server might signal that 0-RTT keys are available.",
            "",
            "   Although TLS only uses one encryption level at a time, QUIC may use",
            "   more than one level.  For instance, after sending its Finished",
            "   message (using a CRYPTO frame at the Handshake encryption level) an",
            "   endpoint can send STREAM data (in 1-RTT encryption).  If the Finished",
            "   message is lost, the endpoint uses the Handshake encryption level to",
            "   retransmit the lost message.  Reordering or loss of packets can mean",
            "   that QUIC will need to handle packets at multiple encryption levels.",
            "   During the handshake, this means potentially handling packets at",
            "   higher and lower encryption levels than the current encryption level",
            "   used by TLS.",
            "",
            "   In particular, server implementations need to be able to read packets",
            "   at the Handshake encryption level at the same time as the 0-RTT",
            "   encryption level.  A client could interleave ACK frames that are",
            "   protected with Handshake keys with 0-RTT data, and the server needs",
            "   to process those acknowledgments in order to detect lost Handshake",
            "   packets.",
            "",
            "   QUIC also needs access to keys that might not ordinarily be available",
            "   to a TLS implementation.  For instance, a client might need to",
            "   acknowledge Handshake packets before it is ready to send CRYPTO",
            "   frames at that encryption level.  TLS therefore needs to provide keys",
            "   to QUIC before it might produce them for its own use."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "80d45779e9fc63ca",
            "80d45779e9fc63ca",
            "80d45779e9fc63ca",
            "d658381659295dcf",
            "d658381659295dcf",
            "d658381659295dcf"
          ],
          "title": "Encryption Level Changes"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.5",
          "lines": [
            "   Figure 5 summarizes the exchange between QUIC and TLS for both client",
            "   and server.  Solid arrows indicate packets that carry handshake data;",
            "   dashed arrows show where application data can be sent.  Each arrow is",
            "   tagged with the encryption level used for that transmission.",
            "",
            "   Client                                                    Server",
            "   ======                                                    ======",
            "",
            "   Get Handshake",
            "                        Initial ------------->",
            "   Install tx 0-RTT keys",
            "                        0-RTT - - - - - - - ->",
            "",
            "                                                 Handshake Received",
            "                                                      Get Handshake",
            "                        <------------- Initial",
            "                                              Install rx 0-RTT keys",
            "                                             Install Handshake keys",
            "                                                      Get Handshake",
            "                        <----------- Handshake",
            "                                              Install tx 1-RTT keys",
            "                        <- - - - - - - - 1-RTT",
            "",
            "   Handshake Received (Initial)",
            "   Install Handshake keys",
            "   Handshake Received (Handshake)",
            "   Get Handshake",
            "                        Handshake ----------->",
            "   Handshake Complete",
            "   Install 1-RTT keys",
            "                        1-RTT - - - - - - - ->",
            "",
            "                                                 Handshake Received",
            "                                                 Handshake Complete",
            "                                                Handshake Confirmed",
            "                                              Install rx 1-RTT keys",
            "                        <--------------- 1-RTT",
            "                              (HANDSHAKE_DONE)",
            "   Handshake Confirmed",
            "",
            "             Figure 5: Interaction Summary between QUIC and TLS",
            "",
            "   Figure 5 shows the multiple packets that form a single \"flight\" of",
            "   messages being processed individually, to show what incoming messages",
            "   trigger different actions.  This shows multiple \"Get Handshake\"",
            "   invocations to retrieve handshake messages at different encryption",
            "   levels.  New handshake messages are requested after incoming packets",
            "   have been processed.",
            "",
            "   Figure 5 shows one possible structure for a simple handshake",
            "   exchange.  The exact process varies based on the structure of",
            "   endpoint implementations and the order in which packets arrive.",
            "   Implementations could use a different number of operations or execute",
            "   them in other orders."
          ],
          "title": "TLS Interface Summary"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   This document describes how TLS 1.3 [TLS13] is used with QUIC.",
            "",
            "   In practice, the TLS handshake will negotiate a version of TLS to",
            "   use.  This could result in a version of TLS newer than 1.3 being",
            "   negotiated if both endpoints support that version.  This is",
            "   acceptable provided that the features of TLS 1.3 that are used by",
            "   QUIC are supported by the newer version.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff3892d7e82b2059",
                  "511d57f420209d23"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT offer TLS versions older than 1.3."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  A badly"
              }
            ],
            "   configured TLS implementation could negotiate TLS 1.2 or another",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   older version of TLS.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a9f7f03ae812e2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST terminate the connection if a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a9f7f03ae812e2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "version of TLS older than 1.3 is negotiated."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "511d57f420209d23",
            "7a9f7f03ae812e2e",
            "7a9f7f03ae812e2e"
          ],
          "title": "TLS Version"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The first Initial packet from a client contains the start or all of",
            "   its first cryptographic handshake message, which for TLS is the",
            "   ClientHello.  Servers might need to parse the entire ClientHello",
            "   (e.g., to access extensions such as Server Name Identification (SNI)",
            "   or Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation (ALPN)) in order to decide",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   whether to accept the new incoming QUIC connection.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "ClientHello spans multiple Initial packets, such servers would need"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "to buffer the first received fragments, which could consume excessive"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "resources if the client's address has not yet been validated.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb",
                  "0b26957a366da714"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "To"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb",
                  "0b26957a366da714"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "avoid this, servers MAY use the Retry feature (see Section 8.1 of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb",
                  "0b26957a366da714"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "[QUIC-TRANSPORT]) to only buffer partial ClientHello messages from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c4563fafea83efb",
                  "0b26957a366da714"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "clients with a validated address."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   QUIC packet and framing add at least 36 bytes of overhead to the",
            "   ClientHello message.  That overhead increases if the client chooses a",
            "   Source Connection ID field longer than zero bytes.  Overheads also do",
            "   not include the token or a Destination Connection ID longer than 8",
            "   bytes, both of which might be required if a server sends a Retry",
            "   packet.",
            "",
            "   A typical TLS ClientHello can easily fit into a 1200-byte packet.",
            "   However, in addition to the overheads added by QUIC, there are",
            "   several variables that could cause this limit to be exceeded.  Large",
            "   session tickets, multiple or large key shares, and long lists of",
            "   supported ciphers, signature algorithms, versions, QUIC transport",
            "   parameters, and other negotiable parameters and extensions could",
            "   cause this message to grow.",
            "",
            "   For servers, in addition to connection IDs and tokens, the size of",
            "   TLS session tickets can have an effect on a client's ability to",
            "   connect efficiently.  Minimizing the size of these values increases",
            "   the probability that clients can use them and still fit their entire",
            "   ClientHello message in their first Initial packet.",
            "",
            "   The TLS implementation does not need to ensure that the ClientHello",
            "   is large enough to meet QUIC's requirements for datagrams that carry",
            "   Initial packets; see Section 14.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  QUIC",
            "   implementations use PADDING frames or packet coalescing to ensure",
            "   that datagrams are large enough."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "0b26957a366da714",
            "0b26957a366da714",
            "0b26957a366da714",
            "0b26957a366da714"
          ],
          "title": "ClientHello Size"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4",
          "lines": [
            "   The requirements for authentication depend on the application",
            "   protocol that is in use.  TLS provides server authentication and",
            "   permits the server to request client authentication.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06dac9ba9b4467d3",
                  "736d0ae1db312afa"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "A client MUST authenticate the identity of the server."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This"
              }
            ],
            "   typically involves verification that the identity of the server is",
            "   included in a certificate and that the certificate is issued by a",
            "   trusted entity (see for example [RFC2818]).",
            "",
            "      |  Note: Where servers provide certificates for authentication,",
            "      |  the size of the certificate chain can consume a large number of",
            "      |  bytes.  Controlling the size of certificate chains is critical",
            "      |  to performance in QUIC as servers are limited to sending 3",
            "      |  bytes for every byte received prior to validating the client",
            "      |  address; see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  The size of a",
            "      |  certificate chain can be managed by limiting the number of",
            "      |  names or extensions; using keys with small public key",
            "      |  representations, like ECDSA; or by using certificate",
            "      |  compression [COMPRESS].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10911a7e2758f207",
                  "60f61abdc28ce953"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "A server MAY request that the client authenticate during the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10911a7e2758f207",
                  "60f61abdc28ce953"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "handshake."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10911a7e2758f207"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10911a7e2758f207",
                  "583726e720646243"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "A server MAY refuse a connection if the client is unable"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10911a7e2758f207",
                  "583726e720646243"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "to authenticate when requested."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The requirements for client"
              }
            ],
            "   authentication vary based on application protocol and deployment.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "5e6d99e00cf3be38"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "A server MUST NOT use post-handshake client authentication (as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "5e6d99e00cf3be38"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "defined in Section 4.6.2 of [TLS13]) because the multiplexing offered"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "5e6d99e00cf3be38"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "by QUIC prevents clients from correlating the certificate request"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "5e6d99e00cf3be38"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "with the application-level event that triggered it (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "5e6d99e00cf3be38"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "[HTTP2-TLS13])."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
                  "7331307381553d6f"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "More specifically, servers MUST NOT send post-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
                  "7331307381553d6f"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "handshake TLS CertificateRequest messages, and clients MUST treat"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
                  "7331307381553d6f"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "receipt of such messages as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e8e9da03f1da4f26",
                  "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
                  "7331307381553d6f"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "PROTOCOL_VIOLATION."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "736d0ae1db312afa",
            "60f61abdc28ce953",
            "60f61abdc28ce953",
            "583726e720646243",
            "583726e720646243",
            "5e6d99e00cf3be38",
            "5e6d99e00cf3be38",
            "5e6d99e00cf3be38",
            "5e6d99e00cf3be38",
            "5e6d99e00cf3be38",
            "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
            "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
            "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
            "30a6d9459a0cbdbd",
            "7331307381553d6f",
            "7331307381553d6f",
            "7331307381553d6f",
            "7331307381553d6f"
          ],
          "title": "Peer Authentication"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.5",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC can use the session resumption feature of TLS 1.3.  It does this",
            "   by carrying NewSessionTicket messages in CRYPTO frames after the",
            "   handshake is complete.  Session resumption can be used to provide",
            "   0-RTT and can also be used when 0-RTT is disabled.",
            "",
            "   Endpoints that use session resumption might need to remember some",
            "   information about the current connection when creating a resumed",
            "   connection.  TLS requires that some information be retained; see",
            "   Section 4.6.1 of [TLS13].  QUIC itself does not depend on any state",
            "   being retained when resuming a connection unless 0-RTT is also used;",
            "   see Section 7.4.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT] and Section 4.6.1.  Application",
            "   protocols could depend on state that is retained between resumed",
            "   connections.",
            "",
            "   Clients can store any state required for resumption along with the",
            "   session ticket.  Servers can use the session ticket to help carry",
            "   state.",
            "",
            "   Session resumption allows servers to link activity on the original",
            "   connection with the resumed connection, which might be a privacy",
            "   issue for clients.  Clients can choose not to enable resumption to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   avoid creating this correlation.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd659fe2b23d5ab8",
                  "6d8c284b4bfaa356"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Clients SHOULD NOT reuse tickets as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd659fe2b23d5ab8",
                  "6d8c284b4bfaa356"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "that allows entities other than the server to correlate connections;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd659fe2b23d5ab8",
                  "6d8c284b4bfaa356"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "see Appendix C.4 of [TLS13]."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6d8c284b4bfaa356",
            "6d8c284b4bfaa356",
            "6d8c284b4bfaa356"
          ],
          "title": "Session Resumption"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6",
          "lines": [
            "   The 0-RTT feature in QUIC allows a client to send application data",
            "   before the handshake is complete.  This is made possible by reusing",
            "   negotiated parameters from a previous connection.  To enable this,",
            "   0-RTT depends on the client remembering critical parameters and",
            "   providing the server with a TLS session ticket that allows the server",
            "   to recover the same information.",
            "",
            "   This information includes parameters that determine TLS state, as",
            "   governed by [TLS13], QUIC transport parameters, the chosen",
            "   application protocol, and any information the application protocol",
            "   might need; see Section 4.6.3.  This information determines how 0-RTT",
            "   packets and their contents are formed.",
            "",
            "   To ensure that the same information is available to both endpoints,",
            "   all information used to establish 0-RTT comes from the same",
            "   connection.  Endpoints cannot selectively disregard information that",
            "   might alter the sending or processing of 0-RTT.",
            "",
            "   [TLS13] sets a limit of seven days on the time between the original",
            "   connection and any attempt to use 0-RTT.  There are other constraints",
            "   on 0-RTT usage, notably those caused by the potential exposure to",
            "   replay attack; see Section 9.2."
          ],
          "title": "0-RTT"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The TLS early_data extension in the NewSessionTicket message is",
            "   defined to convey (in the max_early_data_size parameter) the amount",
            "   of TLS 0-RTT data the server is willing to accept.  QUIC does not use",
            "   TLS early data.  QUIC uses 0-RTT packets to carry early data.",
            "   Accordingly, the max_early_data_size parameter is repurposed to hold",
            "   a sentinel value 0xffffffff to indicate that the server is willing to",
            "   accept QUIC 0-RTT data.  To indicate that the server does not accept",
            "   0-RTT data, the early_data extension is omitted from the",
            "   NewSessionTicket.  The amount of data that the client can send in",
            "   QUIC 0-RTT is controlled by the initial_max_data transport parameter",
            "   supplied by the server.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e78f71c7fa7ac313",
                  "8e34ffaa41163500"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Servers MUST NOT send the early_data extension with a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e78f71c7fa7ac313",
                  "8e34ffaa41163500"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "max_early_data_size field set to any value other than 0xffffffff."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "A"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bcd2ce0383a4f57c",
                  "4eb8ad70446164db"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "client MUST treat receipt of a NewSessionTicket that contains an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bcd2ce0383a4f57c",
                  "4eb8ad70446164db"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "early_data extension with any other value as a connection error of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bcd2ce0383a4f57c",
                  "4eb8ad70446164db"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A client that wishes to send 0-RTT packets uses the early_data",
            "   extension in the ClientHello message of a subsequent handshake; see",
            "   Section 4.2.10 of [TLS13].  It then sends application data in 0-RTT",
            "   packets.",
            "",
            "   A client that attempts 0-RTT might also provide an address validation",
            "   token if the server has sent a NEW_TOKEN frame; see Section 8.1 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "8e34ffaa41163500",
            "8e34ffaa41163500",
            "4eb8ad70446164db",
            "4eb8ad70446164db",
            "4eb8ad70446164db",
            "4eb8ad70446164db"
          ],
          "title": "Enabling 0-RTT"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6.2",
          "lines": [
            "   A server accepts 0-RTT by sending an early_data extension in the",
            "   EncryptedExtensions; see Section 4.2.10 of [TLS13].  The server then",
            "   processes and acknowledges the 0-RTT packets that it receives.",
            "",
            "   A server rejects 0-RTT by sending the EncryptedExtensions without an",
            "   early_data extension.  A server will always reject 0-RTT if it sends",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   a TLS HelloRetryRequest.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a691f2136953be6",
                  "fb566a2bc8f6302c"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "When rejecting 0-RTT, a server MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a691f2136953be6",
                  "fb566a2bc8f6302c"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "process any 0-RTT packets, even if it could."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "819f38a82b2d22a6",
                  "1f447322cb298a76"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "When 0-RTT was"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "819f38a82b2d22a6",
                  "1f447322cb298a76"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "rejected, a client SHOULD treat receipt of an acknowledgment for a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "819f38a82b2d22a6",
                  "1f447322cb298a76"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "0-RTT packet as a connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION, if it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "819f38a82b2d22a6",
                  "1f447322cb298a76"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "is able to detect the condition."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   When 0-RTT is rejected, all connection characteristics that the",
            "   client assumed might be incorrect.  This includes the choice of",
            "   application protocol, transport parameters, and any application",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   configuration.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3590e715ce241d7f",
                  "714474469180745e"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "The client therefore MUST reset the state of all"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3590e715ce241d7f",
                  "714474469180745e"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "streams, including application state bound to those streams."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2834113e31baf7c1",
                  "20ce51973fbdc645"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "A client MAY reattempt 0-RTT if it receives a Retry or Version"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2834113e31baf7c1",
                  "20ce51973fbdc645"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Negotiation packet."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  These packets do not signify rejection of 0-RTT."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "fb566a2bc8f6302c",
            "fb566a2bc8f6302c",
            "1f447322cb298a76",
            "1f447322cb298a76",
            "1f447322cb298a76",
            "1f447322cb298a76",
            "714474469180745e",
            "714474469180745e",
            "20ce51973fbdc645",
            "20ce51973fbdc645"
          ],
          "title": "Accepting and Rejecting 0-RTT"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6.3",
          "lines": [
            "   When a server receives a ClientHello with the early_data extension,",
            "   it has to decide whether to accept or reject 0-RTT data from the",
            "   client.  Some of this decision is made by the TLS stack (e.g.,",
            "   checking that the cipher suite being resumed was included in the",
            "   ClientHello; see Section 4.2.10 of [TLS13]).  Even when the TLS stack",
            "   has no reason to reject 0-RTT data, the QUIC stack or the application",
            "   protocol using QUIC might reject 0-RTT data because the configuration",
            "   of the transport or application associated with the resumed session",
            "   is not compatible with the server's current configuration.",
            "",
            "   QUIC requires additional transport state to be associated with a",
            "   0-RTT session ticket.  One common way to implement this is using",
            "   stateless session tickets and storing this state in the session",
            "   ticket.  Application protocols that use QUIC might have similar",
            "   requirements regarding associating or storing state.  This associated",
            "   state is used for deciding whether 0-RTT data must be rejected.  For",
            "   example, HTTP/3 settings [QUIC-HTTP] determine how 0-RTT data from",
            "   the client is interpreted.  Other applications using QUIC could have",
            "   different requirements for determining whether to accept or reject",
            "   0-RTT data."
          ],
          "title": "Validating 0-RTT Configuration"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.7",
          "lines": [
            "   The HelloRetryRequest message (see Section 4.1.4 of [TLS13]) can be",
            "   used to request that a client provide new information, such as a key",
            "   share, or to validate some characteristic of the client.  From the",
            "   perspective of QUIC, HelloRetryRequest is not differentiated from",
            "   other cryptographic handshake messages that are carried in Initial",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   packets.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e0e815522bde54a",
                  "512e9116bca109fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Although it is in principle possible to use this feature"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e0e815522bde54a",
                  "512e9116bca109fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "for address verification, QUIC implementations SHOULD instead use the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e0e815522bde54a",
                  "512e9116bca109fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Retry feature; see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "512e9116bca109fa",
            "512e9116bca109fa",
            "512e9116bca109fa"
          ],
          "title": "HelloRetryRequest"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.8",
          "lines": [
            "   If TLS experiences an error, it generates an appropriate alert as",
            "   defined in Section 6 of [TLS13].",
            "",
            "   A TLS alert is converted into a QUIC connection error.  The",
            "   AlertDescription value is added to 0x0100 to produce a QUIC error",
            "   code from the range reserved for CRYPTO_ERROR; see Section 20.1 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  The resulting value is sent in a QUIC",
            "   CONNECTION_CLOSE frame of type 0x1c.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89c1cc13c79a503"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "QUIC is only able to convey an alert level of \"fatal\".  In TLS 1.3,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89c1cc13c79a503"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the only existing uses for the \"warning\" level are to signal"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89c1cc13c79a503"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "connection close; see Section 6.1 of [TLS13].  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89c1cc13c79a503",
                  "6abd3fb11212117b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "As QUIC provides"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89c1cc13c79a503",
                  "6abd3fb11212117b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "alternative mechanisms for connection termination and the TLS"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89c1cc13c79a503",
                  "6abd3fb11212117b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "connection is only closed if an error is encountered, a QUIC endpoint"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d89c1cc13c79a503",
                  "6abd3fb11212117b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST treat any alert from TLS as if it were at the \"fatal\" level."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1d46b552cdd1fae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "QUIC permits the use of a generic code in place of a specific error"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1d46b552cdd1fae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "code; see Section 11 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  For TLS alerts, this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1d46b552cdd1fae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "includes replacing any alert with a generic alert, such as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1d46b552cdd1fae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "handshake_failure (0x0128 in QUIC).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1d46b552cdd1fae",
                  "168ba8c6f079d159"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "Endpoints MAY use a generic"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1d46b552cdd1fae",
                  "168ba8c6f079d159"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "error code to avoid possibly exposing confidential information."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6abd3fb11212117b",
            "6abd3fb11212117b",
            "6abd3fb11212117b",
            "6abd3fb11212117b",
            "168ba8c6f079d159",
            "168ba8c6f079d159"
          ],
          "title": "TLS Errors"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.9",
          "lines": [
            "   After QUIC has completed a move to a new encryption level, packet",
            "   protection keys for previous encryption levels can be discarded.",
            "   This occurs several times during the handshake, as well as when keys",
            "   are updated; see Section 6.",
            "",
            "   Packet protection keys are not discarded immediately when new keys",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   are available.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9634b11acf975237",
                  "c4c46c02cc63bd35",
                  "17c261c7811f3ad9"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If packets from a lower encryption level contain"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9634b11acf975237",
                  "c4c46c02cc63bd35",
                  "17c261c7811f3ad9"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "CRYPTO frames, frames that retransmit that data MUST be sent at the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9634b11acf975237",
                  "c4c46c02cc63bd35",
                  "17c261c7811f3ad9"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "same encryption level."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Similarly, an endpoint generates"
              }
            ],
            "   acknowledgments for packets at the same encryption level as the",
            "   packet being acknowledged.  Thus, it is possible that keys for a",
            "   lower encryption level are needed for a short time after keys for a",
            "   newer encryption level are available.",
            "",
            "   An endpoint cannot discard keys for a given encryption level unless",
            "   it has received all the cryptographic handshake messages from its",
            "   peer at that encryption level and its peer has done the same.",
            "   Different methods for determining this are provided for Initial keys",
            "   (Section 4.9.1) and Handshake keys (Section 4.9.2).  These methods do",
            "   not prevent packets from being received or sent at that encryption",
            "   level because a peer might not have received all the acknowledgments",
            "   necessary.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fbb16ce258921092",
                  "f1fb2b0613ada526"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Though an endpoint might retain older keys, new data MUST be sent at"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fbb16ce258921092",
                  "f1fb2b0613ada526"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the highest currently available encryption level."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Only ACK frames"
              }
            ],
            "   and retransmissions of data in CRYPTO frames are sent at a previous",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   encryption level.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b3f8278c55d0240",
                  "a5ecd973b6a49fff"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "These packets MAY also include PADDING frames."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "17c261c7811f3ad9",
            "17c261c7811f3ad9",
            "17c261c7811f3ad9",
            "f1fb2b0613ada526",
            "f1fb2b0613ada526",
            "a5ecd973b6a49fff"
          ],
          "title": "Discarding Unused Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.9.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Packets protected with Initial secrets (Section 5.2) are not",
            "   authenticated, meaning that an attacker could spoof packets with the",
            "   intent to disrupt a connection.  To limit these attacks, Initial",
            "   packet protection keys are discarded more aggressively than other",
            "   keys.",
            "",
            "   The successful use of Handshake packets indicates that no more",
            "   Initial packets need to be exchanged, as these keys can only be",
            "   produced after receiving all CRYPTO frames from Initial packets.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "08c13935a12086c0",
                  "41d208e3a6ed32b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "Thus, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b80423a10d3d896",
                  "08c13935a12086c0",
                  "41d208e3a6ed32b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "a client MUST discard Initial keys when it first sends a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7b80423a10d3d896",
                  "08c13935a12086c0",
                  "41d208e3a6ed32b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Handshake packet"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "08c13935a12086c0",
                  "41d208e3a6ed32b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c038cebdbdc01b4c",
                  "08c13935a12086c0",
                  "41d208e3a6ed32b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "a server MUST discard Initial keys when it first"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c038cebdbdc01b4c",
                  "08c13935a12086c0",
                  "41d208e3a6ed32b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "successfully processes a Handshake packet."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ace332f699397066",
                  "4cdcbeff17bf0b5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT send"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ace332f699397066",
                  "4cdcbeff17bf0b5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Initial packets after this point."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   This results in abandoning loss recovery state for the Initial",
            "   encryption level and ignoring any outstanding Initial packets."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "08c13935a12086c0",
            "08c13935a12086c0",
            "08c13935a12086c0",
            "41d208e3a6ed32b5",
            "41d208e3a6ed32b5",
            "41d208e3a6ed32b5",
            "4cdcbeff17bf0b5d",
            "4cdcbeff17bf0b5d"
          ],
          "title": "Discarding Initial Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.9.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d4159722090e13a",
                  "8f9fccd266b916c5",
                  "c15c15459c143973"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST discard its Handshake keys when the TLS handshake is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d4159722090e13a",
                  "8f9fccd266b916c5",
                  "c15c15459c143973"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "confirmed (Section 4.1.2)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c15c15459c143973",
            "c15c15459c143973"
          ],
          "title": "Discarding Handshake Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.9.3",
          "lines": [
            "   0-RTT and 1-RTT packets share the same packet number space, and",
            "   clients do not send 0-RTT packets after sending a 1-RTT packet",
            "   (Section 5.6).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b5dee0b238d917b7",
                  "1f873c82be82355f"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "Therefore, a client SHOULD discard 0-RTT keys as soon as it installs"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b5dee0b238d917b7",
                  "1f873c82be82355f"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "1-RTT keys as they have no use after that moment."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d3eadc03f7eb43c",
                  "ffe98a460c92108f"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Additionally, a server MAY discard 0-RTT keys as soon as it receives"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d3eadc03f7eb43c",
                  "ffe98a460c92108f"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "a 1-RTT packet."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  However, due to packet reordering, a 0-RTT packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   could arrive after a 1-RTT packet.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee028385c043ed75",
                  "46c4022250f4bfb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Servers MAY temporarily retain"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee028385c043ed75",
                  "46c4022250f4bfb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "0-RTT keys to allow decrypting reordered packets without requiring"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee028385c043ed75",
                  "46c4022250f4bfb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "their contents to be retransmitted with 1-RTT keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9e7da17b3f3a6d1",
                  "789c84b6cda0d53f"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "After receiving"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9e7da17b3f3a6d1",
                  "789c84b6cda0d53f"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "a 1-RTT packet, servers MUST discard 0-RTT keys within a short time;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9e7da17b3f3a6d1",
                  "789c84b6cda0d53f"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "the RECOMMENDED time period is three times the Probe Timeout (PTO,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9e7da17b3f3a6d1",
                  "789c84b6cda0d53f"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "see [QUIC-RECOVERY])."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9eb2267a4cf4cc1e",
                  "05d25b3d18397669"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "A server MAY discard 0-RTT keys earlier if it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9eb2267a4cf4cc1e",
                  "05d25b3d18397669"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "determines that it has received all 0-RTT packets, which can be done"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9eb2267a4cf4cc1e",
                  "05d25b3d18397669"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "by keeping track of missing packet numbers."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1f873c82be82355f",
            "1f873c82be82355f",
            "ffe98a460c92108f",
            "ffe98a460c92108f",
            "46c4022250f4bfb0",
            "46c4022250f4bfb0",
            "46c4022250f4bfb0",
            "789c84b6cda0d53f",
            "789c84b6cda0d53f",
            "789c84b6cda0d53f",
            "789c84b6cda0d53f",
            "05d25b3d18397669",
            "05d25b3d18397669",
            "05d25b3d18397669"
          ],
          "title": "Discarding 0-RTT Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   As with TLS over TCP, QUIC protects packets with keys derived from",
            "   the TLS handshake, using the AEAD algorithm [AEAD] negotiated by TLS.",
            "",
            "   QUIC packets have varying protections depending on their type:",
            "",
            "   *  Version Negotiation packets have no cryptographic protection.",
            "",
            "   *  Retry packets use AEAD_AES_128_GCM to provide protection against",
            "      accidental modification and to limit the entities that can produce",
            "      a valid Retry; see Section 5.8.",
            "",
            "   *  Initial packets use AEAD_AES_128_GCM with keys derived from the",
            "      Destination Connection ID field of the first Initial packet sent",
            "      by the client; see Section 5.2.",
            "",
            "   *  All other packets have strong cryptographic protections for",
            "      confidentiality and integrity, using keys and algorithms",
            "      negotiated by TLS.",
            "",
            "   This section describes how packet protection is applied to Handshake",
            "   packets, 0-RTT packets, and 1-RTT packets.  The same packet",
            "   protection process is applied to Initial packets.  However, as it is",
            "   trivial to determine the keys used for Initial packets, these packets",
            "   are not considered to have confidentiality or integrity protection.",
            "   Retry packets use a fixed key and so similarly lack confidentiality",
            "   and integrity protection."
          ],
          "title": "Packet Protection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.1",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC derives packet protection keys in the same way that TLS derives",
            "   record protection keys.",
            "",
            "   Each encryption level has separate secret values for protection of",
            "   packets sent in each direction.  These traffic secrets are derived by",
            "   TLS (see Section 7.1 of [TLS13]) and are used by QUIC for all",
            "   encryption levels except the Initial encryption level.  The secrets",
            "   for the Initial encryption level are computed based on the client's",
            "   initial Destination Connection ID, as described in Section 5.2.",
            "",
            "   The keys used for packet protection are computed from the TLS secrets",
            "   using the KDF provided by TLS.  In TLS 1.3, the HKDF-Expand-Label",
            "   function described in Section 7.1 of [TLS13] is used with the hash",
            "   function from the negotiated cipher suite.  All uses of HKDF-Expand-",
            "   Label in QUIC use a zero-length Context.",
            "",
            "   Note that labels, which are described using strings, are encoded as",
            "   bytes using ASCII [ASCII] without quotes or any trailing NUL byte.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e367be82e4c560f",
                  "e408c13ed2a103ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Other versions of TLS MUST provide a similar function in order to be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e367be82e4c560f",
                  "e408c13ed2a103ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "used with QUIC."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa081df36a1edab0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The current encryption level secret and the label \"quic key\" are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa081df36a1edab0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "input to the KDF to produce the AEAD key;"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "89423e93314a6765"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the label \"quic iv\" is used"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "89423e93314a6765"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "to derive the Initialization Vector (IV); see Section 5.3."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "821594ead9fd2c0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "821594ead9fd2c0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "header protection key uses the \"quic hp\" label; see Section 5.4."
              }
            ],
            "   Using these labels provides key separation between QUIC and TLS; see",
            "   Section 9.6.",
            "",
            "   Both \"quic key\" and \"quic hp\" are used to produce keys, so the Length",
            "   provided to HKDF-Expand-Label along with these labels is determined",
            "   by the size of keys in the AEAD or header protection algorithm.  The",
            "   Length provided with \"quic iv\" is the minimum length of the AEAD",
            "   nonce or 8 bytes if that is larger; see [AEAD].",
            "",
            "   The KDF used for initial secrets is always the HKDF-Expand-Label",
            "   function from TLS 1.3; see Section 5.2."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e408c13ed2a103ed",
            "e408c13ed2a103ed"
          ],
          "title": "Packet Protection Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Initial packets apply the packet protection process, but use a secret",
            "   derived from the Destination Connection ID field from the client's",
            "   first Initial packet.",
            "",
            "   This secret is determined by using HKDF-Extract (see Section 2.2 of",
            "   [HKDF]) with a salt of 0x38762cf7f55934b34d179ae6a4c80cadccbb7f0a and",
            "   the input keying material (IKM) of the Destination Connection ID",
            "   field.  This produces an intermediate pseudorandom key (PRK) that is",
            "   used to derive two separate secrets for sending and receiving.",
            "",
            "   The secret used by clients to construct Initial packets uses the PRK",
            "   and the label \"client in\" as input to the HKDF-Expand-Label function",
            "   from TLS [TLS13] to produce a 32-byte secret.  Packets constructed by",
            "   the server use the same process with the label \"server in\".  The hash",
            "   function for HKDF when deriving initial secrets and keys is SHA-256",
            "   [SHA].",
            "",
            "   This process in pseudocode is:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e6f2f2f479d173a4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "initial_salt = 0x38762cf7f55934b34d179ae6a4c80cadccbb7f0a"
              }
            ],
            "   initial_secret = HKDF-Extract(initial_salt,",
            "                                 client_dst_connection_id)",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6d9c8ffd09608d9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "client_initial_secret = HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6d9c8ffd09608d9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"client in\", \"\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6d9c8ffd09608d9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Hash.length)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1fbb882851383f95"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "server_initial_secret = HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1fbb882851383f95"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "\"server in\", \"\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                             "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1fbb882851383f95"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Hash.length)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The connection ID used with HKDF-Expand-Label is the Destination",
            "   Connection ID in the Initial packet sent by the client.  This will be",
            "   a randomly selected value unless the client creates the Initial",
            "   packet after receiving a Retry packet, where the Destination",
            "   Connection ID is selected by the server.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "684ca41db0d4b592",
                  "77f809cab45640c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Future versions of QUIC SHOULD generate a new salt value, thus"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "684ca41db0d4b592",
                  "77f809cab45640c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "ensuring that the keys are different for each version of QUIC."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This"
              }
            ],
            "   prevents a middlebox that recognizes only one version of QUIC from",
            "   seeing or modifying the contents of packets from future versions.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65a4e70ffeb030f8",
                  "9e77c0b9b84b3ebb"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "The HKDF-Expand-Label function defined in TLS 1.3 MUST be used for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65a4e70ffeb030f8",
                  "9e77c0b9b84b3ebb"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Initial packets even where the TLS versions offered do not include"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65a4e70ffeb030f8",
                  "9e77c0b9b84b3ebb"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "TLS 1.3."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The secrets used for constructing subsequent Initial packets change",
            "   when a server sends a Retry packet to use the connection ID value",
            "   selected by the server.  The secrets do not change when a client",
            "   changes the Destination Connection ID it uses in response to an",
            "   Initial packet from the server.",
            "",
            "      |  Note: The Destination Connection ID field could be any length",
            "      |  up to 20 bytes, including zero length if the server sends a",
            "      |  Retry packet with a zero-length Source Connection ID field.",
            "      |  After a Retry, the Initial keys provide the client no assurance",
            "      |  that the server received its packet, so the client has to rely",
            "      |  on the exchange that included the Retry packet to validate the",
            "      |  server address; see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   Appendix A contains sample Initial packets."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "77f809cab45640c5",
            "77f809cab45640c5",
            "9e77c0b9b84b3ebb",
            "9e77c0b9b84b3ebb",
            "9e77c0b9b84b3ebb"
          ],
          "title": "Initial Secrets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data (AEAD) function",
            "   (see [AEAD]) used for QUIC packet protection is the AEAD that is",
            "   negotiated for use with the TLS connection.  For example, if TLS is",
            "   using the TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 cipher suite, the AEAD_AES_128_GCM",
            "   function is used.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66f34cb3bdfb337e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "QUIC can use any of the cipher suites defined in [TLS13] with the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66f34cb3bdfb337e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "exception of TLS_AES_128_CCM_8_SHA256."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dff6c3b4472db05",
                  "54fd7c99b12900da"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "A cipher suite MUST NOT be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dff6c3b4472db05",
                  "54fd7c99b12900da"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "negotiated unless a header protection scheme is defined for the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dff6c3b4472db05",
                  "54fd7c99b12900da"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "cipher suite."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This document defines a header protection scheme for"
              }
            ],
            "   all cipher suites defined in [TLS13] aside from",
            "   TLS_AES_128_CCM_8_SHA256.  These cipher suites have a 16-byte",
            "   authentication tag and produce an output 16 bytes larger than their",
            "   input.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72b4bdd84640af61",
                  "82c52e4a7e587882"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST NOT reject a ClientHello that offers a cipher suite"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72b4bdd84640af61",
                  "82c52e4a7e587882"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "that it does not support, or it would be impossible to deploy a new"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "72b4bdd84640af61",
                  "82c52e4a7e587882"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "cipher suite."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This also applies to TLS_AES_128_CCM_8_SHA256."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   When constructing packets, the AEAD function is applied prior to",
            "   applying header protection; see Section 5.4.  The unprotected packet",
            "   header is part of the associated data (A).  When processing packets,",
            "   an endpoint first removes the header protection.",
            "",
            "   The key and IV for the packet are computed as described in",
            "   Section 5.1.  The nonce, N, is formed by combining the packet",
            "   protection IV with the packet number.  The 62 bits of the",
            "   reconstructed QUIC packet number in network byte order are left-",
            "   padded with zeros to the size of the IV.  The exclusive OR of the",
            "   padded packet number and the IV forms the AEAD nonce.",
            "",
            "   The associated data, A, for the AEAD is the contents of the QUIC",
            "   header, starting from the first byte of either the short or long",
            "   header, up to and including the unprotected packet number.",
            "",
            "   The input plaintext, P, for the AEAD is the payload of the QUIC",
            "   packet, as described in [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   The output ciphertext, C, of the AEAD is transmitted in place of P.",
            "",
            "   Some AEAD functions have limits for how many packets can be encrypted",
            "   under the same key and IV; see Section 6.6.  This might be lower than",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   the packet number limit.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a4f413588cda8ee",
                  "1fd7a4b503ba35ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST initiate a key update"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a4f413588cda8ee",
                  "1fd7a4b503ba35ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "(Section 6) prior to exceeding any limit set for the AEAD that is in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a4f413588cda8ee",
                  "1fd7a4b503ba35ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "use."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "54fd7c99b12900da",
            "54fd7c99b12900da",
            "54fd7c99b12900da",
            "82c52e4a7e587882",
            "82c52e4a7e587882",
            "82c52e4a7e587882",
            "1fd7a4b503ba35ad",
            "1fd7a4b503ba35ad",
            "1fd7a4b503ba35ad"
          ],
          "title": "AEAD Usage"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.4",
          "lines": [
            "   Parts of QUIC packet headers, in particular the Packet Number field,",
            "   are protected using a key that is derived separately from the packet",
            "   protection key and IV.  The key derived using the \"quic hp\" label is",
            "   used to provide confidentiality protection for those fields that are",
            "   not exposed to on-path elements.",
            "",
            "   This protection applies to the least significant bits of the first",
            "   byte, plus the Packet Number field.  The four least significant bits",
            "   of the first byte are protected for packets with long headers; the",
            "   five least significant bits of the first byte are protected for",
            "   packets with short headers.  For both header forms, this covers the",
            "   reserved bits and the Packet Number Length field; the Key Phase bit",
            "   is also protected for packets with a short header.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb8b47056d5f406b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The same header protection key is used for the duration of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb8b47056d5f406b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "connection, with the value not changing after a key update (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb8b47056d5f406b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 6).  This allows header protection to be used to protect the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb8b47056d5f406b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "key phase."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   This process does not apply to Retry or Version Negotiation packets,",
            "   which do not contain a protected payload or any of the fields that",
            "   are protected by this process."
          ],
          "title": "Header Protection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Header protection is applied after packet protection is applied (see",
            "   Section 5.3).  The ciphertext of the packet is sampled and used as",
            "   input to an encryption algorithm.  The algorithm used depends on the",
            "   negotiated AEAD.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2f46bde2122e74f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The output of this algorithm is a 5-byte mask that is applied to the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2f46bde2122e74f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "protected header fields using exclusive OR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The least significant"
              }
            ],
            "   bits of the first byte of the packet are masked by the least",
            "   significant bits of the first mask byte, and the packet number is",
            "   masked with the remaining bytes.  Any unused bytes of mask that might",
            "   result from a shorter packet number encoding are unused.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Figure 6 shows a sample algorithm for applying header protection."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Removing header protection only differs in the order in which the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet number length (pn_length) is determined (here \"^\" is used to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "represent exclusive OR)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "mask = header_protection(hp_key, sample)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "pn_length = (packet[0] & 0x03) + 1"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "if (packet[0] & 0x80) == 0x80:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "# Long header: 4 bits masked"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet[0] ^= mask[0] & 0x0f"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "else:"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "# Short header: 5 bits masked"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet[0] ^= mask[0] & 0x1f"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "# pn_offset is the start of the Packet Number field."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7693a35e027d1e45"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet[pn_offset:pn_offset+pn_length] ^= mask[1:1+pn_length]"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "                   Figure 6: Header Protection Pseudocode",
            "",
            "   Specific header protection functions are defined based on the",
            "   selected cipher suite; see Section 5.4.3 and Section 5.4.4.",
            "",
            "   Figure 7 shows an example long header packet (Initial) and a short",
            "   header packet (1-RTT).  Figure 7 shows the fields in each header that",
            "   are covered by header protection and the portion of the protected",
            "   packet payload that is sampled.",
            "",
            "   Initial Packet {",
            "     Header Form (1) = 1,",
            "     Fixed Bit (1) = 1,",
            "     Long Packet Type (2) = 0,",
            "     Reserved Bits (2),         # Protected",
            "     Packet Number Length (2),  # Protected",
            "     Version (32),",
            "     DCID Len (8),",
            "     Destination Connection ID (0..160),",
            "     SCID Len (8),",
            "     Source Connection ID (0..160),",
            "     Token Length (i),",
            "     Token (..),",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Packet Number (8..32),     # Protected",
            "     Protected Payload (0..24), # Skipped Part",
            "     Protected Payload (128),   # Sampled Part",
            "     Protected Payload (..)     # Remainder",
            "   }",
            "",
            "   1-RTT Packet {",
            "     Header Form (1) = 0,",
            "     Fixed Bit (1) = 1,",
            "     Spin Bit (1),",
            "     Reserved Bits (2),         # Protected",
            "     Key Phase (1),             # Protected",
            "     Packet Number Length (2),  # Protected",
            "     Destination Connection ID (0..160),",
            "     Packet Number (8..32),     # Protected",
            "     Protected Payload (0..24), # Skipped Part",
            "     Protected Payload (128),   # Sampled Part",
            "     Protected Payload (..),    # Remainder",
            "   }",
            "",
            "             Figure 7: Header Protection and Ciphertext Sample",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec03f4619272e58d",
                  "471701866ffdb361"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Before a TLS cipher suite can be used with QUIC, a header protection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ec03f4619272e58d",
                  "471701866ffdb361"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "algorithm MUST be specified for the AEAD used with that cipher suite."
              }
            ],
            "   This document defines algorithms for AEAD_AES_128_GCM,",
            "   AEAD_AES_128_CCM, AEAD_AES_256_GCM (all these AES AEADs are defined",
            "   in [AEAD]), and AEAD_CHACHA20_POLY1305 (defined in [CHACHA]).  Prior",
            "   to TLS selecting a cipher suite, AES header protection is used",
            "   (Section 5.4.3), matching the AEAD_AES_128_GCM packet protection."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "471701866ffdb361",
            "471701866ffdb361"
          ],
          "title": "Header Protection Application"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The header protection algorithm uses both the header protection key",
            "   and a sample of the ciphertext from the packet Payload field.",
            "",
            "   The same number of bytes are always sampled, but an allowance needs",
            "   to be made for the removal of protection by a receiving endpoint,",
            "   which will not know the length of the Packet Number field.  The",
            "   sample of ciphertext is taken starting from an offset of 4 bytes",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   after the start of the Packet Number field.  That is, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95928c9fe45ad76e",
                  "514e4f6ef5fcbc34"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "in sampling"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95928c9fe45ad76e",
                  "514e4f6ef5fcbc34"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet ciphertext for header protection, the Packet Number field is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95928c9fe45ad76e",
                  "514e4f6ef5fcbc34"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "assumed to be 4 bytes long"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " (its maximum possible encoded length)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10579a4f30f5cfec",
                  "398241f624ccfe6d"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST discard packets that are not long enough to contain"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10579a4f30f5cfec",
                  "398241f624ccfe6d"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "a complete sample."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   To ensure that sufficient data is available for sampling, packets are",
            "   padded so that the combined lengths of the encoded packet number and",
            "   protected payload is at least 4 bytes longer than the sample required",
            "   for header protection.  The cipher suites defined in [TLS13] -- other",
            "   than TLS_AES_128_CCM_8_SHA256, for which a header protection scheme",
            "   is not defined in this document -- have 16-byte expansions and",
            "   16-byte header protection samples.  This results in needing at least",
            "   3 bytes of frames in the unprotected payload if the packet number is",
            "   encoded on a single byte, or 2 bytes of frames for a 2-byte packet",
            "   number encoding.",
            "",
            "   The sampled ciphertext can be determined by the following pseudocode:",
            "",
            "   # pn_offset is the start of the Packet Number field.",
            "   sample_offset = pn_offset + 4",
            "",
            "   sample = packet[sample_offset..sample_offset+sample_length]",
            "",
            "   Where the packet number offset of a short header packet can be",
            "   calculated as:",
            "",
            "   pn_offset = 1 + len(connection_id)",
            "",
            "   And the packet number offset of a long header packet can be",
            "   calculated as:",
            "",
            "   pn_offset = 7 + len(destination_connection_id) +",
            "                   len(source_connection_id) +",
            "                   len(payload_length)",
            "   if packet_type == Initial:",
            "       pn_offset += len(token_length) +",
            "                    len(token)",
            "",
            "   For example, for a packet with a short header, an 8-byte connection",
            "   ID, and protected with AEAD_AES_128_GCM, the sample takes bytes 13 to",
            "   28 inclusive (using zero-based indexing).",
            "",
            "   Multiple QUIC packets might be included in the same UDP datagram.",
            "   Each packet is handled separately."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "398241f624ccfe6d",
            "398241f624ccfe6d"
          ],
          "title": "Header Protection Sample"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.4.3",
          "lines": [
            "   This section defines the packet protection algorithm for",
            "   AEAD_AES_128_GCM, AEAD_AES_128_CCM, and AEAD_AES_256_GCM.",
            "   AEAD_AES_128_GCM and AEAD_AES_128_CCM use 128-bit AES in Electronic",
            "   Codebook (ECB) mode.  AEAD_AES_256_GCM uses 256-bit AES in ECB mode.",
            "   AES is defined in [AES].",
            "",
            "   This algorithm samples 16 bytes from the packet ciphertext.  This",
            "   value is used as the input to AES-ECB.  In pseudocode, the header",
            "   protection function is defined as:",
            "",
            "   header_protection(hp_key, sample):",
            "     mask = AES-ECB(hp_key, sample)"
          ],
          "title": "AES-Based Header Protection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.4.4",
          "lines": [
            "   When AEAD_CHACHA20_POLY1305 is in use, header protection uses the raw",
            "   ChaCha20 function as defined in Section 2.4 of [CHACHA].  This uses a",
            "   256-bit key and 16 bytes sampled from the packet protection output.",
            "",
            "   The first 4 bytes of the sampled ciphertext are the block counter.  A",
            "   ChaCha20 implementation could take a 32-bit integer in place of a",
            "   byte sequence, in which case, the byte sequence is interpreted as a",
            "   little-endian value.",
            "",
            "   The remaining 12 bytes are used as the nonce.  A ChaCha20",
            "   implementation might take an array of three 32-bit integers in place",
            "   of a byte sequence, in which case, the nonce bytes are interpreted as",
            "   a sequence of 32-bit little-endian integers.",
            "",
            "   The encryption mask is produced by invoking ChaCha20 to protect 5",
            "   zero bytes.  In pseudocode, the header protection function is defined",
            "   as:",
            "",
            "   header_protection(hp_key, sample):",
            "     counter = sample[0..3]",
            "     nonce = sample[4..15]",
            "     mask = ChaCha20(hp_key, counter, nonce, {0,0,0,0,0})"
          ],
          "title": "ChaCha20-Based Header Protection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.5",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c7f19ee578eb2e0",
                  "099fbeb3d5e5e361"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Once an endpoint successfully receives a packet with a given packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c7f19ee578eb2e0",
                  "099fbeb3d5e5e361"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "number, it MUST discard all packets in the same packet number space"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c7f19ee578eb2e0",
                  "099fbeb3d5e5e361"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "with higher packet numbers if they cannot be successfully unprotected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c7f19ee578eb2e0",
                  "099fbeb3d5e5e361"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "with either the same key, or -- if there is a key update -- a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c7f19ee578eb2e0",
                  "099fbeb3d5e5e361"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "subsequent packet protection key; see Section 6."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1139ca1a70c9d9c",
                  "2f1142e99acbb2f4"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Similarly, a packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1139ca1a70c9d9c",
                  "2f1142e99acbb2f4"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "that appears to trigger a key update but cannot be unprotected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a1139ca1a70c9d9c",
                  "2f1142e99acbb2f4"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "successfully MUST be discarded."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Failure to unprotect a packet does not necessarily indicate the",
            "   existence of a protocol error in a peer or an attack.  The truncated",
            "   packet number encoding used in QUIC can cause packet numbers to be",
            "   decoded incorrectly if they are delayed significantly."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "099fbeb3d5e5e361",
            "099fbeb3d5e5e361",
            "099fbeb3d5e5e361",
            "099fbeb3d5e5e361",
            "099fbeb3d5e5e361",
            "2f1142e99acbb2f4",
            "2f1142e99acbb2f4",
            "2f1142e99acbb2f4"
          ],
          "title": "Receiving Protected Packets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.6",
          "lines": [
            "   If 0-RTT keys are available (see Section 4.6.1), the lack of replay",
            "   protection means that restrictions on their use are necessary to",
            "   avoid replay attacks on the protocol.",
            "",
            "   Of the frames defined in [QUIC-TRANSPORT], the STREAM, RESET_STREAM,",
            "   STOP_SENDING, and CONNECTION_CLOSE frames are potentially unsafe for",
            "   use with 0-RTT as they carry application data.  Application data that",
            "   is received in 0-RTT could cause an application at the server to",
            "   process the data multiple times rather than just once.  Additional",
            "   actions taken by a server as a result of processing replayed",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   application data could have unwanted consequences.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f07b33fe5528a1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "A client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f07b33fe5528a1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "therefore MUST NOT use 0-RTT for application data unless specifically"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f07b33fe5528a1e"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "requested by the application that is in use."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "98def066aa0e9cb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "An application protocol that uses QUIC MUST include a profile that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "98def066aa0e9cb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "defines acceptable use of 0-RTT; otherwise, 0-RTT can only be used to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "98def066aa0e9cb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "carry QUIC frames that do not carry application data."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  For example, a"
              }
            ],
            "   profile for HTTP is described in [HTTP-REPLAY] and used for HTTP/3;",
            "   see Section 10.9 of [QUIC-HTTP].",
            "",
            "   Though replaying packets might result in additional connection",
            "   attempts, the effect of processing replayed frames that do not carry",
            "   application data is limited to changing the state of the affected",
            "   connection.  A TLS handshake cannot be successfully completed using",
            "   replayed packets.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff5d76d27a1ba6b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "A client MAY wish to apply additional restrictions on what data it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff5d76d27a1ba6b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "sends prior to the completion of the TLS handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A client otherwise treats 0-RTT keys as equivalent to 1-RTT keys,",
            "   except that it cannot send certain frames with 0-RTT keys; see",
            "   Section 12.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   A client that receives an indication that its 0-RTT data has been",
            "   accepted by a server can send 0-RTT data until it receives all of the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   server's handshake messages.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d667f7c2999d51c"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "A client SHOULD stop sending 0-RTT data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d667f7c2999d51c"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "if it receives an indication that 0-RTT data has been rejected."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf8577a771718715"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "A server MUST NOT use 0-RTT keys to protect packets; it uses 1-RTT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf8577a771718715"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "keys to protect acknowledgments of 0-RTT packets."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21bb3806e971bc47",
                  "062885a1f7e5d933"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "A client MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21bb3806e971bc47",
                  "062885a1f7e5d933"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "attempt to decrypt 0-RTT packets it receives and instead MUST discard"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21bb3806e971bc47",
                  "062885a1f7e5d933"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "them."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a51688a17ecb552"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "Once a client has installed 1-RTT keys, it MUST NOT send any more"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a51688a17ecb552"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "0-RTT packets."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      |  Note: 0-RTT data can be acknowledged by the server as it",
            "      |  receives it, but any packets containing acknowledgments of",
            "      |  0-RTT data cannot have packet protection removed by the client",
            "      |  until the TLS handshake is complete.  The 1-RTT keys necessary",
            "      |  to remove packet protection cannot be derived until the client",
            "      |  receives all server handshake messages."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4f07b33fe5528a1e",
            "4f07b33fe5528a1e",
            "4f07b33fe5528a1e",
            "98def066aa0e9cb1",
            "98def066aa0e9cb1",
            "98def066aa0e9cb1",
            "ff5d76d27a1ba6b0",
            "ff5d76d27a1ba6b0",
            "1d667f7c2999d51c",
            "1d667f7c2999d51c",
            "cf8577a771718715",
            "cf8577a771718715",
            "21bb3806e971bc47",
            "21bb3806e971bc47",
            "21bb3806e971bc47",
            "062885a1f7e5d933",
            "062885a1f7e5d933",
            "062885a1f7e5d933",
            "2a51688a17ecb552",
            "2a51688a17ecb552"
          ],
          "title": "Use of 0-RTT Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.7",
          "lines": [
            "   Due to reordering and loss, protected packets might be received by an",
            "   endpoint before the final TLS handshake messages are received.  A",
            "   client will be unable to decrypt 1-RTT packets from the server,",
            "   whereas a server will be able to decrypt 1-RTT packets from the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   client.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb0e5ebcd57e9903",
                  "1bbeb270688617a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Endpoints in either role MUST NOT decrypt 1-RTT packets from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb0e5ebcd57e9903",
                  "1bbeb270688617a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "their peer prior to completing the handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Even though 1-RTT keys are available to a server after receiving the",
            "   first handshake messages from a client, it is missing assurances on",
            "   the client state:",
            "",
            "   *  The client is not authenticated, unless the server has chosen to",
            "      use a pre-shared key and validated the client's pre-shared key",
            "      binder; see Section 4.2.11 of [TLS13].",
            "",
            "   *  The client has not demonstrated liveness, unless the server has",
            "      validated the client's address with a Retry packet or other means;",
            "      see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   *  Any received 0-RTT data that the server responds to might be due",
            "      to a replay attack.",
            "",
            "   Therefore, the server's use of 1-RTT keys before the handshake is",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   complete is limited to sending data.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9839dfbc3a8995a",
                  "182f07301f7d385b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "A server MUST NOT process"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9839dfbc3a8995a",
                  "182f07301f7d385b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "incoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9839dfbc3a8995a",
                  "182f07301f7d385b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "complete."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Because sending acknowledgments indicates that all frames"
              }
            ],
            "   in a packet have been processed, a server cannot send acknowledgments",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   for 1-RTT packets until the TLS handshake is complete.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48e1933c20cf925a"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "Received"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48e1933c20cf925a"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "packets protected with 1-RTT keys MAY be stored and later decrypted"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48e1933c20cf925a"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "and used once the handshake is complete."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      |  Note: TLS implementations might provide all 1-RTT secrets prior",
            "      |  to handshake completion.  Even where QUIC implementations have",
            "      |  1-RTT read keys, those keys are not to be used prior to",
            "      |  completing the handshake.",
            "",
            "   The requirement for the server to wait for the client Finished",
            "   message creates a dependency on that message being delivered.  A",
            "   client can avoid the potential for head-of-line blocking that this",
            "   implies by sending its 1-RTT packets coalesced with a Handshake",
            "   packet containing a copy of the CRYPTO frame that carries the",
            "   Finished message, until one of the Handshake packets is acknowledged.",
            "   This enables immediate server processing for those packets.",
            "",
            "   A server could receive packets protected with 0-RTT keys prior to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   receiving a TLS ClientHello.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3a8509be94bb311"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "The server MAY retain these packets for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f3a8509be94bb311"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "later decryption in anticipation of receiving a ClientHello."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A client generally receives 1-RTT keys at the same time as the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   handshake completes.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e4a2fe383a627047",
                  "0297a9b292a1e8d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Even if it has 1-RTT secrets, a client MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e4a2fe383a627047",
                  "0297a9b292a1e8d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "process incoming 1-RTT protected packets before the TLS handshake is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e4a2fe383a627047",
                  "0297a9b292a1e8d8"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "complete."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1bbeb270688617a7",
            "1bbeb270688617a7",
            "182f07301f7d385b",
            "182f07301f7d385b",
            "182f07301f7d385b",
            "48e1933c20cf925a",
            "48e1933c20cf925a",
            "48e1933c20cf925a",
            "f3a8509be94bb311",
            "f3a8509be94bb311",
            "0297a9b292a1e8d8",
            "0297a9b292a1e8d8",
            "0297a9b292a1e8d8"
          ],
          "title": "Receiving Out-of-Order Protected Packets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.8",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1daba603d71d486",
                  "664e71049f747416"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Retry packets (see Section 17.2.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) carry a Retry"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1daba603d71d486",
                  "664e71049f747416"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Integrity Tag that provides two properties: it allows the discarding"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1daba603d71d486",
                  "664e71049f747416"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "of packets that have accidentally been corrupted by the network, and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1daba603d71d486",
                  "664e71049f747416"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "only an entity that observes an Initial packet can send a valid Retry"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1daba603d71d486",
                  "664e71049f747416"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "122483d4aff0eb24"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The Retry Integrity Tag is a 128-bit field that is computed as the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "122483d4aff0eb24"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "output of AEAD_AES_128_GCM [AEAD] used with the following inputs:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "122483d4aff0eb24"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  The secret key, K, is 128 bits equal to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "122483d4aff0eb24"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "0xbe0c690b9f66575a1d766b54e368c84e."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5128d3af8add560"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  The nonce, N, is 96 bits equal to 0x461599d35d632bf2239825bb."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   *  The plaintext, P, is empty.",
            "",
            "   *  The associated data, A, is the contents of the Retry Pseudo-",
            "      Packet, as illustrated in Figure 8:",
            "",
            "   The secret key and the nonce are values derived by calling HKDF-",
            "   Expand-Label using",
            "   0xd9c9943e6101fd200021506bcc02814c73030f25c79d71ce876eca876e6fca8e as",
            "   the secret, with labels being \"quic key\" and \"quic iv\" (Section 5.1).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Retry Pseudo-Packet {"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ODCID Length (8),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Original Destination Connection ID (0..160),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Header Form (1) = 1,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Fixed Bit (1) = 1,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Long Packet Type (2) = 3,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Unused (4),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Version (32),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "DCID Len (8),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Destination Connection ID (0..160),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "SCID Len (8),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Source Connection ID (0..160),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56277a119d4727a0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Retry Token (..),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "}"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "                       Figure 8: Retry Pseudo-Packet",
            "",
            "   The Retry Pseudo-Packet is not sent over the wire.  It is computed by",
            "   taking the transmitted Retry packet, removing the Retry Integrity",
            "   Tag, and prepending the two following fields:",
            "",
            "   ODCID Length:  The ODCID Length field contains the length in bytes of",
            "      the Original Destination Connection ID field that follows it,",
            "      encoded as an 8-bit unsigned integer.",
            "",
            "   Original Destination Connection ID:  The Original Destination",
            "      Connection ID contains the value of the Destination Connection ID",
            "      from the Initial packet that this Retry is in response to.  The",
            "      length of this field is given in ODCID Length.  The presence of",
            "      this field ensures that a valid Retry packet can only be sent by",
            "      an entity that observes the Initial packet."
          ],
          "title": "Retry Packet Integrity"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c526bcbf9f49200",
                  "6aae86c09b28a2ec"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Once the handshake is confirmed (see Section 4.1.2), an endpoint MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c526bcbf9f49200",
                  "6aae86c09b28a2ec"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "initiate a key update."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The Key Phase bit indicates which packet protection keys are used to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   protect the packet.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11565c5939538494"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The Key Phase bit is initially set to 0 for the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11565c5939538494"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "first set of 1-RTT packets and toggled to signal each subsequent key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11565c5939538494"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "update."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The Key Phase bit allows a recipient to detect a change in keying",
            "   material without needing to receive the first packet that triggered",
            "   the change.  An endpoint that notices a changed Key Phase bit updates",
            "   keys and decrypts the packet that contains the changed value.",
            "",
            "   Initiating a key update results in both endpoints updating keys.",
            "   This differs from TLS where endpoints can update keys independently.",
            "",
            "   This mechanism replaces the key update mechanism of TLS, which relies",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   on KeyUpdate messages sent using 1-RTT encryption keys.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "265c964a8e1af351",
                  "034f2d2b05a2f036"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Endpoints"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "265c964a8e1af351",
                  "034f2d2b05a2f036"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "MUST NOT send a TLS KeyUpdate message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a6a711495ef4818",
                  "2cb68bcd82b06b0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST treat the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a6a711495ef4818",
                  "2cb68bcd82b06b0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "receipt of a TLS KeyUpdate message as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a6a711495ef4818",
                  "2cb68bcd82b06b0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "0x010a, equivalent to a fatal TLS alert of unexpected_message; see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a6a711495ef4818",
                  "2cb68bcd82b06b0d"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Section 4.8."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Figure 9 shows a key update process, where the initial set of keys",
            "   used (identified with @M) are replaced by updated keys (identified",
            "   with @N).  The value of the Key Phase bit is indicated in brackets",
            "   [].",
            "",
            "      Initiating Peer                    Responding Peer",
            "",
            "   @M [0] QUIC Packets",
            "",
            "   ... Update to @N",
            "   @N [1] QUIC Packets",
            "                         -------->",
            "                                            Update to @N ...",
            "                                         QUIC Packets [1] @N",
            "                         <--------",
            "                                         QUIC Packets [1] @N",
            "                                       containing ACK",
            "                         <--------",
            "   ... Key Update Permitted",
            "",
            "   @N [1] QUIC Packets",
            "            containing ACK for @N packets",
            "                         -------->",
            "                                    Key Update Permitted ...",
            "",
            "                            Figure 9: Key Update"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6aae86c09b28a2ec",
            "6aae86c09b28a2ec",
            "034f2d2b05a2f036",
            "034f2d2b05a2f036",
            "2cb68bcd82b06b0d",
            "2cb68bcd82b06b0d",
            "2cb68bcd82b06b0d",
            "2cb68bcd82b06b0d"
          ],
          "title": "Key Update"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Endpoints maintain separate read and write secrets for packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "protection.  An endpoint initiates a key update by updating its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet protection write secret and using that to protect new packets."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The endpoint creates a new write secret from the existing write"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "secret as performed in Section 7.2 of [TLS13].  This uses the KDF"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "function provided by TLS with a label of \"quic ku\".  The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "corresponding key and IV are created from that secret as defined in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5739e8fc0428f0f2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 5.1.  The header protection key is not updated."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   For example, to update write keys with TLS 1.3, HKDF-Expand-Label is",
            "   used as:",
            "",
            "   secret_<n+1> = HKDF-Expand-Label(secret_<n>, \"quic ku\",",
            "                                    \"\", Hash.length)",
            "",
            "   The endpoint toggles the value of the Key Phase bit and uses the",
            "   updated key and IV to protect all subsequent packets.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d2cfb4c5d3d2a7b",
                  "379db28dea1894f9",
                  "2bea64447cf4e3b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate a key update prior to having confirmed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1d2cfb4c5d3d2a7b",
                  "379db28dea1894f9",
                  "2bea64447cf4e3b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "the handshake (Section 4.1.2)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ca78cbaca5bc27a",
                  "3ad82f1956fef698"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST NOT initiate a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ca78cbaca5bc27a",
                  "3ad82f1956fef698"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "subsequent key update unless it has received an acknowledgment for a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3ca78cbaca5bc27a",
                  "3ad82f1956fef698"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "packet that was sent protected with keys from the current key phase."
              }
            ],
            "   This ensures that keys are available to both peers before another key",
            "   update can be initiated.  This can be implemented by tracking the",
            "   lowest packet number sent with each key phase and the highest",
            "   acknowledged packet number in the 1-RTT space: once the latter is",
            "   higher than or equal to the former, another key update can be",
            "   initiated.",
            "",
            "      |  Note: Keys of packets other than the 1-RTT packets are never",
            "      |  updated; their keys are derived solely from the TLS handshake",
            "      |  state.",
            "",
            "   The endpoint that initiates a key update also updates the keys that",
            "   it uses for receiving packets.  These keys will be needed to process",
            "   packets the peer sends after updating.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30f8ca71e3644b02",
                  "c09e8fafe3b815f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST retain old keys until it has successfully"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30f8ca71e3644b02",
                  "c09e8fafe3b815f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "unprotected a packet sent using the new keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a61ba7172b3b019",
                  "bfb306e93fa0087f",
                  "033118c11634d35a",
                  "3c7cebfbc7d3303d"
                ],
                "status_id": 27,
                "text": "An endpoint SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a61ba7172b3b019",
                  "bfb306e93fa0087f",
                  "033118c11634d35a",
                  "3c7cebfbc7d3303d"
                ],
                "status_id": 27,
                "text": "retain old keys for some time after unprotecting a packet sent using"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a61ba7172b3b019",
                  "bfb306e93fa0087f",
                  "033118c11634d35a",
                  "3c7cebfbc7d3303d"
                ],
                "status_id": 27,
                "text": "the new keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Discarding old keys too early can cause delayed"
              }
            ],
            "   packets to be discarded.  Discarding packets will be interpreted as",
            "   packet loss by the peer and could adversely affect performance."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2bea64447cf4e3b0",
            "2bea64447cf4e3b0",
            "3ad82f1956fef698",
            "3ad82f1956fef698",
            "3ad82f1956fef698",
            "c09e8fafe3b815f3",
            "c09e8fafe3b815f3",
            "3c7cebfbc7d3303d",
            "3c7cebfbc7d3303d",
            "3c7cebfbc7d3303d"
          ],
          "title": "Initiating a Key Update"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2",
          "lines": [
            "   A peer is permitted to initiate a key update after receiving an",
            "   acknowledgment of a packet in the current key phase.  An endpoint",
            "   detects a key update when processing a packet with a key phase that",
            "   differs from the value used to protect the last packet it sent.  To",
            "   process this packet, the endpoint uses the next packet protection key",
            "   and IV.  See Section 6.3 for considerations about generating these",
            "   keys.",
            "",
            "   If a packet is successfully processed using the next key and IV, then",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   the peer has initiated a key update.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35061e3f43ac31dc",
                  "350a4f115e2ba3b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "The endpoint MUST update its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35061e3f43ac31dc",
                  "350a4f115e2ba3b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "send keys to the corresponding key phase in response, as described in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35061e3f43ac31dc",
                  "350a4f115e2ba3b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Section 6.1."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7b0117d103dba20",
                  "6daf94142c799a6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Sending keys MUST be updated before sending an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e7b0117d103dba20",
                  "6daf94142c799a6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "acknowledgment for the packet that was received with updated keys."
              }
            ],
            "   By acknowledging the packet that triggered the key update in a packet",
            "   protected with the updated keys, the endpoint signals that the key",
            "   update is complete.",
            "",
            "   An endpoint can defer sending the packet or acknowledgment according",
            "   to its normal packet sending behavior; it is not necessary to",
            "   immediately generate a packet in response to a key update.  The next",
            "   packet sent by the endpoint will use the updated keys.  The next",
            "   packet that contains an acknowledgment will cause the key update to",
            "   be completed.  If an endpoint detects a second update before it has",
            "   sent any packets with updated keys containing an acknowledgment for",
            "   the packet that initiated the key update, it indicates that its peer",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   has updated keys twice without awaiting confirmation.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd12f67be6ced3d1",
                  "e30b25d33b7c41ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "An endpoint"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd12f67be6ced3d1",
                  "e30b25d33b7c41ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "MAY treat such consecutive key updates as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd12f67be6ced3d1",
                  "e30b25d33b7c41ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "KEY_UPDATE_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c446bf8d17454af",
                  "d8d4b6c620a23258",
                  "51e24a309f5e5b34"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "An endpoint that receives an acknowledgment that is carried in a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c446bf8d17454af",
                  "d8d4b6c620a23258",
                  "51e24a309f5e5b34"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "packet protected with old keys where any acknowledged packet was"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c446bf8d17454af",
                  "d8d4b6c620a23258",
                  "51e24a309f5e5b34"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "protected with newer keys MAY treat that as a connection error of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4c446bf8d17454af",
                  "d8d4b6c620a23258",
                  "51e24a309f5e5b34"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This indicates that a peer has received and"
              }
            ],
            "   acknowledged a packet that initiates a key update, but has not",
            "   updated keys in response."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "350a4f115e2ba3b3",
            "350a4f115e2ba3b3",
            "350a4f115e2ba3b3",
            "6daf94142c799a6b",
            "6daf94142c799a6b",
            "e30b25d33b7c41ab",
            "e30b25d33b7c41ab",
            "e30b25d33b7c41ab",
            "51e24a309f5e5b34",
            "51e24a309f5e5b34",
            "51e24a309f5e5b34",
            "51e24a309f5e5b34"
          ],
          "title": "Responding to a Key Update"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.3",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61f8c6d2d80f06e9",
                  "dab49bc0c242cb09",
                  "93f0d95b312575a7",
                  "589b56449b7d569d"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "Endpoints responding to an apparent key update MUST NOT generate a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61f8c6d2d80f06e9",
                  "dab49bc0c242cb09",
                  "93f0d95b312575a7",
                  "589b56449b7d569d"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "timing side-channel signal that might indicate that the Key Phase bit"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61f8c6d2d80f06e9",
                  "dab49bc0c242cb09",
                  "93f0d95b312575a7",
                  "589b56449b7d569d"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "was invalid (see Section 9.5)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Endpoints can use randomized packet"
              }
            ],
            "   protection keys in place of discarded keys when key updates are not",
            "   yet permitted.  Using randomized keys ensures that attempting to",
            "   remove packet protection does not result in timing variations, and",
            "   results in packets with an invalid Key Phase bit being rejected.",
            "",
            "   The process of creating new packet protection keys for receiving",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   packets could reveal that a key update has occurred.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "694e44bb6acc2636",
                  "18a9a8a46896f49b",
                  "246ace45610f51e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "An endpoint MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "694e44bb6acc2636",
                  "18a9a8a46896f49b",
                  "246ace45610f51e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "generate new keys as part of packet processing, but this creates a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "694e44bb6acc2636",
                  "18a9a8a46896f49b",
                  "246ace45610f51e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "timing signal that could be used by an attacker to learn when key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "694e44bb6acc2636",
                  "18a9a8a46896f49b",
                  "246ace45610f51e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 30,
                "text": "updates happen and thus leak the value of the Key Phase bit."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Endpoints are generally expected to have current and next receive",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   packet protection keys available.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25add3573021acbb",
                  "676c6386553d983e",
                  "ff38c0324287dce0"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "For a short period after a key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25add3573021acbb",
                  "676c6386553d983e",
                  "ff38c0324287dce0"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "update completes, up to the PTO, endpoints MAY defer generation of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25add3573021acbb",
                  "676c6386553d983e",
                  "ff38c0324287dce0"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "the next set of receive packet protection keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25add3573021acbb",
                  "676c6386553d983e"
                ],
                "status_id": 31,
                "text": "  This allows"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "25add3573021acbb",
                  "676c6386553d983e"
                ],
                "status_id": 31,
                "text": "endpoints to retain only two sets of receive keys; see Section 6.5."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfe89f1cf06d5998",
                  "582c387a1905cd7d",
                  "f3a68a80a8ecf04b"
                ],
                "status_id": 32,
                "text": "Once generated, the next set of packet protection keys SHOULD be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfe89f1cf06d5998",
                  "582c387a1905cd7d",
                  "f3a68a80a8ecf04b"
                ],
                "status_id": 32,
                "text": "retained, even if the packet that was received was subsequently"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfe89f1cf06d5998",
                  "582c387a1905cd7d",
                  "f3a68a80a8ecf04b"
                ],
                "status_id": 32,
                "text": "discarded."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Packets containing apparent key updates are easy to"
              }
            ],
            "   forge, and while the process of key update does not require",
            "   significant effort, triggering this process could be used by an",
            "   attacker for DoS.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ce287691eae7b134",
                  "91e61e47318bcc37",
                  "62f608bc210cd886"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "For this reason, endpoints MUST be able to retain two sets of packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ce287691eae7b134",
                  "91e61e47318bcc37",
                  "62f608bc210cd886"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "protection keys for receiving packets: the current and the next."
              }
            ],
            "   Retaining the previous keys in addition to these might improve",
            "   performance, but this is not essential."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "589b56449b7d569d",
            "589b56449b7d569d",
            "589b56449b7d569d",
            "246ace45610f51e2",
            "246ace45610f51e2",
            "246ace45610f51e2",
            "246ace45610f51e2",
            "ff38c0324287dce0",
            "ff38c0324287dce0",
            "ff38c0324287dce0",
            "f3a68a80a8ecf04b",
            "f3a68a80a8ecf04b",
            "f3a68a80a8ecf04b",
            "62f608bc210cd886",
            "62f608bc210cd886"
          ],
          "title": "Timing of Receive Key Generation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.4",
          "lines": [
            "   An endpoint never sends packets that are protected with old keys.",
            "   Only the current keys are used.  Keys used for protecting packets can",
            "   be discarded immediately after switching to newer keys.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d92a841171a38b9d",
                  "ff40a701e4f2b0e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Packets with higher packet numbers MUST be protected with either the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d92a841171a38b9d",
                  "ff40a701e4f2b0e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "same or newer packet protection keys than packets with lower packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d92a841171a38b9d",
                  "ff40a701e4f2b0e2"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "numbers."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0674dec53d6bcf1b",
                  "ce6046b36f5547b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "An endpoint that successfully removes protection with old"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0674dec53d6bcf1b",
                  "ce6046b36f5547b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "keys when newer keys were used for packets with lower packet numbers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0674dec53d6bcf1b",
                  "ce6046b36f5547b5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "MUST treat this as a connection error of type KEY_UPDATE_ERROR."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ff40a701e4f2b0e2",
            "ff40a701e4f2b0e2",
            "ff40a701e4f2b0e2",
            "ce6046b36f5547b5",
            "ce6046b36f5547b5",
            "ce6046b36f5547b5"
          ],
          "title": "Sending with Updated Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.5",
          "lines": [
            "   For receiving packets during a key update, packets protected with",
            "   older keys might arrive if they were delayed by the network.",
            "   Retaining old packet protection keys allows these packets to be",
            "   successfully processed.",
            "",
            "   As packets protected with keys from the next key phase use the same",
            "   Key Phase value as those protected with keys from the previous key",
            "   phase, it is necessary to distinguish between the two if packets",
            "   protected with old keys are to be processed.  This can be done using",
            "   packet numbers.  A recovered packet number that is lower than any",
            "   packet number from the current key phase uses the previous packet",
            "   protection keys; a recovered packet number that is higher than any",
            "   packet number from the current key phase requires the use of the next",
            "   packet protection keys.",
            "",
            "   Some care is necessary to ensure that any process for selecting",
            "   between previous, current, and next packet protection keys does not",
            "   expose a timing side channel that might reveal which keys were used",
            "   to remove packet protection.  See Section 9.5 for more information.",
            "",
            "   Alternatively, endpoints can retain only two sets of packet",
            "   protection keys, swapping previous for next after enough time has",
            "   passed to allow for reordering in the network.  In this case, the Key",
            "   Phase bit alone can be used to select keys.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "180212e5e4ea11c2",
                  "3fde51f9b7de0bbe",
                  "4ec8d9177db4bff5",
                  "9af88fd84ea0aeb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "An endpoint MAY allow a period of approximately the Probe Timeout"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "180212e5e4ea11c2",
                  "3fde51f9b7de0bbe",
                  "4ec8d9177db4bff5",
                  "9af88fd84ea0aeb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "(PTO; see [QUIC-RECOVERY]) after promoting the next set of receive"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "180212e5e4ea11c2",
                  "3fde51f9b7de0bbe",
                  "4ec8d9177db4bff5",
                  "9af88fd84ea0aeb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "keys to be current before it creates the subsequent set of packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "180212e5e4ea11c2",
                  "3fde51f9b7de0bbe",
                  "4ec8d9177db4bff5",
                  "9af88fd84ea0aeb1"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "protection keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a783bb45523980ec",
                  "d4c69c45f89e79cc",
                  "a5912ff6801cb849"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "These updated keys MAY replace the previous keys at"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a783bb45523980ec",
                  "d4c69c45f89e79cc",
                  "a5912ff6801cb849"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "that time."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  With the caveat that PTO is a subjective measure -- that"
              }
            ],
            "   is, a peer could have a different view of the RTT -- this time is",
            "   expected to be long enough that any reordered packets would be",
            "   declared lost by a peer even if they were acknowledged and short",
            "   enough to allow a peer to initiate further key updates.",
            "",
            "   Endpoints need to allow for the possibility that a peer might not be",
            "   able to decrypt packets that initiate a key update during the period",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   when the peer retains old keys.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "002da5ed4b3e0c06",
                  "359b8d76ccfb8e52"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "Endpoints SHOULD wait three times"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "002da5ed4b3e0c06",
                  "359b8d76ccfb8e52"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "the PTO before initiating a key update after receiving an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "002da5ed4b3e0c06",
                  "359b8d76ccfb8e52"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "acknowledgment that confirms that the previous key update was"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "002da5ed4b3e0c06",
                  "359b8d76ccfb8e52"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "received."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Failing to allow sufficient time could lead to packets"
              }
            ],
            "   being discarded.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "17b275836631ee34",
                  "eac71bb105a71e24",
                  "6446671c7555d65f",
                  "fe38612b261d4850"
                ],
                "status_id": 32,
                "text": "An endpoint SHOULD retain old read keys for no more than three times"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "17b275836631ee34",
                  "eac71bb105a71e24",
                  "6446671c7555d65f",
                  "fe38612b261d4850"
                ],
                "status_id": 32,
                "text": "the PTO after having received a packet protected using the new keys."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c639b2b4243e0235",
                  "d1b764154a18cb9a",
                  "90990392c7ab14f6",
                  "6acffcbdcc4e3f9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 27,
                "text": "After this period, old read keys and their corresponding secrets"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c639b2b4243e0235",
                  "d1b764154a18cb9a",
                  "90990392c7ab14f6",
                  "6acffcbdcc4e3f9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 27,
                "text": "SHOULD be discarded."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9af88fd84ea0aeb1",
            "9af88fd84ea0aeb1",
            "9af88fd84ea0aeb1",
            "9af88fd84ea0aeb1",
            "a5912ff6801cb849",
            "a5912ff6801cb849",
            "359b8d76ccfb8e52",
            "359b8d76ccfb8e52",
            "359b8d76ccfb8e52",
            "359b8d76ccfb8e52",
            "fe38612b261d4850",
            "fe38612b261d4850",
            "6acffcbdcc4e3f9c",
            "6acffcbdcc4e3f9c"
          ],
          "title": "Receiving with Different Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.6",
          "lines": [
            "   This document sets usage limits for AEAD algorithms to ensure that",
            "   overuse does not give an adversary a disproportionate advantage in",
            "   attacking the confidentiality and integrity of communications when",
            "   using QUIC.",
            "",
            "   The usage limits defined in TLS 1.3 exist for protection against",
            "   attacks on confidentiality and apply to successful applications of",
            "   AEAD protection.  The integrity protections in authenticated",
            "   encryption also depend on limiting the number of attempts to forge",
            "   packets.  TLS achieves this by closing connections after any record",
            "   fails an authentication check.  In comparison, QUIC ignores any",
            "   packet that cannot be authenticated, allowing multiple forgery",
            "   attempts.",
            "",
            "   QUIC accounts for AEAD confidentiality and integrity limits",
            "   separately.  The confidentiality limit applies to the number of",
            "   packets encrypted with a given key.  The integrity limit applies to",
            "   the number of packets decrypted within a given connection.  Details",
            "   on enforcing these limits for each AEAD algorithm follow below.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c206d2dbf74e1435",
                  "d518f88ec61ea83b",
                  "11be776677e6a56b",
                  "2770efe716ebe6f8"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST count the number of encrypted packets for each set of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c206d2dbf74e1435",
                  "d518f88ec61ea83b",
                  "11be776677e6a56b",
                  "2770efe716ebe6f8"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d1de4e8ad616782",
                  "9d032f4772ecda74",
                  "262f2eec59323154",
                  "0bcb268a49e6973e"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "If the total number of encrypted packets with the same key"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d1de4e8ad616782",
                  "9d032f4772ecda74",
                  "262f2eec59323154",
                  "0bcb268a49e6973e"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "exceeds the confidentiality limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d1de4e8ad616782",
                  "9d032f4772ecda74",
                  "262f2eec59323154",
                  "0bcb268a49e6973e"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "MUST stop using those keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7f6b4e9a97e80a96",
                  "51b3517774ca81f4",
                  "550d809b3a216f4e",
                  "7d78b881f55910c7"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST initiate a key update"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7f6b4e9a97e80a96",
                  "51b3517774ca81f4",
                  "550d809b3a216f4e",
                  "7d78b881f55910c7"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "before sending more protected packets than the confidentiality limit"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7f6b4e9a97e80a96",
                  "51b3517774ca81f4",
                  "550d809b3a216f4e",
                  "7d78b881f55910c7"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "for the selected AEAD permits."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1f8aec9477a0fe3e",
                  "df6c62d1909d8ffa",
                  "6bd50ae4311d8611"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "If a key update is not possible or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1f8aec9477a0fe3e",
                  "df6c62d1909d8ffa",
                  "6bd50ae4311d8611"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "integrity limits are reached, the endpoint MUST stop using the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1f8aec9477a0fe3e",
                  "df6c62d1909d8ffa",
                  "6bd50ae4311d8611"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "connection and only send stateless resets in response to receiving"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1f8aec9477a0fe3e",
                  "df6c62d1909d8ffa",
                  "6bd50ae4311d8611"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "packets."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ac463fada73bbd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "It is RECOMMENDED that endpoints immediately close the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ac463fada73bbd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "connection with a connection error of type AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED before"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ac463fada73bbd8"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "reaching a state where key updates are not possible."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d52a2c4ea436770"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "For AEAD_AES_128_GCM and AEAD_AES_256_GCM, the confidentiality limit"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d52a2c4ea436770"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "is 2^23 encrypted packets; see Appendix B.1."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5a076a5060208c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "For"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5a076a5060208c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "AEAD_CHACHA20_POLY1305, the confidentiality limit is greater than the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5a076a5060208c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "number of possible packets (2^62) and so can be disregarded."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  For"
              }
            ],
            "   AEAD_AES_128_CCM, the confidentiality limit is 2^21.5 encrypted",
            "   packets; see Appendix B.2.  Applying a limit reduces the probability",
            "   that an attacker can distinguish the AEAD in use from a random",
            "   permutation; see [AEBounds], [ROBUST], and [GCM-MU].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69abfb9a7acc8085",
                  "104ac1883b69337d",
                  "0abcf1c3ee65970e",
                  "6fe3e67c090b6ba1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "In addition to counting packets sent, endpoints MUST count the number"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69abfb9a7acc8085",
                  "104ac1883b69337d",
                  "0abcf1c3ee65970e",
                  "6fe3e67c090b6ba1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "of received packets that fail authentication during the lifetime of a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "69abfb9a7acc8085",
                  "104ac1883b69337d",
                  "0abcf1c3ee65970e",
                  "6fe3e67c090b6ba1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "connection."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "268ce322d030fff0",
                  "357022de47101199",
                  "df1eb4146e3a5bda"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If the total number of received packets that fail"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "268ce322d030fff0",
                  "357022de47101199",
                  "df1eb4146e3a5bda"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "authentication within the connection, across all keys, exceeds the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "268ce322d030fff0",
                  "357022de47101199",
                  "df1eb4146e3a5bda"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "integrity limit for the selected AEAD, the endpoint MUST immediately"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "268ce322d030fff0",
                  "357022de47101199",
                  "df1eb4146e3a5bda"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "close the connection with a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "268ce322d030fff0",
                  "357022de47101199",
                  "df1eb4146e3a5bda"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "AEAD_LIMIT_REACHED and not process any more packets."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   For AEAD_AES_128_GCM and AEAD_AES_256_GCM, the integrity limit is",
            "   2^52 invalid packets; see Appendix B.1.  For AEAD_CHACHA20_POLY1305,",
            "   the integrity limit is 2^36 invalid packets; see [AEBounds].  For",
            "   AEAD_AES_128_CCM, the integrity limit is 2^21.5 invalid packets; see",
            "   Appendix B.2.  Applying this limit reduces the probability that an",
            "   attacker can successfully forge a packet; see [AEBounds], [ROBUST],",
            "   and [GCM-MU].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30aa8efed8eac449"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "Endpoints that limit the size of packets MAY use higher"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30aa8efed8eac449"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "confidentiality and integrity limits; see Appendix B for details."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "176b1f914604de67",
                  "945d7661ab80386f"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "Future analyses and specifications MAY relax confidentiality or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "176b1f914604de67",
                  "945d7661ab80386f"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "integrity limits for an AEAD."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b6282f5371e7671",
                  "b62620fd58b9ddf7",
                  "ce750c73b5172e04"
                ],
                "status_id": 29,
                "text": "Any TLS cipher suite that is specified for use with QUIC MUST define"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b6282f5371e7671",
                  "b62620fd58b9ddf7",
                  "ce750c73b5172e04"
                ],
                "status_id": 29,
                "text": "limits on the use of the associated AEAD function that preserves"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b6282f5371e7671",
                  "b62620fd58b9ddf7",
                  "ce750c73b5172e04"
                ],
                "status_id": 29,
                "text": "margins for confidentiality and integrity."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b62620fd58b9ddf7"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b62620fd58b9ddf7",
                  "a80853f16cf3fd95"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "That is, limits MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b62620fd58b9ddf7",
                  "a80853f16cf3fd95"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "specified for the number of packets that can be authenticated and for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b62620fd58b9ddf7",
                  "a80853f16cf3fd95"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "the number of packets that can fail authentication."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Providing a"
              }
            ],
            "   reference to any analysis upon which values are based -- and any",
            "   assumptions used in that analysis -- allows limits to be adapted to",
            "   varying usage conditions."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2770efe716ebe6f8",
            "2770efe716ebe6f8",
            "0bcb268a49e6973e",
            "0bcb268a49e6973e",
            "0bcb268a49e6973e",
            "7d78b881f55910c7",
            "7d78b881f55910c7",
            "7d78b881f55910c7",
            "6bd50ae4311d8611",
            "6bd50ae4311d8611",
            "6bd50ae4311d8611",
            "6bd50ae4311d8611",
            "7ac463fada73bbd8",
            "7ac463fada73bbd8",
            "7ac463fada73bbd8",
            "6fe3e67c090b6ba1",
            "6fe3e67c090b6ba1",
            "6fe3e67c090b6ba1",
            "df1eb4146e3a5bda",
            "df1eb4146e3a5bda",
            "df1eb4146e3a5bda",
            "df1eb4146e3a5bda",
            "df1eb4146e3a5bda",
            "30aa8efed8eac449",
            "30aa8efed8eac449",
            "945d7661ab80386f",
            "945d7661ab80386f",
            "ce750c73b5172e04",
            "ce750c73b5172e04",
            "ce750c73b5172e04",
            "a80853f16cf3fd95",
            "a80853f16cf3fd95",
            "a80853f16cf3fd95"
          ],
          "title": "Limits on AEAD Usage"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.7",
          "lines": [
            "   The KEY_UPDATE_ERROR error code (0x0e) is used to signal errors",
            "   related to key updates."
          ],
          "title": "Key Update Error Code"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7",
          "lines": [
            "   Initial packets are not protected with a secret key, so they are",
            "   subject to potential tampering by an attacker.  QUIC provides",
            "   protection against attackers that cannot read packets but does not",
            "   attempt to provide additional protection against attacks where the",
            "   attacker can observe and inject packets.  Some forms of tampering --",
            "   such as modifying the TLS messages themselves -- are detectable, but",
            "   some -- such as modifying ACKs -- are not.",
            "",
            "   For example, an attacker could inject a packet containing an ACK",
            "   frame to make it appear that a packet had not been received or to",
            "   create a false impression of the state of the connection (e.g., by",
            "   modifying the ACK Delay).  Note that such a packet could cause a",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   legitimate packet to be dropped as a duplicate.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd8a605de8dedccf",
                  "ea1803fd8ec529a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "Implementations"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd8a605de8dedccf",
                  "ea1803fd8ec529a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "SHOULD use caution in relying on any data that is contained in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd8a605de8dedccf",
                  "ea1803fd8ec529a7"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "Initial packets that is not otherwise authenticated."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   It is also possible for the attacker to tamper with data that is",
            "   carried in Handshake packets, but because that sort of tampering",
            "   requires modifying TLS handshake messages, any such tampering will",
            "   cause the TLS handshake to fail."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ea1803fd8ec529a7",
            "ea1803fd8ec529a7",
            "ea1803fd8ec529a7"
          ],
          "title": "Security of Initial Messages"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8",
          "lines": [
            "   Certain aspects of the TLS handshake are different when used with",
            "   QUIC.",
            "",
            "   QUIC also requires additional features from TLS.  In addition to",
            "   negotiation of cryptographic parameters, the TLS handshake carries",
            "   and authenticates values for QUIC transport parameters."
          ],
          "title": "QUIC-Specific Adjustments to the TLS Handshake"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.1",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC requires that the cryptographic handshake provide authenticated",
            "   protocol negotiation.  TLS uses Application-Layer Protocol",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Negotiation [ALPN] to select an application protocol.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ede3619837a05d30",
                  "689657dfdaab4240",
                  "2da524ff2f98f915",
                  "039855da59c7f98e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Unless another"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ede3619837a05d30",
                  "689657dfdaab4240",
                  "2da524ff2f98f915",
                  "039855da59c7f98e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "mechanism is used for agreeing on an application protocol, endpoints"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ede3619837a05d30",
                  "689657dfdaab4240",
                  "2da524ff2f98f915",
                  "039855da59c7f98e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST use ALPN for this purpose."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc5f238987ffede7",
                  "bd4b99188979d27a",
                  "1778b5465a3f5873"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "When using ALPN, endpoints MUST immediately close a connection (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc5f238987ffede7",
                  "bd4b99188979d27a",
                  "1778b5465a3f5873"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Section 10.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) with a no_application_protocol TLS"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc5f238987ffede7",
                  "bd4b99188979d27a",
                  "1778b5465a3f5873"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "alert (QUIC error code 0x0178; see Section 4.8) if an application"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc5f238987ffede7",
                  "bd4b99188979d27a",
                  "1778b5465a3f5873"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "protocol is not negotiated."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de8f01db8dd83199",
                  "9fe60922f02a56b5",
                  "23d56e364c31d5cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "While [ALPN] only specifies that servers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de8f01db8dd83199",
                  "9fe60922f02a56b5",
                  "23d56e364c31d5cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "use this alert, QUIC clients MUST use error 0x0178 to terminate a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de8f01db8dd83199",
                  "9fe60922f02a56b5",
                  "23d56e364c31d5cf"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "connection when ALPN negotiation fails."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a043e1c8b3823930",
                  "5ed623961d875f12"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "An application protocol MAY restrict the QUIC versions that it can"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a043e1c8b3823930",
                  "5ed623961d875f12"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "operate over."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9d24ad72aa239123",
                  "ee9e684402018f09"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Servers MUST select an application protocol compatible"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9d24ad72aa239123",
                  "ee9e684402018f09"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "with the QUIC version that the client has selected."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "033f25753e780b8c",
                  "cc28d7765c1cfff3"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "The server MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "033f25753e780b8c",
                  "cc28d7765c1cfff3"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "treat the inability to select a compatible application protocol as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "033f25753e780b8c",
                  "cc28d7765c1cfff3"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "connection error of type 0x0178 (no_application_protocol)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0be7acb45327d480",
                  "d91e15ff45d84f66"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Similarly, a client MUST treat the selection of an incompatible"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0be7acb45327d480",
                  "d91e15ff45d84f66"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "application protocol by a server as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0be7acb45327d480",
                  "d91e15ff45d84f66"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "0x0178."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "039855da59c7f98e",
            "039855da59c7f98e",
            "039855da59c7f98e",
            "1778b5465a3f5873",
            "1778b5465a3f5873",
            "1778b5465a3f5873",
            "1778b5465a3f5873",
            "23d56e364c31d5cf",
            "23d56e364c31d5cf",
            "23d56e364c31d5cf",
            "5ed623961d875f12",
            "5ed623961d875f12",
            "ee9e684402018f09",
            "ee9e684402018f09",
            "cc28d7765c1cfff3",
            "cc28d7765c1cfff3",
            "cc28d7765c1cfff3",
            "d91e15ff45d84f66",
            "d91e15ff45d84f66",
            "d91e15ff45d84f66"
          ],
          "title": "Protocol Negotiation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.2",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC transport parameters are carried in a TLS extension.  Different",
            "   versions of QUIC might define a different method for negotiating",
            "   transport configuration.",
            "",
            "   Including transport parameters in the TLS handshake provides",
            "   integrity protection for these values.",
            "",
            "      enum {",
            "         quic_transport_parameters(0x39), (65535)",
            "      } ExtensionType;",
            "",
            "   The extension_data field of the quic_transport_parameters extension",
            "   contains a value that is defined by the version of QUIC that is in",
            "   use.",
            "",
            "   The quic_transport_parameters extension is carried in the ClientHello",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   and the EncryptedExtensions messages during the handshake.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06544aa7cd3aaff4",
                  "d83c14f909a39375",
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Endpoints"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06544aa7cd3aaff4",
                  "d83c14f909a39375",
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "MUST send the quic_transport_parameters extension;"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d8d9e05a2d7409e",
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "endpoints that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d8d9e05a2d7409e",
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "receive ClientHello or EncryptedExtensions messages without the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d8d9e05a2d7409e",
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "quic_transport_parameters extension MUST close the connection with an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d8d9e05a2d7409e",
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "error of type 0x016d (equivalent to a fatal TLS missing_extension"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d8d9e05a2d7409e",
                  "9dc6b60202f2921c",
                  "f4e3ebe2df46f85e"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "alert, see Section 4.8)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Transport parameters become available prior to the completion of the",
            "   handshake.  A server might use these values earlier than handshake",
            "   completion.  However, the value of transport parameters is not",
            "   authenticated until the handshake completes, so any use of these",
            "   parameters cannot depend on their authenticity.  Any tampering with",
            "   transport parameters will cause the handshake to fail.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcce37975c44f791",
                  "ae4ac4230c4cd2f4"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT send this extension in a TLS connection that does"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcce37975c44f791",
                  "ae4ac4230c4cd2f4"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "not use QUIC (such as the use of TLS with TCP defined in [TLS13])."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcce37975c44f791"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcce37975c44f791"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "A"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcce37975c44f791",
                  "cf1c029210930bfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "fatal unsupported_extension alert MUST be sent by an implementation"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcce37975c44f791",
                  "cf1c029210930bfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "that supports this extension if the extension is received when the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dcce37975c44f791",
                  "cf1c029210930bfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "transport is not QUIC."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Negotiating the quic_transport_parameters extension causes the",
            "   EndOfEarlyData to be removed; see Section 8.3."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9dc6b60202f2921c",
            "9dc6b60202f2921c",
            "9dc6b60202f2921c",
            "9dc6b60202f2921c",
            "9dc6b60202f2921c",
            "9dc6b60202f2921c",
            "f4e3ebe2df46f85e",
            "f4e3ebe2df46f85e",
            "f4e3ebe2df46f85e",
            "f4e3ebe2df46f85e",
            "f4e3ebe2df46f85e",
            "f4e3ebe2df46f85e",
            "ae4ac4230c4cd2f4",
            "ae4ac4230c4cd2f4",
            "cf1c029210930bfe",
            "cf1c029210930bfe",
            "cf1c029210930bfe",
            "cf1c029210930bfe"
          ],
          "title": "QUIC Transport Parameters Extension"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The TLS EndOfEarlyData message is not used with QUIC.  QUIC does not",
            "   rely on this message to mark the end of 0-RTT data or to signal the",
            "   change to Handshake keys.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "63fafd04034871c2",
                  "27408493e90d2af0"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT send the EndOfEarlyData message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b9ecf44d20a3ca85",
                  "943e7aa406a973c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "A server MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b9ecf44d20a3ca85",
                  "943e7aa406a973c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "treat receipt of a CRYPTO frame in a 0-RTT packet as a connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b9ecf44d20a3ca85",
                  "943e7aa406a973c5"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   As a result, EndOfEarlyData does not appear in the TLS handshake",
            "   transcript."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "27408493e90d2af0",
            "943e7aa406a973c5",
            "943e7aa406a973c5",
            "943e7aa406a973c5"
          ],
          "title": "Removing the EndOfEarlyData Message"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.4",
          "lines": [
            "   Appendix D.4 of [TLS13] describes an alteration to the TLS 1.3",
            "   handshake as a workaround for bugs in some middleboxes.  The TLS 1.3",
            "   middlebox compatibility mode involves setting the legacy_session_id",
            "   field to a 32-byte value in the ClientHello and ServerHello, then",
            "   sending a change_cipher_spec record.  Both field and record carry no",
            "   semantic content and are ignored.",
            "",
            "   This mode has no use in QUIC as it only applies to middleboxes that",
            "   interfere with TLS over TCP.  QUIC also provides no means to carry a",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   change_cipher_spec record.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ececce7ea36caa8b",
                  "b008c9c12c477ce8"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "A client MUST NOT request the use of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ececce7ea36caa8b",
                  "b008c9c12c477ce8"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "TLS 1.3 compatibility mode."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5a319c10e01f136",
                  "d4805ded1c2ec3fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A server SHOULD treat the receipt of a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5a319c10e01f136",
                  "d4805ded1c2ec3fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "TLS ClientHello with a non-empty legacy_session_id field as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5a319c10e01f136",
                  "d4805ded1c2ec3fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "connection error of type PROTOCOL_VIOLATION."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b008c9c12c477ce8",
            "b008c9c12c477ce8",
            "d4805ded1c2ec3fa",
            "d4805ded1c2ec3fa",
            "d4805ded1c2ec3fa"
          ],
          "title": "Prohibit TLS Middlebox Compatibility Mode"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9",
          "lines": [
            "   All of the security considerations that apply to TLS also apply to",
            "   the use of TLS in QUIC.  Reading all of [TLS13] and its appendices is",
            "   the best way to gain an understanding of the security properties of",
            "   QUIC.",
            "",
            "   This section summarizes some of the more important security aspects",
            "   specific to the TLS integration, though there are many security-",
            "   relevant details in the remainder of the document."
          ],
          "title": "Security Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Use of TLS session tickets allows servers and possibly other entities",
            "   to correlate connections made by the same client; see Section 4.5 for",
            "   details."
          ],
          "title": "Session Linkability"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.2",
          "lines": [
            "   As described in Section 8 of [TLS13], use of TLS early data comes",
            "   with an exposure to replay attack.  The use of 0-RTT in QUIC is",
            "   similarly vulnerable to replay attack.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71b854025292d1a9",
                  "fcf570b91d5bdd84"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST implement and use the replay protections described in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71b854025292d1a9",
                  "fcf570b91d5bdd84"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "[TLS13], however it is recognized that these protections are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71b854025292d1a9",
                  "fcf570b91d5bdd84"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "imperfect."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Therefore, additional consideration of the risk of replay"
              }
            ],
            "   is needed.",
            "",
            "   QUIC is not vulnerable to replay attack, except via the application",
            "   protocol information it might carry.  The management of QUIC protocol",
            "   state based on the frame types defined in [QUIC-TRANSPORT] is not",
            "   vulnerable to replay.  Processing of QUIC frames is idempotent and",
            "   cannot result in invalid connection states if frames are replayed,",
            "   reordered, or lost.  QUIC connections do not produce effects that",
            "   last beyond the lifetime of the connection, except for those produced",
            "   by the application protocol that QUIC serves.",
            "",
            "   TLS session tickets and address validation tokens are used to carry",
            "   QUIC configuration information between connections, specifically, to",
            "   enable a server to efficiently recover state that is used in",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   connection establishment and address validation.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "32dd7dcb761ae45e",
                  "55732214e6ed577f",
                  "9033644da74ed437"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "These MUST NOT be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "32dd7dcb761ae45e",
                  "55732214e6ed577f",
                  "9033644da74ed437"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "used to communicate application semantics between endpoints; clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "32dd7dcb761ae45e",
                  "55732214e6ed577f",
                  "9033644da74ed437"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "MUST treat them as opaque values."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The potential for reuse of these"
              }
            ],
            "   tokens means that they require stronger protections against replay.",
            "",
            "   A server that accepts 0-RTT on a connection incurs a higher cost than",
            "   accepting a connection without 0-RTT.  This includes higher",
            "   processing and computation costs.  Servers need to consider the",
            "   probability of replay and all associated costs when accepting 0-RTT.",
            "",
            "   Ultimately, the responsibility for managing the risks of replay",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   attacks with 0-RTT lies with an application protocol.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e74ec16465335dc9",
                  "18e8515012cacb42"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "An application"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e74ec16465335dc9",
                  "18e8515012cacb42"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "protocol that uses QUIC MUST describe how the protocol uses 0-RTT and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e74ec16465335dc9",
                  "18e8515012cacb42"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "the measures that are employed to protect against replay attack."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  An"
              }
            ],
            "   analysis of replay risk needs to consider all QUIC protocol features",
            "   that carry application semantics.",
            "",
            "   Disabling 0-RTT entirely is the most effective defense against replay",
            "   attack.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "560ef9d48a202672",
                  "dda726d8a0439df1"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "QUIC extensions MUST either describe how replay attacks affect their"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "560ef9d48a202672",
                  "dda726d8a0439df1"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "operation or prohibit the use of the extension in 0-RTT."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d76c21602a655134",
                  "0c59a338ee91220b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Application"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d76c21602a655134",
                  "0c59a338ee91220b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "protocols MUST either prohibit the use of extensions that carry"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d76c21602a655134",
                  "0c59a338ee91220b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "application semantics in 0-RTT or provide replay mitigation"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d76c21602a655134",
                  "0c59a338ee91220b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "strategies."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "fcf570b91d5bdd84",
            "fcf570b91d5bdd84",
            "fcf570b91d5bdd84",
            "55732214e6ed577f",
            "55732214e6ed577f",
            "55732214e6ed577f",
            "9033644da74ed437",
            "9033644da74ed437",
            "9033644da74ed437",
            "18e8515012cacb42",
            "18e8515012cacb42",
            "18e8515012cacb42",
            "dda726d8a0439df1",
            "dda726d8a0439df1",
            "0c59a338ee91220b",
            "0c59a338ee91220b",
            "0c59a338ee91220b",
            "0c59a338ee91220b"
          ],
          "title": "Replay Attacks with 0-RTT"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.3",
          "lines": [
            "   A small ClientHello that results in a large block of handshake",
            "   messages from a server can be used in packet reflection attacks to",
            "   amplify the traffic generated by an attacker.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   QUIC includes three defenses against this attack.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43093a82e36c1559",
                  "bcea154c686257c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "First, the packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43093a82e36c1559",
                  "bcea154c686257c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "containing a ClientHello MUST be padded to a minimum size."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Second,"
              }
            ],
            "   if responding to an unverified source address, the server is",
            "   forbidden to send more than three times as many bytes as the number",
            "   of bytes it has received (see Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]).",
            "   Finally, because acknowledgments of Handshake packets are",
            "   authenticated, a blind attacker cannot forge them.  Put together,",
            "   these defenses limit the level of amplification."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "bcea154c686257c3",
            "bcea154c686257c3"
          ],
          "title": "Packet Reflection Attack Mitigation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.4",
          "lines": [
            "   [NAN] analyzes authenticated encryption algorithms that provide nonce",
            "   privacy, referred to as \"Hide Nonce\" (HN) transforms.  The general",
            "   header protection construction in this document is one of those",
            "   algorithms (HN1).  Header protection is applied after the packet",
            "   protection AEAD, sampling a set of bytes (\"sample\") from the AEAD",
            "   output and encrypting the header field using a pseudorandom function",
            "   (PRF) as follows:",
            "",
            "   protected_field = field XOR PRF(hp_key, sample)",
            "",
            "   The header protection variants in this document use a pseudorandom",
            "   permutation (PRP) in place of a generic PRF.  However, since all PRPs",
            "   are also PRFs [IMC], these variants do not deviate from the HN1",
            "   construction.",
            "",
            "   As \"hp_key\" is distinct from the packet protection key, it follows",
            "   that header protection achieves AE2 security as defined in [NAN] and",
            "   therefore guarantees privacy of \"field\", the protected packet header.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13a726ded1b484d0",
                  "2c70cdac2be658ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Future header protection variants based on this construction MUST use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13a726ded1b484d0",
                  "2c70cdac2be658ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "a PRF to ensure equivalent security guarantees."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Use of the same key and ciphertext sample more than once risks",
            "   compromising header protection.  Protecting two different headers",
            "   with the same key and ciphertext sample reveals the exclusive OR of",
            "   the protected fields.  Assuming that the AEAD acts as a PRF, if L",
            "   bits are sampled, the odds of two ciphertext samples being identical",
            "   approach 2^(-L/2), that is, the birthday bound.  For the algorithms",
            "   described in this document, that probability is one in 2^64.",
            "",
            "   To prevent an attacker from modifying packet headers, the header is",
            "   transitively authenticated using packet protection; the entire packet",
            "   header is part of the authenticated additional data.  Protected",
            "   fields that are falsified or modified can only be detected once the",
            "   packet protection is removed."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2c70cdac2be658ab",
            "2c70cdac2be658ab"
          ],
          "title": "Header Protection Analysis"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.5",
          "lines": [
            "   An attacker could guess values for packet numbers or Key Phase and",
            "   have an endpoint confirm guesses through timing side channels.",
            "   Similarly, guesses for the packet number length can be tried and",
            "   exposed.  If the recipient of a packet discards packets with",
            "   duplicate packet numbers without attempting to remove packet",
            "   protection, they could reveal through timing side channels that the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   packet number matches a received packet.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0920eed442940b3d",
                  "409078de1a468b84",
                  "7005140a837b7a0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "For authentication to be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0920eed442940b3d",
                  "409078de1a468b84",
                  "7005140a837b7a0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "free from side channels, the entire process of header protection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0920eed442940b3d",
                  "409078de1a468b84",
                  "7005140a837b7a0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "removal, packet number recovery, and packet protection removal MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0920eed442940b3d",
                  "409078de1a468b84",
                  "7005140a837b7a0b"
                ],
                "status_id": 25,
                "text": "be applied together without timing and other side channels."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "53754ae8ea61233e",
                  "6b6ffff309f5c221"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "For the sending of packets, construction and protection of packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "53754ae8ea61233e",
                  "6b6ffff309f5c221"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "payloads and packet numbers MUST be free from side channels that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "53754ae8ea61233e",
                  "6b6ffff309f5c221"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "would reveal the packet number or its encoded size."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   During a key update, the time taken to generate new keys could reveal",
            "   through timing side channels that a key update has occurred.",
            "   Alternatively, where an attacker injects packets, this side channel",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   could reveal the value of the Key Phase on injected packets.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ca80978e16f737c"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "After"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ca80978e16f737c"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "receiving a key update, an endpoint SHOULD generate and save the next"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ca80978e16f737c"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "set of receive packet protection keys, as described in Section 6.3."
              }
            ],
            "   By generating new keys before a key update is received, receipt of",
            "   packets will not create timing signals that leak the value of the Key",
            "   Phase.",
            "",
            "   This depends on not doing this key generation during packet",
            "   processing, and it can require that endpoints maintain three sets of",
            "   packet protection keys for receiving: for the previous key phase, for",
            "   the current key phase, and for the next key phase.  Endpoints can",
            "   instead choose to defer generation of the next receive packet",
            "   protection keys until they discard old keys so that only two sets of",
            "   receive keys need to be retained at any point in time."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7005140a837b7a0b",
            "7005140a837b7a0b",
            "7005140a837b7a0b",
            "7005140a837b7a0b",
            "6b6ffff309f5c221",
            "6b6ffff309f5c221",
            "6b6ffff309f5c221",
            "4ca80978e16f737c",
            "4ca80978e16f737c",
            "4ca80978e16f737c"
          ],
          "title": "Header Protection Timing Side Channels"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.6",
          "lines": [
            "   In using TLS, the central key schedule of TLS is used.  As a result",
            "   of the TLS handshake messages being integrated into the calculation",
            "   of secrets, the inclusion of the QUIC transport parameters extension",
            "   ensures that the handshake and 1-RTT keys are not the same as those",
            "   that might be produced by a server running TLS over TCP.  To avoid",
            "   the possibility of cross-protocol key synchronization, additional",
            "   measures are provided to improve key separation.",
            "",
            "   The QUIC packet protection keys and IVs are derived using a different",
            "   label than the equivalent keys in TLS.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a4fea428cdb7f3e2",
                  "4ec23e3f6de38651"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "To preserve this separation, a new version of QUIC SHOULD define new"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a4fea428cdb7f3e2",
                  "4ec23e3f6de38651"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "labels for key derivation for packet protection key and IV, plus the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a4fea428cdb7f3e2",
                  "4ec23e3f6de38651"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "header protection keys."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This version of QUIC uses the string \"quic\"."
              }
            ],
            "   Other versions can use a version-specific label in place of that",
            "   string.",
            "",
            "   The initial secrets use a key that is specific to the negotiated QUIC",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   version.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6b9c791d85e5d9f9",
                  "ebf376eba13fb050"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "New QUIC versions SHOULD define a new salt value used in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6b9c791d85e5d9f9",
                  "ebf376eba13fb050"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "calculating initial secrets."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4ec23e3f6de38651",
            "4ec23e3f6de38651",
            "4ec23e3f6de38651",
            "ebf376eba13fb050",
            "ebf376eba13fb050"
          ],
          "title": "Key Diversity"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.7",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC depends on endpoints being able to generate secure random",
            "   numbers, both directly for protocol values such as the connection ID,",
            "   and transitively via TLS.  See [RFC4086] for guidance on secure",
            "   random number generation."
          ],
          "title": "Randomness"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10",
          "lines": [
            "   IANA has registered a codepoint of 57 (or 0x39) for the",
            "   quic_transport_parameters extension (defined in Section 8.2) in the",
            "   \"TLS ExtensionType Values\" registry [TLS-REGISTRIES].",
            "",
            "   The Recommended column for this extension is marked Yes. The TLS 1.3",
            "   Column includes CH (ClientHello) and EE (EncryptedExtensions).",
            "",
            "   +=======+===========================+=====+=============+===========+",
            "   | Value | Extension Name            | TLS | Recommended | Reference |",
            "   |       |                           | 1.3 |             |           |",
            "   +=======+===========================+=====+=============+===========+",
            "   |    57 | quic_transport_parameters | CH, | Y           | This      |",
            "   |       |                           | EE  |             | document  |",
            "   +-------+---------------------------+-----+-------------+-----------+",
            "",
            "              Table 2: TLS ExtensionType Values Registry Entry"
          ],
          "title": "IANA Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [AEAD]     McGrew, D., \"An Interface and Algorithms for Authenticated",
            "              Encryption\", RFC 5116, DOI 10.17487/RFC5116, January 2008,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc5116>.",
            "",
            "   [AES]      \"Advanced encryption standard (AES)\", National Institute",
            "              of Standards and Technology report,",
            "              DOI 10.6028/nist.fips.197, November 2001,",
            "              <https://doi.org/10.6028/nist.fips.197>.",
            "",
            "   [ALPN]     Friedl, S., Popov, A., Langley, A., and E. Stephan,",
            "              \"Transport Layer Security (TLS) Application-Layer Protocol",
            "              Negotiation Extension\", RFC 7301, DOI 10.17487/RFC7301,",
            "              July 2014, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7301>.",
            "",
            "   [CHACHA]   Nir, Y. and A. Langley, \"ChaCha20 and Poly1305 for IETF",
            "              Protocols\", RFC 8439, DOI 10.17487/RFC8439, June 2018,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8439>.",
            "",
            "   [HKDF]     Krawczyk, H. and P. Eronen, \"HMAC-based Extract-and-Expand",
            "              Key Derivation Function (HKDF)\", RFC 5869,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC5869, May 2010,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc5869>.",
            "",
            "   [QUIC-RECOVERY]",
            "              Iyengar, J., Ed. and I. Swett, Ed., \"QUIC Loss Detection",
            "              and Congestion Control\", RFC 9002, DOI 10.17487/RFC9002,",
            "              May 2021, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9002>.",
            "",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]",
            "              Iyengar, J., Ed. and M. Thomson, Ed., \"QUIC: A UDP-Based",
            "              Multiplexed and Secure Transport\", RFC 9000,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC9000, May 2021,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9000>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC2119]  Bradner, S., \"Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate",
            "              Requirement Levels\", BCP 14, RFC 2119,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC2119, March 1997,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2119>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC4086]  Eastlake 3rd, D., Schiller, J., and S. Crocker,",
            "              \"Randomness Requirements for Security\", BCP 106, RFC 4086,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC4086, June 2005,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc4086>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC8174]  Leiba, B., \"Ambiguity of Uppercase vs Lowercase in RFC",
            "              2119 Key Words\", BCP 14, RFC 8174, DOI 10.17487/RFC8174,",
            "              May 2017, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8174>.",
            "",
            "   [SHA]      Dang, Q., \"Secure Hash Standard\", National Institute of",
            "              Standards and Technology report,",
            "              DOI 10.6028/nist.fips.180-4, July 2015,",
            "              <https://doi.org/10.6028/nist.fips.180-4>.",
            "",
            "   [TLS-REGISTRIES]",
            "              Salowey, J. and S. Turner, \"IANA Registry Updates for TLS",
            "              and DTLS\", RFC 8447, DOI 10.17487/RFC8447, August 2018,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8447>.",
            "",
            "   [TLS13]    Rescorla, E., \"The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol",
            "              Version 1.3\", RFC 8446, DOI 10.17487/RFC8446, August 2018,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8446>."
          ],
          "title": "Normative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.2",
          "lines": [
            "   [AEBounds] Luykx, A. and K. Paterson, \"Limits on Authenticated",
            "              Encryption Use in TLS\", 28 August 2017,",
            "              <https://www.isg.rhul.ac.uk/~kp/TLS-AEbounds.pdf>.",
            "",
            "   [ASCII]    Cerf, V., \"ASCII format for network interchange\", STD 80,",
            "              RFC 20, DOI 10.17487/RFC0020, October 1969,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc20>.",
            "",
            "   [CCM-ANALYSIS]",
            "              Jonsson, J., \"On the Security of CTR + CBC-MAC\", Selected",
            "              Areas in Cryptography, SAC 2002, Lecture Notes in Computer",
            "              Science, vol 2595, pp. 76-93, DOI 10.1007/3-540-36492-7_7,",
            "              2003, <https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-36492-7_7>.",
            "",
            "   [COMPRESS] Ghedini, A. and V. Vasiliev, \"TLS Certificate",
            "              Compression\", RFC 8879, DOI 10.17487/RFC8879, December",
            "              2020, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8879>.",
            "",
            "   [GCM-MU]   Hoang, V., Tessaro, S., and A. Thiruvengadam, \"The Multi-",
            "              user Security of GCM, Revisited: Tight Bounds for Nonce",
            "              Randomization\", CCS '18: Proceedings of the 2018 ACM",
            "              SIGSAC Conference on Computer and Communications Security,",
            "              pp. 1429-1440, DOI 10.1145/3243734.3243816, 2018,",
            "              <https://doi.org/10.1145/3243734.3243816>.",
            "",
            "   [HTTP-REPLAY]",
            "              Thomson, M., Nottingham, M., and W. Tarreau, \"Using Early",
            "              Data in HTTP\", RFC 8470, DOI 10.17487/RFC8470, September",
            "              2018, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8470>.",
            "",
            "   [HTTP2-TLS13]",
            "              Benjamin, D., \"Using TLS 1.3 with HTTP/2\", RFC 8740,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC8740, February 2020,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8740>.",
            "",
            "   [IMC]      Katz, J. and Y. Lindell, \"Introduction to Modern",
            "              Cryptography, Second Edition\", ISBN 978-1466570269, 6",
            "              November 2014.",
            "",
            "   [NAN]      Bellare, M., Ng, R., and B. Tackmann, \"Nonces Are Noticed:",
            "              AEAD Revisited\", Advances in Cryptology - CRYPTO 2019,",
            "              Lecture Notes in Computer Science, vol 11692, pp. 235-265,",
            "              DOI 10.1007/978-3-030-26948-7_9, 2019,",
            "              <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-26948-7_9>.",
            "",
            "   [QUIC-HTTP]",
            "              Bishop, M., Ed., \"Hypertext Transfer Protocol Version 3",
            "              (HTTP/3)\", Work in Progress, Internet-Draft, draft-ietf-",
            "              quic-http-34, 2 February 2021,",
            "              <https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-quic-http-34>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC2818]  Rescorla, E., \"HTTP Over TLS\", RFC 2818,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC2818, May 2000,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2818>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC5280]  Cooper, D., Santesson, S., Farrell, S., Boeyen, S.,",
            "              Housley, R., and W. Polk, \"Internet X.509 Public Key",
            "              Infrastructure Certificate and Certificate Revocation List",
            "              (CRL) Profile\", RFC 5280, DOI 10.17487/RFC5280, May 2008,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc5280>.",
            "",
            "   [ROBUST]   Fischlin, M., Günther, F., and C. Janson, \"Robust",
            "              Channels: Handling Unreliable Networks in the Record",
            "              Layers of QUIC and DTLS 1.3\", 16 May 2020,",
            "              <https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/718>."
          ],
          "title": "Informative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A",
          "lines": [
            "   This section shows examples of packet protection so that",
            "   implementations can be verified incrementally.  Samples of Initial",
            "   packets from both client and server plus a Retry packet are defined.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfc72f68488f0259",
                  "98d57ec3959acd30"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "These packets use an 8-byte client-chosen Destination Connection ID"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfc72f68488f0259",
                  "98d57ec3959acd30"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "of 0x8394c8f03e515708."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Some intermediate values are included.  All"
              }
            ],
            "   values are shown in hexadecimal."
          ],
          "title": "Sample Packet Protection"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d4c074d2fa1ef3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The labels generated during the execution of the HKDF-Expand-Label"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d4c074d2fa1ef3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "function (that is, HkdfLabel.label) and part of the value given to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d4c074d2fa1ef3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the HKDF-Expand function in order to produce its output are:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0d4c074d2fa1ef3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "client in:  00200f746c73313320636c69656e7420696e00"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23e6ee57a2907434"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "server in:  00200f746c7331332073657276657220696e00"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c597486bb186912c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "quic key:  00100e746c7331332071756963206b657900"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c58817b3e9942a81"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "quic iv:  000c0d746c733133207175696320697600"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "15717eaef748cb7f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "quic hp:  00100d746c733133207175696320687000"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The initial secret is common:",
            "",
            "   initial_secret = HKDF-Extract(initial_salt, cid)",
            "       = 7db5df06e7a69e432496adedb0085192",
            "         3595221596ae2ae9fb8115c1e9ed0a44",
            "",
            "   The secrets for protecting client packets are:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2d9e44e4a1135986"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "client_initial_secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2d9e44e4a1135986"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret, \"client in\", \"\", 32)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2d9e44e4a1135986"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= c00cf151ca5be075ed0ebfb5c80323c4"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2d9e44e4a1135986"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "2d6b7db67881289af4008f1f6c357aea"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   key = HKDF-Expand-Label(client_initial_secret, \"quic key\", \"\", 16)",
            "       = 1f369613dd76d5467730efcbe3b1a22d",
            "",
            "   iv  = HKDF-Expand-Label(client_initial_secret, \"quic iv\", \"\", 12)",
            "       = fa044b2f42a3fd3b46fb255c",
            "",
            "   hp  = HKDF-Expand-Label(client_initial_secret, \"quic hp\", \"\", 16)",
            "       = 9f50449e04a0e810283a1e9933adedd2",
            "",
            "   The secrets for protecting server packets are:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa11ffc4777901b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "server_initial_secret"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa11ffc4777901b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= HKDF-Expand-Label(initial_secret, \"server in\", \"\", 32)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa11ffc4777901b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= 3c199828fd139efd216c155ad844cc81"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "         "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa11ffc4777901b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "fb82fa8d7446fa7d78be803acdda951b"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   key = HKDF-Expand-Label(server_initial_secret, \"quic key\", \"\", 16)",
            "       = cf3a5331653c364c88f0f379b6067e37",
            "",
            "   iv  = HKDF-Expand-Label(server_initial_secret, \"quic iv\", \"\", 12)",
            "       = 0ac1493ca1905853b0bba03e",
            "",
            "   hp  = HKDF-Expand-Label(server_initial_secret, \"quic hp\", \"\", 16)",
            "       = c206b8d9b9f0f37644430b490eeaa314"
          ],
          "title": "Keys"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The client sends an Initial packet.  The unprotected payload of this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet contains the following CRYPTO frame, plus enough PADDING"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "frames to make a 1162-byte payload:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "060040f1010000ed0303ebf8fa56f129 39b9584a3896472ec40bb863cfd3e868"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "04fe3a47f06a2b69484c000004130113 02010000c000000010000e00000b6578"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "616d706c652e636f6dff01000100000a 00080006001d00170018001000070005"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "04616c706e0005000501000000000033 00260024001d00209370b2c9caa47fba"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "baf4559fedba753de171fa71f50f1ce1 5d43e994ec74d748002b000302030400"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "0d0010000e0403050306030203080408 050806002d00020101001c0002400100"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "3900320408ffffffffffffffff050480 00ffff07048000ffff08011001048000"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1009a3ade3d74c5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "75300901100f088394c8f03e51570806 048000ffff"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a08fc6dd1452ae3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The unprotected header indicates a length of 1182 bytes: the 4-byte"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a08fc6dd1452ae3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet number, 1162 bytes of frames, and the 16-byte authentication"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a08fc6dd1452ae3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "tag.  The header includes the connection ID and a packet number of 2:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a08fc6dd1452ae3e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "c300000001088394c8f03e5157080000449e00000002"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Protecting the payload produces output that is sampled for header"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "protection.  Because the header uses a 4-byte packet number encoding,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the first 16 bytes of the protected payload is sampled and then"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "applied to the header as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "sample = d1b1c98dd7689fb8ec11d242b123dc9b"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "mask = AES-ECB(hp, sample)[0..4]"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "        "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= 437b9aec36"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "header[0] ^= mask[0] & 0x0f"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "        "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= c0"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "header[18..21] ^= mask[1..4]"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "        "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "= 7b9aec34"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0edf808a1032e31d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "header = c000000001088394c8f03e5157080000449e7b9aec34"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83c9da7019784665"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The resulting protected packet is:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83c9da7019784665"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "c000000001088394c8f03e5157080000 449e7b9aec34d1b1c98dd7689fb8ec11"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
