          ],
          "title": "Copyright Notice"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-table-of-contents",
          "lines": [
            "   1.  Introduction",
            "   2.  Conventions and Definitions",
            "   3.  Design of the QUIC Transmission Machinery",
            "   4.  Relevant Differences between QUIC and TCP",
            "     4.1.  Separate Packet Number Spaces",
            "     4.2.  Monotonically Increasing Packet Numbers",
            "     4.3.  Clearer Loss Epoch",
            "     4.4.  No Reneging",
            "     4.5.  More ACK Ranges",
            "     4.6.  Explicit Correction for Delayed Acknowledgments",
            "     4.7.  Probe Timeout Replaces RTO and TLP",
            "     4.8.  The Minimum Congestion Window Is Two Packets",
            "     4.9.  Handshake Packets Are Not Special",
            "   5.  Estimating the Round-Trip Time",
            "     5.1.  Generating RTT Samples",
            "     5.2.  Estimating min_rtt",
            "     5.3.  Estimating smoothed_rtt and rttvar",
            "   6.  Loss Detection",
            "     6.1.  Acknowledgment-Based Detection",
            "       6.1.1.  Packet Threshold",
            "       6.1.2.  Time Threshold",
            "     6.2.  Probe Timeout",
            "       6.2.1.  Computing PTO",
            "       6.2.2.  Handshakes and New Paths",
            "       6.2.3.  Speeding up Handshake Completion",
            "       6.2.4.  Sending Probe Packets",
            "     6.3.  Handling Retry Packets",
            "     6.4.  Discarding Keys and Packet State",
            "   7.  Congestion Control",
            "     7.1.  Explicit Congestion Notification",
            "     7.2.  Initial and Minimum Congestion Window",
            "     7.3.  Congestion Control States",
            "       7.3.1.  Slow Start",
            "       7.3.2.  Recovery",
            "       7.3.3.  Congestion Avoidance",
            "     7.4.  Ignoring Loss of Undecryptable Packets",
            "     7.5.  Probe Timeout",
            "     7.6.  Persistent Congestion",
            "       7.6.1.  Duration",
            "       7.6.2.  Establishing Persistent Congestion",
            "       7.6.3.  Example",
            "     7.7.  Pacing",
            "     7.8.  Underutilizing the Congestion Window",
            "   8.  Security Considerations",
            "     8.1.  Loss and Congestion Signals",
            "     8.2.  Traffic Analysis",
            "     8.3.  Misreporting ECN Markings",
            "   9.  References",
            "     9.1.  Normative References",
            "     9.2.  Informative References",
            "   Appendix A.  Loss Recovery Pseudocode",
            "     A.1.  Tracking Sent Packets",
            "       A.1.1.  Sent Packet Fields",
            "     A.2.  Constants of Interest",
            "     A.3.  Variables of Interest",
            "     A.4.  Initialization",
            "     A.5.  On Sending a Packet",
            "     A.6.  On Receiving a Datagram",
            "     A.7.  On Receiving an Acknowledgment",
            "     A.8.  Setting the Loss Detection Timer",
            "     A.9.  On Timeout",
            "     A.10. Detecting Lost Packets",
            "     A.11. Upon Dropping Initial or Handshake Keys",
            "   Appendix B.  Congestion Control Pseudocode",
            "     B.1.  Constants of Interest",
            "     B.2.  Variables of Interest",
            "     B.3.  Initialization",
            "     B.4.  On Packet Sent",
            "     B.5.  On Packet Acknowledgment",
            "     B.6.  On New Congestion Event",
            "     B.7.  Process ECN Information",
            "     B.8.  On Packets Lost",
            "     B.9.  Removing Discarded Packets from Bytes in Flight",
            "   Contributors",
            "   Authors' Addresses"
          ],
          "title": "Table of Contents"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC is a secure, general-purpose transport protocol, described in",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  This document describes loss detection and",
            "   congestion control mechanisms for QUIC."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"NOT RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and",
            "   \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP",
            "   14 [RFC2119] [RFC8174] when, and only when, they appear in all",
            "   capitals, as shown here.",
            "",
            "   Definitions of terms that are used in this document:",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2efbb435e95bd25e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Ack-eliciting frames:  All frames other than ACK, PADDING, and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2efbb435e95bd25e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "CONNECTION_CLOSE are considered ack-eliciting."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37da5e4a96d2e8b4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Ack-eliciting packets:  Packets that contain ack-eliciting frames"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37da5e4a96d2e8b4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "elicit an ACK from the receiver within the maximum acknowledgment"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37da5e4a96d2e8b4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "delay and are called ack-eliciting packets."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   In-flight packets:  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "033b8b36ecff8f1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Packets are considered in flight when they are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "033b8b36ecff8f1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "ack-eliciting or contain a PADDING frame"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": ", and they have been sent"
              }
            ],
            "      but are not acknowledged, declared lost, or discarded along with",
            "      old keys."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions and Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [
            "   All transmissions in QUIC are sent with a packet-level header, which",
            "   indicates the encryption level and includes a packet sequence number",
            "   (referred to below as a packet number).  The encryption level",
            "   indicates the packet number space, as described in Section 12.3 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  Packet numbers never repeat within a packet number",
            "   space for the lifetime of a connection.  Packet numbers are sent in",
            "   monotonically increasing order within a space, preventing ambiguity.",
            "   It is permitted for some packet numbers to never be used, leaving",
            "   intentional gaps.",
            "",
            "   This design obviates the need for disambiguating between",
            "   transmissions and retransmissions; this eliminates significant",
            "   complexity from QUIC's interpretation of TCP loss detection",
            "   mechanisms.",
            "",
            "   QUIC packets can contain multiple frames of different types.  The",
            "   recovery mechanisms ensure that data and frames that need reliable",
            "   delivery are acknowledged or declared lost and sent in new packets as",
            "   necessary.  The types of frames contained in a packet affect recovery",
            "   and congestion control logic:",
            "",
            "   *  All packets are acknowledged, though packets that contain no ack-",
            "      eliciting frames are only acknowledged along with ack-eliciting",
            "      packets.",
            "",
            "   *  Long header packets that contain CRYPTO frames are critical to the",
            "      performance of the QUIC handshake and use shorter timers for",
            "      acknowledgment.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   *  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "273599fb1c7f15ff",
                  "558f55d751b2367e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Packets containing frames besides ACK or CONNECTION_CLOSE frames"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "273599fb1c7f15ff",
                  "558f55d751b2367e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "count toward congestion control limits and are considered to be in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "273599fb1c7f15ff",
                  "558f55d751b2367e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "flight."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   *  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fdac12e4a1f70443"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "PADDING frames cause packets to contribute toward bytes in flight"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fdac12e4a1f70443"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "without directly causing an acknowledgment to be sent."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "title": "Design of the QUIC Transmission Machinery"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [
            "   Readers familiar with TCP's loss detection and congestion control",
            "   will find algorithms here that parallel well-known TCP ones.",
            "   However, protocol differences between QUIC and TCP contribute to",
            "   algorithmic differences.  These protocol differences are briefly",
            "   described below."
          ],
          "title": "Relevant Differences between QUIC and TCP"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC uses separate packet number spaces for each encryption level,",
            "   except 0-RTT and all generations of 1-RTT keys use the same packet",
            "   number space.  Separate packet number spaces ensures that the",
            "   acknowledgment of packets sent with one level of encryption will not",
            "   cause spurious retransmission of packets sent with a different",
            "   encryption level.  Congestion control and round-trip time (RTT)",
            "   measurement are unified across packet number spaces."
          ],
          "title": "Separate Packet Number Spaces"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   TCP conflates transmission order at the sender with delivery order at",
            "   the receiver, resulting in the retransmission ambiguity problem",
            "   [RETRANSMISSION].  QUIC separates transmission order from delivery",
            "   order: packet numbers indicate transmission order, and delivery order",
            "   is determined by the stream offsets in STREAM frames.",
            "",
            "   QUIC's packet number is strictly increasing within a packet number",
            "   space and directly encodes transmission order.  A higher packet",
            "   number signifies that the packet was sent later, and a lower packet",
            "   number signifies that the packet was sent earlier.  When a packet",
            "   containing ack-eliciting frames is detected lost, QUIC includes",
            "   necessary frames in a new packet with a new packet number, removing",
            "   ambiguity about which packet is acknowledged when an ACK is received.",
            "   Consequently, more accurate RTT measurements can be made, spurious",
            "   retransmissions are trivially detected, and mechanisms such as Fast",
            "   Retransmit can be applied universally, based only on packet number.",
            "",
            "   This design point significantly simplifies loss detection mechanisms",
            "   for QUIC.  Most TCP mechanisms implicitly attempt to infer",
            "   transmission ordering based on TCP sequence numbers -- a nontrivial",
            "   task, especially when TCP timestamps are not available."
          ],
          "title": "Monotonically Increasing Packet Numbers"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC starts a loss epoch when a packet is lost.  The loss epoch ends",
            "   when any packet sent after the start of the epoch is acknowledged.",
            "   TCP waits for the gap in the sequence number space to be filled, and",
            "   so if a segment is lost multiple times in a row, the loss epoch may",
            "   not end for several round trips.  Because both should reduce their",
            "   congestion windows only once per epoch, QUIC will do it once for",
            "   every round trip that experiences loss, while TCP may only do it once",
            "   across multiple round trips."
          ],
          "title": "Clearer Loss Epoch"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC ACK frames contain information similar to that in TCP Selective",
            "   Acknowledgments (SACKs) [RFC2018].  However, QUIC does not allow a",
            "   packet acknowledgment to be reneged, greatly simplifying",
            "   implementations on both sides and reducing memory pressure on the",
            "   sender."
          ],
          "title": "No Reneging"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.5",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC supports many ACK ranges, as opposed to TCP's three SACK ranges.",
            "   In high-loss environments, this speeds recovery, reduces spurious",
            "   retransmits, and ensures forward progress without relying on",
            "   timeouts."
          ],
          "title": "More ACK Ranges"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC endpoints measure the delay incurred between when a packet is",
            "   received and when the corresponding acknowledgment is sent, allowing",
            "   a peer to maintain a more accurate RTT estimate; see Section 13.2 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
          ],
          "title": "Explicit Correction for Delayed Acknowledgments"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.7",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC uses a probe timeout (PTO; see Section 6.2), with a timer based",
            "   on TCP's retransmission timeout (RTO) computation; see [RFC6298].",
            "   QUIC's PTO includes the peer's maximum expected acknowledgment delay",
            "   instead of using a fixed minimum timeout.",
            "",
            "   Similar to the RACK-TLP loss detection algorithm for TCP [RFC8985],",
            "   QUIC does not collapse the congestion window when the PTO expires,",
            "   since a single packet loss at the tail does not indicate persistent",
            "   congestion.  Instead, QUIC collapses the congestion window when",
            "   persistent congestion is declared; see Section 7.6.  In doing this,",
            "   QUIC avoids unnecessary congestion window reductions, obviating the",
            "   need for correcting mechanisms such as Forward RTO-Recovery (F-RTO)",
            "   [RFC5682].  Since QUIC does not collapse the congestion window on a",
            "   PTO expiration, a QUIC sender is not limited from sending more in-",
            "   flight packets after a PTO expiration if it still has available",
            "   congestion window.  This occurs when a sender is application limited",
            "   and the PTO timer expires.  This is more aggressive than TCP's RTO",
            "   mechanism when application limited, but identical when not",
            "   application limited.",
            "",
            "   QUIC allows probe packets to temporarily exceed the congestion window",
            "   whenever the timer expires."
          ],
          "title": "Probe Timeout Replaces RTO and TLP"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.8",
          "lines": [
            "   TCP uses a minimum congestion window of one packet.  However, loss of",
            "   that single packet means that the sender needs to wait for a PTO to",
            "   recover (Section 6.2), which can be much longer than an RTT.  Sending",
            "   a single ack-eliciting packet also increases the chances of incurring",
            "   additional latency when a receiver delays its acknowledgment.",
            "",
            "   QUIC therefore recommends that the minimum congestion window be two",
            "   packets.  While this increases network load, it is considered safe",
            "   since the sender will still reduce its sending rate exponentially",
            "   under persistent congestion (Section 6.2)."
          ],
          "title": "The Minimum Congestion Window Is Two Packets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.9",
          "lines": [
            "   TCP treats the loss of SYN or SYN-ACK packet as persistent congestion",
            "   and reduces the congestion window to one packet; see [RFC5681].  QUIC",
            "   treats loss of a packet containing handshake data the same as other",
            "   losses."
          ],
          "title": "Handshake Packets Are Not Special"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   At a high level, an endpoint measures the time from when a packet was",
            "   sent to when it is acknowledged as an RTT sample.  The endpoint uses",
            "   RTT samples and peer-reported host delays (see Section 13.2 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) to generate a statistical description of the",
            "   network path's RTT.  An endpoint computes the following three values",
            "   for each path: the minimum value over a period of time (min_rtt), an",
            "   exponentially weighted moving average (smoothed_rtt), and the mean",
            "   deviation (referred to as \"variation\" in the rest of this document)",
            "   in the observed RTT samples (rttvar)."
          ],
          "title": "Estimating the Round-Trip Time"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06be693fbf3aa30c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "An endpoint generates an RTT sample on receiving an ACK frame that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06be693fbf3aa30c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "meets the following two conditions:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06be693fbf3aa30c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  the largest acknowledged packet number is newly acknowledged, and"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "06be693fbf3aa30c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  at least one of the newly acknowledged packets was ack-eliciting."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The RTT sample, latest_rtt, is generated as the time elapsed since",
            "   the largest acknowledged packet was sent:",
            "",
            "   latest_rtt = ack_time - send_time_of_largest_acked",
            "",
            "   An RTT sample is generated using only the largest acknowledged packet",
            "   in the received ACK frame.  This is because a peer reports",
            "   acknowledgment delays for only the largest acknowledged packet in an",
            "   ACK frame.  While the reported acknowledgment delay is not used by",
            "   the RTT sample measurement, it is used to adjust the RTT sample in",
            "   subsequent computations of smoothed_rtt and rttvar (Section 5.3).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d561c2a6971145fb",
                  "f0e771eb4dbe72cf",
                  "30366f5989233f4a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "To avoid generating multiple RTT samples for a single packet, an ACK"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d561c2a6971145fb",
                  "f0e771eb4dbe72cf",
                  "30366f5989233f4a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "frame SHOULD NOT be used to update RTT estimates if it does not newly"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d561c2a6971145fb",
                  "f0e771eb4dbe72cf",
                  "30366f5989233f4a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "acknowledge the largest acknowledged packet."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11166da2d2bfe684",
                  "bec31b36bba0fe18",
                  "a2caaec3050db9df"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "An RTT sample MUST NOT be generated on receiving an ACK frame that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "11166da2d2bfe684",
                  "bec31b36bba0fe18",
                  "a2caaec3050db9df"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "does not newly acknowledge at least one ack-eliciting packet."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  A peer"
              }
            ],
            "   usually does not send an ACK frame when only non-ack-eliciting",
            "   packets are received.  Therefore, an ACK frame that contains",
            "   acknowledgments for only non-ack-eliciting packets could include an",
            "   arbitrarily large ACK Delay value.  Ignoring such ACK frames avoids",
            "   complications in subsequent smoothed_rtt and rttvar computations.",
            "",
            "   A sender might generate multiple RTT samples per RTT when multiple",
            "   ACK frames are received within an RTT.  As suggested in [RFC6298],",
            "   doing so might result in inadequate history in smoothed_rtt and",
            "   rttvar.  Ensuring that RTT estimates retain sufficient history is an",
            "   open research question."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "30366f5989233f4a",
            "30366f5989233f4a",
            "30366f5989233f4a",
            "a2caaec3050db9df",
            "a2caaec3050db9df"
          ],
          "title": "Generating RTT Samples"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.2",
          "lines": [
            "   min_rtt is the sender's estimate of the minimum RTT observed for a",
            "   given network path over a period of time.  In this document, min_rtt",
            "   is used by loss detection to reject implausibly small RTT samples.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23ebf841357e91a4",
                  "f8a5fa09bac58f72",
                  "0ad1df424f066d8e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "min_rtt MUST be set to the latest_rtt on the first RTT sample."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "186f4960aa82fcc3",
                  "347b1679ab91e7fa",
                  "dfbc703486f10bbf"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "min_rtt MUST be set to the lesser of min_rtt and latest_rtt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "186f4960aa82fcc3",
                  "347b1679ab91e7fa",
                  "dfbc703486f10bbf"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "(Section 5.1) on all other samples."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   An endpoint uses only locally observed times in computing the min_rtt",
            "   and does not adjust for acknowledgment delays reported by the peer.",
            "   Doing so allows the endpoint to set a lower bound for the",
            "   smoothed_rtt based entirely on what it observes (see Section 5.3) and",
            "   limits potential underestimation due to erroneously reported delays",
            "   by the peer.",
            "",
            "   The RTT for a network path may change over time.  If a path's actual",
            "   RTT decreases, the min_rtt will adapt immediately on the first low",
            "   sample.  If the path's actual RTT increases, however, the min_rtt",
            "   will not adapt to it, allowing future RTT samples that are smaller",
            "   than the new RTT to be included in smoothed_rtt.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "46db57fc3684cf2f",
                  "0080620a0a2a1a14",
                  "7ce5d2f26e71341e",
                  "c5cd63a12e5a6236",
                  "3107573d5f2c1be9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Endpoints SHOULD set the min_rtt to the newest RTT sample after"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "46db57fc3684cf2f",
                  "0080620a0a2a1a14",
                  "7ce5d2f26e71341e",
                  "c5cd63a12e5a6236",
                  "3107573d5f2c1be9"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "persistent congestion is established."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This avoids repeatedly"
              }
            ],
            "   declaring persistent congestion when the RTT increases.  This also",
            "   allows a connection to reset its estimate of min_rtt and smoothed_rtt",
            "   after a disruptive network event; see Section 5.3.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b463d78740c1506",
                  "0fc98c3b448b7dc0"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Endpoints MAY reestablish the min_rtt at other times in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b463d78740c1506",
                  "0fc98c3b448b7dc0"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "connection, such as when traffic volume is low and an acknowledgment"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b463d78740c1506",
                  "0fc98c3b448b7dc0"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "is received with a low acknowledgment delay."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3770d887cc5c0992",
                  "0f18efeb842adc87"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "Implementations SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3770d887cc5c0992",
                  "0f18efeb842adc87"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "NOT refresh the min_rtt value too often since the actual minimum RTT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3770d887cc5c0992",
                  "0f18efeb842adc87"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "of the path is not frequently observable."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "0ad1df424f066d8e",
            "dfbc703486f10bbf",
            "dfbc703486f10bbf",
            "3107573d5f2c1be9",
            "3107573d5f2c1be9",
            "0fc98c3b448b7dc0",
            "0fc98c3b448b7dc0",
            "0fc98c3b448b7dc0",
            "0f18efeb842adc87",
            "0f18efeb842adc87",
            "0f18efeb842adc87"
          ],
          "title": "Estimating min_rtt"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.3",
          "lines": [
            "   smoothed_rtt is an exponentially weighted moving average of an",
            "   endpoint's RTT samples, and rttvar estimates the variation in the RTT",
            "   samples using a mean variation.",
            "",
            "   The calculation of smoothed_rtt uses RTT samples after adjusting them",
            "   for acknowledgment delays.  These delays are decoded from the ACK",
            "   Delay field of ACK frames as described in Section 19.3 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   The peer might report acknowledgment delays that are larger than the",
            "   peer's max_ack_delay during the handshake (Section 13.2.1 of",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a5eb849c74868d1",
                  "11f224b0fbbb9895",
                  "297380de9761d246"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "To account for this, the endpoint SHOULD ignore"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a5eb849c74868d1",
                  "11f224b0fbbb9895",
                  "297380de9761d246"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "max_ack_delay until the handshake is confirmed, as defined in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8a5eb849c74868d1",
                  "11f224b0fbbb9895",
                  "297380de9761d246"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  When they occur, these large"
              }
            ],
            "   acknowledgment delays are likely to be non-repeating and limited to",
            "   the handshake.  The endpoint can therefore use them without limiting",
            "   them to the max_ack_delay, avoiding unnecessary inflation of the RTT",
            "   estimate.",
            "",
            "   Note that a large acknowledgment delay can result in a substantially",
            "   inflated smoothed_rtt if there is an error either in the peer's",
            "   reporting of the acknowledgment delay or in the endpoint's min_rtt",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   estimate.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd487125fa58a81c",
                  "dbe52249c8c602b8",
                  "4316cff8be451e7f"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Therefore, prior to handshake confirmation, an endpoint"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd487125fa58a81c",
                  "dbe52249c8c602b8",
                  "4316cff8be451e7f"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "MAY ignore RTT samples if adjusting the RTT sample for acknowledgment"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd487125fa58a81c",
                  "dbe52249c8c602b8",
                  "4316cff8be451e7f"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "delay causes the sample to be less than the min_rtt."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   After the handshake is confirmed, any acknowledgment delays reported",
            "   by the peer that are greater than the peer's max_ack_delay are",
            "   attributed to unintentional but potentially repeating delays, such as",
            "   scheduler latency at the peer or loss of previous acknowledgments.",
            "   Excess delays could also be due to a noncompliant receiver.",
            "   Therefore, these extra delays are considered effectively part of path",
            "   delay and incorporated into the RTT estimate.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Therefore, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e4285b013065e5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "when adjusting an RTT sample using peer-reported"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e4285b013065e5d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "acknowledgment delays, an endpoint:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e4285b013065e5d",
                  "11cc2c049fc8f475",
                  "078235cc849f37bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "*  MAY ignore the acknowledgment delay for Initial packets, since"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e4285b013065e5d",
                  "078235cc849f37bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "these acknowledgments are not delayed by the peer (Section 13.2.1"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e4285b013065e5d",
                  "078235cc849f37bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]);"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "841529c88d7393e4",
                  "e971e3d6e543adc7",
                  "0e0430f6455f6ee4"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "*  SHOULD ignore the peer's max_ack_delay until the handshake is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "841529c88d7393e4",
                  "e971e3d6e543adc7",
                  "0e0430f6455f6ee4"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "confirmed;"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae07a593a5e1494b",
                  "83269f2e9c58a82d",
                  "25043f14f27bfdc4",
                  "78cbfd9c8f5b1bc0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "*  MUST use the lesser of the acknowledgment delay and the peer's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae07a593a5e1494b",
                  "83269f2e9c58a82d",
                  "25043f14f27bfdc4",
                  "78cbfd9c8f5b1bc0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "max_ack_delay after the handshake is confirmed;"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae07a593a5e1494b",
                  "25043f14f27bfdc4",
                  "78cbfd9c8f5b1bc0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": " and"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35352745e00c890e",
                  "00b9c8c9a5c60229",
                  "4162916a03fb1fb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "*  MUST NOT subtract the acknowledgment delay from the RTT sample if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35352745e00c890e",
                  "00b9c8c9a5c60229",
                  "4162916a03fb1fb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "the resulting value is smaller than the min_rtt."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This limits the"
              }
            ],
            "      underestimation of the smoothed_rtt due to a misreporting peer.",
            "",
            "   Additionally, an endpoint might postpone the processing of",
            "   acknowledgments when the corresponding decryption keys are not",
            "   immediately available.  For example, a client might receive an",
            "   acknowledgment for a 0-RTT packet that it cannot decrypt because",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   1-RTT packet protection keys are not yet available to it.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e15246eb8affcaad",
                  "860e6682ce4cedb4"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "In such"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e15246eb8affcaad",
                  "860e6682ce4cedb4"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "cases, an endpoint SHOULD subtract such local delays from its RTT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e15246eb8affcaad",
                  "860e6682ce4cedb4"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "sample until the handshake is confirmed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Similar to [RFC6298], smoothed_rtt and rttvar are computed as",
            "   follows.",
            "",
            "   An endpoint initializes the RTT estimator during connection",
            "   establishment and when the estimator is reset during connection",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   migration; see Section 9.4 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b59f9cc03a858b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Before any RTT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b59f9cc03a858b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "samples are available for a new path or when the estimator is reset,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b59f9cc03a858b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the estimator is initialized using the initial RTT; see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b59f9cc03a858b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 6.2.2."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b59f9cc03a858b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "smoothed_rtt and rttvar are initialized as follows, where kInitialRtt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b59f9cc03a858b36"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "contains the initial RTT value:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   smoothed_rtt = kInitialRtt",
            "   rttvar = kInitialRtt / 2",
            "",
            "   RTT samples for the network path are recorded in latest_rtt; see",
            "   Section 5.1.  On the first RTT sample after initialization, the",
            "   estimator is reset using that sample.  This ensures that the",
            "   estimator retains no history of past samples.  Packets sent on other",
            "   paths do not contribute RTT samples to the current path, as described",
            "   in Section 9.4 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3acd98099138c57b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "On the first RTT sample after initialization, smoothed_rtt and rttvar"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3acd98099138c57b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "are set as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3acd98099138c57b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "smoothed_rtt = latest_rtt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3acd98099138c57b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "rttvar = latest_rtt / 2"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "On subsequent RTT samples, smoothed_rtt and rttvar evolve as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ack_delay = decoded acknowledgment delay from ACK frame"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "if (handshake confirmed):"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ack_delay = min(ack_delay, max_ack_delay)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "adjusted_rtt = latest_rtt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "if (latest_rtt >= min_rtt + ack_delay):"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "adjusted_rtt = latest_rtt - ack_delay"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "smoothed_rtt = 7/8 * smoothed_rtt + 1/8 * adjusted_rtt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "rttvar_sample = abs(smoothed_rtt - adjusted_rtt)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d3cf8ee4749535ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "rttvar = 3/4 * rttvar + 1/4 * rttvar_sample"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "297380de9761d246",
            "297380de9761d246",
            "297380de9761d246",
            "4316cff8be451e7f",
            "4316cff8be451e7f",
            "4316cff8be451e7f",
            "078235cc849f37bc",
            "078235cc849f37bc",
            "078235cc849f37bc",
            "0e0430f6455f6ee4",
            "0e0430f6455f6ee4",
            "78cbfd9c8f5b1bc0",
            "78cbfd9c8f5b1bc0",
            "4162916a03fb1fb0",
            "4162916a03fb1fb0",
            "860e6682ce4cedb4",
            "860e6682ce4cedb4",
            "860e6682ce4cedb4"
          ],
          "title": "Estimating smoothed_rtt and rttvar"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC senders use acknowledgments to detect lost packets and a PTO to",
            "   ensure acknowledgments are received; see Section 6.2.  This section",
            "   provides a description of these algorithms.",
            "",
            "   If a packet is lost, the QUIC transport needs to recover from that",
            "   loss, such as by retransmitting the data, sending an updated frame,",
            "   or discarding the frame.  For more information, see Section 13.3 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   Loss detection is separate per packet number space, unlike RTT",
            "   measurement and congestion control, because RTT and congestion",
            "   control are properties of the path, whereas loss detection also",
            "   relies upon key availability."
          ],
          "title": "Loss Detection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Acknowledgment-based loss detection implements the spirit of TCP's",
            "   Fast Retransmit [RFC5681], Early Retransmit [RFC5827], Forward",
            "   Acknowledgment [FACK], SACK loss recovery [RFC6675], and RACK-TLP",
            "   [RFC8985].  This section provides an overview of how these algorithms",
            "   are implemented in QUIC.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29557453ab628c65"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A packet is declared lost if it meets all of the following"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29557453ab628c65"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "conditions:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29557453ab628c65"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  The packet is unacknowledged, in flight, and was sent prior to an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29557453ab628c65"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "acknowledged packet."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29557453ab628c65"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  The packet was sent kPacketThreshold packets before an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29557453ab628c65"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "acknowledged packet (Section 6.1.1), or it was sent long enough in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "29557453ab628c65"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the past (Section 6.1.2)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The acknowledgment indicates that a packet sent later was delivered,",
            "   and the packet and time thresholds provide some tolerance for packet",
            "   reordering.",
            "",
            "   Spuriously declaring packets as lost leads to unnecessary",
            "   retransmissions and may result in degraded performance due to the",
            "   actions of the congestion controller upon detecting loss.",
            "   Implementations can detect spurious retransmissions and increase the",
            "   packet or time reordering threshold to reduce future spurious",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   retransmissions and loss events.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65ea1316449b5532",
                  "179dc30e32127dfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Implementations with adaptive time"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65ea1316449b5532",
                  "179dc30e32127dfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "thresholds MAY choose to start with smaller initial reordering"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "65ea1316449b5532",
                  "179dc30e32127dfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "thresholds to minimize recovery latency."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "179dc30e32127dfe",
            "179dc30e32127dfe",
            "179dc30e32127dfe"
          ],
          "title": "Acknowledgment-Based Detection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.1.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04fdbaaa99ae6be9",
                  "abb7cf127c9cd3cf",
                  "f2ab3eb9477c7f5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The RECOMMENDED initial value for the packet reordering threshold"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04fdbaaa99ae6be9",
                  "abb7cf127c9cd3cf",
                  "f2ab3eb9477c7f5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "(kPacketThreshold) is 3, based on best practices for TCP loss"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04fdbaaa99ae6be9",
                  "abb7cf127c9cd3cf",
                  "f2ab3eb9477c7f5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "detection [RFC5681] [RFC6675]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04fdbaaa99ae6be9"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04fdbaaa99ae6be9",
                  "161a9bc2bd881036",
                  "d50ce1d23d0bd6a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "In order to remain similar to TCP,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04fdbaaa99ae6be9",
                  "161a9bc2bd881036",
                  "d50ce1d23d0bd6a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "implementations SHOULD NOT use a packet threshold less than 3; see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04fdbaaa99ae6be9",
                  "161a9bc2bd881036",
                  "d50ce1d23d0bd6a2"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "[RFC5681]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Some networks may exhibit higher degrees of packet reordering,",
            "   causing a sender to detect spurious losses.  Additionally, packet",
            "   reordering could be more common with QUIC than TCP because network",
            "   elements that could observe and reorder TCP packets cannot do that",
            "   for QUIC and also because QUIC packet numbers are encrypted.",
            "   Algorithms that increase the reordering threshold after spuriously",
            "   detecting losses, such as RACK [RFC8985], have proven to be useful in",
            "   TCP and are expected to be at least as useful in QUIC."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f2ab3eb9477c7f5a",
            "f2ab3eb9477c7f5a",
            "f2ab3eb9477c7f5a",
            "d50ce1d23d0bd6a2",
            "d50ce1d23d0bd6a2",
            "d50ce1d23d0bd6a2"
          ],
          "title": "Packet Threshold"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.1.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43001241a1e625f5",
                  "70405a31ed5d8975",
                  "9a631063a214836a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Once a later packet within the same packet number space has been"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43001241a1e625f5",
                  "70405a31ed5d8975",
                  "9a631063a214836a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "acknowledged, an endpoint SHOULD declare an earlier packet lost if it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "43001241a1e625f5",
                  "70405a31ed5d8975",
                  "9a631063a214836a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "was sent a threshold amount of time in the past."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e69ba4620851bfa",
                  "b106b2d2ed37f029",
                  "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "To avoid declaring"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e69ba4620851bfa",
                  "b106b2d2ed37f029",
                  "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "packets as lost too early, this time threshold MUST be set to at"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e69ba4620851bfa",
                  "b106b2d2ed37f029",
                  "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "least the local timer granularity, as indicated by the kGranularity"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7e69ba4620851bfa",
                  "b106b2d2ed37f029",
                  "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "constant."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a2068dd1bad87a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The time threshold is:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5a2068dd1bad87a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "max(kTimeThreshold * max(smoothed_rtt, latest_rtt), kGranularity)"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2082ecfda240a082",
                  "0c5f974e5584f76f",
                  "4a603cfeb1739748"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "If packets sent prior to the largest acknowledged packet cannot yet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2082ecfda240a082",
                  "0c5f974e5584f76f",
                  "4a603cfeb1739748"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "be declared lost, then a timer SHOULD be set for the remaining time."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Using max(smoothed_rtt, latest_rtt) protects from the two following",
            "   cases:",
            "",
            "   *  the latest RTT sample is lower than the smoothed RTT, perhaps due",
            "      to reordering where the acknowledgment encountered a shorter path;",
            "",
            "   *  the latest RTT sample is higher than the smoothed RTT, perhaps due",
            "      to a sustained increase in the actual RTT, but the smoothed RTT",
            "      has not yet caught up.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35512c0db9658474",
                  "82240dd2d9c53533",
                  "5584ded4937204b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The RECOMMENDED time threshold (kTimeThreshold), expressed as an RTT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35512c0db9658474",
                  "82240dd2d9c53533",
                  "5584ded4937204b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "multiplier, is 9/8."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6468572b659f3298",
                  "5f02e6c590a0c6be",
                  "debabb64eb1f6cb4"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The RECOMMENDED value of the timer granularity"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6468572b659f3298",
                  "5f02e6c590a0c6be",
                  "debabb64eb1f6cb4"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "(kGranularity) is 1 millisecond."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "      |  Note: TCP's RACK [RFC8985] specifies a slightly larger",
            "      |  threshold, equivalent to 5/4, for a similar purpose.",
            "      |  Experience with QUIC shows that 9/8 works well.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e1caec4bd859f4e",
                  "afbac7a0811efe43"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Implementations MAY experiment with absolute thresholds, thresholds"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e1caec4bd859f4e",
                  "afbac7a0811efe43"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "from previous connections, adaptive thresholds, or the including of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3e1caec4bd859f4e",
                  "afbac7a0811efe43"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "RTT variation."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Smaller thresholds reduce reordering resilience and"
              }
            ],
            "   increase spurious retransmissions, and larger thresholds increase",
            "   loss detection delay."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9a631063a214836a",
            "9a631063a214836a",
            "9a631063a214836a",
            "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2",
            "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2",
            "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2",
            "5fa2ce2ae1b306b2",
            "4a603cfeb1739748",
            "4a603cfeb1739748",
            "5584ded4937204b8",
            "5584ded4937204b8",
            "debabb64eb1f6cb4",
            "debabb64eb1f6cb4",
            "afbac7a0811efe43",
            "afbac7a0811efe43",
            "afbac7a0811efe43"
          ],
          "title": "Time Threshold"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf411599b8e09400"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A Probe Timeout (PTO) triggers the sending of one or two probe"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf411599b8e09400"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "datagrams when ack-eliciting packets are not acknowledged within the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf411599b8e09400"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "expected period of time or the server may not have validated the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf411599b8e09400"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "client's address.  A PTO enables a connection to recover from loss of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf411599b8e09400"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "tail packets or acknowledgments."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   As with loss detection, the PTO is per packet number space.  That is,",
            "   a PTO value is computed per packet number space.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "619f4e4b5888fc3c",
                  "1266287e0b2528e4",
                  "96d4dd072e49509b"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A PTO timer expiration event does not indicate packet loss and MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "619f4e4b5888fc3c",
                  "1266287e0b2528e4",
                  "96d4dd072e49509b"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "NOT cause prior unacknowledged packets to be marked as lost."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  When an"
              }
            ],
            "   acknowledgment is received that newly acknowledges packets, loss",
            "   detection proceeds as dictated by the packet and time threshold",
            "   mechanisms; see Section 6.1.",
            "",
            "   The PTO algorithm used in QUIC implements the reliability functions",
            "   of Tail Loss Probe [RFC8985], RTO [RFC5681], and F-RTO algorithms for",
            "   TCP [RFC5682].  The timeout computation is based on TCP's RTO period",
            "   [RFC6298]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "96d4dd072e49509b",
            "96d4dd072e49509b"
          ],
          "title": "Probe Timeout"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35184366f667ec58",
                  "4d218ad71c593273"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "When an ack-eliciting packet is transmitted, the sender schedules a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35184366f667ec58",
                  "4d218ad71c593273"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "timer for the PTO period as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35184366f667ec58",
                  "4d218ad71c593273"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "PTO = smoothed_rtt + max(4*rttvar, kGranularity) + max_ack_delay"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5040cc1ae20351f7",
                  "66164cdfa3a7375b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The PTO period is the amount of time that a sender ought to wait for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5040cc1ae20351f7",
                  "66164cdfa3a7375b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "an acknowledgment of a sent packet."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This time period includes the"
              }
            ],
            "   estimated network RTT (smoothed_rtt), the variation in the estimate",
            "   (4*rttvar), and max_ack_delay, to account for the maximum time by",
            "   which a receiver might delay sending an acknowledgment.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb62b97d5cd685a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "When the PTO is armed for Initial or Handshake packet number spaces,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb62b97d5cd685a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the max_ack_delay in the PTO period computation is set to 0, since"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb62b97d5cd685a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the peer is expected to not delay these packets intentionally; see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb62b97d5cd685a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 13.2.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ac90f508dcc2554",
                  "57c27658044ffcd3",
                  "e4b0cd8fe7ad3df2",
                  "980f088aed264721"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The PTO period MUST be at least kGranularity to avoid the timer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8ac90f508dcc2554",
                  "57c27658044ffcd3",
                  "e4b0cd8fe7ad3df2",
                  "980f088aed264721"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "expiring immediately."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f252e25e8dea1ef",
                  "dcd7e7e320d3a9fb"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "When ack-eliciting packets in multiple packet number spaces are in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f252e25e8dea1ef",
                  "dcd7e7e320d3a9fb"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "flight, the timer MUST be set to the earlier value of the Initial and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6f252e25e8dea1ef",
                  "dcd7e7e320d3a9fb"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Handshake packet number spaces."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "36a04f484d1d2b61",
                  "5c8b70b076afa1db",
                  "2ab1e0ec916091fa",
                  "093b17cbceb9e8d4",
                  "8d39e13aa49a1896",
                  "570d2c57cab9aeb3"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST NOT set its PTO timer for the Application Data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "36a04f484d1d2b61",
                  "5c8b70b076afa1db",
                  "2ab1e0ec916091fa",
                  "093b17cbceb9e8d4",
                  "8d39e13aa49a1896",
                  "570d2c57cab9aeb3"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "packet number space until the handshake is confirmed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Doing so"
              }
            ],
            "   prevents the endpoint from retransmitting information in packets when",
            "   either the peer does not yet have the keys to process them or the",
            "   endpoint does not yet have the keys to process their acknowledgments.",
            "   For example, this can happen when a client sends 0-RTT packets to the",
            "   server; it does so without knowing whether the server will be able to",
            "   decrypt them.  Similarly, this can happen when a server sends 1-RTT",
            "   packets before confirming that the client has verified the server's",
            "   certificate and can therefore read these 1-RTT packets.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfb2099e4e4d19ef",
                  "7ffe428365623743",
                  "0ac7f0a3f344961f",
                  "32f851e8865a9486",
                  "b965610601ca5c57",
                  "3cfc936925268a57",
                  "f00244a4dff09344",
                  "6ed62d0996c28ea0",
                  "fea735ed6b114ce5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "A sender SHOULD restart its PTO timer every time an ack-eliciting"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfb2099e4e4d19ef",
                  "7ffe428365623743",
                  "0ac7f0a3f344961f",
                  "32f851e8865a9486",
                  "b965610601ca5c57",
                  "3cfc936925268a57",
                  "f00244a4dff09344",
                  "6ed62d0996c28ea0",
                  "fea735ed6b114ce5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "packet is sent"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfb2099e4e4d19ef",
                  "b965610601ca5c57",
                  "3cfc936925268a57",
                  "f00244a4dff09344",
                  "6ed62d0996c28ea0",
                  "fea735ed6b114ce5"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": " or acknowledged,"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfb2099e4e4d19ef",
                  "f00244a4dff09344",
                  "6ed62d0996c28ea0",
                  "fea735ed6b114ce5"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": " or when Initial or Handshake keys are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cfb2099e4e4d19ef",
                  "f00244a4dff09344",
                  "6ed62d0996c28ea0",
                  "fea735ed6b114ce5"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "discarded (Section 4.9 of [QUIC-TLS])."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This ensures the PTO is"
              }
            ],
            "   always set based on the latest estimate of the RTT and for the",
            "   correct packet across packet number spaces.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27c80f23a520b367",
                  "f281291316da23ed",
                  "68e2f3c0bb1cae13"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "When a PTO timer expires, the PTO backoff MUST be increased,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27c80f23a520b367",
                  "f281291316da23ed",
                  "68e2f3c0bb1cae13"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "resulting in the PTO period being set to twice its current value."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The PTO backoff factor is reset when an acknowledgment is received,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "except in the following case.  A server might take longer to respond"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "to packets during the handshake than otherwise.  To protect such a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "server from repeated client probes, the PTO backoff is not reset at a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "client that is not yet certain that the server has finished"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "validating the client's address.  That is, a client does not reset"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the PTO backoff factor on receiving acknowledgments in Initial"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "88d051a46b631aaa"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packets."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   This exponential reduction in the sender's rate is important because",
            "   consecutive PTOs might be caused by loss of packets or",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   acknowledgments due to severe congestion.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "993e2750146a6793"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Even when there are ack-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "993e2750146a6793"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "eliciting packets in flight in multiple packet number spaces, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "993e2750146a6793"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "exponential increase in PTO occurs across all spaces to prevent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "993e2750146a6793"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "excess load on the network.  For example, a timeout in the Initial"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "993e2750146a6793"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet number space doubles the length of the timeout in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "993e2750146a6793"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Handshake packet number space."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The total length of time over which consecutive PTOs expire is",
            "   limited by the idle timeout.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "910fc4ea30db54d7",
                  "156e9ee025f41d35",
                  "6fa1e580d96cff4c",
                  "6d7dda14ee9a081e",
                  "d714b384eb870b8b",
                  "b05fcb157378b39f"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The PTO timer MUST NOT be set if a timer is set for time threshold"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "910fc4ea30db54d7",
                  "156e9ee025f41d35",
                  "6fa1e580d96cff4c",
                  "6d7dda14ee9a081e",
                  "d714b384eb870b8b",
                  "b05fcb157378b39f"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "loss detection; see Section 6.1.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6fa1e580d96cff4c",
                  "6d7dda14ee9a081e",
                  "d714b384eb870b8b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  A timer that is set for time"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6fa1e580d96cff4c",
                  "6d7dda14ee9a081e",
                  "d714b384eb870b8b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "threshold loss detection will expire earlier than the PTO timer in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6fa1e580d96cff4c",
                  "6d7dda14ee9a081e",
                  "d714b384eb870b8b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "most cases and is less likely to spuriously retransmit data."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "980f088aed264721",
            "980f088aed264721",
            "dcd7e7e320d3a9fb",
            "dcd7e7e320d3a9fb",
            "dcd7e7e320d3a9fb",
            "570d2c57cab9aeb3",
            "570d2c57cab9aeb3",
            "fea735ed6b114ce5",
            "fea735ed6b114ce5",
            "fea735ed6b114ce5",
            "68e2f3c0bb1cae13",
            "68e2f3c0bb1cae13",
            "b05fcb157378b39f",
            "b05fcb157378b39f"
          ],
          "title": "Computing PTO"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "499745d6365282d7",
                  "f1c9300306aae2f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Resumed connections over the same network MAY use the previous"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "499745d6365282d7",
                  "f1c9300306aae2f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "connection's final smoothed RTT value as the resumed connection's"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "499745d6365282d7",
                  "f1c9300306aae2f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "initial RTT."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01061e51b92464af",
                  "17f5cad1156001bd",
                  "f3411d34ad8a5cbe"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "When no previous RTT is available, the initial RTT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01061e51b92464af",
                  "17f5cad1156001bd",
                  "f3411d34ad8a5cbe"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "SHOULD be set to 333 milliseconds."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01061e51b92464af",
                  "17f5cad1156001bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  This results in handshakes"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01061e51b92464af",
                  "17f5cad1156001bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "starting with a PTO of 1 second, as recommended for TCP's initial"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "01061e51b92464af",
                  "17f5cad1156001bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "RTO; see Section 2 of [RFC6298]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51545b329595ac1a",
                  "5edb51b2f445fae0"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A connection MAY use the delay between sending a PATH_CHALLENGE and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51545b329595ac1a",
                  "5edb51b2f445fae0"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "receiving a PATH_RESPONSE to set the initial RTT (see kInitialRtt in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51545b329595ac1a",
                  "5edb51b2f445fae0"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Appendix A.2) for a new path, but the delay SHOULD NOT be considered"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "51545b329595ac1a",
                  "5edb51b2f445fae0"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "an RTT sample."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   When the Initial keys and Handshake keys are discarded (see",
            "   Section 6.4), any Initial packets and Handshake packets can no longer",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   be acknowledged, so they are removed from bytes in flight.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37a240fa3c9a3568",
                  "aa4b3332be67a74b",
                  "0e5a9d88bd0af789"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "When"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37a240fa3c9a3568",
                  "aa4b3332be67a74b",
                  "0e5a9d88bd0af789"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Initial or Handshake keys are discarded, the PTO and loss detection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37a240fa3c9a3568",
                  "aa4b3332be67a74b",
                  "0e5a9d88bd0af789"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "timers MUST be reset, because discarding keys indicates forward"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37a240fa3c9a3568",
                  "aa4b3332be67a74b",
                  "0e5a9d88bd0af789"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "progress and the loss detection timer might have been set for a now-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37a240fa3c9a3568",
                  "aa4b3332be67a74b",
                  "0e5a9d88bd0af789"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "discarded packet number space."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f1c9300306aae2f3",
            "f1c9300306aae2f3",
            "f1c9300306aae2f3",
            "f3411d34ad8a5cbe",
            "f3411d34ad8a5cbe",
            "5edb51b2f445fae0",
            "5edb51b2f445fae0",
            "5edb51b2f445fae0",
            "5edb51b2f445fae0",
            "0e5a9d88bd0af789",
            "0e5a9d88bd0af789",
            "0e5a9d88bd0af789",
            "0e5a9d88bd0af789",
            "0e5a9d88bd0af789"
          ],
          "title": "Handshakes and New Paths"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Until the server has validated the client's address on the path, the",
            "   amount of data it can send is limited to three times the amount of",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   data received, as specified in Section 8.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7d4d021df1dad35",
                  "6f23233b2035ddaa",
                  "8a00e94f75ab1120",
                  "46037ed79a62ffec"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7d4d021df1dad35",
                  "6f23233b2035ddaa",
                  "8a00e94f75ab1120",
                  "46037ed79a62ffec"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "no additional data can be sent, the server's PTO timer MUST NOT be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7d4d021df1dad35",
                  "6f23233b2035ddaa",
                  "8a00e94f75ab1120",
                  "46037ed79a62ffec"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "armed until datagrams have been received from the client because"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7d4d021df1dad35",
                  "6f23233b2035ddaa",
                  "8a00e94f75ab1120",
                  "46037ed79a62ffec"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "packets sent on PTO count against the anti-amplification limit."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   When the server receives a datagram from the client, the",
            "   amplification limit is increased and the server resets the PTO timer.",
            "   If the PTO timer is then set to a time in the past, it is executed",
            "   immediately.  Doing so avoids sending new 1-RTT packets prior to",
            "   packets critical to the completion of the handshake.  In particular,",
            "   this can happen when 0-RTT is accepted but the server fails to",
            "   validate the client's address.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe379c3d7ecbf299",
                  "3d1290cf82b38685"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Since the server could be blocked until more datagrams are received"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe379c3d7ecbf299",
                  "3d1290cf82b38685"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "from the client, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe379c3d7ecbf299",
                  "cab1c729d210e177",
                  "dedff4a41954610e",
                  "3d1290cf82b38685"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "it is the client's responsibility to send packets to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe379c3d7ecbf299",
                  "cab1c729d210e177",
                  "dedff4a41954610e",
                  "3d1290cf82b38685"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unblock the server until it is certain that the server has finished"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fe379c3d7ecbf299",
                  "cab1c729d210e177",
                  "dedff4a41954610e",
                  "3d1290cf82b38685"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "its address validation"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": " (see Section 8 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c89e671c8f6045ce",
                  "24fb183b0139ee65",
                  "55cdc9e127aabb0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "That is,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c89e671c8f6045ce",
                  "24fb183b0139ee65",
                  "55cdc9e127aabb0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "the client MUST set the PTO timer if the client has not received an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c89e671c8f6045ce",
                  "24fb183b0139ee65",
                  "55cdc9e127aabb0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "acknowledgment for any of its Handshake packets and the handshake is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c89e671c8f6045ce",
                  "24fb183b0139ee65",
                  "55cdc9e127aabb0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "not confirmed (see Section 4.1.2 of [QUIC-TLS]), even if there are no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c89e671c8f6045ce",
                  "24fb183b0139ee65",
                  "55cdc9e127aabb0e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "packets in flight."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "12dca41cd9c20df6",
                  "cf2b22526ff26305",
                  "f98f6bfc990cd879"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "When the PTO fires, the client MUST send a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "12dca41cd9c20df6",
                  "cf2b22526ff26305",
                  "f98f6bfc990cd879"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Handshake packet if it has Handshake keys, otherwise it MUST send an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "12dca41cd9c20df6",
                  "cf2b22526ff26305",
                  "f98f6bfc990cd879"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Initial packet in a UDP datagram with a payload of at least 1200"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "12dca41cd9c20df6",
                  "cf2b22526ff26305",
                  "f98f6bfc990cd879"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "bytes."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "46037ed79a62ffec",
            "46037ed79a62ffec",
            "46037ed79a62ffec",
            "46037ed79a62ffec",
            "55cdc9e127aabb0e",
            "55cdc9e127aabb0e",
            "55cdc9e127aabb0e",
            "55cdc9e127aabb0e",
            "55cdc9e127aabb0e",
            "cf2b22526ff26305",
            "cf2b22526ff26305",
            "cf2b22526ff26305",
            "cf2b22526ff26305",
            "f98f6bfc990cd879",
            "f98f6bfc990cd879",
            "f98f6bfc990cd879",
            "f98f6bfc990cd879"
          ],
          "title": "Before Address Validation"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   When a server receives an Initial packet containing duplicate CRYPTO",
            "   data, it can assume the client did not receive all of the server's",
            "   CRYPTO data sent in Initial packets, or the client's estimated RTT is",
            "   too small.  When a client receives Handshake or 1-RTT packets prior",
            "   to obtaining Handshake keys, it may assume some or all of the",
            "   server's Initial packets were lost.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0fa5b3588139e100",
                  "7a175129504699e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "To speed up handshake completion under these conditions, an endpoint"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0fa5b3588139e100",
                  "7a175129504699e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "MAY, for a limited number of times per connection, send a packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0fa5b3588139e100",
                  "7a175129504699e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "containing unacknowledged CRYPTO data earlier than the PTO expiry,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0fa5b3588139e100",
                  "7a175129504699e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "subject to the address validation limits in Section 8.1 of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0fa5b3588139e100",
                  "7a175129504699e7"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "[QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Doing so at most once for each connection is"
              }
            ],
            "   adequate to quickly recover from a single packet loss.  An endpoint",
            "   that always retransmits packets in response to receiving packets that",
            "   it cannot process risks creating an infinite exchange of packets.",
            "",
            "   Endpoints can also use coalesced packets (see Section 12.2 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) to ensure that each datagram elicits at least one",
            "   acknowledgment.  For example, a client can coalesce an Initial packet",
            "   containing PING and PADDING frames with a 0-RTT data packet, and a",
            "   server can coalesce an Initial packet containing a PING frame with",
            "   one or more packets in its first flight."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7a175129504699e7",
            "7a175129504699e7",
            "7a175129504699e7",
            "7a175129504699e7",
            "7a175129504699e7"
          ],
          "title": "Speeding up Handshake Completion"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.4",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "85a58012b86ba8b4",
                  "1e1ca2c2722b8e80",
                  "09f1100027fe05a1",
                  "741ded0fe9dcca22",
                  "ac15b86678539649",
                  "69ca26bab0e3e3a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "When a PTO timer expires, a sender MUST send at least one ack-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "85a58012b86ba8b4",
                  "1e1ca2c2722b8e80",
                  "09f1100027fe05a1",
                  "741ded0fe9dcca22",
                  "ac15b86678539649",
                  "69ca26bab0e3e3a3"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "eliciting packet in the packet number space as a probe."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c3504a09973c51b",
                  "653b3e8a33f0e3c2",
                  "05535811e1e743b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "An endpoint"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c3504a09973c51b",
                  "653b3e8a33f0e3c2",
                  "05535811e1e743b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "MAY send up to two full-sized datagrams containing ack-eliciting"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c3504a09973c51b",
                  "653b3e8a33f0e3c2",
                  "05535811e1e743b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "packets to avoid an expensive consecutive PTO expiration due to a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c3504a09973c51b",
                  "653b3e8a33f0e3c2",
                  "05535811e1e743b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "single lost datagram or to transmit data from multiple packet number"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c3504a09973c51b",
                  "653b3e8a33f0e3c2",
                  "05535811e1e743b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "spaces."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b750a90452391da",
                  "1b6d63d465a9d6cd",
                  "5544f519d146b7bd",
                  "b37fb0a44a754a58"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "All probe packets sent on a PTO MUST be ack-eliciting."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ba8283bee7a8ed18",
                  "5ab3137e80ed34ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "In addition to sending data in the packet number space for which the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ba8283bee7a8ed18",
                  "5ab3137e80ed34ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "timer expired, the sender SHOULD send ack-eliciting packets from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ba8283bee7a8ed18",
                  "5ab3137e80ed34ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "other packet number spaces with in-flight data, coalescing packets if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ba8283bee7a8ed18",
                  "5ab3137e80ed34ae"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "possible."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This is particularly valuable when the server has both"
              }
            ],
            "   Initial and Handshake data in flight or when the client has both",
            "   Handshake and Application Data in flight because the peer might only",
            "   have receive keys for one of the two packet number spaces.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67a35d35539f8ba3",
                  "2fcd2d32fb6c1a4f",
                  "043671e0e3d8e7ce",
                  "c6729db755f29f44"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the sender wants to elicit a faster acknowledgment on PTO, it can"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67a35d35539f8ba3",
                  "2fcd2d32fb6c1a4f",
                  "043671e0e3d8e7ce",
                  "c6729db755f29f44"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "skip a packet number to eliminate the acknowledgment delay."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6517fc9046ac8de",
                  "8948368fa6d90183",
                  "6b76f132c56d3922"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "An endpoint SHOULD include new data in packets that are sent on PTO"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6517fc9046ac8de",
                  "8948368fa6d90183",
                  "6b76f132c56d3922"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "expiration."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6517fc9046ac8de",
                  "8948368fa6d90183"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6517fc9046ac8de",
                  "8948368fa6d90183",
                  "0ea8e25507365f90"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "Previously sent data MAY be sent if no new data can be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a6517fc9046ac8de",
                  "8948368fa6d90183",
                  "0ea8e25507365f90"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "sent."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a584ee87d1f9d50d",
                  "32c5200d17b71a65"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Implementations MAY use alternative strategies for determining"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a584ee87d1f9d50d",
                  "32c5200d17b71a65"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "the content of probe packets, including sending new or retransmitted"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a584ee87d1f9d50d",
                  "32c5200d17b71a65"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "data based on the application's priorities."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   It is possible the sender has no new or previously sent data to send.",
            "   As an example, consider the following sequence of events: new",
            "   application data is sent in a STREAM frame, deemed lost, then",
            "   retransmitted in a new packet, and then the original transmission is",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   acknowledged.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87f720eeddeb6dce",
                  "5d650893388b102f",
                  "c8c6401ae082b878"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "When there is no data to send, the sender SHOULD send"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87f720eeddeb6dce",
                  "5d650893388b102f",
                  "c8c6401ae082b878"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "a PING or other ack-eliciting frame in a single packet, rearming the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87f720eeddeb6dce",
                  "5d650893388b102f",
                  "c8c6401ae082b878"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "PTO timer."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e1ca500203f749c",
                  "a0ab66bc3388b870"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "Alternatively, instead of sending an ack-eliciting packet, the sender"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e1ca500203f749c",
                  "a0ab66bc3388b870"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "MAY mark any packets still in flight as lost."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Doing so avoids"
              }
            ],
            "   sending an additional packet but increases the risk that loss is",
            "   declared too aggressively, resulting in an unnecessary rate reduction",
            "   by the congestion controller.",
            "",
            "   Consecutive PTO periods increase exponentially, and as a result,",
            "   connection recovery latency increases exponentially as packets",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   continue to be dropped in the network.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c53e84a391b0c9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Sending two packets on PTO"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c53e84a391b0c9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "expiration increases resilience to packet drops, thus reducing the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c53e84a391b0c9f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "probability of consecutive PTO events."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   When the PTO timer expires multiple times and new data cannot be",
            "   sent, implementations must choose between sending the same payload",
            "   every time or sending different payloads.  Sending the same payload",
            "   may be simpler and ensures the highest priority frames arrive first.",
            "   Sending different payloads each time reduces the chances of spurious",
            "   retransmission."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "69ca26bab0e3e3a3",
            "69ca26bab0e3e3a3",
            "05535811e1e743b3",
            "05535811e1e743b3",
            "05535811e1e743b3",
            "05535811e1e743b3",
            "05535811e1e743b3",
            "b37fb0a44a754a58",
            "5ab3137e80ed34ae",
            "5ab3137e80ed34ae",
            "5ab3137e80ed34ae",
            "5ab3137e80ed34ae",
            "6b76f132c56d3922",
            "6b76f132c56d3922",
            "0ea8e25507365f90",
            "0ea8e25507365f90",
            "32c5200d17b71a65",
            "32c5200d17b71a65",
            "32c5200d17b71a65",
            "c8c6401ae082b878",
            "c8c6401ae082b878",
            "c8c6401ae082b878",
            "a0ab66bc3388b870",
            "a0ab66bc3388b870"
          ],
          "title": "Sending Probe Packets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.3",
          "lines": [
            "   A Retry packet causes a client to send another Initial packet,",
            "   effectively restarting the connection process.  A Retry packet",
            "   indicates that the Initial packet was received but not processed.  A",
            "   Retry packet cannot be treated as an acknowledgment because it does",
            "   not indicate that a packet was processed or specify the packet",
            "   number.",
            "",
            "   Clients that receive a Retry packet reset congestion control and loss",
            "   recovery state, including resetting any pending timers.  Other",
            "   connection state, in particular cryptographic handshake messages, is",
            "   retained; see Section 17.2.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7d3b1c2e86bb0eed",
                  "6e7349279bb93031"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "The client MAY compute an RTT estimate to the server as the time"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7d3b1c2e86bb0eed",
                  "6e7349279bb93031"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "period from when the first Initial packet was sent to when a Retry or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7d3b1c2e86bb0eed",
                  "6e7349279bb93031"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "a Version Negotiation packet is received."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6927a5ab7f017c99",
                  "939b44edeb923934"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "The client MAY use this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6927a5ab7f017c99",
                  "939b44edeb923934"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "value in place of its default for the initial RTT estimate."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6e7349279bb93031",
            "6e7349279bb93031",
            "6e7349279bb93031",
            "939b44edeb923934",
            "939b44edeb923934"
          ],
          "title": "Handling Retry Packets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.4",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af9301e8b8e1b06f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "When Initial and Handshake packet protection keys are discarded (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af9301e8b8e1b06f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 4.9 of [QUIC-TLS]), all packets that were sent with those"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af9301e8b8e1b06f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "keys can no longer be acknowledged because their acknowledgments"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af9301e8b8e1b06f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "cannot be processed.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20b2a2b893f8bb6d",
                  "af9301e8b8e1b06f",
                  "711f3d0a6cdc09db",
                  "a447177add9f3a13"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The sender MUST discard all recovery state"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20b2a2b893f8bb6d",
                  "af9301e8b8e1b06f",
                  "711f3d0a6cdc09db",
                  "a447177add9f3a13"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "associated with those packets and MUST remove them from the count of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "20b2a2b893f8bb6d",
                  "af9301e8b8e1b06f",
                  "711f3d0a6cdc09db",
                  "a447177add9f3a13"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "bytes in flight."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Endpoints stop sending and receiving Initial packets once they start",
            "   exchanging Handshake packets; see Section 17.2.2.1 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  At this point, recovery state for all in-flight",
            "   Initial packets is discarded.",
            "",
            "   When 0-RTT is rejected, recovery state for all in-flight 0-RTT",
            "   packets is discarded.",
            "",
            "   If a server accepts 0-RTT, but does not buffer 0-RTT packets that",
            "   arrive before Initial packets, early 0-RTT packets will be declared",
            "   lost, but that is expected to be infrequent.",
            "",
            "   It is expected that keys are discarded at some time after the packets",
            "   encrypted with them are either acknowledged or declared lost.",
            "   However, Initial and Handshake secrets are discarded as soon as",
            "   Handshake and 1-RTT keys are proven to be available to both client",
            "   and server; see Section 4.9.1 of [QUIC-TLS]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "711f3d0a6cdc09db",
            "711f3d0a6cdc09db",
            "711f3d0a6cdc09db",
            "a447177add9f3a13",
            "a447177add9f3a13",
            "a447177add9f3a13"
          ],
          "title": "Discarding Keys and Packet State"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7",
          "lines": [
            "   This document specifies a sender-side congestion controller for QUIC",
            "   similar to TCP NewReno [RFC6582].",
            "",
            "   The signals QUIC provides for congestion control are generic and are",
            "   designed to support different sender-side algorithms.  A sender can",
            "   unilaterally choose a different algorithm to use, such as CUBIC",
            "   [RFC8312].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c4348552ae1ccdb1",
                  "9d7f56e2dd823cde"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "If a sender uses a different controller than that specified in this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c4348552ae1ccdb1",
                  "9d7f56e2dd823cde"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "document, the chosen controller MUST conform to the congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c4348552ae1ccdb1",
                  "9d7f56e2dd823cde"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "control guidelines specified in Section 3.1 of [RFC8085]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80cf1104cc623a69",
                  "d7f637543b076917"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Similar to TCP, "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80cf1104cc623a69",
                  "f45295eda009dda3",
                  "d0509a65ca091f54",
                  "d7f637543b076917"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packets containing only ACK frames do not count"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80cf1104cc623a69",
                  "f45295eda009dda3",
                  "d0509a65ca091f54",
                  "d7f637543b076917"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "toward bytes in flight and are not congestion controlled"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "80cf1104cc623a69",
                  "f45295eda009dda3",
                  "d7f637543b076917"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a55ddc680046ce0",
                  "6680c8afa985c409"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Unlike"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a55ddc680046ce0",
                  "6680c8afa985c409"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "TCP, QUIC can detect the loss of these packets and MAY use that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a55ddc680046ce0",
                  "6680c8afa985c409"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "information to adjust the congestion controller or the rate of ACK-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a55ddc680046ce0",
                  "6680c8afa985c409"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "only packets being sent, but this document does not describe a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7a55ddc680046ce0",
                  "6680c8afa985c409"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "mechanism for doing so."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The congestion controller is per path, so packets sent on other paths",
            "   do not alter the current path's congestion controller, as described",
            "   in Section 9.4 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   The algorithm in this document specifies and uses the controller's",
            "   congestion window in bytes.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61dc3581ae6950c6",
                  "aa4c13ec7b14a05e",
                  "5051ba9d620362f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST NOT send a packet if it would cause bytes_in_flight"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61dc3581ae6950c6",
                  "aa4c13ec7b14a05e",
                  "5051ba9d620362f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "(see Appendix B.2) to be larger than the congestion window, unless"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61dc3581ae6950c6",
                  "aa4c13ec7b14a05e",
                  "5051ba9d620362f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "the packet is sent on a PTO timer expiration (see Section 6.2) or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "61dc3581ae6950c6",
                  "aa4c13ec7b14a05e",
                  "5051ba9d620362f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "when entering recovery (see Section 7.3.2)."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9d7f56e2dd823cde",
            "9d7f56e2dd823cde",
            "9d7f56e2dd823cde",
            "6680c8afa985c409",
            "6680c8afa985c409",
            "6680c8afa985c409",
            "6680c8afa985c409",
            "6680c8afa985c409",
            "5051ba9d620362f6",
            "5051ba9d620362f6",
            "5051ba9d620362f6",
            "5051ba9d620362f6"
          ],
          "title": "Congestion Control"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d15cb43e5f1bc0de",
                  "9d6e8edb576f8824"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If a path has been validated to support Explicit Congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d15cb43e5f1bc0de",
                  "9d6e8edb576f8824"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Notification (ECN) [RFC3168] [RFC8311], QUIC treats a Congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d15cb43e5f1bc0de",
                  "9d6e8edb576f8824"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Experienced (CE) codepoint in the IP header as a signal of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d15cb43e5f1bc0de",
                  "9d6e8edb576f8824"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "congestion."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This document specifies an endpoint's response when the"
              }
            ],
            "   peer-reported ECN-CE count increases; see Section 13.4.2 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
          ],
          "title": "Explicit Congestion Notification"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC begins every connection in slow start with the congestion window",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   set to an initial value.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56bd4a68cdd0e5f1",
                  "83118d8b0ca0ad99",
                  "6a8586acac0e25a9",
                  "6acb57e6056ee130",
                  "1c60eb14e9787351"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Endpoints SHOULD use an initial congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56bd4a68cdd0e5f1",
                  "83118d8b0ca0ad99",
                  "6a8586acac0e25a9",
                  "6acb57e6056ee130",
                  "1c60eb14e9787351"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "window of ten times the maximum datagram size (max_datagram_size),"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56bd4a68cdd0e5f1",
                  "83118d8b0ca0ad99",
                  "6a8586acac0e25a9",
                  "6acb57e6056ee130",
                  "1c60eb14e9787351"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "while limiting the window to the larger of 14,720 bytes or twice the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "56bd4a68cdd0e5f1",
                  "83118d8b0ca0ad99",
                  "6a8586acac0e25a9",
                  "6acb57e6056ee130",
                  "1c60eb14e9787351"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "maximum datagram size."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This follows the analysis and recommendations"
              }
            ],
            "   in [RFC6928], increasing the byte limit to account for the smaller",
            "   8-byte overhead of UDP compared to the 20-byte overhead for TCP.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ab4a7660ed88cc5a",
                  "f4e8a87e5b2b4d02",
                  "f10f4fb2ce56872b",
                  "d1110d44eb561ad1"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "If the maximum datagram size changes during the connection, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ab4a7660ed88cc5a",
                  "f4e8a87e5b2b4d02",
                  "f10f4fb2ce56872b",
                  "d1110d44eb561ad1"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "initial congestion window SHOULD be recalculated with the new size."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e438bfbf5264594b",
                  "0d0dc909bf3d7158",
                  "480c4dacd46ce70b",
                  "fe7a094ef163db6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "If the maximum datagram size is decreased in order to complete the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e438bfbf5264594b",
                  "0d0dc909bf3d7158",
                  "480c4dacd46ce70b",
                  "fe7a094ef163db6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "handshake, the congestion window SHOULD be set to the new initial"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e438bfbf5264594b",
                  "0d0dc909bf3d7158",
                  "480c4dacd46ce70b",
                  "fe7a094ef163db6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "congestion window."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Prior to validating the client's address, the server can be further",
            "   limited by the anti-amplification limit as specified in Section 8.1",
            "   of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  Though the anti-amplification limit can prevent",
            "   the congestion window from being fully utilized and therefore slow",
            "   down the increase in congestion window, it does not directly affect",
            "   the congestion window.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95053af2652b95d7",
                  "45a111ba594af915"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The minimum congestion window is the smallest value the congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95053af2652b95d7",
                  "45a111ba594af915"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "window can attain in response to loss, an increase in the peer-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "95053af2652b95d7",
                  "45a111ba594af915"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "reported ECN-CE count, or persistent congestion."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45a111ba594af915"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f700264561f35874",
                  "45a111ba594af915",
                  "1caf21afbd22ac63"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The RECOMMENDED"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f700264561f35874",
                  "45a111ba594af915",
                  "1caf21afbd22ac63"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "value is 2 * max_datagram_size."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1c60eb14e9787351",
            "1c60eb14e9787351",
            "1c60eb14e9787351",
            "1c60eb14e9787351",
            "d1110d44eb561ad1",
            "d1110d44eb561ad1",
            "fe7a094ef163db6a",
            "fe7a094ef163db6a",
            "fe7a094ef163db6a",
            "1caf21afbd22ac63",
            "1caf21afbd22ac63"
          ],
          "title": "Initial and Minimum Congestion Window"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The NewReno congestion controller described in this document has",
            "   three distinct states, as shown in Figure 1.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "New path or      +------------+"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "               "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "persistent congestion |   Slow     |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "           "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "(O)---------------------->|   Start    |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                     "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+------------+"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                           "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "|"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Loss or |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                           "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "ECN-CE increase |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                                           "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "v"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+------------+     Loss or       +------------+"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "| Congestion |  ECN-CE increase  |  Recovery  |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "| Avoidance  |------------------>|   Period   |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "    "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+------------+                   +------------+"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "              "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "^                            |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "              "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "|                            |"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "              "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "+----------------------------+"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                 "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Acknowledgment of packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "                   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6404f792deea0d9b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "sent during recovery"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "            Figure 1: Congestion Control States and Transitions",
            "",
            "   These states and the transitions between them are described in",
            "   subsequent sections."
          ],
          "title": "Congestion Control States"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.3.1",
          "lines": [
            "   A NewReno sender is in slow start any time the congestion window is",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   below the slow start threshold.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc788967c0b635ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A sender begins in slow start"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc788967c0b635ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "because the slow start threshold is initialized to an infinite value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "414ce10ba143cf31"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "While a sender is in slow start, the congestion window increases by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "414ce10ba143cf31"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the number of bytes acknowledged when each acknowledgment is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "414ce10ba143cf31"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "processed.  This results in exponential growth of the congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "414ce10ba143cf31"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "window."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10472dc7e243c8a8",
                  "369b750b8e995f27",
                  "6faffbbdbddc00ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The sender MUST exit slow start and enter a recovery period when a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10472dc7e243c8a8",
                  "369b750b8e995f27",
                  "6faffbbdbddc00ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "packet is lost or when the ECN-CE count reported by its peer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10472dc7e243c8a8",
                  "369b750b8e995f27",
                  "6faffbbdbddc00ef"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "increases."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A sender reenters slow start any time the congestion window is less",
            "   than the slow start threshold, which only occurs after persistent",
            "   congestion is declared."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6faffbbdbddc00ef",
            "6faffbbdbddc00ef",
            "6faffbbdbddc00ef"
          ],
          "title": "Slow Start"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.3.2",
          "lines": [
            "   A NewReno sender enters a recovery period when it detects the loss of",
            "   a packet or when the ECN-CE count reported by its peer increases.  A",
            "   sender that is already in a recovery period stays in it and does not",
            "   reenter it.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bbf5fb72d9d569e",
                  "2b8da48fe292cff9"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "On entering a recovery period, a sender MUST set the slow start"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bbf5fb72d9d569e",
                  "2b8da48fe292cff9"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "threshold to half the value of the congestion window when loss is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6bbf5fb72d9d569e",
                  "2b8da48fe292cff9"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "detected."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9f2a2cb541b8640",
                  "cf6da80a29e5304a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "The congestion window MUST be set to the reduced value of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c9f2a2cb541b8640",
                  "cf6da80a29e5304a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "the slow start threshold before exiting the recovery period."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b517065d12152a1",
                  "2ca7994362c1a04c",
                  "992ba3a30bb896d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Implementations MAY reduce the congestion window immediately upon"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b517065d12152a1",
                  "2ca7994362c1a04c",
                  "992ba3a30bb896d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "entering a recovery period or use other mechanisms, such as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b517065d12152a1",
                  "2ca7994362c1a04c",
                  "992ba3a30bb896d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Proportional Rate Reduction [PRR], to reduce the congestion window"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b517065d12152a1",
                  "2ca7994362c1a04c",
                  "992ba3a30bb896d5"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "more gradually."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "81a8932f8597fe53",
                  "e63921a24d08c063",
                  "d3097f515666ae44",
                  "405e5bfd1dc5ffa8",
                  "0aadc8a133af1132"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the congestion window is reduced immediately, a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "81a8932f8597fe53",
                  "e63921a24d08c063",
                  "d3097f515666ae44",
                  "405e5bfd1dc5ffa8",
                  "0aadc8a133af1132"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "single packet can be sent prior to reduction.  This speeds up loss"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "81a8932f8597fe53",
                  "e63921a24d08c063",
                  "d3097f515666ae44",
                  "405e5bfd1dc5ffa8",
                  "0aadc8a133af1132"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "recovery if the data in the lost packet is retransmitted and is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "81a8932f8597fe53",
                  "e63921a24d08c063",
                  "d3097f515666ae44",
                  "405e5bfd1dc5ffa8",
                  "0aadc8a133af1132"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "similar to TCP as described in Section 5 of [RFC6675]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The recovery period aims to limit congestion window reduction to once",
            "   per round trip.  Therefore, during a recovery period, the congestion",
            "   window does not change in response to new losses or increases in the",
            "   ECN-CE count.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa93a650d62f3089",
                  "6d18e58924ed62b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A recovery period ends and the sender enters congestion avoidance"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa93a650d62f3089",
                  "6d18e58924ed62b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "when a packet sent during the recovery period is acknowledged."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This"
              }
            ],
            "   is slightly different from TCP's definition of recovery, which ends",
            "   when the lost segment that started recovery is acknowledged",
            "   [RFC5681]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2b8da48fe292cff9",
            "2b8da48fe292cff9",
            "2b8da48fe292cff9",
            "cf6da80a29e5304a",
            "cf6da80a29e5304a",
            "992ba3a30bb896d5",
            "992ba3a30bb896d5",
            "992ba3a30bb896d5",
            "992ba3a30bb896d5"
          ],
          "title": "Recovery"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.3.3",
          "lines": [
            "   A NewReno sender is in congestion avoidance any time the congestion",
            "   window is at or above the slow start threshold and not in a recovery",
            "   period.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d7350ae80e110b45",
                  "e2e05e0324a0b93a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "A sender in congestion avoidance uses an Additive Increase"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d7350ae80e110b45",
                  "e2e05e0324a0b93a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Multiplicative Decrease (AIMD) approach that MUST limit the increase"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d7350ae80e110b45",
                  "e2e05e0324a0b93a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "to the congestion window to at most one maximum datagram size for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d7350ae80e110b45",
                  "e2e05e0324a0b93a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "each congestion window that is acknowledged."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The sender exits congestion avoidance and enters a recovery period",
            "   when a packet is lost or when the ECN-CE count reported by its peer",
            "   increases."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "e2e05e0324a0b93a",
            "e2e05e0324a0b93a",
            "e2e05e0324a0b93a",
            "e2e05e0324a0b93a"
          ],
          "title": "Congestion Avoidance"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.4",
          "lines": [
            "   During the handshake, some packet protection keys might not be",
            "   available when a packet arrives, and the receiver can choose to drop",
            "   the packet.  In particular, Handshake and 0-RTT packets cannot be",
            "   processed until the Initial packets arrive, and 1-RTT packets cannot",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   be processed until the handshake completes.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8aef9dcf5a49752a",
                  "cc137cf78bfce47d"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Endpoints MAY ignore the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8aef9dcf5a49752a",
                  "cc137cf78bfce47d"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "loss of Handshake, 0-RTT, and 1-RTT packets that might have arrived"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8aef9dcf5a49752a",
                  "cc137cf78bfce47d"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "before the peer had packet protection keys to process those packets."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71e4d5d7c44f1d9e",
                  "73eb1c087163c432"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT ignore the loss of packets that were sent after"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "71e4d5d7c44f1d9e",
                  "73eb1c087163c432"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "the earliest acknowledged packet in a given packet number space."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "cc137cf78bfce47d",
            "cc137cf78bfce47d",
            "cc137cf78bfce47d",
            "73eb1c087163c432",
            "73eb1c087163c432"
          ],
          "title": "Ignoring Loss of Undecryptable Packets"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.5",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f5b88cfeca0cf5dc",
                  "fc84900fa484f2c0",
                  "291d4e52691375ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Probe packets MUST NOT be blocked by the congestion controller."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "A"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e741b0bce1bf664",
                  "7ef3df077344ba7d",
                  "e0cf357c5ebccf98"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "sender MUST however count these packets as being additionally in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e741b0bce1bf664",
                  "7ef3df077344ba7d",
                  "e0cf357c5ebccf98"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "flight, since these packets add network load without establishing"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e741b0bce1bf664",
                  "7ef3df077344ba7d",
                  "e0cf357c5ebccf98"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "packet loss."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that sending probe packets might cause the"
              }
            ],
            "   sender's bytes in flight to exceed the congestion window until an",
            "   acknowledgment is received that establishes loss or delivery of",
            "   packets."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "291d4e52691375ee",
            "e0cf357c5ebccf98",
            "e0cf357c5ebccf98",
            "e0cf357c5ebccf98",
            "e0cf357c5ebccf98"
          ],
          "title": "Probe Timeout"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.6",
          "lines": [
            "   When a sender establishes loss of all packets sent over a long enough",
            "   duration, the network is considered to be experiencing persistent",
            "   congestion."
          ],
          "title": "Persistent Congestion"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.6.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a",
                  "69092c005929e694"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "The persistent congestion duration is computed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a",
                  "69092c005929e694"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "(smoothed_rtt + max(4*rttvar, kGranularity) + max_ack_delay) *"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "       "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a",
                  "69092c005929e694"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "kPersistentCongestionThreshold"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Unlike the PTO computation in Section 6.2, this duration includes the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "max_ack_delay irrespective of the packet number spaces in which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "losses are established."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "This duration allows a sender to send as many packets before"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "establishing persistent congestion, including some in response to PTO"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "expiration, as TCP does with Tail Loss Probes [RFC8985] and an RTO"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4e676ff3c99ada6a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "[RFC5681]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Larger values of kPersistentCongestionThreshold cause the sender to",
            "   become less responsive to persistent congestion in the network, which",
            "   can result in aggressive sending into a congested network.  Too small",
            "   a value can result in a sender declaring persistent congestion",
            "   unnecessarily, resulting in reduced throughput for the sender.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31ae9a0c2946cdfc",
                  "a950ee1ce762bfdd",
                  "b5b164874db0819b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The RECOMMENDED value for kPersistentCongestionThreshold is 3, which"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31ae9a0c2946cdfc",
                  "a950ee1ce762bfdd",
                  "b5b164874db0819b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "results in behavior that is approximately equivalent to a TCP sender"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31ae9a0c2946cdfc",
                  "a950ee1ce762bfdd",
                  "b5b164874db0819b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "declaring an RTO after two TLPs."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   This design does not use consecutive PTO events to establish",
            "   persistent congestion, since application patterns impact PTO",
            "   expiration.  For example, a sender that sends small amounts of data",
            "   with silence periods between them restarts the PTO timer every time",
            "   it sends, potentially preventing the PTO timer from expiring for a",
            "   long period of time, even when no acknowledgments are being received.",
            "   The use of a duration enables a sender to establish persistent",
            "   congestion without depending on PTO expiration."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b5b164874db0819b",
            "b5b164874db0819b",
            "b5b164874db0819b"
          ],
          "title": "Duration"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.6.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "755d847798e7812a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A sender establishes persistent congestion after the receipt of an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "755d847798e7812a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "acknowledgment if two packets that are ack-eliciting are declared"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "755d847798e7812a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "lost, and:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "755d847798e7812a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "*  across all packet number spaces, none of the packets sent between"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "755d847798e7812a"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the send times of these two packets are acknowledged;"
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   *  the duration between the send times of these two packets exceeds",
            "      the persistent congestion duration (Section 7.6.1); and",
            "",
            "   *  a prior RTT sample existed when these two packets were sent.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "055d69735a042efe",
                  "d42d9548813f5739",
                  "a46172fe6a1c7a7e",
                  "77e29682ff6c7e87"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "These two packets MUST be ack-eliciting, since a receiver is required"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "055d69735a042efe",
                  "d42d9548813f5739",
                  "a46172fe6a1c7a7e",
                  "77e29682ff6c7e87"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "to acknowledge only ack-eliciting packets within its maximum"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "055d69735a042efe",
                  "d42d9548813f5739",
                  "a46172fe6a1c7a7e",
                  "77e29682ff6c7e87"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "acknowledgment delay; see Section 13.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "860c1d9fea846e30",
                  "75477eae2a666ae2",
                  "82f8fc86c740484e"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The persistent congestion period SHOULD NOT start until there is at"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "860c1d9fea846e30",
                  "75477eae2a666ae2",
                  "82f8fc86c740484e"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "least one RTT sample."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "860c1d9fea846e30"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "  Before the first RTT sample, a sender arms its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "860c1d9fea846e30"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "PTO timer based on the initial RTT (Section 6.2.2), which could be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "860c1d9fea846e30"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "substantially larger than the actual RTT.  Requiring a prior RTT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "860c1d9fea846e30"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "sample prevents a sender from establishing persistent congestion with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "860c1d9fea846e30"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "potentially too few probes."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e4fd98a92068f05",
                  "c9e34257a277df4d"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Since network congestion is not affected by packet number spaces,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e4fd98a92068f05",
                  "c9e34257a277df4d"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "persistent congestion SHOULD consider packets sent across packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9e4fd98a92068f05",
                  "c9e34257a277df4d"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "number spaces."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67e35b18116074f2",
                  "c3d79640708b15dc",
                  "06bdae7ef5528bb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "A sender that does not have state for all packet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67e35b18116074f2",
                  "c3d79640708b15dc",
                  "06bdae7ef5528bb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "number spaces or an implementation that cannot compare send times"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67e35b18116074f2",
                  "c3d79640708b15dc",
                  "06bdae7ef5528bb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "across packet number spaces MAY use state for just the packet number"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67e35b18116074f2",
                  "c3d79640708b15dc",
                  "06bdae7ef5528bb2"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "space that was acknowledged."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This might result in erroneously"
              }
            ],
            "   declaring persistent congestion, but it will not lead to a failure to",
            "   detect persistent congestion.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b2f8a02fbc87ade",
                  "103176956d09a9b9",
                  "cc0a7a6365d0ea10"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "When persistent congestion is declared, the sender's congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b2f8a02fbc87ade",
                  "103176956d09a9b9",
                  "cc0a7a6365d0ea10"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "window MUST be reduced to the minimum congestion window"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b2f8a02fbc87ade",
                  "103176956d09a9b9",
                  "cc0a7a6365d0ea10"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "(kMinimumWindow), similar to a TCP sender's response on an RTO"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b2f8a02fbc87ade",
                  "103176956d09a9b9",
                  "cc0a7a6365d0ea10"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "[RFC5681]."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "77e29682ff6c7e87",
            "77e29682ff6c7e87",
            "77e29682ff6c7e87",
            "82f8fc86c740484e",
            "82f8fc86c740484e",
            "c9e34257a277df4d",
            "c9e34257a277df4d",
            "c9e34257a277df4d",
            "06bdae7ef5528bb2",
            "06bdae7ef5528bb2",
            "06bdae7ef5528bb2",
            "06bdae7ef5528bb2",
            "cc0a7a6365d0ea10",
            "cc0a7a6365d0ea10",
            "cc0a7a6365d0ea10",
            "cc0a7a6365d0ea10"
          ],
          "title": "Establishing Persistent Congestion"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.6.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The following example illustrates how a sender might establish",
            "   persistent congestion.  Assume:",
            "",
            "   smoothed_rtt + max(4*rttvar, kGranularity) + max_ack_delay = 2",
            "   kPersistentCongestionThreshold = 3",
            "",
            "   Consider the following sequence of events:",
            "",
            "              +========+===================================+",
            "              | Time   | Action                            |",
            "              +========+===================================+",
            "              | t=0    | Send packet #1 (application data) |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=1    | Send packet #2 (application data) |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=1.2  | Receive acknowledgment of #1      |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=2    | Send packet #3 (application data) |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=3    | Send packet #4 (application data) |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=4    | Send packet #5 (application data) |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=5    | Send packet #6 (application data) |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=6    | Send packet #7 (application data) |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=8    | Send packet #8 (PTO 1)            |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=12   | Send packet #9 (PTO 2)            |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "              | t=12.2 | Receive acknowledgment of #9      |",
            "              +--------+-----------------------------------+",
            "",
            "                                 Table 1",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7da947407a7d1da6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Packets 2 through 8 are declared lost when the acknowledgment for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7da947407a7d1da6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "packet 9 is received at \"t = 12.2\"."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f4bb13ff9bd12dab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "The congestion period is calculated as the time between the oldest"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f4bb13ff9bd12dab"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "and newest lost packets: \"8 - 1 = 7\"."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  The persistent congestion"
              }
            ],
            "   duration is \"2 * 3 = 6\".  Because the threshold was reached and",
            "   because none of the packets between the oldest and the newest lost",
            "   packets were acknowledged, the network is considered to have",
            "   experienced persistent congestion.",
            "",
            "   While this example shows PTO expiration, they are not required for",
            "   persistent congestion to be established."
          ],
          "title": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.7",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "029561a2dc3b35de",
                  "627371eae1ad5e3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "A sender SHOULD pace sending of all in-flight packets based on input"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "029561a2dc3b35de",
                  "627371eae1ad5e3a"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "from the congestion controller."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Sending multiple packets into the network without any delay between",
            "   them creates a packet burst that might cause short-term congestion",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   and losses.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "437052ec1f753df5",
                  "6ef71d6719880d8b"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Senders MUST either use pacing or limit such bursts."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8baaf4eb248a1d44",
                  "142aeada4e84f635",
                  "eced398c52b4e356"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "Senders SHOULD limit bursts to the initial congestion window"
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8baaf4eb248a1d44",
                  "eced398c52b4e356"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "; see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8baaf4eb248a1d44",
                  "eced398c52b4e356"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "Section 7.2."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "615f733d5f40e5cb",
                  "cd2dc0faa9d081d4"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "A sender with knowledge that the network path to the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "615f733d5f40e5cb",
                  "cd2dc0faa9d081d4"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "receiver can absorb larger bursts MAY use a higher limit."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   An implementation should take care to architect its congestion",
            "   controller to work well with a pacer.  For instance, a pacer might",
            "   wrap the congestion controller and control the availability of the",
            "   congestion window, or a pacer might pace out packets handed to it by",
            "   the congestion controller.",
            "",
            "   Timely delivery of ACK frames is important for efficient loss",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   recovery.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dffab42ec48fcc47",
                  "69e44c4262e309dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "To avoid delaying their delivery to the peer, packets"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dffab42ec48fcc47",
                  "69e44c4262e309dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "containing only ACK frames SHOULD therefore not be paced."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Endpoints can implement pacing as they choose.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453",
                  "82f5adce235cd6ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A perfectly paced"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453",
                  "82f5adce235cd6ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "sender spreads packets exactly evenly over time.  For a window-based"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453",
                  "82f5adce235cd6ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "congestion controller, such as the one in this document, that rate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453",
                  "82f5adce235cd6ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "can be computed by averaging the congestion window over the RTT."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453",
                  "82f5adce235cd6ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Expressed as a rate in units of bytes per time, where"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453",
                  "82f5adce235cd6ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "congestion_window is in bytes:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453",
                  "82f5adce235cd6ad"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "rate = N * congestion_window / smoothed_rtt"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Or expressed as an inter-packet interval in units of time:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "58186f61d1351453"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "interval = ( smoothed_rtt * packet_size / congestion_window ) / N"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3cb8e5e1c6369a57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Using a value for \"N\" that is small, but at least 1 (for example,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3cb8e5e1c6369a57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "1.25) ensures that variations in RTT do not result in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3cb8e5e1c6369a57"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "underutilization of the congestion window."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Practical considerations, such as packetization, scheduling delays,",
            "   and computational efficiency, can cause a sender to deviate from this",
            "   rate over time periods that are much shorter than an RTT.",
            "",
            "   One possible implementation strategy for pacing uses a leaky bucket",
            "   algorithm, where the capacity of the \"bucket\" is limited to the",
            "   maximum burst size and the rate the \"bucket\" fills is determined by",
            "   the above function."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "627371eae1ad5e3a",
            "627371eae1ad5e3a",
            "6ef71d6719880d8b",
            "eced398c52b4e356",
            "eced398c52b4e356",
            "cd2dc0faa9d081d4",
            "cd2dc0faa9d081d4",
            "69e44c4262e309dd",
            "69e44c4262e309dd"
          ],
          "title": "Pacing"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.8",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4038864e594da582",
                  "abae1b47e18fda3d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "When bytes in flight is smaller than the congestion window and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4038864e594da582",
                  "abae1b47e18fda3d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "sending is not pacing limited, the congestion window is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4038864e594da582",
                  "abae1b47e18fda3d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "underutilized.  This can happen due to insufficient application data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4038864e594da582",
                  "abae1b47e18fda3d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "or flow control limits.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4038864e594da582",
                  "abae1b47e18fda3d",
                  "412c81ff8202b111"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "When this occurs, the congestion window"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4038864e594da582",
                  "abae1b47e18fda3d",
                  "412c81ff8202b111"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "SHOULD NOT be increased in either slow start or congestion avoidance."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A sender that paces packets (see Section 7.7) might delay sending",
            "   packets and not fully utilize the congestion window due to this",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   delay.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da3d60441b578dde",
                  "71a2485004a71caa"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "A sender SHOULD NOT consider itself application limited if it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "da3d60441b578dde",
                  "71a2485004a71caa"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "would have fully utilized the congestion window without pacing delay."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "107fa52a41aa186f",
                  "03a229c2334a2d5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "A sender MAY implement alternative mechanisms to update its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "107fa52a41aa186f",
                  "03a229c2334a2d5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "congestion window after periods of underutilization, such as those"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "107fa52a41aa186f",
                  "03a229c2334a2d5a"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "proposed for TCP in [RFC7661]."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "412c81ff8202b111",
            "412c81ff8202b111",
            "71a2485004a71caa",
            "71a2485004a71caa",
            "03a229c2334a2d5a",
            "03a229c2334a2d5a",
            "03a229c2334a2d5a"
          ],
          "title": "Underutilizing the Congestion Window"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Security Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Loss detection and congestion control fundamentally involve the",
            "   consumption of signals, such as delay, loss, and ECN markings, from",
            "   unauthenticated entities.  An attacker can cause endpoints to reduce",
            "   their sending rate by manipulating these signals: by dropping",
            "   packets, by altering path delay strategically, or by changing ECN",
            "   codepoints."
          ],
          "title": "Loss and Congestion Signals"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Packets that carry only ACK frames can be heuristically identified by",
            "   observing packet size.  Acknowledgment patterns may expose",
            "   information about link characteristics or application behavior.  To",
            "   reduce leaked information, endpoints can bundle acknowledgments with",
            "   other frames, or they can use PADDING frames at a potential cost to",
            "   performance."
          ],
          "title": "Traffic Analysis"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.3",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b14d0fd63537279"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "A receiver can misreport ECN markings to alter the congestion"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b14d0fd63537279"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "response of a sender.  Suppressing reports of ECN-CE markings could"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b14d0fd63537279"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "cause a sender to increase their send rate.  This increase could"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b14d0fd63537279"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "result in congestion and loss."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f26b49d2d26567",
                  "1362daf7dad3713c",
                  "a6c58d93916763bd",
                  "34169af20e1b1b9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A sender can detect suppression of reports by marking occasional"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f26b49d2d26567",
                  "1362daf7dad3713c",
                  "a6c58d93916763bd",
                  "34169af20e1b1b9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "packets that it sends with an ECN-CE marking."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f26b49d2d26567",
                  "1362daf7dad3713c",
                  "34169af20e1b1b9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "  If a packet sent with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f26b49d2d26567",
                  "1362daf7dad3713c",
                  "34169af20e1b1b9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "an ECN-CE marking is not reported as having been CE marked when the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f26b49d2d26567",
                  "1362daf7dad3713c",
                  "34169af20e1b1b9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "packet is acknowledged, then the sender can disable ECN for that path"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f26b49d2d26567",
                  "1362daf7dad3713c",
                  "34169af20e1b1b9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "by not setting ECN-Capable Transport (ECT) codepoints in subsequent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "52f26b49d2d26567",
                  "1362daf7dad3713c",
                  "34169af20e1b1b9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "packets sent on that path [RFC3168]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Reporting additional ECN-CE markings will cause a sender to reduce",
            "   their sending rate, which is similar in effect to advertising reduced",
            "   connection flow control limits and so no advantage is gained by doing",
            "   so.",
            "",
            "   Endpoints choose the congestion controller that they use.  Congestion",
            "   controllers respond to reports of ECN-CE by reducing their rate, but",
            "   the response may vary.  Markings can be treated as equivalent to loss",
            "   [RFC3168], but other responses can be specified, such as [RFC8511] or",
            "   [RFC8311]."
          ],
          "title": "Misreporting ECN Markings"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [QUIC-TLS] Thomson, M., Ed. and S. Turner, Ed., \"Using TLS to Secure",
